{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.653494+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_007a4c022e83a30c049dd1ef1105f4a4024b9c76a577c21173cdee5f417435ca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2609.03669, 'Volterra Integral Reduction \\ for Boundary Diffusion Problems'] For every compact set $K\subset\mathbb R$, the spatial derivative of the
transition density $p(t,x,y)$ admits, as $t\to0^+$, the asymptotic expansion
\begin{equation} 
\partial_x p(t,x,y)
=
e^{-d^2(x,y)/(2t)}\!\left[
c_0(x,y)\,t^{-3/2}
+
c_1(x,y)\,t^{-1/2}
+
O_K\!\left(
t^{1/2}
\right)
\right],
\end{equation}
uniformly for $(x,y)\in K\times K$, in which $c_0(x,y)$ and $c_1(x,y)$ are explicit coefficients given in Remark~\ref{rem:coefficients}, while $d(x,y)$ is a suitable distance defined in Lemma~\ref{lemma:BB}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.374621+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_007c87cb684ce14664835202b64d60c60b26a80e51bd2e35f21fef75e0ce777b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 17 (Martingale Criterion) of arXiv:2606.04245, 'Properties of a Special Type of Filtration and its Martingale Criteria'] Let $\cT=\{t\in\RR_+:\PP(\gamma\geq t)>0\}$. 
    Let $F=(F_t)_{t\in\cT}$ be an $\cH$-measurable process with càdlàg paths, and let $L$ be an arbitrary random variable.

    Consider the process $M=(M_t)_{t\in\RR_+}$ defined by the equality:
    \begin{equation}
       M_t =F(t)\ind_{\{t<\gamma\} }+L\ind_{\{t\geq \gamma\}}. 
    \end{equation}   
    Then the following statements are equivalent:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item 
        The process $(M_t)_{t\in\cT}$ is a martingale.

        \item 
        For all $t\in\cT$, the integrability condition  \begin{equation}
            \EE(|M_t|)<\infty
        \end{equation}
        holds, and
        \begin{equation}
            \EE(M_t-M_0|\cH)=0\quad\text{a.s.}
        \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.067827+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_007e09ff7d699fcc6235e8552447439694d456edfb8e3a4ec4666b2d1049a486","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2606.00945, 'Ising model and percolation: from hexagonal lattice to 3-12 lattice'] Fix a $2$-polygon $(\Omega; A, B)$ and assume that $\Omega$ is flat at $B$. 
Let $\phi$ be a conformal map from $\Omega$ onto the upper-half plane $\HH$ such that $\phi(A)=\infty$ and $\phi(B)=0$. Define $\IO(z)=\sqrt{\phi'(z)/\phi'(B)}$. 
Suppose $(\Omega_{\312}^\delta;A^\delta,B^\delta)$ is a family of discrete $2$-polygons such that $(\Omega_{\312}^\delta;A^\delta,B^\delta)$ converges to $(\Omega; A, B)$ in the Carath\'{e}odory sense as $\delta\to 0$ and also assume that $\Omega_{\312}^\delta$ is flat near $B^\delta$. 
Set
\begin{align}
\beta_{\312}=\frac{1}{2}\log \frac{1+\sqrt{4\sqrt{3}-3}}{2}, \qquad x_{\312}=\frac{2}{1+\sqrt{4\sqrt{3}-3}}.
\end{align}
Consider Ising model with inverse temperature $\beta_{\312}$ in $(\Omega_{\312}^\delta;A^\delta,B^\delta)$ with Dobrushin boundary conditions.
Then the observable $\IO_{\312}^{\delta}(x_{\312}; \cdot)$ defined in~\eqref{eqn::Ising_observable} converges to $\IO$ uniformly on any compact subset of $\Omega$ as $\delta\to 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.053783+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_007f64ccfcc00dc4e9667e5da72da6fddc07aa7ad620c37c5ec7d47e6f6e9931","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 3 of arXiv:2607.01291, 'On perturbations that preserve the connectivity properties in tree percolations'] Let $C\subset[0,1]$ be a Cantor set. There is a constant $c>0$ and a sequence $\{q_n\}_{n\in\N}\subset(0,1)$ (allowed to depend on $C$) with $\prod_{n\in\N} q_n=0$, such that for all $\tfrac14\le\lambda\le\tfrac12$, $0<t<\tfrac12$,
