{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:33:11.952669+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_012fa4691b80edde119fc5b3f4e0d44e3ba99baca89717fdcf8347234b0f4705","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:mgf-comparison of arXiv:2607.14087, 'Stochastic Domination of Gaussian Maxima: A Resolution of the Weak Simplex Conjecture'] \label[corollary]{cor:mgf}
Let $G$ be any $m\times m$ correlation matrix, let
$\xi\sim\mathcal N(0,G)$, and let
$\xi^\triangle\sim\mathcal N(0,G_\triangle)$.  Then
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb E\exp\!\left\{\lambda\max_i\xi_i\right\}
  \leq
  \mathbb E\exp\!\left\{\lambda\max_i\xi_i^\triangle\right\}
  \qquad(\lambda>0).
\end{equation}
If $G\neq G_\triangle$, then (equation eq:mgf-comparison of the paper) is strict for every
$\lambda>0$.  Equivalently, equality for any one $\lambda>0$ holds if and
only if $G=G_\triangle$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.337785+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0130a066c97f26af6520e7dce323ce63c7ccdb80722cd9e36bc148f82c775ab9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 14 of arXiv:2506.15037, '2BSDE with uncertain horizon and application to stochastic control in erratic environments'] We say that $(\mathbb{P}, \beta)$ is a weak solution for \eqref{eq:Driftless SDE} if the distribution of $X^{t,x, \beta}_t$ under $ \mathbb{P}$ is $\delta_{x(t)}$, where $\delta$ denotes the Dirac measure and there exists a $\mathbb P$-Brownian motion, denoted by $W^{\mathbb{P}}$, such that
\[
X_s = x(t) + \int_t^s \sigma(r, X_{\cdot\wedge r}, \beta_r) dW_r^{\mathbb{P}}, \quad s \in [t, T], \quad \mathbb{P}\text{-a.s.}
\]
We denote by
\[
    \mathcal{N}(t, x) := \left\{ (\mathbb{P}, \beta): \text{ weak solutions of \eqref{eq:Driftless SDE}}\right\}
\]
and by $\mathcal{P}(t, x)$ the set of probability measures such that there exists an $\F$-optional process $\beta$ such that the probability coupled with the process $\beta$ is a weak solution of \eqref{eq:Driftless SDE}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.597951+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0131cc5afff8bf821cd948b8448d15e1109cb6a23af4222be58c9844f61f9c12","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:diffusion+jumpTypeUpperBound of arXiv:2412.05030, 'Characterization of Subordinate Symmetric Markov Processes'] The following estimate holds under the assumption in Proposition (prop:diffusion+jumpType of the paper),
