		\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.588877+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_01368b48f1e30115973cdc015d34b0c1657c79ec00be37b8c0902391291c9d09","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2608.05842, 'Asymptotic Expansion of the Kallianpur–Striebel Formula under Perturbations of Linear Mode'] Let $i=0,1,2,\cdots$. If a family of random variables $\{\eta_t^\epsilon\}_{0<\epsilon<1,t\geq 0}$ satisfies
