{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.679091+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0176752c8246381fbd8b2ed25cf4b79560b9bb7be3b4da34109226a89fe8b218","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mydef 1 of arXiv:2607.25986, 'Asymptotics of a two-species particle system associated to the doubly parabolic Keller-Seg'] Fix some $\rho_0 \in \Pp(\R^2)$ and some nonnegative $c_0\in L^\infty(\R^2)$. 
Consider the canonical space $C(\R_+,\R^2)$ equipped with its
canonical process $(w_t)_{t\geq 0}$ and its canonical filtration. Let $\Q \in \Pp(C(\R_+,\R^2))$
and denote $(\Q_t)_{t\geq 0}$ its family of one-dimensional time marginals. 
We say that $\Q$ solves the non-linear 
martingale problem $\mathcal{(MP)}(\rho_0,c_0)$ if
\begin{equation}

\int_0^t \int_{\R^2} \int_0^s \int_{\R^2}   (K^{\theta,\lambda}_{s-u}(x-y) + 
|\nabla K^{\theta,\lambda}_{s-u}(x-y)|) \Q_u(\dd y)  \dd u   \Q_s(\dd x) \dd s < \infty,
\end{equation}
and if for any $\varphi \in C_c^2(\R^2)$, the process
\begin{equation}

M^\varphi_t:=\varphi(w_t)-f(w_0)-\int_0^t \Big[ \Delta \varphi(w_u)+\chi \nabla \varphi(w_u)\cdot 
\Big(\nabla b_s^{c_0,\theta,\lambda}(w_s) + \int_0^u (\nabla K^{\theta,\lambda}_{u-r}\ast \Q_r)(w_u) \dd r \Big) \Big]\dd u
\end{equation}
is a $\Q$-martingale.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.297805+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0177813e6bc969304603b804f14daeba3e7460921a3f1209901754b1792386eb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Theorem~2.3 in \cite{forien_stepping_2019}) of arXiv:2606.23242, 'Correction to ``The stepping stone model in a random environment'' - limit theorems for th'] For all $ 0 < \varepsilon < T $ and $ R > 0 $ and for $ \mu $-almost every environment $ \omega \in \Omega $,
