{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.119658+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_017f69d4aa9254d5181366db322dc45c8cf27b181443f3a2104fc67e5189e9c7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma interpolation of arXiv:2608.17031, 'A shape theorem for periodic branching diffusion'] For $t \geq 0$, let $\mathcal{X}_t:=\{X_t(v):v\in \mathcal{N}_t\}$ and $\bar{\mathbf{v}}$ the effective drift. Fix $T>0$ and $\kappa>0$. Consider the event
    \begin{equation*}
