 =-(j+1)\sqrt{2j(N-j)}
\end{equation}
for $1\le j<k$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:53:39.186463+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0269d6c39f0b8d99c37fbfd1913f94e228f5fc5e742a63d3c959ef9fd2fab3c0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thmint 2 of arXiv:2608.27022, 'On LCK Geometry of Gauduchon Connections'] Let $(M, J, \omega)$ be an lck manifold and assume $\omega$ is Gauduchon satisfying the {second Bismut--Einstein equation}
