{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.578354+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0272f9a32a7c27d8bd1461823bfda822d60d3a6bdc3c2e199601d8cc25e63123","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2606.14876, 'High-Order Talagrand and Eldan--Gross Inequalities via Besov-Type Variance Functionals'] For all $k\in \Nbb_{\leq n}$, $f:\cube^n\to [-1,1]$, and $p\in [1,2)$,
