  for any particle lifespan $\ell > C_0$.

\item If $\alpha \ge d$, then for any $\rho \in (0, 1)$, there exist positive constants $C$ and $C_0$ such that
  \begin{align*}
    \lim_{L \to \infty} \mathbb P_L^+\left(\frac{|\mathcal{A}(CL)|}{L^d} \geq \rho\right) = 1
  \end{align*}
  for any particle lifespan $\ell > C_0$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.719428+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0292bf22fe2e23ba0ca69f9bdbdca68b0f2db89761f1063c64c61960b51e6b41","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2608.17449, 'Spectral Simplicity and Joint Eigenvalue Densities\\ for a Non-Gaussian Brownian Time Chan'] For every $\mu\in\mathcal M_*$ and every real-valued $h\in L^2(\mu)$,
\begin{equation}
