{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.645058+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02de625a63fd2530b632a8378c4eb4ff3c178398f2875b8e0fec04cd696b22f7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main of arXiv:2411.13926, 'Random walks on random walks:\\ non-perturbative results in high dimensions'] Consider the RWRW model  on $\mathbb{Z}^d$ with $\lambda \in [0,\infty)$ and  $d\geq 5$. 

\begin{itemize}
\item[a)] The Strong law of large numbers (SLLN):

There exists a  $v \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d$ such that
\begin{equation} \lim_{t \rightarrow \infty} \frac{X_t}{t} = v \quad P_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}}\text{-almost surely and in }L_1
\end{equation}

\item[b)]  Large deviation bounds (LDBs):

For every $\epsilon >0$ there exists constants $C,c>0$ such that 
\begin{equation}
P_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{P}}} \left( \left| \frac{X_t}{t} - v \right| > \epsilon \right) \leq Ce^{-ct}, \quad \text{ for all } t \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}},
\end{equation}
with $v\in \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d$ as in (equation eq:SLLN of the paper).
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

