{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.781978+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02e1d084301b20e5f24316806e3e5f9c5b31eeeb9bd99dffe7b6c2c24ba99b8c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 7 of arXiv:2609.03054, 'The classes of bivariate Schur and Herglotz matrix-valued rational functions: realizations'] Let $F\in\mathbb C^{n\times n}(z_1,z_2)$ be a rational matrix function as in Theorem~\ref{thm:posReRHP}~{\rm(i)}.  
