{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.250697+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02e703666f01d79c23695bbf0bcd834a0610a8d0340a833c44bff5b015b85d5b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq: loops to be inserted in STEP2 of arXiv:2411.16398, 'Large Deviations of Cover Time of Tori in Dimensions $d\geq 3$'] For each $\omega \in \mathcal{A}$ and $\boldsymbol{x}\in \mathcal{R}(\mathcal{L}_{\boldsymbol{F}}^{\beta_N}(\omega))$, we define the collection of loops to be inserted in the second step as follows:
