{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:08.166499+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02e85fa989d9fe44ff46a614e3dea667c17f7b46dde4e4193da2fb0a8406f73e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:jointSurvival of arXiv:2608.13452, 'Wasserstein stability of the zero cell of a Poisson hyperplane tessellation under directio'] Given the coupling $(Z_0^{(1)},Z_0^{(2)})$ defined by (equation eq:couplingZeroCells of the paper),
    we have, for all $r_1, r_2 > 0$,
    \begin{align*} 
        \mathbb{P}\bigl[\rho_{Z_0^{(1)}}(u) \geq r_1, \rho_{Z_0^{(2)}}(u) \geq r_2\bigr]
        &= \exp( - \gamma F_u(r_1,r_2) ),
    \end{align*}
    where
    \begin{align} 
        F_u(r_1,r_2)= F_u^{\Phi}(r_1,r_2)
        := \frac{1}{2} \int_{(S^{d-1})^2} |\langle r_1 u , v_1\rangle|+ |\langle r_2 u, v_2 \rangle| + |\langle r_1 u , v_1\rangle - \langle r_2 u, v_2 \rangle| \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} \Phi(v_1 , v_2) .
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.301493+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02ec94df5e25c3cca62fdc048f3ba369abe189c4c179df46f581fbf42a3a1be4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:resultknownmask of arXiv:2602.11129, 'Information-Theoretic Thresholds for Bipartite Latent-Space Graphs Under Noisy Observation'] Consider any fixed $p \in (0,1)$. 
    Then, the following holds with probability $1 - o(n)$ over $\ \mathbf{M} \sim \mathbb{M}(n, m, q)$ whenever $d \gg \log(n)^3$.

    \vspace{0.5em}
    If $p \neq \frac{1}{2}$ then:\hspace{1em} $\begin{aligned}[t]
            \hspace{0.8cm}\dtv{\mathbb{W}_{\mathbf{M}}(n, m, p, d)}{ \mathbb{M}(n, m, p)} &= \begin{cases} 1 - o(1) & \text{if } d \ll nmq^2  \hspace{1.3cm} \text{ or } \hspace{.1cm} d \ll m\sqrt{n}q  \\
            o(1) & \text{if } d \gg nmq^2\log(n) \hspace{.1cm} \text{ and } \hspace{.1cm} d \gg m\sqrt{n}q \log(n)
            \end{cases}
        \end{aligned}$

    \vspace{0.5em}
    If $p = \frac{1}{2}$ then:\hspace{1em} $\begin{aligned}[t]
        \hspace{0.8cm}\dtv{\mathbb{W}_{\mathbf{M}}(n, m, p, d)}{ \mathbb{M}(n, m, p)} &= \begin{cases} 1 - o(1) & \text{if } d \ll nmq^2 \\
            o(1) & \text{if } d \gg nmq^2\log(n)
            \end{cases}
        \end{aligned}$

    \vspace{0.5em}
    \noindent Here, $o(1)$ denotes a function that tends to zero as $n \rightarrow \infty$. Recall further that $m \ge n$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.299586+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02eceeaef2a51d5fe64745f5e2d9721ea20bd4cff229fb75a5c9c0df8d54a7c2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop IRL linearity of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] Assume~(hyp: pseudo lsc density of the paper),~(hyp: pseudo uniformity of the paper) and~(hyp: null border of the paper). 
