{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.020637+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_032d3cc9af3d3995b7c87ed4798fd1f98dff78b4adec7dbebc307de838560f23","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:C=G of arXiv:2605.15545, 'Crossover from subcritical to critical decay: \\ random walk, self-avoiding walk, percolat'] Let $\Lambda$ be symmetric and positive-definite,
and let $x,\eta \in \mathbb{R}^d$.
Define $a^2= \eta\cdot \Lambda^{-1} \eta$.
Then
\begin{equation} 
\mathbb{C}(x;\eta,\Lambda)
=  \frac 1 {\sqrt{\det \Lambda}}
