{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.570454+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03523bad158dc29ed69f7bb9573d604f2426e080edabfdcd56daf76efd51da18","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:overlap-sde of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] For indices $i$ with $|\lambda_i - 2| \leq N^{-2/3+\varepsilon/2}$, the overlap satisfies
