{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.432621+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03858fee016cd2cbc8468affb75a1c2568915a89667f4360356fe85213de6f69","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:centered-lyapunov-moment-equivalence of arXiv:2605.20697, 'Uniform-in-time propagation of chaos for \\ Second-Order Consensus-Based Optimization'] Let \(p\geqslant2\). Under the parameter conditions of (assump:admissibility of the paper), the strict positivity of the equivalence constants \(c_1^{(2)}>0\) and \(c_1(a_p,p)>0\) is guaranteed. Define the constant \(K_{p,\gamma} := \max\{1+2^{p-1}\gamma^{-p}, \, 2^{p-1}\}\), and set
\begin{equation}
    C_{p,1} := \frac{1}{K_{p,\gamma}} \begin{cases} c_1^{(2)}, & p=2,\\ c_1(a_p,p), & p>2 \end{cases}, \qquad
