{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:29.005426+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0391b79fc015cbb5fcb7e168722e27cf26698ec1e8d2894b4a1423b68b142d71","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop instP gau LB of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] There exists a deterministic constant $c \in (0, \infty)$ such that,
