{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.538989+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03bd7be7e40697313c922658ee6cffb702540952c41a93033cc05d064ddd2129","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t.BQ of arXiv:2411.12003, 'Central Limit Theorem for non-stationary random products of $\SL(2, \R)$ matrices'] Let $\{X_k, k \ge 1\}$ be independent and identically distributed random matrices in ${\mathrm{SL}}(d, {\mathbb R})$. 
    Assume that $G_X$ is non-compact and  
    \textit{strongly irreducible}
    and
    \begin{equation} 
        \mathbb{E}\left[(\log \|X_1\|)^2 \right]

        < \infty.
    \end{equation}
    Then there exists $\sigma>0$ such that the random variables
