{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.596744+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_043ef63693a7bd0306015f689b5018560d7504b996767694598e0b2a30891c40","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop couple_iid of arXiv:2412.03415, 'Critical first passage percolation on random graphs'] First consider the shortest weight graph ${\sf SWG}^v$ from a single randomly sampled vertex $v$. Fix any $m_n = o(\sqrt{n})$.  Then under Assumptions (ass of the paper):
\begin{enumeratea}
\item {\bf Probability of collision from a single source:} Then the probability of collision $\pr( R_{\mathrm{col}}\leqslant m_n) \to 0$ as $n\to \infty$. 
\item {\bf Coupling to an {\it i.i.d.} sequence:} Let $\mathbf{d}$ be a given degree sequence and let $L_n = \sum_{i=1}^n d_i$. Consider the empirical distribution
 \begin{equation} 
 g^{(n)}_k :=\sum_{i=1}^n \frac{ (k+1)\mathds{1}\{d_i=k+1\}}{L_n}, \qquad k\geqslant 0.
 \end{equation} 
Let $\set{Y_i^{\scriptscriptstyle(n)}:i\geqslant 2}$ be an \emph{i.i.d.}~sequence with distribution $(g^{(n)}_k)_{k\geqslant 0}$.  There is a coupling of $(B_{R_i})_{2\leqslant i\leqslant m_n }$ with $(Y_i)_{2\leqslant i\leqslant m_n}$ such that 
\[\pr(\cap_{i=2}^{m_n}\set{B_{R_i} = Y_i^{\scriptscriptstyle(n)}}) \to 1, \qquad \text{ as } n\to\infty. \]
\item {\bf Collision events from multiple sources:} Next consider the growth from two clusters first from $v$ and then from $u$ as described above. Then $\pr( \min (R^v, \tilde{R}^u) \leqslant m_n) \to 0$ as $n\to \infty$. 
\item {\bf Coupling for multiple sources:} The coupling in (b) with an \emph{i.i.d.}~sequence for a single source ${\sf SWG}^v$ continues to hold starting from two distinct randomly sampled sources.  
\end{enumeratea}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:41.019152+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_043ef6c507946d027e89887c20524f06181fdabe8b8c359e7da441d3454f70b0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem mt2 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] Fix $T\ge 1$, and assume that conditions (equation 2-80 of the paper), (equation 2-90 of the paper)
