{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.736956+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0456f9a717759ac43bc52725a8b0821ea0594d8756ee7459ac2cdbfe0f4681a1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 38 of arXiv:2605.02002, 'Glauber dynamics for random field Ising models on bounded degree graphs and MLSI'] Let $p\geq 1,t\geq 0$, consider a subset $A\subseteq [p]$ and a tuple of vertices $u_1,\cdots,u_p\in G$. Then for any sequence of integers $(\ell_i)_{i\in A}$ where 
