{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.570906+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_04572c66ef00976142ea29aac773ec0edd1bd600b3d7d6b4572f186e9402999d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:decorrelation of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] For distinct indices $i \neq j$ with $|\lambda_i - 2|, |\lambda_j - 2| \leq N^{-2/3+\varepsilon/2}$ and $t \leq t_* = N^{-1/3+\varepsilon}$:
