{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.684821+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_048c30233c0120aa73693d13ebe1255bca8bbec3ce06bbb2c80eb2b33f358e5a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2608.30898, 'Necessity of Ladyzhenskaya \& Ural'tseva's sufficient conditions in nonuniform ellipticity'] Let $q\in (1,2)$ be any number. There exist $\ell_{p}\equiv \ell_{p}(q)>0$, a cube $Q_{p}:=(-\ell_{p},\ell_{p})^{2}\subset \mathbb{R}^{2}$ and a function $u\in W^{1,\infty}(Q_{p})$ with $\sup_{(x,y)\in \bar{Q}_{p}}\snr{Du(x,y)}\le 1$, analytic in a neighborhood of $Q_{p}$, such that $u$ is a local maximizer of functional $\mathcal{J}_{q}(\ \cdot\ ;Q_{p})$ in \eqref{0.0}. Specifically, integral identity
