{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.285905+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_053c9fee547d867d3bb5bc128fa08731469738c9f42838ee275cf3b53a2205a1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem A1 of arXiv:2411.01847, 'Well-Posedness of Stochastic Chemotaxis System'] Let $\left(e^{-tA}\right)_{t\geq 0}$ be the Neumann heat semigroup in $\mathcal{O}$.

       Let $\nu_1$ denote the first nonzero eigenvalue of $A$ on $\mathcal{O}$ under Neumann boundary condition. Then, there exists a constant $C$, depending only on $\mathcal{O}$, such that:
      \begin{itemize}
