{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.706551+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_054eaffbcec411f24e9b7660a0dc99a4f633fccbaa38299e7993116ef4bf1d4e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:Bsup of arXiv:2510.24424, 'On the Fourier Coefficients of Critical Gaussian Multiplicative Chaos'] Let $B_t$ be a standard linear Brownian motion. Then there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $t>e$, $a>0$,
    \begin{align}
        \mathbb{P}\Big(\sup_{s\in [e,t]}B_s\leq a\Big) \leq C\frac{(a+1)}{\sqrt{t}+1}.
    \end{align}
    Furthermore, if $a,b>0$ and $\mathbb{P}_{(0,a)}^{(t,b)}$ denotes the law of a Brownian bridge of length $t>e$ from $a$ to $b$, then
    \begin{align}
        \mathbb{P}_{(0,a)}^{(t,b)}\Big(B_s\geq 0,\forall s\in [e,t]\Big) \leq C \frac{(a+1)(b+1)}{t+1}.
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.455105+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0552da640980bbfde45a50ec507498f129cf328d41c6a869084b28e7dba35295","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 (Strong failure of regularity persistence) of arXiv:2609.02523, '\bf Strong Ill-Posedness in critical and subcritical regimes for the Hunter--Saxton equati'] For any $s\in (1, \nicefrac {3}{2}]$, there exists an initial datum
