{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.244974+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05b6718db756a6cfa2ad175b581084d26840fa05702ebdaf5a7bba102eda6db1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 6 (Level lines of the discrete height) of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Given $a,b,c>0$ and the height function $H$ of a tiling $\eta$ of $\mX_{a,b,c}$ we define the level lines $\mathtt U_{a,b,c}^h:[0,a+c]\cap(1/N)\mathbb Z\mapsto[0,b+c]\cap(1/N)(\mathbb Z+1/2)$ with $h\in[0,b]\cap(1/N)(\mathbb Z+1/2)$ as
