{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.201279+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06a825dbca87746a9aec8ad5c1c3bcdd9a66dd7a12394acb7a0a9ee238d6437d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:ent_stab of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] Suppose there exists a deterministic function $\kappa:[0,1]\to {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} _+$ such that  $\l({\rm Cov}[\ensuremath{\mathcal T}_v\rho_t]) \le \kappa(t)$ a.s., for all $t \in [0,1],$ for all $v\in{\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} ^{L}$.
	Then,  for all functions $F\ge 0$,
