{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.707078+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06b223706c5d88ca6fc62082ce6d11a6ce4e4cc999974a19d707268b40f96934","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:intro-Einaiiagapi of arXiv:2412.09290, 'Asymptotics of Harish-Chandra transform and infinitesimal freeness'] (Theorem (Einaiiagapi of the paper))
  Let $A$ be a random Hermitian matrix of size $N$. Assume that for every finite $r$ one has
  \begin{equation}
    \lim_{N \rightarrow \infty} N \left( \frac{1}{N} \log \mathbb{E}[H \text{}
    C (x_1, \ldots, x_r, 0^{N - r} ; \lambda_1 (A), \ldots, \lambda_N (A))] -
    \sum_{i = 1}^r \Psi (x_i) \right) = \sum_{i = 1}^r \Phi (x_i), 
  \end{equation}
  where $\Psi, \Phi$ are smooth functions in a (complex) neighborhood of $0$ and the
  above convergence is uniform in a (complex) neighborhood of $0^r$. Then one has the following     limit:
  \begin{equation}
    \lim_{N \rightarrow \infty} N \left( \frac{1}{N^{k + 1}} \mathbb{E} \left[
    \sum_{i = 1}^N \lambda_i^k (A) \right] -\ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\mu}}_k \right)
    =\ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\mu}}'_k, 
  \end{equation}
  where 
  \begin{equation}
    \ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\mu}}_n = \sum_{m = 0}^{n - 1} \frac{n!}{m! (m + 1) ! (n - m) !}
    \frac{\mathrm{d}^m}{\mathrm{d} x^m} ((\Psi' (x))^{n - m}) {\mbox{\rotatebox[origin=c]{-90}{${-\!\!-}$}}}_{x =
    0}, 
  \end{equation}
  \begin{equation}
    \ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\mu}}'_k := \sum_{m = 0}^{k - 1} \frac{k!}{m! (m + 1) !
    (k - m - 1) !}  \left. \frac{\mathrm{d}^m}{\mathrm{d} x^m} ((\Psi' (x))^{k - m
    - 1} \Phi' (x)) \right|_{x = 0} . 
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.500887+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06b2e6a9935de366afc4debc5d7201d3dfcc7169d9cc4d2ac9f9d8b81dcdde04","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:block-cap-coordinate-lower of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[corollary]{cor:block-growing-cutoff-separation}
Retain the notation of (thm:mesoscopic-block-lower of the paper).  Every
\(x\in\mathcal K_{N,t}\) satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \left\lVertx\right\rVert_\infty\ge\frac{t}{\sqrt{k_N}}
 =\left(\frac{t}{\sqrt c}+o(1)\right)N^{-1/(2p)}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, if a point cutoff \(D_{N,r_N}\) from
(thm:growing-point-cutoff of the paper) intersects \(\mathcal K_{N,t}\), then
\begin{equation}
 q_N^{\rm gr}=\sqrt N\,r_N^{p-1}
 \ge
 \left(t^{p-1}c^{-(p-1)/2}+o(1)\right)N^{1/(2p)}.
\end{equation}
In particular, every growing cutoff for which
\(q_N^{\rm gr}=O(1)\), and hence every cutoff in the pressure-universal
regime \(q_N^{\rm gr}\to0\), is eventually disjoint from the entire cap
\(\mathcal K_{N,t}\) that creates the coherent-block critical point.","status":"unverified"}

