{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.284343+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_07268673a89560ec4cf5156f1e02d7038fdaed67db53deac9b7a7162ef5f615b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 12 (Finite-task audit planner) of arXiv:2608.21496, '2608.21496'] For every $a$ and $0<\alpha<1$, with probability at least $1-\alpha$,
