{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:06:21.737242+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_072e957e625e0f33810596802a82b59f7dd197dc900332be48ec9a291092c796","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 34 of arXiv:2607.21374, 'Local structure at the maximum and sharp persistence asymptotics of rough fractional Brown'] Let \(m_H:=\lceil1/H\rceil\).  Then, for every \(T>0\),
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal Z(2^{-1/H}T)
  \leq p_*^{-m_H}\mathcal Z(T)

