{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.774075+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_073a4c14ed540681910565c3c75abce98797ee02e2ce16000d140379cbaf6fad","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:PropertiesHarmonic of arXiv:2609.01464, 'Removability of non-isolated singularities for Einstein metrics and RCD spaces'] Let $n\geqslant 2$ be an integer. Let $(X,\mathrm{d},\mathcal{H}^n)$ be an $\mathrm{RCD}(-K,n)$ space, with $0\leqslant K\leqslant 1$. 
    Let $u:B_3(x)\to \mathbb R$ be a harmonic function, and let 
    \[
    D:=\fint_{B_2(x)} ||\nabla u|^2-1|\mathrm{d}\mathcal{H}^n.
    \] 
    Then there exists $C:=C(n)$ such that:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item For every $0<r<1$ we have that
        \begin{equation}
        r^2\fint_{B_r(x)}|\operatorname{Hess} u|^2\mathrm{d}\mathcal{H}^n \leqslant C(n)\left(Kr^2 + \fint_{B_{2r}(x)}||\nabla u|^2-1|\mathrm{d}\mathcal{H}^n\right);
        \end{equation}
        \item We have that for almost every $y\in B_1(x)$
        \begin{equation}
        |\nabla u|^2(y)\leqslant 1+C(n)(D+K).
        \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:48:17.116296+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_073ae52cf62f0c927eb9599b0645f7e8befe1a2d4b7a2f5c129d2d3963b2f571","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 137 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Adopt the notation and assumptions of \Cref{cor:cella1}, and denote
	\begin{flalign}
          \widetilde{\mathcal{H}} (\hat{x}, \hat{y}) = \mathfrak{d}^{-1/2} \mathfrak{e}^{-3/2} \mathcal{H}_{q;a,b,c} (x, y) \quad \text{if}\quad \gamma'>0,\\
