{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:53:51.341861+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_07448cbdbee06d16f5c20f24d9e2ed0439a9487abc5e46b41ddbf2280ca4fb1f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop.reg of arXiv:2605.05904, 'Schr\"odinger's problem with constraints'] Under Assumption (a:main of the paper), the following statements hold:
\begin{enumerate}
\item  For any $t\in (0,1], y\in E $, there exists $q(\cdot, t; \cdot, y) \in C^{1,2}([0,t)\times E)$ such that
\begin{align} 
\begin{split}
\bbP^{s,z}(Z_t\in dy)&=q(s,t;z,y)dy,  \quad s<t,\, z\in E\quad \text{and}\\
L(s,t;z)&:=\bbP^{s,z}(Z_t=\ell)=1-\int_E q(s,t;z,y)dy, \quad s<t,\,\, z\in E. 
\end{split}
\end{align}
Moreover, if $\ell$ is finite, for all $t>s$ and $y\in E$ we have
\[
\lim_{z\rightarrow \ell}q(s,t;z,y)=0.
\]
\item  The transition density $q$ and its derivatives satisfy the following bounds:
\[
|D_s^\alpha D_z^\beta q(s,t;z,y)|\leq c(t-s)^{-\frac{1+2\alpha +\beta}{2}}\exp\left(-C\frac{(y-z)^2}{t-s}\right),
\]
for $2\alpha+\beta \leq 2$, where  $c$ and $C$ are constants independent of $s,t,z$ and $y$, and $D_s^{\alpha}$ (resp. $D_z^{\alpha}$) denotes the $\alpha$-th partial derivative with respect to $s$ (resp. $z$).

\item  For any $r>0$, $y\in E$, and $t>0$, 
\begin{align}
&\sup_{\substack{z\in B_r^c(y)\\s<t}}q(s,t;z,y)<\infty,\quad \text{and}\\
&\lim_{s\rightarrow 0}\int_{B_r^c(z)}q(0,t-s;x,y)q(t-s,t;y,z)dy=0, \quad \forall x\in E, 
\end{align}
where $B_r(y):=\{z\in E:|y-z|<r\}$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.096432+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0744f701a316e08b23cf10fd66b1fddd1d991b9ff940548d16939e16923e47c4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Sharp reduced-Palm hole asymptotics) of arXiv:2608.20101, '\bfseries Largest bulk gap of the complex Ginibre ensemble'] As \(r\to\infty\),
