{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.501566+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_077b53de0008985e34bfedc1aa2651557b6f7af721c315eb2f752974fc7b8f4a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma expectation_truncated_gaussian of arXiv:2607.22480, 'Distinguishability threshold for random geometric graphs'] Let $t$ be a real number and let $X\sim \mathcal{N}(0, \sigma^2)$. If $X_t^+$ denotes the variable $X$ conditioned on $X\geq t\sigma$, and $X_t^-$ denotes the variable $X$ conditioned on $X\leq t\sigma$, then
\begin{align*}
    &\mathbb{E}\big[X_t^-\big]=-\lambda(t)\sigma \qquad \text{ and }\qquad\Var\big(X_t^-\big)=\sigma^2\Big(1-t\lambda(t)-\lambda(t)^2\Big),\text{ and }\\
    &\mathbb{E}\big[X_t^+\big]=\lambda(-t)\sigma\qquad \text{ and }\qquad\Var\big(X_t^+\big)=\sigma^2\Big(1+t\lambda(-t)-\lambda(-t)^2\Big).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:55:57.002861+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0782423aaa8453194aa9d78e798da1cb06066f3b0697af44ae04a2860240f84c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2609.02790, 'Full-Model Optimality for Tunable Linear Generative Priors in Compressed Sensing'] Under Lemma \ref{Under_E(k)} assumption, let  \(M_k = A_kG_k \) be a sequence of matrices evolving as \( M_k = [M_{k-1}, m_k] \), where \( m_k = \sigma_ka_k \) is an additional column vector. The projection matrices associated with these matrices are given by:
\[
