{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.923598+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_07b8a8c7a77ab8576a6d11d0a8c6700c98a535a98f85e14be3c3efff9f0ba6d3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:multinomial_measures of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Let $G = (V,E)$ be a bipartite graph with 
 vertex multiplicities ${\mathbf N} = (N_v)_{v\in V}$. Given edge weights $(w_e)_{e\in E}$, the corresponding \textit{multinomial dimer measure} is the probability measure on $\Omega_{{\mathbf N}}$ where
\begin{align*}
    \mathbb{P}(M) = \frac{\left|\pi^{-1}(M)\right|}{Z} \prod_{e\in M} w_e^{M_e}
\end{align*}
where $Z=Z_{G,{\mathbf N}}$ is the same partition function, given below. In other words, the multinomial dimer measure is the measure on $\Omega_{{\mathbf N}}$ which is the projection of the Boltzmann measure on dimer covers of $G_{{\mathbf N}}$ defined in (equation eq:lifted_measures of the paper). We also refer to the measure in (equation eq:lifted_measures of the paper) as the \textit{lifted} version of the multinomial dimer measure.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.726578+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_07bcf2301cd785a2d1a9ebe3333f3d9b14dce360609de6f3d387f3d8e7a72caf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma operators_with_M of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] Fix a path $\pi(t,dx)=\rho_t(x)\;dx$ in $ {\mathcal{D}}([0,T],\mathscr{M}_{ac})$. Assume $ {\rho}$  {to satisfy the same hypothesis as in Lemma (decomposition_lemma of the paper).} Then, there exists an $M\in L^2(\sigma(\rho)^{-1})$ satisfying 
