{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.749203+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_07d8cf7b6a5f3f26026badc89470b5804422f12c0b0b2ae6bd9b3d52e129ce34","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:non_lin_MP of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] Let $\nu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$. A probability measure $\mathbb{P}_{\nu}$, on $(C_{\infty},\mathcal{B})$, is a solution to NL-MP$({\bf b},{\boldsymbol\sigma};\nu)$ if it is a solution to MP$({\bf b}_{\boldsymbol\mu}, {\boldsymbol\sigma}_{\boldsymbol\mu};0,\nu)$ (see Definition (def:MP_lin of the paper)), with 
