{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.257756+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_07f11de687dbbd375f6d56dc4ab2e569b5155bbf9e5e131375a719fc1eddc217","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition OLKasefzs of arXiv:2603.12774, 'Synchronization by noise for stochastic differential equations driven by fractional Browni'] For each $\omega=(\omega^-,\omega^+)\in \tilde{\Omega}$, $n\in\mathbb{N}$ and each Borel set $A\subseteq \mathbb{R}^d$, we define
