{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.910313+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0841c43983d958050ffdce5461abd0ab417e724aaa4a701aca14286b2a66bf28","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:weak, density of arXiv:2411.00663, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of invariant capacities and applications'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},V,T)$ be a  capacity preserving system, where $(\Omega,\mathcal{F})$ is standard and $V$ is an upper probability. Then $V$ is weakly mixing if and only if there exists $Q\in\mathcal{ M}^{wm}(T)\cap\operatorname{core}(V)$   such that for any $f\in L^\infty(\Omega,\mathcal{F},Q)$, there exists a subset $J=J_f$ of $\mathbb{N}$ with  $D(J)=0$ such that for any $g\in L^\infty(\Omega,\mathcal{F},Q)$,
