{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.330105+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08868d3108f7cd296205849dd8a3fabd456430e5d0e0c7973dc8d0162e9f2d6e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2BE of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] Let $f:\Omega\longrightarrow\mathbb{R}$ be a local function whose support is included in $\{0,\hdots ,\ell_0-1\}$ for some $\ell_0\ge 1$. Then, there exists a constant $C_{15}=C_{15}(\kappa ,\rho ,\mathcal{E} ,f)>0$ such that for any $t\in [0,T]$, any $\ell\ge\ell_0$ and any measurable function $v:[0,T]\longrightarrow\ell^2(\mathbb{Z} )$, we have 
