{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.149859+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08af11063072d04e5c76d1099356f983b7e24ad1f7c5c0b823ccdd760c013fd9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem high-mass-decays of arXiv:2607.05097, 'Asymptotics of Lyapunov Exponents and Phase Transitions for Fluids with Degenerate Forcing'] For every $\tilde z_0 \in \mathbb{R}^d$, $\eta \in (0,\eta^*(\tilde z_0))$, and $C, \kappa, \rho > 0$ there is some $\delta > 0$ such that for all $v_0 \in S^{n-1}$, $z_0 \in \mathbb{R}^d$ with $\|\tilde z_0 - z_0\| < \delta$, and $\epsilon < \delta$ we have
    \begin{align*}
       \mathbb{P}\Big( \sup_{t \leq T_\epsilon} \|P_{\eta}(z_0)v^\epsilon(t)\| \leq \delta \text{ and } \|x^\epsilon(T_\epsilon)\| \geq e^{(\lambda-\eta+\kappa)T_\epsilon}\|x_0\|\Big) < \rho\,,
    \end{align*}
    where we set $T_\epsilon = C\ln \epsilon^{-1}$ and $\lambda \coloneqq \lambda^\epsilon(z_0) \coloneqq \lambda(A^\epsilon(z_0))$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.259240+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08af4e690a1f4f67a6e84adf35882fa98c0c4274707928676bf0d43c6e475945","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition integrability of arXiv:2410.23509, 'Dynkin Games for L\'evy Processes'] Consider a L\'evy process $X$,
