{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:55:57.002622+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08b3993dcb60c4e14b330b505ba0f07181a5287d9724656a7644f1fb7042b413","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2609.02790, 'Full-Model Optimality for Tunable Linear Generative Priors in Compressed Sensing'] Under the same assumptions as Lemma \ref{Under_E(k)}, for fixed $m \in [1,n]$, $k \in [m+1,n]$, let $T_1(k)=\big\langle G_k^2,P_{G_k^TA_k^T} \big\rangle=\big\langle G_k^2,P_{M_k^T} \big\rangle$  ,
