{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.677396+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08b8660dde2ecba2aaaf29b9283599c57f49cf1b243cd7f286203c34d8878fbd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop main of arXiv:2411.12149, 'Airy limit for $\beta$-additions through Dunkl operators'] Let $z_{c}(N)>0,\ z_{c}>0$ be the unique root of $V'_{N}(z),\ V'(z)$ on $(0,\frac{1}{a_{1}})$ respectively. Then $V_{N}(z_{c}(N))>0,\ V(z_{c})>0$, and  
