		-\bigl(b^{-m}+c^{-m}\bigr)B_{m+1}(1-t)\Bigr],
	\end{multline}
	where $W_m=\kappa^{-m}+(1-\kappa)^{-m}+\eta^{-m}+(1-\eta)^{-m}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.341774+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08c7c4828c8344a2fee9d78dfb93e479ef069a8fb2a1f31774271740eea888b6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 (Deterministic drift bound under small-set sparsity) of arXiv:2604.20514, 'Macroscopic loops in the random loop model on sparse random graphs'] Let \(G=(V,E)\) be a finite graph with \(|V|=n\), and assume that \eqref{eq:A1}
