{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.359675+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08d65f4bf75240e8e6f42849a64fe2de335b46d39bf45d7cddf90bc74618f842","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:holder-controlled2 of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] For any $s\in[0,1)$, the covariance function $Q_s$ is  uniformly of H\"older controlled $2$-dimensional $1/(2H)$-variation, that is, there exists a constant $C=C(H)$  such that for any $(s,u,t)\in[0,1]_\leq^3$ one has
