{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.655805+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08e9bc964ea808436efecd9eab3f6503de538049f7c82dc4c0337e999987339a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2605.16162, 'Deconfinement For $\mathrm{SO}(3)$ Lattice Yang--Mills at Strong Coupling'] Suppose $k<N$ and both $k$ and $N$ are odd. Then if $Q \sim \mrm{Haar}(\mrm{SO}(N))$,
