{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.592386+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08eadcaf931127d155f8a52a0ad7e73f339662fe269808fd7180bd53f34af2fd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor Kor: Diag.matrix, char. Poly. superkrit. Reg. of arXiv:2509.15790, 'Covariance matrices of volume power functionals of random simplicial complexes -- an asymp'] Assuming the situation of Theorem (Thm: EW.e, ER.e superkrit. Reg. of the paper) set  $D=\text{diag}(\lambda_1,\dots,\lambda_1,\lambda_2)\in \mathbb{R}^{n \times n}$
and $S \in \mathbb{R}^{n \times n}$ with column vectors $v_1, \dots,v_n$.
Under the given conditions $\Sigma_n$ is similar to $D$ and $D=S^{-1} \Sigma_n S$, where $S^{-1} = (\tilde{s}_{ij})\in \mathbb{R}^{n \times n}$ with entries
\begin{align*} 
\tilde{s}_{ij} = \left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
