{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.405333+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08ecf3ca336e63eb559287a229890348dedab4624b43751fc70097aa93707975","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2604.06516, 'From stochastic individual-based models to free-boundary Hamilton-Jacobi equations'] The set $\Omega_a$ is an open set. The function $u_a$ belongs to $C(\adh(\Omega_a))$ and it is the unique locally Lipschitz-continuous and bounded above viscosity solution of the following Hamilton-Jacobi equation  
