{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.641052+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_090fcbf22d27e2acd916eb08c22561b8860593a0daaea4470f5a677916f3deab","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem PI-3 of arXiv:2411.13788, '\bf Gradient bounds and Liouville property for a class of hypoelliptic diffusion via coupl'] Let $f\in C^1\left(\mathbb{R}^{m_0}\times\cdots\times\mathbb{R}^{m_r}\right)$ be a globally Lipschitz bounded function. Then for any $t\ge0$, $x=(x^{(1)},\cdots,x^{(r+1)})\in \mathbb{R}^{m_0}\times\cdots\times\mathbb{R}^{m_r}$,  we have
