Then 
\begin{align}
    \rho_{2n}^{(2)}(0,\lambda)=\frac{1}{2\pi^2} \sum_{j=1}^\infty \mathbf{v}_n^{T} \cdot \mathbf{s}_{2j}\,  \lambda^{2j}.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.574449+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_094f445c08e4dd1ff27d562895566be2f49a518701f5f87e2deb332ef6482b8b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:coercivity_est of arXiv:2605.15742, 'Turbulent stretching of FENE dumbbell polymer model via special stochastic scaling and sin'] Let $\kappa/(2+ \kappa_T \beta)> 1$, then there exists $\eta >0$ such that if $k_T\beta \le \eta$, there exists positive constants $C$, $\theta$ such that for every $f\in V_0$ it holds 
