{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.693313+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_095e46ef669cd91bf3c96c954394c698f5893cd4ae7f2ab6ea970046abae16e3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:300.3.7 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] For each $k \geq 1$ there exists a measure $\nu_k$ on $\mathbb{R}^{{\rm Q}(k)}$ with Radon marginals such that, for any $M \in (0,\infty)$,  
\begin{multline}

