{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.076930+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0993513e257cbc6c80587c446fe30179b79530760b0c5d5db2e293c2e9cb56f5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:sine_HP of arXiv:2509.15446, 'On the pair correlation function of the $\Sineb$ process'] Fix $\beta>0$ and let $\rho_{\beta,\beta/2}^{(1)}$ be the density (one-point function) of the  $\operatorname{HP}_{\beta, \beta/2}$ process. Let $\rho_{\beta}^{(2)}$ denote the pair correlation (two-point function) of the  $\operatorname{Sine}_{\beta}$ process. Then
