{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.803817+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09a01cc0488a0cb6dfb94c0ebfa9e1b7c76b30967c42533a5064aab1ad1517de","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:variance-bounds of arXiv:2605.17082, 'Spectral Purification in Reversible Markov Chains: Hidden Parameters, Observable Equivalen'] Assume $\lambda_2 > \lambda_3$. Then for any $k \ge 0$,
