{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.322886+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09a075ef3b966ade3df72b9ebbd225c5fb149e9fce84261db37345f070db8bae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 (Weighted transitions) of arXiv:2608.30304, '2608.30304'] Let $a,b\ge-\tfrac12$, $n\ge1$ and $-1<x<1$. Then
\begin{align}
F_{n,a,b}(x)&\le A^L_{n,a,b}\,F_{n-1,a,b+2}(x)
+B^L_{n,a,b}\,(1+x)^{-1/2}F_{n-1,a,b+1}(x),\\
F_{n,a,b}(x)&\le A^R_{n,a,b}\,F_{n-1,a+2,b}(x)
+B^R_{n,a,b}\,(1-x)^{-1/2}F_{n-1,a+1,b}(x),
