    \langle y_1 - y_2, g(x,y_1)-g(x,y_2) \rangle + \frac{p-1}{2} |\sigma(x,y_1)-\sigma(x,y_2)|_F^2 \leq -\beta|y_1-y_2|^2.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:18.867385+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a76c8e622efba87e2ca818cb2fd9c2bf9d69cddcbefd76d5eee5a2b6ed22eaf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defprop gamma fct of arXiv:2609.02409, 'Membranes and Maps'] The power series
    \begin{equation}
        \gamfct{x}{u}
        =
        \exp\bigg(
            \sum_{k>0}
                \frac{B_{2k}}{2k \, (2k+1)!} \,
                B_{2k+1}(x) \,
                u^{2k}
        \bigg) \,.
    \end{equation}
    is the unique element of $\bQ[x]\llbracket u \rrbracket$ satisfying
    \begin{equation}

        \gamfct{x+1}{u}
        =
        \cS(u x) \, \gamfct{x}{u} \,,
        \qquad
        \gamfct{0}{u}
        =
        1 \,.
    \end{equation}
    Here, $B_k(x)$ denotes the Bernoulli polynomial $\frac{t \mathrm{e}^{x t}}{\mathrm{e}^{t}-1} \eqqcolon \sum_{k\geq 0} \frac{B_k(x)}{k!} t^k $, and $B_k \coloneqq B_k(0)$ denotes the Bernoulli number.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.871826+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a773943419fb78cf549c9f632a02ddd695543df418b22e844011fc6621604ab","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:approx_psi_phi of arXiv:2605.07832, 'A Bismut -Elworthy formula for BSDEs with degenerate noise'] Let $\psi$ and $\phi$ satisfy Hypothesis (ip-psiphi-li of the paper). Hence, there exist sequences $(\psi_n)$ and $(\phi_n)$ such that
\begin{enumerate}[\rm(i)]
\item for every $n\in\mathbb N$ we have $\phi_n\in\mathcal G^{1}(H,\mathbb R)$ and $\psi(t,\cdot,\cdot,\cdot)\in\mathcal G^{1,1,1}(H\times \mathbb R\times U,\mathbb R)$ for every $t\in[0,T]$;
\item for every $n\in\mathbb N$ there exist constants $C_n>0$ and $m_n\geq0$ such that 
\begin{align*}
|\nabla_x\psi_n(t,x,y,z)h|\leq C_n|h|(1+|z|)(1+|x|+|y|)^{m_n}, \qquad |\nabla_x\phi_n(x)h|\leq C_n|h|
\end{align*}
for every $t\in[0,T]$ and every $(x,y,z,h)\in H\times \mathbb R\times U\times H$;
\item there exist positive constants $\widetilde L_\psi$, $\widetilde K_\psi$ and $ \widetilde K_\phi$, which only depend on $L_\psi,K_\psi$, $K_\phi$ and $m$, such that
\begin{align*}
& |\psi_n(t,x,y_1,z_1)-\psi_n(t,x,y_2,z_2)|\leq \widetilde L_\psi(|y_1-y_2|+|z_!-z_2|), \\
& |\psi_n(t,x,0,0)\leq K_\psi(1+|x|^m), \qquad |\phi_n(x)|\leq K_\phi(1+|x|^m)
\end{align*}
for every $n\in\mathbb N$, every $t>0$ and every $(x,y,z)\in H\times \mathbb R\times U$;
\item $(\psi_n)$ and $(\phi_n)$ pointwise converge to $\psi$ and $\phi$, respectively, as $n$ tends to infinity.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.284972+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a77b46c9326d60a00643d173785671414566f7010bfc0fee4059e6859799265","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm eq:C_ell of arXiv:2604.20629, 'Rates of forgetting for the sequentially Markov coalescent'] Let $(Y_{\ell})_{\ell\ge0}$ denote the SMC process from Definition~(def:smc of the paper).
