{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.372781+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a8cd47f1e01d6f62c8f508479c5d814ca492f00145713a0678643e2ddccbdb3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 (Tightness criterion check for regularly-varying covariance) of arXiv:2606.04179, 'Functional Scaling Limits of Interpolated Correlated Random Walks in Hölder Topology'] If \(\abs{\rho(k)} =  \abs{k}^{-\alpha}\slowVar(k)\) for a slowly
    varying function \(\slowVar\), then for all \(p\in [2, \infty)\) and all
