{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.734319+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0aa76036be7ef9797252689720a51cc03c56f4e6d887c6e967f82cda49381739","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 1 (Proposition 2.5 and Lemma 2.8 in \cite{Geiss:Ylinen:21}) of arXiv:2506.10213, 'Coupling of forward-backward stochastic differential equations on the Wiener space, and ap'] Let \(X, X_1, \dots, X_n \in L^0(R\times\Omega^0)\), and let \(Y_i \in \cC(X_i)\) for \(i=1,\dots,n\).
\begin{enumerate}
    \item The joint distribution is preserved; i.e. one has the following
    $$(Y_1,\dots,Y_n) \stackrel{d}{=} (X_1,\dots,X_n).$$
    \item For all Borel functions \(g:\R^n\to\R\),
    $$g(Y_1,\dots,Y_n) \in \cC\bigl(g(X_1,\dots,X_n)\bigr).$$
    \item For \(Y\in L^0([0,T]\times\Omega^1)\), we have \(Y\in \cC_T(X)\)
