{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:27.006169+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ad338caaa001a70ccda5853173f9197f5fe8052b156f973e694013798b61264","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor of arXiv:2505.11700, 'Distribution of the cokernels of determinantal row-sparse matrices'] Suppose that the following hold: 
\begin{enumerate}
\item 
for every prime $p$, $p \nmid k_n$ for all sufficiently large $n$;
\item 
for every $\epsilon>0$, $k_n < n^{\epsilon}$ for all sufficiently large $n$;
\item 
for every $\delta >0$, $\delta \log\log n < k_n$ for all sufficiently large $n$. 
\end{enumerate}
Let $S$ be a finite set of primes and for each $p \in S$, let $G_p$ be a finite abelian $p$-group. Then
$$
\lim_{n \to \infty} \mathbb{P}\left(\bigoplus_{p\in S}\mathrm{cok}(A_n)_p \cong \bigoplus_{p\in S} G_p\right) = \prod_{p\in S} \frac{1}{|\mathrm{Aut}(G_p)|}\prod_{j=1}^{\infty}(1-p^{-j})=  \prod_{p \in S} \nu_{\mathrm{CL}, p}(G_p).
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:33.535118+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ad5afbfe58aa114bd444dd9b3b4908d765deb03b6df517ea391302629eb3487","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2603.28093, 'Random Stability of Random Variables'] Assume $\mathbb E[X] < \infty$. We can define $L$ as a complex-valued function on the half-plane $\mathbb H = \{z \in \mathbb C\mid \mathrm{Re}(z) > 0\}$. This function is analytic on $\mathbb H$, and we have: 
