{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.336963+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0b12007f5c943c0dbc2da886e0527f39e392fade94e78e93c2c0cdc34331668f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 (2BSDE with erratic horizon) of arXiv:2506.15037, '2BSDE with uncertain horizon and application to stochastic control in erratic environments'] The tuple $(Y,Z,U, (K^{\mathbb P})_{\p\in \mathcal P_0},(M^{\mathbb P})_{\mathbb P\in \mathcal P_0})\addd{}$ is solution to the 2BSDE with erratic horizon driven by $F^\mathbb P$ with terminal condition $\xi$ if 
