{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.757343+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0b1487c5e968a7756dd808c4e9ee62b4ec3717184b04277f4cdab0544286f708","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma rescomY of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Under the assumptions of Theorem (MixEV of the paper), let $G$ and $G_{{\mathfrak t}}$ denote the resolvents of ${H_{\Lambda}}$ and ${H_{\Lambda}}({\mathfrak t})$, respectively. 
Let $F: \mathbb{R}^n \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ be a function whose derivatives satisfy the following bound: for any fixed $l\in \mathbb{Z}_+$, there exists a constant $C_l>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \begin{aligned}
        \max_{\left\lvert \alpha \right\rvert=1,2,\ldots,l}\max_x\left|F^{(\alpha)}(x)\right|(|x|+1)^{-C_l} \leqslant C_l.
    \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
Denote $\widehat m=\left\langle G \right\rangle$ and $\widehat m_t=\left\langle G_t \right\rangle$ for any $t\in \qa{0,{\mathfrak t}}$. Then, there exists a constant $\sigma_0>0$ such that for any constant $0<\sigma<\sigma_0$, and for any sequences of real numbers $\ha{E_1\left({i}\right)}_{i=1}^n$ and $\ha{E_2\left({t}\right)}_{i=1}^n$ satisfying
\begin{equation}\nonumber
    \begin{aligned}
        \left|E_1\left({i}\right)-E^+\right| \leqslant N^{-2 / 3+\sigma}, \quad\left|E_2\left({i}\right)-E^+\right| \leqslant N^{-2 / 3+\sigma}, \quad {i=1,2,\ldots,n},
    \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
setting $\eta=N^{-2 / 3-\sigma}$, we have
\begin{equation}
    \begin{aligned}
        \Bigg|\mathbb{E} &F\left({DN} \int_{E_1\left({1}\right)}^{E_2\left({1}\right)} \mathrm{~d} y \operatorname{Im} \widehat m(y+\mathrm{i} \eta),\ldots,DN \int_{E_1\left({n}\right)}^{E_2\left({n}\right)} \mathrm{~d} y \operatorname{Im} \widehat m(y+\mathrm{i} \eta)\right)\\
        &-\mathbb{E} F\left(DN \int_{E_1\left({1}\right)}^{E_2\left({1}\right)} \mathrm{~d} y \operatorname{Im} \widehat m_{{\mathfrak t}}(y+\mathrm{i} \eta),\ldots,DN \int_{E_1\left({n}\right)}^{E_2\left({n}\right)} \mathrm{~d} y \operatorname{Im} \widehat m_{{\mathfrak t}}(y+\mathrm{i} \eta)\right)\Bigg| \lesssim N^{-\delta}
    \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
for some small constant $\delta>0$ depending only on $\delta_A,\ \varepsilon_A$, and the constants $C_l$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.792450+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0b152185ce541967b76e4216b2516ab4cb668398cee90615e5070a06d5363c73","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo 3 of arXiv:2609.00186, 'Macroscopic scalar curvature bounds on surfaces'] Let $(\Sigma,g)$ be a closed oriented Riemannian surface of genus $k= 1$. Then, for every $r>0$,
