uniformly for~$x$ in any compact subset of~$\R^2\setminus\{0\}$, where~$x_\delta$ denotes the vertex of~$\delta\Z^2$ closest to~$x$ (if there are more than one, choose one arbitrarily), and~$f(\delta)=\delta^{1/8+o(1)}$ as~$\delta$ tends to $0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

