{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.571558+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0bd3e8afd165ce7817bd24d2eb510663e4940f5696543b360f4ca3727069095c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 6 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d=6$. There exist $c,C,M>0$ such that, for every $n\geq 2$,
