{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.829756+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c64b541a480b4c8821a54824baaed35b47edc620bb1f7c3307fe54eef03f649","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 (Visible informative maps) of arXiv:2604.10792, 'Variable-Length Markov Chains on Finite Quivers: Boundary-Window Identifiability, Exact De'] For an admissible depth $m$ and visible states $y,y'\in\cS_m$, define the stationary one-step visible transition law by
\begin{equation}
q_{y,y'}^{(m)}(\theta):=P_{\theta,\mathrm{stat}}(Z_{t+1}^{(m)}=y'\mid Z_t^{(m)}=y),
\end{equation}
whenever the conditioning event has positive stationary probability.
