{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.291916+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cb6fc5c631a131a18d6ded30e5fabef339c3d16955cae84eded4dfba161be26","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:2G_randomD of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Let $X$ satisfy Assumption~(ass:chi of the paper)(i).  Fix a (large) $L>0$ and (small) $c_0,\epsilon,\nu,\xi>0$. Let $\theta>0$ be a (possibly, $N$-dependent) small parameter.  Consider $k_j\in[N]$ and denote $x_j:=k_j/N$, $j=1,2$. There exists a universal constant $d>0$ such that
