{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.251901+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cf9b1859e9f2ea84cd0598df24c4ede40cb664208243ce9836e45b93fe0299c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2604.15226, '\bfseries Nonlinear Schrödinger equations with spatial white noise potential on full space'] Let $\alpha,\mu \in \R$ and $p,q \in [1,\infty ]$. Then there exists a constant $C>0$ such that
