{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.971535+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d27a52397c84bf23ff5fa8bb43ae3f214bb59633719951f8cdf1511c1621477","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defin R\'enyi divergence of arXiv:2506.23062, 'Shifted Composition IV\@: \\ Toward Ballistic Acceleration for Log-Concave Sampling'] The R\'enyi divergence of order $q > 1$ between two probability measures $\mu$, $\nu$ is defined as
