where $Z_{1},\dots,Z_{d}$ are independent $\mathcal{N}(0,1)$-distributed random variables. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.337230+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d6722f719f7b0be80ce9fe46311147c07a1d0bb1b629cd7209b1ca249299dcf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2607.27150, 'Modelling Anomalous Diffusion: The Role of CTRWs and Non-Local Dynamics'] Assume that the Laplace exponent  $\psi$, in the case when $b_\psi=0$ in \eqref{eq:psi Laplace defn},  satisfies the weak lower scaling at infinity, i.e., there exist $a_\psi>0$ and $\delta_\psi\in (0,1)$ such that
