{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:47:04.926253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d88e9fee30bb09320b8849dac13dad86291ae47f6815983538afc0ad93828dd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition proposition2 of arXiv:2412.02486, 'On the curvatures of \\ random complex submanifolds'] Let $(M,g,J)$ be a K\"ahler manifold, $E\to M$ be a complex vector bundle of rank $r$, and $s\in \mathscr{C}^\infty(M,E)$ vanishing transversely along a $J$-complex submanifold $Z(s)$. Then,  
