{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.895765+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d8a3926e1ce58c7cd0046b3631f956d1e12887f1691be1c2f1e82ccf22b4058","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem gaussian of arXiv:2510.23430, 'On the Martin boundary for discrete TASEP'] Let $\sigma>0$, $x_1, \dots, x_k\in\mathbb R$. Then
