{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.362823+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0db7ceace06bd5fcc6306212faf3cfa4709810a5aafa40ce6b285fd827fa07ff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 71 (Growth of $k_i$) of arXiv:2511.09517, 'From Cannings model to Brownian motion conditioned on local time profile'] There exists $c=c(\varepsilon)>0$ such that for all $n,i\ge 1$,
