{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.775746+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0db9c6b92644f17988614d7198d6d3c24b5b47c90a8362183274845b77a9f903","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:correlation_stopping of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] There is some $\lambda_0 > 1$ and $C, c > 0$ such that for all $\lambda \geqslant \lambda_0$
