{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:38:25.226522+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0dc088d76c6245dfec34e13009fa9cbebf5827290a73132a5091aace6de7cb2e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Zlotnik of arXiv:2609.00627, 'Global well-posedness of radially symmetric strong solutions to two-dimensional compressib'] Let the function $y \in W^{1, 1}(0, T) $ satisfy $$ y^{\prime}(t)=g(y)+h^{\prime}(t) \enspace on \enspace [0, T], y(0)=y_0,  $$
	with $g \in C(R)$ and $h \in W^{1, 1}(0, T). $ If $g(\infty)=-\infty$ and 
	\begin{equation}
		h(t_2)-h(t_1) \le N_0 +N_1(t_2-t_1)
	\end{equation}
	for all $0 \le t_1 < t_2 \le T$ with some $N_0 \ge 0$ and $N_1 \ge 0$, then $$y(t)\le max(y_0, \zeta_0) +N_0 <\infty \enspace on \enspace [0, T],  $$
