{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:52.209003+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0dd7391f1a30246a67fa54b3abf1459dad9be2e444429b52c13ad9ca64700861","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 13 (Upper and lower escape probabilities) of arXiv:2512.09136, 'On the Green's functions and Martin boundary structure of a planar diffusion in a disconti'] Let $(a_0, b_0) \in \R^2$. Then: $$\P_{(a_0,b_0)}\bigl(B_t \underset{t\to+\infty}{\longrightarrow} +\infty\bigr) = h_{\alpha_{\mu^+}}(b_0),\quad \textnormal{and}\quad \P_{(a_0,b_0)}\bigl(B_t \underset{t\to+\infty}{\longrightarrow} -\infty\bigr) = h_{\alpha_{\mu^-}}(b_0).$$
In particular,
\begin{align}
\P_{(a_0,b_0)}\bigl(B_t \underset{t\to+\infty}{\longrightarrow} +\infty\bigr) &= 1 - \P_{(a_0,b_0)}\bigl(B_t \underset{t\to+\infty}{\longrightarrow} -\infty\bigr) \\
& = \begin{cases}
1 + \frac{\mu_2^-}{\mu_2^+ - \mu_2^-} e^{-2 b_0 \mu^+_2 / \Sigma_{22}^+} & \text{if } b_0 \geq 0, \\
\frac{\mu_2^+}{\mu_2^+ - \mu_2^-} e^{-2 b_0 \mu_2^- / \Sigma_{22}^-} & \text{if } b_0 < 0.
\end{cases}
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.302722+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ddb6443948bc375e1c73341c182f7bfdb4eb83df394c6f162149591cc8adf8b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 30 of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Define functions $  {\mathpzc F},\mathpzc G_{ij}$ on $\ak$ by 
    \begin{align*}
          {\mathpzc F} (   \beta)&:= \int_I x e^{   \beta \bullet    x - \log M(   \beta)}\mu(\mathrm d   x),\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\mathpzc G_{ij}(   \beta):= \int_I x_ix_j e^{   \beta \bullet    x - \log M(   \beta)}\mu(\mathrm d   x).
    \end{align*}
    There exists $C>0$ such that the following bounds hold uniformly over $   \beta \in \ak$ and $\x\in I^k$ and $1\le i<j\le k$ and $A\in \mathbb N$:
    \begin{align*}
       \bigg| \int_{I^k} (   a_i-   x_i)\qdif(\x,\dr \bfa) -   {\mathpzc F}(   \beta)\bigg| &\leq Ce^{C\cdot A} \bigg(|   \beta|^{2p-1}e^{-\frac1{\Con} \min_{i<j}|   x_i-   x_j|} +|   \beta|^{A}\bigg)
       \\\bigg| \int_{I^k} (   a_i-   x_i)(   a_i-   x_i)^T\qdif(\x,\dr \bfa)-\mathpzc G(\beta)\bigg| &\leq Ce^{C\cdot A} \bigg(|   \beta|^{2p-2}e^{-\frac1{\Con} \min_{i<j}|   x_i-   x_j|}+|   \beta|^{A-1}\bigg)\\\bigg| \int_{I^k} (   a_i-   x_i)(   a_j-   x_j)^T\qdif(\x,\dr \bfa)-   {\mathpzc F(\beta)}  {\mathpzc F(\beta)}^T\bigg| &\leq Ce^{C\cdot A} \bigg(|   \beta|^{2p-2}e^{-\frac1{\Con} \min_{i<j}|   x_i-   x_j|}+|   \beta|^{A-1}\bigg).
    \end{align*}
    In the left side of the second and third bounds, one could interpret the expression using any norm on $d\times d$ matrices.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.139272+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ddfebd741ae0d69746d3c9ce282c7c0577be0525427c84eb1fe5f5d61e53d2b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition reducible_interval of arXiv:2507.01236, 'Disintegration theorem for multifunctions, \\ with applications to empirical Wasserstein d'] Let $(\Omega, \mathcal{A}, \mu)$ be a probability space with a given cover by measurable sets $B_1, \ldots, B_n$, and let $I \in 2^{[n]}$.  We will say that~$I$ is \emph{reducible} if there exists a nonempty proper subset~$J$ of~$I$ such that
\begin{equation}

\mu\!\left( \left( \bigcup_{i \in J} B_i \right) \cap \left( \bigcup_{i \in I \setminus J} B_i \right) \right) = 0.
\end{equation}
We will say that~$I$ is \emph{irreducible} if it is not reducible.","status":"unverified"}

