{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.679386+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0de84ee5ac8090fd2fce5ece3ce873826e56cdc62f34ea629b8dc754347ebf8f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2609.03750, '\bf Pullback Measure Attractors, Zero-Noise Limits, and Moderate Deviations for 2D Stochas'] Suppose Hypotheses \ref{PEeqAssum-2.3} and \ref{PEeqAssum-2.5} hold. Let $v_0\in \mathcal{H}$ and $g, \partial_{z}g\in L^4([0,T];H)$. Then there exists $\epsilon_{0}>0$ such that the following estimates hold:
\begin{align}
	\sup_{\epsilon\in (0,\epsilon_{0})}\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\sup_{t\in [0,T]}|u^{\epsilon}(t)|^2\right]+\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}\left[\|u^{\epsilon}(t)\|^2\right]dt\right)\leq C_{\epsilon_{0},T},
\end{align}
and
\begin{align}
	\sup_{\epsilon\in (0,\epsilon_{0})}\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\sup_{t\in [0,T]}|\partial_{z}u^{\epsilon}(t)|^2\right]+\int_{0}^{T}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\partial_{z}u^{\epsilon}(t)\|^2\right]dt\right)\leq C_{\epsilon_{0},T},
\end{align}
where $C_{\epsilon_{0},T} > 0$ is a constant that depends on $\epsilon_{0}$ and $T$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.964543+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0dea0d54b8e1955a06561c407164f3a234017fdd5a0b8d559a39c8852b7fcf70","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 2 (Collection of nested sequences $\mathcal{D}$ generated by a stochastic chain) of arXiv:2607.28614, 'Tampered Memory Elephant Random Walk on one-dimensional integer lattice'] Consider a stochastic chain $\{L_n\}_{n \ge 1}$ taking values in $\{0, 1\}$, such that $L_1 \equiv 1$.
Setting $D_1^c \equiv 1$, we define $D_n^c$ recursively as 
\begin{equation}

D^c_{n+1}= \begin{cases}
D^c_n \cup \{n+1\}, & \text{ if } L_{n+1}=1,\\
D^c_n, & \text{ otherwise.}
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
In this case, we refer to $\mathcal{D}$ as the collection of nested sequences generated by the chain $\{L_n\}_{n \ge 1}$.","status":"unverified"}

