{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.742529+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e51300daf8c1cba866f0d16f739b514fc04dad9bec2983eede31e71883e83cc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 48 of arXiv:2506.10494, 'Geometric Jensen-Shannon Divergence Between Gaussian Measures On Hilbert Space'] Let $A,B,\{A_k\}_{k \in \Nbb}, \{B_k\}_{k \in \Nbb} \in \Sym(\Hcal) \cap \HS(\Hcal)$ be such that $I + A > 0$, $I+B > 0$, $I+A_k > $, $I+B_k > 0$ $\forall k \in \Nbb$. Assume that
