for any weak solution $   u_{\kappa,l} $ to (equation Eq_viscous_reg of the paper) in the sense of Definition (def_weak_sol of the paper) with initial value $u_0$ {satisfying (equation assumption_m_plus_one of the paper)}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:11:57.342604+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0eb21c0466de817822333f7f4e2af7ade82a7f4274a04c08229a3da1b477e488","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 32 of arXiv:2607.23791, 'Precise cover times for branching random walks on Hamming graphs: (iterated) logarithmic c'] Fix $c,w,\lambda,\delta>0$ and choose $C_{\rm shell}$ so that
$\lambda\delta C_{\rm shell}>2$.  Then
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{\ell>C_{\rm shell}\log\log d}^{d}
 \binom d\ell\exp\!\left(-cw e^{\lambda\delta\ell}\right)=o(1).
