{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.847064+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ebbdd05f445d7e2f93af32e9a094dda14115d5458576c01e9702e76530dc0e8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: transposition of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] Consider $I_k:=\{1,\ldots,k\}$, $I^i_{k}:=\{1,\ldots,i-1,i+1,\ldots,k\}$ and $\tau_1,\ldots,\tau_k\in{\mathcal T}$. Setting $w=\tau_1\cdots\tau_k$, the following identity holds true:
