{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.902460+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0edfe6006e617f6ff936cef2178e12746ff2dee0caf58ec2ec9be8f4029bd9d9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2510.26960, 'Free energy fluctuations in SK and related spin glass models: \\ A literature survey'] Consider an MSK model with species density matrix $\Lambda=\Lambda_N+O(N^{-1})$ and variance profile matrix $\Delta^2$.Let $\beta_c$ be as given in (equation eq:bcrit_msk of the paper). If $\Delta^2$ is positive semi-definite, then the following statements hold for the free energy $F_N(\beta)$.
