{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.423629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f17c43c217b0776bb2262516a83c6c46c3a6ea388be99d7396a251cd585b58f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p: gaussian mixing of arXiv:2605.22803, 'Persistence of asymptotic variance under transport:\\ from hyperfluctuation to stealthy hy'] Let $p\in[-d, 2]$. Assume that $Z$ is a Gaussian random field and assume that $Z$ and $\Phi$ are independent. Further, assume that
