{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.766413+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f6da556942fec9ac5406322b378479b547408db73a3a974fe5a2f8abc81d274","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 of arXiv:2607.09575, 'Probabilistic estimates for a system of\\noisy integrate-and-fire neurons'] Suppose $\nu^N$ converges weakly towards $\nu^*$ on $(D_{\mathscr{S}^\prime},M_1)$. Then, for every $a > 0$, we have uniformly in $N \ge 1$ and $t \in [0,T]$ that 
