{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:08.935330+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f778a4c3b19475b5cb05886e7a56d315a66b4df5f8c2ec9ee151013653bf8e2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def_betacorner of arXiv:2411.10829, 'Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble and its Laplace transform'] Fix $\beta>0$.\footnote{Compared to [GS1] or [BGC], we set $\beta=2\theta$.} The \emph{$\beta$-corners process with top row $\lambda_1>\dots>\lambda_N$}
is a random array
$\{y^n_i\}_{1\leq i\leq n\leq N}\in \mathcal G_N$ with top row $(\lambda_1,\dots,\lambda_N)$, in which
the $N(N-1)/2$ coordinates $y_i^n$, $1\le i \le n<N$, have the probability density
\begin{equation}

\frac{1}{Z_{N; \beta}} \cdot
\prod_{n=1}^{N-1} \left[\prod_{1\le i<j\le n} |y_j^n-y_i^n|^{2-\beta}\right] \cdot \left[\prod_{a=1}^n \prod_{b=1}^{n+1}
|y^n_a-y^{n+1}_b|^{\beta/2-1}\right],
\end{equation}
where $Z_{N; \beta}$ is the normalization constant:
\begin{equation}

Z_{N; \beta} =\left[\prod_{n=1}^N \frac{ \Gamma(\beta/2)^n}{\Gamma(k\beta/2)}\right] \cdot \prod_{1\le i < j \le N}
 |\lambda_j-\lambda_i|^{\beta-1}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.329311+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f784ab78f5d44f8471b96112d185995b8c44880bc9d30083bab99c638e1c6c6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 11 of arXiv:2607.06428, 'Impact of spinning on the early-warning signs in non-Markovian stochastic systems'] Let $H\in(0,1)$, $\sigma>0$, $\tau\ge0$ and $(x_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a solution to \eqref{eq:fast system simplified} that satisfies \nameref{S1}. Then, we get that
