{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.846922+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f84743c04779fe11e0135b76473351b45483902b74dc72c532e7f26e78c2ab8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 31 of arXiv:2511.10535, 'Eigenvalues of Brownian Motions on $\mathrm{GL}(N,\mathbb{C})$'] Given a $(\rho,\zeta)$-Brownian motion $B^N$, driven by $W^N$, there exists a constant $C_{\rho, T}$ such that for all $k\geq 0$ and $t\leq T$,
