{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:43:55.660173+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f960206db99337ea84b230034d2fb7ee8fafa54cc0da4ca7426a6087ec2209b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma stochastic_convergence of arXiv:2604.07497, 'The Three-Dimensional Stochastic EMHD System: Local Well-Posedness and Maximal Pathwise So'] Let $X$ be a separable Hilbert space and $\left( \Omega, {\mathcal F}, {\mathbb P} \right)$ be a probability space. Consider a sequence of stochastic bases ${\mathcal S}^n = \left( \Omega, {\mathcal F}, {\mathbb F}^n, {\mathbb P} \right)$ and ${\mathbb W}^n$ a sequence of ${\mathbb F}$-adapted cylindrical Wiener process with reproducing kernel Hilbert space $\mathscr{U}$. Suppose that the sequence $\{G^n\}_{n \in {\mathbb N}}$ of $X$-valued ${\mathbb F}^n$ predictable processes satisfy that $G^n \in L^2([0,T];L_2(\mathscr{U},X))$ almost surely. In addition, suppose also that we have a stochastic basis ${\mathcal S} = \left( \Omega, {\mathcal F}, {\mathbb F}, {\mathbb P} \right)$ and an ${\mathbb F}$ predictable process $G \in L^2 ([0,T];L_2(\mathscr{U},X))$. Then if 
\begin{equation*}
W^n \to W \ \ \text{in probability in } C([0,T];\mathscr{U}) \ \ \text{and} \quad
G^n \to G \ \ \text{in probability in } C([0,T];L_2(\mathscr{U},X)),
\end{equation*}
it holds that 
$\displaystyle \int_0^t G^n dW^n \to \int_0^t G dW  \ \ \text{in probability in } C([0,T];X).$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.976147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f9625d54f0a20095c38082506c497a070416ac3ee88755a92d998fa5c2498df","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 11 of arXiv:2606.11271, '\LARGE The $K$-th nearest neighbor random walk on a Poisson point process gets trapped'] For any given $\varepsilon >0$, $R\in \N^*$ and $u \in \Z^d$, the block $\Lambda_R(u)$ is said $\varepsilon$-good if both following statements are satisfied.
