{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.354989+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0fa78352c17eb91bd1d6912d76c0e16561c339cf9d998ec4a8ee12dc9ef32c0a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:global_energy_estimate of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] There exists a constant $C>0$ such that, for any $N\geq 1$, any interval $I=(0,T)\subseteq {\mathbb R}_+$ with $T<\infty$,
