{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.757323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_101045d33cd56284ea2fc1841823e15de169a0228af6916d18ee829d88ff9401","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm thm! of arXiv:2604.24061, 'A characterization of ruin-inducing probability measures in a renewal risk model'] The following assertions hold:
\begin{enumerate}
\item
for every  $Q{\,\in\,}\hyperlink{ms}{\mathcal M^{\mathcal H}_S}$ there exists an essentially unique pair $(\gamma,\delta){\,\in\,}\hyperlink{fp}{\mathcal F_P}{\,\times\,}\hyperlink{gp}{\mathcal G_P}$ so that the conditions 
\begin{gather}
