{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.191854+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1029523ba5487a5b4fcc72650f4fa585aa7a2e7c9722c47722815add88cdc57b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2606.31455, 'Discrete time-multidimensional renewal theory and applications'] For $n\ge 1$ and $k=(k_1,\ldots,k_d)\in\mathbb{N}^d$,

