{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.862490+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_10abb9247fcdace59319a8ee12b56c27e857a043d6aa280ffe41e47ec42b8bc7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 16 (Winning probability for \(n_m\to\infty\)) of arXiv:2605.21424, 'A dice game, a multinomial walk, and the inverted Dirichlet distribution'] With \(X_2,\ldots,X_m\) and \(\pi_1\) as in Theorem \ref{thm:rep-pi1}(i),  
