	In case $(ii)$, in the case where $a_i$ or $b_i$ is a function, the inequality $a_i<b_i$ is meant for $u$ large enough.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:38:13.632462+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_10d2f3e53256dd3dc3db13fadd8d0e0303ac4dca51f2f6004d633f022d65cd07","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 (Spherical tangent-indicatrix characterization) of arXiv:2609.00673, '2609.00673'] Let \(T_0,\ldots,T_{n-1}\in S^2\) be the unit edge tangents of a polygon.
Then the polygon is a discrete general helix if and only if its tangent
indicatrix is contained in the intersection
\[
S^2\cap\{X\in\mathbb R^3:X\cdot U=c\}
\]
for some unit vector \(U\) and some \(c\in[-1,1]\).  If \(0<|c|<1\),
this intersection is a small circle on \(S^2\); if \(c=0\), it is a
great circle; and if $|c|=1$, it consists of the single point $\{cU\}$.  Under the standing assumptions $n\ge3$ and $0<\theta_i<\pi$, the last case cannot occur.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.889846+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_10d3742621bf7a34a0d1ff9e305f52aef4f419ccb5d6bf096f053f776cd625e5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Hanson:Wright of arXiv:2607.04047, 'Top Singular Value in Sum-Products of Random Matrices'] There exists some universal constant $c > 0$ such that for every $\epsilon > 0$ and $\theta \in \mathbb{R}^n$, 
\begin{align*}
    &\;
    {\mathbb P}\Big( 
        \,
        \Big|  
            \| X \theta \|^2
            -
            \Big(
                \mfrac{1}{m} \msum_{i \leq m} 
                \| X_{i,N-1:1} \theta \|^2
            \Big)
        \Big| 
        > \epsilon \, 
        \Big(
                \mfrac{1}{m} \msum_{i \leq m} 
                \| X_{i,N-1:1} \theta \|^2
            \Big)
    \Big)
    \;\leq\;
    2
    e^{
        - c n  \min\{ \epsilon^2, \epsilon\}
    }
    \;.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.759118+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_10deb6acdb096462ae8c84746bb9fd8caf3798d010e08a1f848fd716153b226c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2608.17493, 'Integrals of some compound processes'] $M\sim CP(\lambda, F)$ if and only if $M$ is a stochastic process having independent increments, $M(0)=0$ a.s. and, for $t\ge0, x\in\mathbb{R}$,
	\begin{align}
