{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.485213+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_10e1f7c23c976e4bdc50597257edbbc567addc01bc9224080fe68601b96919fa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2608.18075, '2608.18075'] Let $F_S(t)=\langle\beta_t,S\rho_t\rangle$ on $I\Subset(0,T)$.
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
\item If $S$ is a finite Fourier matrix and $F_S\equiv0$, then
\begin{align}
 F_{[S,\mathcal{C}]}\equiv0
 \qquad\text{for every finite Lie word }\mathcal{C}.
\end{align}
\item Suppose $R_1,R_2$ are finite Fourier matrices,
$F_{R_1}\equiv0$, and $\mathcal{C}_n$ are Lie words with
\begin{align*}
 \mathcal{C}_n\to R_2\quad\text{in }\mathcal B(H^1,H).
\end{align*}
If $F_{[R_1,\mathcal{C}_n]}\equiv0$ for every $n$, then
\begin{align*}
 F_{[R_1,R_2]}\equiv0.
\end{align*}
\end{enumerate}
Thus no operator algebra property of the
$\mathcal B(H^1,H)$ closure is assumed.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.688962+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_10e2bd3426c41fb99040eae1b631a2c25af560bdd3f212f76fc08aea2f7de313","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 29 of arXiv:2605.17296, 'Zero correlations and averaged fields of orthonormal Gaussian Functions'] For every compact $K\subset \C$, as $N \to \infty$, 
