{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.881132+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_10f2997f50e47557c4998636d0446121b234fd4110f46ee570ea24cd12391b8e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:unifbound of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] Assume that $f_\ell$, with $\ell \in \mathbb{N}$ is a sequence of Gaussian fields satisfying (eq:assjet of the paper), with covariances $C_\ell$ such that
