Then we have $\mathbb{P}[\mathcal{G} | X^1 ] \geqslant \mleft( \frac{1 - \Delta/2T}{\alpha} \mright)^2$ almost surely.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.579285+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1102017e6319b37820cd36b7435a6988d004a4375a9933ace26ca74b416a16f9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 35 of arXiv:2608.27372, 'Universality and sharp thresholds for ellipsoid fitting'] For every $i\in[n]$ and
	$u=(u^\theta,u^b)\in\mathsf V\oplus\R$,
	\begin{equation}

		\langle u,H^{(i)}u\rangle
		\ge
		2\beta\left(
		\lambda_\Sigma\|u^\theta\|_2^2+(u^b)^2
		\right)
		+\gamma\|u^\theta\|_{\mathcal B,\theta^{(i)}}^2.
	\end{equation}
	In particular, writing
	\[
		(H^{(i)})^{-1}
		=
		\begin{pmatrix}
			Q^{(i)} & v^{(i)}\\
			(v^{(i)})^* & c^{(i)}
		\end{pmatrix}
	\]
	with respect to $\mathsf V\oplus\R$, where
	$Q^{(i)}:\mathsf V\to\mathsf V$, $v^{(i)}\in\mathsf V$, and
	$c^{(i)}\in\R$, we have
	\begin{equation}

		\|Q^{(i)}\|_{\op}
		\le C\beta^{-1}\lambda_\Sigma^{-1},
		\qquad
		\|v^{(i)}\|_2
		\le C\beta^{-1}\lambda_\Sigma^{-1/2},
		\qquad
		|c^{(i)}|
		\le C\beta^{-1},
	\end{equation}
	for a universal constant $C<\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.800968+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_110485ef4429395485955d396bba4139d634c05a0bb099bbab070fe6ca8ccd4a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 50 of arXiv:2607.10486, 'Weak martingale solutions to stochastic Navier-Stokes-Cahn-Hilliard system with transport '] Let us define the following space 
