{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:59:53.333140+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_111737e1212f350d8d6e82d04f079ef290c27e009397fd6eeb15d6030f7c620f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq-def-(M,1-delta,Z)-admissible of arXiv:2607.22324, 'The conclave process'] {}
    For $M \in \mathbb Z_+$, $0 \leq \delta \leq 1$ and $Z \in \mathbb R_+$, we say $(\mathbf X_1,\ldots,\mathbf X_n) \in \Omega_n$ is an \emph{$(M,\delta,Z)$-admissible} tuple, if 
