{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.474346+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1124dbe33ee2baf3da2254d776a48a437e9e6ef60b9c0b2ff370649c5c8741c1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma16 of arXiv:2511.19391, 'Central limit theorem for supercritical Crump-Mode-Jagers processes counted with non-indiv'] Suppose that assumptions (A1 of the paper)-(A4 of the paper) hold and let $\varphi$ be a characteristic satisfying (C2 of the paper)-(C3 of the paper). Then, for every $h \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$, the function 
