{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:02.092728+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_113fde6a12427b727687c44fda3ffcedbddaa1eefa9519eff12fa5e5e8e05ff5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 4 (\cite{A59}, Theorem 4.4.23  and \cite{Zhu}, Proposition 2.2) of arXiv:2604.25964, 'Strong convergence rate of Euler-Maruyama approximations in temporal-spatial H\"older-norm'] Let $\mathcal{P}$ be the progressive $\sigma$-algebra on $\mathbb{R}_+\times\Omega$ and $\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}_0)$ be the Borel $\sigma$-algebra of \;$\mathbb{R}_0$. Assume that $g$ is a $\mathcal{P}\otimes \mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}_0)$-measurable function such that $\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb{R}_0}\vert g(s,z) \vert^2\nu(dz)ds<\infty$ $\pr$-a.s. for all $T\geq 0$. Then, for any $p\geq 2$, there exists a constant $C_p >0$ such that
	\begin{align*}
		&\mathbb{E}\left[\sup_{0\leq t \leq T}\left\vert \int_0^t\int_{\mathbb{R}_0} g(s,z) \widetilde{N}(d s, d z)\right\vert^p\right]\\
		&\leq C_p \left(\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb{R}_0} \vert g(s,z) \vert^2 \nu(dz)ds\right)^{\frac{p}{2}}\right]+\mathbb{E}\left[\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb{R}_0} \vert g(s,z) \vert^p \nu(dz)ds\right]\right).
	\end{align*}
	Moreover, for any $1\leq p<2$, there exists a constant $C_p >0$ such that
	\begin{align*}
		\mathbb{E}\left[\sup_{0\leq t \leq T}\left\vert \int_0^t\int_{\mathbb{R}_0} g(s,z) \widetilde{N}(d s, d z)\right\vert^p\right]\leq C_p \, \mathbb{E}\left[\left(\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb{R}_0} \vert g(s,z) \vert^2 \nu(dz)ds\right)^{\frac{p}{2}}\right].
	\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.943851+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11419e651a2c4a39c920d62f59215c87399f3150d4de5d6edfbc859a08da6c8e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 5 of arXiv:2608.01860, 'A Variational Characterization of a Gibbs Measure related to the Aviles-Giga Functional'] Let $g:C([0,\infty),H)\to\R$ be such that \[\int_X(|g(W(x))|+1)\exp(-g(W(x))\ \mu(dx)<\infty.\] Then 
