{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.219517+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_115107a5988cb9952a39fcbe65a84532d7a6a309e01d1c22d817f1c006b69c97","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:1.9 of arXiv:2412.06086, 'Zeros of conditional Gaussian analytic functions, random sub-unitary matrices and q-series'] For every complex $a$ it holds in the limit $q\to 1^{-}$ that
 \\[-1ex]
