{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.776897+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_119cc34b7a0a960ecc786748f16513b3f6373aea0e61197cca3dfceec68e3f23","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro:bounds-of-limit-set of arXiv:2411.01364, 'Global Dynamics of Granular Media Equations via Stochastic Order'] Suppose Assumption (asp:potential of the paper) holds. Assume that a bounded subset $B$ in $\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$ is positively invariant under $P^*$ and there exists a connecting orbit $\{\tilde{\nu}_t\}_{t\in \mathbb R}$ from an invariant measure $\nu$ to another invariant measure $\pi$. If 
