{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.901824+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_119ccd8b2df776c6ce1888c6558939704e7a63721152e202f2b379c681fc2043","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:F(beta)SSK+CW of arXiv:2510.26960, 'Free energy fluctuations in SK and related spin glass models: \\ A literature survey'] In the three phases, $F_N$ exhibits the following convergence in distribution as $N\to\infty$. 
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item Spin glass: If $\beta>1$ and $J<1$, then
 \begin{equation} 
\frac{2N^{2/3}}{\beta-1}(F_N(\beta)-F(\beta))\to TW_1.
 \end{equation} 
\item Paramagnetic: If $\beta<1$ and $\beta<1/J$, then
 \begin{equation} 
N(F_N(\beta)-F(\beta))\to\mathcal{N}(f_1,\alpha_1)
 \end{equation} 
where $\alpha_1=-\frac12\log(1-\beta^2)$ and $f_1=-\frac12(\alpha_1+\log(1-\beta J))$.
\item Ferromagnetic: If $J>1$ and $\beta>1/J$, then
 \begin{equation} 
N^{1/2}(F_N(\beta)-F(\beta))\to\mathcal{N}(0,\alpha_2)
 \end{equation} 
where $\alpha_2=\frac12(1-J^{-2})(4\beta-J^{-1})^2.$
\end{enumerate}
Here the limiting free energy $F(\beta)$ is given by the formula
 \begin{equation}  
F(\beta)=\begin{cases} \beta-\frac12\log\beta-\frac34&\text{for spin glass,}\\
\frac14\beta^2&\text{for paramagnetic,}\\
\frac\beta2(J+\frac1J)-\frac12\log(\beta J)-\frac{1}{4J^2}-\frac12&\text{for ferromagnetic.}
\end{cases}
 \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.649385+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11a0609716fe631c21a8ccaa70ed1c5a6dd7a002e127e3323b3ed21c8ba72ac3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_r_eff_Gil_Gab of arXiv:2607.04002, 'Collisions of random walks in unimodular random graphs: applications to the random geometr'] For~$G \in \{\mathcal G_\mathrm{SGil},\mathcal G_\mathrm{Gab} \}$ we have,
