{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.356887+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11b4906d0573742ee1976f6c077e71a3b98c2b2353636497504e772abf781d47","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L42Mohr of arXiv:2412.01635, 'On the Weak Convergence of the Function-Indexed Sequential Empirical Process and its Smoot'] Let $(\xi_{i,n})$ be a strongly mixing triangular array of real random variables with mixing coefficients $(\alpha^\xi(t))_{t \in \mathbb N}$. For $n \in \mathbb N$, $m > 1$, and integers $(i_1,...,i_m)$ with $1 \leq i_1 < ... < i_m \leq n$ let $F_{n,i_1,...,i_m}$ denote the distribution function of $(\xi_{n,i_1},...,\xi_{n,i_m})$ and let $g: \mathbb R^m \to \mathbb R$ be a Borel function such that $$ \int |g(x_1,...,x_m)|^{1+\delta} dF_{n,i_1,...,i_m}(x_1,...,x_m) \leq M_n $$ and $$ \int |g(x_1,...,x_m)|^{1+\delta} dF_{n,i_1,...,i_j}(x_1,...,x_j) dF_{n,i_{j+1},...,i_m}(x_{j+1},...,x_m)\leq M_n $$ holds for some $\delta > 0.$ Then \begin{align*}
		&\bigg| \int g(x_1,...,x_m) dF_{n,i_1,...,i_m}(x_1,...,x_m)\\ 
		&- \int g(x_1,...,x_m) dF_{n,i_1,...,i_j}(x_1,...,x_j) d F_{n,i_{j+1},...,i_m}(x_{j+1},...,x_m) \bigg| \\
		&\leq 4 M_n^{\frac{1}{1+\delta}} \alpha^\xi(i_{j+1} - i_j)^{\frac{\delta}{1+\delta}}.
	\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

