{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.950325+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11c913e5f203349b87c7dbcbd1f1f3e3e0bbf9f98582bef97ec76365079ad6c1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm critical_gauge_scaling_limit of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Fix a $d$-dimensional lattice $\Lambda$ and $R\subset \mathbb{R}^d$ as before. Suppose that $H$ is $C^1$ and solves the gauge PDE: $\text{div}(\nabla F(\nabla H))=0$, and that $g_n$ is the critical gauge function on black vertices of $R_n$ with limiting multiplicity $1$ everywhere on $R_n$. Further suppose that
    \begin{align*}
        \sup_{u\in B\cap\partial R_n} |(1/n) \log g_n(u) - H(u)| = O(1/n).
    \end{align*}
    We equate $(1/n) \log g_n$ defined on $B\cap R_n$ with its linear interpolation to a continuous function. Then
    \begin{align*}
        \lim_{n\to \infty} (1/n) \log g_n 
    \end{align*}
    exists in the topology induced by the supremum norm on continuous functions and is equal to $H$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.191091+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11c93c8e75391fa0b5de5d84ec1f0ee94514b913372179c1f3e49d17148aa51c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 8 of arXiv:2606.31287, '\bf Heat kernel lower bound estimates for symmetric pure jump processes via averaged jump '] (\cite[Definition 1.5]{CKW1})
  \rm Let $U$ and $V$ be open subsets sets of $\sX$ with $\overline{U} \subseteq V$. A measurable function $\vp: \sX \to [0, 1]$ is called a cut-off function for $U \subseteq V$ if $\vp \equiv 1$ on $U$ and $\vp \equiv 0$ on $V^c$. We say that the condition $\CSJ(\phi)$ holds if there exist constants $C_0\in (0,1]$ and $C_1, C_2>0$ such that for every $0 < r \le R$, almost all $x_0 \in \sX$ and any $f \in \sF$, there exists
a cut-off function $\vp \in \sF_b$ for $B(x_0,R) \subset B(x_0,R+r)$ so that the following holds:
\be  \begin{split}
 \int_{B(x_0,R+(1+C_0)r)} f^2 \, d\mu_{\<\vp\>}
\le \,\,&C_1 \int_{U\times U^*}(f(x)-f(y))^2\,J(dx,dy) \\
&+ \frac{C_2}{\phi(r)}  \int_{B(x_0,R+(1+C_0)r)} f(x)^2m(dx),
\end{split}
\ee
where $U=B(x_0,R+r)\setminus B(x_0,R)$ and $U^*=B(x_0,R+(1+C_0)r)\setminus B(x_0,R-C_0r)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:36:12.184200+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11c996506d1c0f6977b31463c75654d06d8750d7c22cb3897742f0a909e17665","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 (A substitution) of arXiv:2609.03881, 'Eulerian insertion operators and an Eulerian form of the Pieri rule'] For every \(f\in\mathbb Q[x,y]\),
