{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.657364+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11cb34a878eb105a1e4acc81d08cf9737a96ab9b362b844b307e370735397694","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn defn4.19 of arXiv:2411.09988, 'A Study in Markov Chains, Loop-Erased Random Walk and Loop Soups'] The \textit{unrooted loop measure} $m=m^p$ is the measure that assigns to each unrooted loop
