{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:30:50.703268+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11fd55834f77bf310b61b81a7856c6c67100f232a62bea119a7fd13f40649179","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm thm-main1 of arXiv:2608.30807, 'Isodiametric-type upper bounds for Steklov eigenvalues'] Let $\Omega\subset \mathbb{R}^n$ be a bounded Lipschitz domain. Then there exists a constant $C(n)>0$ such that for every $k\in \mathbb{N}$, we have
