{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.518788+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12072082a705b32baf7f42a41753b5f4c1a2da31fd93368ad1256a1907d7db76","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Samuels' conjecture) of arXiv:2608.18392, 'On Samuels' Conjecture'] For every integer $n\geq1$, ordered mean vector $0\leq\mu_1\leq\cdots\leq\mu_n$, and $\lambda>\sum_{i=1}^n\mu_i$,
