{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.972847+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1208b5aa002a4a78fbf110edbfe90121f6b18a39b4bc40bb4de909b9164c4429","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:propB of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] Fix $\mu \in[0,1]$, $\tau_i \in \mathfrak{T}$, and $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_i} \in {\mcb{C}}[\tau_i]\,$ for $i = 1,2$. The most important property of the grafting $\big(\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_2}\graft^\mu\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_1}\big)^\tau$, upon which we rely extensively, is that for every $N\in\N$, uniformly in $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_i}$ and $\mu\in(0,1]$ we have
