{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.696254+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12292314cfe0d366fe2a256f89d80e2ef3f47fae47197ab786e432568892e873","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:two-inside of arXiv:2609.00645, 'Global persistence of nearly radial concentrated vortices in a bounded domain'] There exist $\delta,\varepsilon_{\rm in},C_{\rm two}>0$, depending only on
$D,\rho$, and $\mathbf a_{*,i},\kappa_i,M_i,R_i$, $i=1,2$, such that the
following holds.

If $0<\varepsilon<\varepsilon_{\rm in}$ and, at some time $t$,
\begin{equation}
  S_\varepsilon(t)\subset\overline{V_\rho},
  \qquad d_\varepsilon(t)\leq\delta,
\end{equation}
