    sequences $(\epsilon_n)$ converging to $0$ and satisfying
    \begin{align}

      |\epsilon_n|= \mathcal{O}(r_n^{\delta_\epsilon-1})
    \end{align}
    the following holds:
\begin{align}

  \begin{split}
    &
      \frac
      {
    r_n/\xi(u_n)
      }
      {n}
      \\&
      \cdot \
      \sum_{t=1}^{n}
     \left[
      \left(
      \frac
      {
      \left(
      g(X_t)
       -
      g(u_n)
