{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.304477+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12776ed9c44c32de51b6c5ddbfb42aca9190c691fc8b73178882b6b1ef6eb26e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:abs_cont_kernel of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Let $\mu,\widetilde{\mu}$ be probability measures on a space $X$, and let $\nu[dy \mid x]$ be a probability kernel from $X$ to $Y$. Suppose that $\frac{d\widetilde{\mu}}{d\mu}$ has $\mu$-moments of order $p>1$. Then
