{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:35:04.214635+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12caa88836624864b0774f5581776eb37cd683af9b9bcdaa7ff649673846aff5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 19 of arXiv:2608.03956, 'From Triangular Array Progression\\ to Near-Log-Concave State Transitions'] Let $\mathbf{D}^{(n)}$ be an ordered finite subset of $\R$ with cardinality $|\mathbf{D}^{(n)}| = n+1$ for any $n \geq 2$, and $X^{(n)} : \Omega \rightarrow \mathbf{D}^{(n)}$ be a random variable with probability mass function
