{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.393479+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_13481fe0b371ee32ee8879baf4ab1969675fd69b0ced3030cebf2cd0b06c0f7f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:QV-estimate of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] Fix $1/2<\lambda \le 7/8$ and $\phi \in \ensuremath{\mathcal C}_b^\infty(\mathbb{R})$. Then, there exist $C=C(\phi)>0$ satisfying, for all  $T>0$ and $N$ large enough, 
