{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.482070+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_13491edcb9b5e4ff37dbf0dbb5bd96358b5554edb45cfdf240acb7aa205feb3c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition st of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] \noindent  We say that $X$ is smaller than $Y$ in the usual 
