  \}.
   \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.019125+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_13662af4a378f20aa4b97769329fa2d206ce38028fa852921173ff1c89a7eb65","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 8 ($L^1$-Contraction) of arXiv:2605.05986, '\bf Convergence rate of the occupation measure of { classes of ergodic processes toward th'] Let $(P_t)_{t\ge0}$ denote a  {{Markov}} transition   semi-group  {with unique invariant distribution  $\nu$}. If this semi-group satisfies  the following contraction inequality:
