{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.227437+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_140ad3a6d5c0780d54d0bb538bfa4e551d03e5541fd0b5f2df0dace736f4262a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma BBM-F-KPP-Connection of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] For a measurable function $\phi:\mathbb{R} \to [0,1]$, let
\begin{equation}
u_\phi(t,x) = 1 - \mathbb{E}[\prod_{k=1}^{n(t)}\{1-\phi(x- \chi_k(t))\}].
\end{equation}
Then $u = u_\phi$ solves the following F-KPP equation
\begin{equation}
\partial_t u = \frac{1}{2}\partial_x^2 u + u- u^2
\end{equation}
 with the initial condition $u(0,x) = \phi(x)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.578423+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_140dc68557a19594367e45edb919cd577938baaddbfab4bdf79b7434ee279431","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 48 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a subgraph of $\mathbb Z^d$ and let $A\subset V$ be a finite even subset of $G$. Let $\beta>0$. Let $\n$ be distributed according to $\mathbf P_{G,\beta}^{A}$. Let $(\omega_e)_{e\in E(\mathbb Z^d)}$ be an independent Bernoulli percolation with parameter $1-\exp(-\beta)$. For each $e\in \mathbb Z^d$, we define
\begin{equation}
	\eta_e:=\max(\mathds{1}_{\n_e>0},\omega_e).
\end{equation}
Then, the law of $\eta$ is $\phi_{G,\beta}^0[\:\cdot\:|\: \mathcal F_A]$. As a consequence, if $\mathcal A$ is an increasing event, one has
\begin{equation}
	\mathbf P^{A}_{G,\beta}[\mathcal A]\leq \phi_{G,\beta}^0[\mathcal A\: | \: \mathcal F_A].
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.761854+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_140e4c3f99595de0722f0e413491174cffaedf0c95aded7b08d077c862c2a663","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:eigenfunction-square-laplacian of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] The square $\phi^2$ belongs to $H_0^1(D)$ and satisfies
\begin{equation}
 L_0(\phi^2)
 =2\Lambda\phi^2M_x-2\Gamma_\mathcal E(\phi)\,\mathcal L^2
 \qquad\text{in }\mathcal D'(D).
\end{equation}
Equivalently, for every $\zeta\in C_c^\infty(D)$,
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal E(\phi^2,\zeta)
 =2\Lambda\int_D\zeta\phi^2\,dM_x
  -2\int_D\zeta\Gamma_\mathcal E(\phi)\,dz.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:13:21.306469+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_14109427b14f9f5a20320691f9adf19d938fd2e505c5512cf71af8b9c548d76d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 44 of arXiv:2609.01473, 'Keller sequences of exact $\infty$-categories'] Let $\cal{D}$ be an $\infty$-category equipped with an orthogonal factorisation system $(\cal{D}^l,\cal{D}^r)$, such that there is some object $0 \in \cal{D}$ which is initial for maps in $\cal{D}^r$.
    Let $p\colon\cal{E} \to \cal{D}$ be a functor satisfying the following:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item Maps in $\cal{D}^l$ admit $p$-cocartesian lifts given any lift of their domain and maps in $\cal{D}^r$ admit $p$-cartesian lifts for any lift of their target.
        \item The fibre inclusion $\cal{F} := p^{-1}(0) \to \cal{E}$ admits a retraction $r\colon \cal{E} \to \cal{F}$. 
    \end{enumerate}
    Then the functor 
    \[ (r,p)\colon \cal{E} \to  \cal{F} \times \cal{D} \]
    is a weak homotopy equivalence.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.207186+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1416a08ceb7d7044ab208bda4d4be40af37c9be40633d7b3aab178c5e66a1dca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Wt-Div-Simplex of arXiv:2608.29013, 'Weighted Homology and Cohomology of Weighted Polyhedra'] {Daw90}}] 
