{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.270312+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_146bae61b581485f7a292e7da0e3a5b3d051add60283a7170780681b726224a0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mycor t4.1 of arXiv:2411.08430, 'The Restricted Isometry Property of Block Diagonal Matrices Generated by $\varphi$-Sub-Gau'] Let $\xi=(\xi_{1},\cdots, \xi_{n})$ be a random vector with independent centered $\varphi$-sub-Gaussian variables and $\mathcal{A}$ is a family of $m\times n$ fixed matrices. We have for $t\ge 0$
