{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.433903+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_14ee175503959faa5ef42aaa118badd65790cb4565a73afde9ad0d869868d099","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:concentration-ineq of arXiv:2605.20697, 'Uniform-in-time propagation of chaos for \\ Second-Order Consensus-Based Optimization'] Let the objective function \(f\) satisfy
    (assumption:bounded,assumption:lip of the paper), and let \(q>2\). Consider the
    second-order CBO dynamics where the initial positions and velocities are sampled
    i.i.d.\ from some \(\overline\rho_0\in\mathcal P_{2q}(\mathbb R^{2d})\).
    Assume that the parameter conditions in
    (prop:ito-centered-lyapunov-differential of the paper) hold for \(p=2\) and \(p=2q\).
    Let
    \[
        0<\kappa<\min\left\{\lambda_{2},\frac{\lambda_{2q}}q\right\}.
    \]
    For brevity, write
    \[
        c_{1,2q}:=c_1(a_{2q},2q).
    \]
    Then there exists a finite constant \(C_{\mathrm{Bad}}>0\) such that, for any
    threshold \(A>0\) and \(J\in\mathbb N_+\), the pathwise empirical Lyapunov
    functional \(L_2(t)\) satisfies
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb P\left[
            \sup_{t\geqslant0}
            \e^{\kappa t} L_2(t)
            \geqslant
            \mathcal L_2(0)+A
        \right]
        \leqslant
        \frac{C_{\mathrm{Bad}}}{A^q}
        J^{-\frac q2}\,
        \mathcal L_{2q}(0).
    \end{equation}
    Consequently, by norm equivalence result (equation eq:psi2-norm-equivalence of the paper),
    \[
        c_1^{(2)}\mathfrak M_2(\mu_{X_t^J})\leqslant L_2(t),
    \]
    the empirical spatial moments satisfy
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb P\left[
            \sup_{t\geqslant0}
            \e^{\kappa t}
            \mathfrak M_2(\mu_{X_t^J})
            \geqslant
            \frac{\mathcal L_2(0)+A}{c_1^{(2)}}
        \right]
        \leqslant
        \frac{C_{\mathrm{Bad}}}{A^q}
        J^{-\frac q2}\,
        \mathcal L_{2q}(0).
    \end{equation}
    In the above, \(C_{\mathrm{Bad}}:=C_{\mathrm{Bad},q,\kappa}\) is given by
    \begin{align}
        C_{\mathrm{Bad},q,\kappa}
        &:=
        2^q\widetilde C_{\mathrm{MZ},q}
        +
        C_{\mathrm{Mart}},
        \\
        \widetilde C_{\mathrm{MZ},q}
        &:=
        \frac{
            2^{3q-2}C_\phi^q(C_{{\rm MZ},q}+C_{{\rm MZ},2q})
        }{
            c_{1,2q}
        },
        \\
        C_{\mathrm{Mart}}
        &:=
        \frac{
            2^{q+1}C_{\mathrm{BDG},q}C_{\sigma,q}
        }{
            \lambda_{2q}-q\kappa
        }
        \left(
            \frac{q-2}{\lambda_{2q}-q\kappa}
        \right)^{\frac q2-1}.
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

