{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.159585+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_153356dfed36923a80faa8dec613392b385bbe765d8ec39b8a23a3740117f079","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma diag:circ-vs-phi-sym-mon of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] For any compact Lie group $G$, we have a commutative diagram
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{tikzcd}
            \CAlg(\cat{$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top}^\boxtimes)\arrow[rr,"{{{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_\textup{$G$-gl}^\circ[{\textup{triv}}_G(-)]^\otimes}"]\arrow[dr,"\CAlg(\Phi^\otimes\circ\textup{loc})"', bend right=15pt] && \CMon(\Spc)\rlap.
            \\
            &\CMon(\Spc_{\textup{Glo}})\arrow[ur,"\ev_{\mathbb B{G}}"', bend right=15pt]
        \end{tikzcd}
    \end{equation}
    \begin{proof}
        By [schwede2018global]*{Theorem 2.1.15}, $\CAlg(\cat{$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top})$ admits a model structure with weak equivalences and fibrations defined after forgetting the commutative algebra structure; in particular, the localization $\mathfrak U_\textup{gl}$ of $\CAlg(\cat{$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top})$ has finite coproducts and products with products created by the forgetful functor to ${{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_\textup{gl}$. Moreover, as discussed right before Definition 2.5.15 of \emph{op.\ cit.}, $\mathfrak U_\textup{gl}$ is semiadditive.

        It is clear that the bottom composite through the above diagram descends to a finite product-preserving functor $\mathfrak U_\textup{gl}\to\CMon(\Spc)$. By [Gepner-Groth-Nikolaus]*{Corollary~2.5}, it will therefore suffice to prove that $((diag:circ-vs-phi-sym-mon of the paper))$ commutes after postcomposition with the forgetful functor $\CMon(\Spc)\to\Spc$. This however follows immediately from the previous lemma.
    \end{proof}","status":"unverified"}

