{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.516002+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15802feb989ee8581bdbec3b84f1b76d7c1c39e168e959997217124d3404df8f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:s_property_1 of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{def:renormalisation_scheme}
    Let $\xi > 0$ and let $\eta = \eta(\xi) = \lceil 2 \left( 1/\xi - 1 \right) \rceil$.

    Let $\overline{r}_0 \geq r_0 \geq 1$ be two large constants. For $\alpha \in (0,2)$, we define $s = s(\alpha,G,\xi)$ to be the least integer satisfying $c_{\mathrm{vor}} (i+s)^{2d} \ge 2$ and

    \begin{align}

        s^{\xi + \alpha}
        & \geq 
        (1 + s)^{\alpha},
        \\

        (1 + s)^{2 + \eta} 
        & > 
        (1 + \xi) / \xi,
        \\

        (1 + s)^{2 + \eta}
        & \geq 
        \overline{r}_0/(\xi r_0),
        \\

        \frac{
            C_G (1 + \xi)^d 
        }{
            c_G (1 - 2 \xi)^d
        }
        (1+s)^{-2d}
        & < 
        1/2
    \end{align}

    simultaneously. For $i \geq 1$ we iteratively define 

    \begin{equation}

        m_i 
        = 
        (i + s)^{2 + \eta}
        \quad 
        \text{and}
        \quad
        r_i 
        = 
        m_i r_{i-1}.
    \end{equation}

    Let $((\Tile{i}{j})_{j \geq 0})_{i \geq 0}$ be the renormalisation scheme associated to the renormalisation scales $(r_i)_{i \geq 0}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.060728+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1581241aba9bb5afc7dd573c123dec43c480d8926835bb2b7fcd82cc684448cd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2608.19744, 'Conditioned Brownian motion and local equivalence of path ensembles'] Let $K\subset\mathbb R^d$ be compact.  There exist
