{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.185667+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15a18e98d1fc1dcfad6458d1bbd51a84351e72dc3d7909e8b0b0063427de97bb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:HitMixReversible of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] Let $\delta, \varepsilon \in (0, 1)$ and let $(M_t)_{t \geqslant 0}$ be an irreducible reversible Markov chain with mixing time $t_{\textup{mix}}^{(x)}$ and $\delta$-hitting time $\textup{hit}_{1-\delta,x}$ when starting from a state $x\in \Omega$, and spectral gap $\gamma$. Then for all $\delta \leqslant \min\left\{1-\varepsilon, \varepsilon\right\}$,  
