{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.161572+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15f727340b8bfcecd2ac6c8df8c5a4dbe70c1d05f509a5d0ad1795dd6627f853","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Def_PartialConnectionAlongSpaceOfRamifiedLineBundles of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] Given a local infinitesimal uniformiser $\mathscr{F}^\mathbf{Ram}|_\mathscr{U} \to \mathrm{Vect}(X), ({\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}];v) \mapsto \bar v = \bar v({\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}],v)$ as in (Prop_InfinitesimalSliceUniformisers of the paper),
