{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.377774+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1600c2c4e30628b096db6eeb356d39096184043fe44f92177fcd10abbb677ef9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:HKUB of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] Fix $A>0$, $k\ge 1$, $\delta\in (0,\frac14)$, $0<t_0<T$,  and $\hslash>0$. Then, for some $C>0$ and all $\mathbf x, \mathbf y \in \mathbb{Z}^k$, $N\in \mathbb{N}$, $|\beta|\le AN^{-1/8}$, and $t\in [t_0,TN]$, 
