{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.094262+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1626b44e520d06b616f91456a980b721b1453e4781d887690ec1f66a205d7485","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 35 of arXiv:2608.28148, 'Flows and homotopies of Banach Lie algebroids'] Let $c\colon [t_0,t_1]\to A$ be a smooth admissible curve and set $\gamma:=\pi\circ c$. The expression \eqref{eq:transport_operator} is independent of the local trivialisation. For fixed $c$ we obtain an $\R$-linear map 
