{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.612720+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1637f1622e15e1330b33586c059538394d79b88ee6bae64c9c2dcdfd77c920b1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 21 of arXiv:2510.27451, 'Bi-martingale optimal transport and its applications'] For any  plan $\gamma \in \ov\Gamma(\mu,\nu)$ define $\ov\rho \in \Pi_{\succeq_c \mu}(\nu) = \Pi_{\succeq_c \nu}(\mu)$, $\gamma_1 \in \Gamma_{\mathrm{M}}(\mu,\ov\rho)$, and $\gamma_2 \in \Gamma_{\mathrm{M}}(\nu,\ov\rho)$ as above. Then,
