{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.501183+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_166d050e6ef29dc42cdc6969c74c03859217973bdf55bda068c3b3e4a33b6666","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2605.30030, 'Critical exponents for planar random-cluster model with cluster-weight~$q=4$'] Let~$\upsilon:[0,\infty)^2\rightarrow (0,\infty)$ be a function that is increasing in the first variable, decreasing in the second and that 
 satisfies the quasi-multiplicativity relation
\begin{equation*}
    \upsilon(r,\rho)\upsilon(\rho,R) \asymp \upsilon(r,R),\quad\text{for every }0< r\leq \rho\leq R.
\end{equation*}
If there is some constant~$\varsigma>0$ such that
\begin{align}
    \lim_{\eps\to0}\liminf_{N\to\infty} \frac{\log\upsilon(\eps N,N)}{\log \eps} = \lim_{\eps\to0}\limsup_{N\to\infty} \frac{\log\upsilon(\eps N,N)}{\log \eps} = \varsigma,
\end{align}   
then for any positive sequences~$(r_n)_{n\in\N}$ and~$(R_n)_{n\in\N}$ with~$\frac{R_n}{r_n} \to \infty$ as~$n \to \infty$, 
\begin{align}
    \lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{\log\upsilon(r_n,R_n)}{\log(R_n/r_n)} =-\varsigma.
\end{align}
In particular,
\begin{equation}
\lim_{N\to\infty}\frac{\log\upsilon(1,N)}{\log N}=-\varsigma.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.650072+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_166f9c7eea5dc6040ebc4713ed1879bc210d28b3f8efdf7ee3d1fdec431c6915","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2608.29940, 'Counterexamples to the site-percolation analogues\\ of the Easo--Severo--Tassion cutset th'] There exists an infinite, connected, locally finite graph $G$ with a distinguished vertex $\rho$ such that
