{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.975035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_167dd7ec8e500837f1e49992b3a32cd296aa6a36b3d18ed9a5eb139e2ac58cff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 10 of arXiv:2606.11142, 'Strong invariance principles for diffusions, Markov chains and their perturbations.'] (Simplified Theorem 1.1 from \cite{Bitter}). Under the Boundedness Assumption, for every $n$ and pairs $(t_i, x), (t_j, y)$, there exists a constant $C > 0$ such that the error between the transition densities is bounded by:
