{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:38:37.409656+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_16e2016dc387472801b3e1021979bdfd08554172cab05b71cdddbcae36c43423","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 25 of arXiv:2605.15781, 'Mean-Field Backward Stochastic Differential Equations with Nonlinear Resistance and Double'] There exists a constant $C$ independent of $n$, such that
