{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.590949+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_16f7f62b58be4cafa88c8a3bb41c1908322d402ee2c0a4ffd12e0c115155404f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem ContDensL of arXiv:2412.04973, 'On the Laplace equation with non-local dynamical boundary conditions'] Let $\Lambda=0$, $l > 0$, $k \in \mathbb{R}$ and $\alpha \in (0,1]$.  Let assume  $\lambda_1\geq 0.$ Let $w$ be the solution to (equation EsolVVw of the paper). Then, the solution (equation uAlfa of the paper) can be written as 
