{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.065269+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_16fa8abc024615df5b9b2288f3f5931577289df27d5cbda5ce75c6925299574f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2606.28067, 'Ergodic approximation for the invariant distribution: An abstract framework for law-depend'] Let $A,B,\alpha,\beta>0$. The function $h(r)=Ar^{\alpha}+Br^{-\beta}$, $r>0$
