{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.077606+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1789c811d3ce89c2ab73140dd6968a527feb8d2133d0d1e29fcbb204266b9d35","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo dqgreht of arXiv:2507.00737, 'Dispersion models on a circle: universal properties and asymptotic results'] Suppose that for each $s$, ${\sf UCost}^{(s)}$ is in $L^2$, and set
	\[\Psi(s)= \mathbb{E}\left({\sf UCost}^{(s)}\right),  ~~ V(s)= \textrm{Var}\left({\sf UCost}^{(s)}\right).\]
