{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.080581+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_17acd077b94365479ba413990f747c68e9ff361b0a6c7138bbb83b4c226136c3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition bound of arXiv:2412.08334, 'Maker-Breaker on Galton-Watson trees'] Consider the $(1,1)$-Maker-Breaker game on an instantly revealed GW-tree arising from a general offspring distribution $\{\mathbb{P}(\xi=k)=p_k,\,k\in\mathbb{N}_0\}$, in which Breaker starts. Then the following conditions hold:
