{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.726996+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1880d06744e3d8f3ee0c5c8656de16ce6261e7436d9e3d656b92fb71adab8e84","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:gasket_interior_bound of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Fix $a_1 > 0$, $N \in \mathbf{N}$, and let $G_{z,\delta}$ be the event in Lemma~(le:tightness_loop_chain of the paper). There is a constant $c$ depending on $N$ such that the following is true. Suppose that $\gamma\colon [0,1] \to \Upsilon_\Gamma$ is an admissible path and there are times $0 < s_1 < \cdots < s_L < 1$ and $z_l,\delta_l$ such that the following hold for each $l$.
 \begin{itemize}
  \item $\gamma[s_l,s_{l+1}] \subseteq B(z_l,\delta_l)$,
  \item $\gamma[0,s_l], \gamma[s_{l+1},1] \nsubseteq B(z_l,\delta_l^{1-a_1})$,
  \item $G_{z_l,\delta_l}$ occurs.
 \end{itemize}
 Then there exist $s' \in [0,s_1]$, $t' \in [s_L,1]$ such that
 \[ \median{\epsilon}^{-1}\metapproxacres{\epsilon}{V}{\gamma(s')}{\gamma(t')}{\Gamma} \le c\sum_l (\delta_l^\zeta + \epsilon^{a_0}) \]
 for each $V \in \metregions$ such that $\overline{V}$ contains every \emph{simple} admissible path $\widetilde{\gamma}$ between two points on $\gamma$ with $\operatorname{diam_E}(\widetilde{\gamma}) \le 2\max_l \delta_l^{1-a_1}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.963070+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_188104e6d28d0801a4f87295a7dccfb0d3e68b948bd8a73ce865fad9c85435aa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:uld-gronwalls of arXiv:2506.23062, 'Shifted Composition IV\@: \\ Toward Ballistic Acceleration for Log-Concave Sampling'] Let ${(X_t, P_t)}_{t \in [0,h]}$ denote the solution of~(eq:ULD of the paper) started at $(x,p)$. With $h \lesssim 1/\beta^{1/2}$ and $\gamma \lesssim \sqrt{\beta}$, we have the following bounds:
