{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.595306+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18e83f354bddd6d8a920b71a648f3d8e0e0c6a37e230cfaf2f5722c3d7b6acd6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2607.07022, 'Coordinate-wise Elephant Random Walk'] Let $t_0:=k\lceil \ln(2k)\rceil.$ Then, for every $x \in Q_k$ and every $A \subseteq Q_k,$
