{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.856336+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_19354b0ee7efa5ef3789f0db7a47409fb506484d18510d9eb7d15cfac9f9b728","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 of arXiv:2607.17030, 'Stationary measures for log-gamma polymer on a strip and in half-space'] If $|u|<\alpha$ { and $v>-\alpha$}, then
        \begin{multline}
        \frac{\GG_N(\alpha,u,v)}{\Gamma(\alpha+v)\Gamma(\alpha+u)^N\Gamma(\alpha-u)^{N-1}}
        \\=\mathbb E\,\left[(1+\zeta_1+\zeta_1\zeta_2+\ldots+\zeta_1\zeta_2\ldots \zeta_{N-1})^{-u-v}\right],
    \end{multline}
    where 
     $(\zeta_i)_{i\ge 1}$ is a sequence of
    i.i.d. $\mathrm{Beta}_{II}(\alpha+u,\alpha-u)$ random variables.

     If $|v|<\alpha$   and $u>-\alpha$, then
        \begin{multline}
        \frac{\GG_N(\alpha,u,v)}{\Gamma(\alpha+u)\Gamma(\alpha+v)^N\Gamma(\alpha-v)^{N-1}}
        \\ =\mathbb E\,\left[(1+  \zeta_1'+\  \zeta_1'\  \zeta_2'+\ldots+\  \zeta_1'\  \zeta_2'\ldots \  \zeta_{N-1}')^{-u-v}\right],
    \end{multline}
    where 
     $(\  \zeta_i')_{i\ge 1}$ is a sequence of
    i.i.d. $\mathrm{Beta}_{II}(\alpha+v,\alpha-v)$ random variables. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.407761+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_193971ed1eecf97e6aa1db05dcab49733fae616f3c1a5d2e0e8f785c2027fa43","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2604.06645, '2604.06645'] Fix $i\in \{1,...,m\}$ and $k\in \{1,...r\}$ and let $Z_{ik}$ be the stochastic convolution
\begin{equation}
Z_{ik} := \int_0^t\int_D G_i(t-s,x,y)g_{ik}(s,y)W_k(dyds),
\end{equation}
where $g_{ik}:\mathbb R\rightarrow \mathbb R$ is bounded and adapted and $G_i$ is the heat kernel corresponding to the operator $d_i\Delta$. Then, for every $t\in [0,T]$,
\[
\mathbb E\sup_{t\in [0,T]}||Z_{ik}(t)||^p_{W^{\varepsilon,p}(D)}\leq C_{i,k,p,\varepsilon,T}||g_{ik}||_{L^{\infty}(D)}^p,
\]
for $\varepsilon<1-\eta$, where $\eta$ is given in Assumption \ref{assump: convolution singularity}, and for sufficiently large $p$ depending on $\varepsilon$ and $\eta$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.811149+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_193bb475ecf6f0c3347cbc656a25aee1a4e8d7cb28a627716d644d41d3252d0b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lemma_cadlag of arXiv:2603.26307, '\LARGE The incompressible Navier--Stokes--Fourier system with thermal noise'] Let Assumption (Ass:noise of the paper) hold and $(\Omega,\mathfrak{A},\mathbb{P})$, $\mathscr{F}$, $(W_n)_{n\in \mathbb{Z}^3}$, $(B_n)_{n\in \mathbb{Z}^3}$, 
	$(u,\psi ,q)  $ be a weak martingale solution to (equation Eq_new_var of the paper) with divergence-free initial value 
	$u_0 \in L^2(\mathbb{T}^3; \mathbb{R}^3)$ and $\psi_0\in L^2(\mathbb{T}^3)$ non-negative. Then there exists a $\mathbb{P}\otimes \mathrm{d} t $ version $\psi^+$ of $\psi$ which is c\`adl\`ag in the weak topology of $L^2(\mathbb{T}^3)$. Denoting the process of left limits by 
	\begin{equation}\psi^-(t)\,=\,
		\begin{cases}
			\psi_0,& t = 0 ,\\
			\lim_{s\nearrow t}  \psi^+(s), & t\in (0,T],
		\end{cases}
	\end{equation}
	this version satisfies moreover, $\mathbb{P}$-a.s.,
	\begin{align}
		\int_{\mathbb{T}^3}	\eta \bigl(\psi_{t}^{+}   - \psi_{t}^{-} \bigr) \,\mathrm{d} x \,=\, \int_{\{t\}\times \mathbb{T}^3} \eta  \,\mathrm{d} q,
	\end{align} and 
	\begin{align} \begin{split}&
			\int_{\mathbb{T}^3} \psi^+_t \eta   \, \mathrm{d} x \,-\, \int_{\mathbb{T}^3}
			\psi_0 \eta 
			\,\mathrm{d} x 
			\\&\quad=\, \int_0^t \int_{\mathbb{T}^3} -  \bigl(1+ {F_1}/2 +G_1/2\bigr) \nabla \psi \cdot \nabla  \eta \,+\,\psi u\cdot \nabla \eta   \,-\, (F_2/2+G_2/8) \psi \eta \,\mathrm{d} x\,\mathrm{d} s \,+\, \int_{[0,t]\times\mathbb{T}^3} \eta \,\mathrm{d} q
			\\&\qquad + \sum_{i=1}^3
			\sum_{n \in \mathbb{Z}^3}\int_0^t \int_{\mathbb{T}^3}\psi g_n \partial_i \eta  + \frac{1}{2} \psi  \eta \partial_ig_n  \,\mathrm{d} x\,  \mathrm{d} W_{n,s}^i
			\, +\, \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\sum_{i,j =1}^3\sum_{n \in \mathbb{Z}^3}\int_0^t \int_{\mathbb{T}^3}u_j\partial_i (\eta f_n) \,\mathrm{d} x \,\mathrm{d} B_{n,s}^{ji},
		\end{split}
	\end{align}
	for all $\eta \in C^{{\infty}}(\mathbb{T}^3)$ and  $t\in [0,T)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.889577+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_193f003e34d956197473d497c73e30f984da39b56d1b4ff22a4757560b5ce95f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:convergence of arXiv:2607.18824, 'Non-Abelian multiplicative chaos on the circle'] Fix $\varrho$ as above and $\kappa<\min(-2\check h,-\check h-2\lambda_\rho^+)$, with $\lambda_\rho^+$ defined in (equation eq:lambda_rho of the paper).

