{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.908504+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_194511320bf8f4fe64cd5f06e981b7f932205ee2f023e5de1a2ec76cf40de21e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:counterexample:leftsided:weight:operator of arXiv:2608.23765, '\texorpdfstring{Tight Majorizations and Convergence Rates\\ of Nuclear Norm Minimization I'] For any\\ $r,d \in \mathbb{N}$ with $d \ge 220 r$, there exists a measurement operator $\mathcal{A}: \mathbb{R}^{d \times d} \rightarrow \R^m$ satisfying the NSP of order $r$ with constant $\eta_r = 1/10$ and of order $1$ with $\eta_1 = 1/(11r -1)$, a rank-$r$ matrix $\mathbf{X}_\star \in \mathbb{R}^{d \times d}$ and a matrix $\mathbf{X} \in \mathbb{R}^{d \times d}$ such that $\mathbf{X} - \mathbf{X}_\star \in \ker(\mathcal{A})$ and $\nucnorm{\mathbf{X} - \mathbf{X}_\star} \le \frac{ \sigma_r \left( \mathbf{X}_\star \right) }{ \max \left( \eta_1 \sqrt{ d}, 2 \right)  }$, but also
\begin{equation*}
