{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.302250+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_195e31a064ae64ce08400c1dd61aa5e798fd514960aa687298ccea43c9c0bafe","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:boundary1 of arXiv:2601.05361, 'Noise sensitivity in last-passage percolation'] For every $p\in(0,1)$, $\lambda\in(0,1)$ and $u\in{\mathbb{Z}}^2$, we have for every $x\in u+{\mathbb{Z}}_{\ge0}^2$ that
