{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.570824+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_195f8a16d4e7004850d31349051d37fc2a42f3fded917771491ae180227c083e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2606.14443, 'SEMICLASSICAL LIMIT OF POLYAKOV-LIOUVILLE MEASURE and Q-Curvature Uniformization ON EVEN-D'] Let $(h_{\ell})_{\ell\in\N}$ the white noise truncation given in \eqref{eq: white noise trunc}.
	\begin{enumerate}[$(i)$]
		\item
		For each ${\ell}\in\N$, \(h_{\ell}\) is a centered continuous Gaussian field on $M$.
		\item 
		For all $\ell,m\in\N$ with $m>\ell$ and for all $x\in M$, $(h_m-h_{\ell})(x)$ is independent from $h_{\ell}(x)$. 

		\item For all $\ell,m\in\N$ with $m>\ell$, the correlation function of $h_m-h_{\ell}$ is non-negative, i.e. for all $x,y\in M$
		\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}
