{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.317851+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1978a6f5485bd9f317cbd57512236b333b4def6fb285ef104f2772bcee724eb9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Properly norm-minimizing of arXiv:2608.30973, 'Pseudo-Anosov flow and dynamics on guts'] Let \(M\) be a compact 3-manifold whose boundary is a collection of tori.
An oriented surface \(S\) is called \emph{properly norm-minimizing} if \(S\) is norm-minimizing and on each boundary \(P\) of \(M\), components of \(\partial S\cap P\) have the same orientation.

