{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:12:46.875547+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1986e545b9dde8b22a76c4a65d980d96f190f76e88c10a0b63313d1a88418ea6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm_path of arXiv:2608.08532, 'Constrained Maximum Weight Paths in Random Geometric Graphs'] Let~\(\epsilon_1,\epsilon_2\) be as in~((f_eq of the paper)) and suppose
\begin{equation}
r_n \geq \frac{1}{n^{\beta}},\;\;\;\;q_n = \frac{1}{n^{c}}\;\;\;\text{ and }\;\;\; L_n := \frac{\zeta_n}{r_n} \geq 1,
\end{equation} for some constants~\(0 < \beta  < c < \frac{1}{2},\) strictly. Also suppose that the inverse cdf~\(H(.)\) is strictly increasing for all large~\(z.\) For every~\(\gamma,\kappa > 0\) and all~\(0< \varepsilon < 1\) small, there are constants~\(\theta_1,\theta_2  >0\) such that
\begin{equation}
