{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.007201+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1988e8666536fcaabbed59de9a94fd68d3ab8c5c72fdbc49789220a6dd9845d5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1con of arXiv:2606.27844, 'Critical percolation on preferential attachment graphs with infinite variance'] There exist $c, c'>1$, depending on $\mu$, such that, for any $i,j\in\{1,\dots,\lfloor sn\rfloor\}$ and $x\in\{\lfloor sn\rfloor+1,\dots,n\}$, we have
