{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.316771+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1996880e3ec606e4e099b5bd444f8200c35583f077b7d3dd527090d404ed560d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2607.27786, 'Gaussian free field in annulus: \\BPZ equations and crossing probabilities for level lines'] Assume the same setup as in Proposition~\ref{prop::multiannulu_pf_construction}. The law of $n$-annulus $\SLE_{\kappa}(\LFcro{n}^{(\kappa;\ell)})$ in $(\A_r; \ee^{\ii\bs{\alpha}}, \ee^{\ii\bs{\beta}-r})$ is the same as $\Pind{n}^{(\kappa;\ell)}$ weighted by the Radon-Nikodym derivative 
