{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.617797+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1998d38bd6bc5da766e0f6f1c78f186a584a864a2bda6e8e2d9dff7d3e0c574d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 23 of arXiv:2609.01358, 'Regularized spectral expansion of a Rankin--Selberg period and moments'] Let $\varphi\in\1_{n-2}\boxplus\1_1\boxplus\1_1$ be $(s,z)$-independent. Then there exists $\beta_\varphi\in\1_{n-1}\boxplus\1_1$ so that
