{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.512174+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_19e413d6561cfcdd4e491cfe497ef796604c5d863bb1117a12dd5e98aa033dab","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 (Equality in the sub-gamma envelope) of arXiv:2609.02590, 'Directional Optimal Sub-Gamma Scales for Infinitely Divisible Laws'] Suppose that, for some finite $c\geq0$, equality holds in
\eqref{eq:subgamma} on a nonempty open interval. If $c=0$, then
$X\sim N(0,V)$. If $c>0$, then $X$ is a centered compound Poisson variable with
L\'evy density
\begin{equation}
 \nu(\dd x)=\frac{V}{2c^3}e^{-x/c}\one_{(0,\infty)}(x)\,\dd x.

\end{equation}
Equivalently, its jump intensity is $V/(2c^2)$ and its jumps are exponential
with mean $c$. The left equality laws are the reflections of these variables.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.786921+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_19e59ebd16504adb92d3cd7eab2a11d4207aebddd3057b67da367dad27ae35b0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop vertical-maximum-bound-replacement of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] There exists $c_1,c_2$ such that for any $\beta>\beta_0$ the following holds. Let $R$ be a rectangle of width $\ell$ and height at least $e^{-\beta} \bar \alpha \sqrt{\ell}$. Then, for any $ \delta \bar \alpha \le \sqrt{\beta \log \ell}$, and every $\ell \ge \beta e^{2\beta}$, we have 
    \begin{align*}
        \pi^{(-,-,+,-)}(\lambda(\sigma) \text{ reaches }\delta e^{- \beta} \bar \alpha \sqrt{\ell})\le \ell^{c_1}e^{ - c_2 (\delta \bar \alpha)^2}\,.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.872547+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_19e7e00bf1226ab0eb216bd315cd96d4935815a1ea0c60a67acb790b190ca754","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:M3 of arXiv:2608.26765, 'Beyond Client Averaging: A Client-Independent Second-Order Stationary-Bias Component in St'] There exists $C_H<\infty$ such that
