{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.876842+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_19f9d07ab8f345ed9d4be2c47f43e3db901f173c94692254e5bac80710346658","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop punctured-strict of arXiv:2608.27939, 'Entropy and domination for quasi-Hitchin representations'] Assume that at least one Fock--Goncharov coordinate of $\rho$ is not real and positive.  Then there is $\gamma\in\pi_1(S)$ with determinant-one lifts $
