{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.228158+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a2333a321aa83839cca83baa7308fa5addcd925f2bad44433bf8103a2cba370","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma when-does-u-go-to-zero of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] Let $f:\mathbb{R}\to  [0,\infty)$ be a non-negative measurable function supported in $[-K, \infty)$ and $\phi(x) = 1-e^{-f(-x)}$. Then, 
