{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.318938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a4a92e85a5f90285d0c6d0486806112a87f3404c0d9d6f5a1fa5defe157d28f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2411.09058, 'Time-dependent averages of a critical long-range stochastic heat equation'] For  any  $0<\kappa < \frac{d-2}{2}$, let $\{u_t(\mathrm{d} x):t\geq 0\}$ be {a} solution to (equation eq:microshe of the paper) as defined in [mueller2004singular]. For $t=t_R>0$, the time-dependent spatial averages $u_{t_R}(B_R)$ have the following limits:
    \begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*]
