{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:22:48.877857+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a9fe3daa5c473abd32de4caf34e67510acf7f482dc176e81e6ef599b6b431c2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 13 of arXiv:2608.29152, 'Uniform Statistical Convergence of Empirical Sinkhorn Potentials\\ with Exponential and Po'] For $0<\eps\le1$, constants $A_0,L_0,D_{\cX},D_{\cY}<\infty$, $\gamma_{\mathrm{osc}},q\ge0$, and metric dimensions $\mathfrak d_{\cX},\mathfrak d_{\cY}\ge1$, let $\mathfrak M_\eps$ contain all models $(\cX,\cY,\mu,\nu,c_\eps)$ where the supports $\cX,\cY$ have covering numbers bounded by $(1+D_{\cX}/t)^{\mathfrak d_{\cX}}$ and $(1+D_{\cY}/t)^{\mathfrak d_{\cY}}$, respectively.
