{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.784179+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1afb9dfcc591b96b39d5a78871a70ea0f282f97a9e99954379fda8f369b219ec","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] From a set $D = \mathsf{Dis}_{k-1}(B) \subset \mathscr{B}_{k-1}$ having $|\mathsf{Dis}_{k-1}(B)|\le s_k$, we construct $R_1,...,R_K$ as follows. Start with candidate set $\mathcal R = \{B': B'\in \mathsf{Dis}_{k-1}(B)\}$;  repeat the following process
        \begin{itemize}
            \item If the current candidate $\mathcal R$ contains two squares $R, R'$ of side-length $a \ell_{k-1}$ and $b \ell_{k-1}$ within distance $10 \ell_{k-1}$, then replace $R,R'$ in $\mathcal R$ with $R''$ which is a smallest square covering both squares.  
        \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.365181+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1afc0a6d54696c3dbc6f2f5e33c41d3a9e7582411b71269919e16589d6dd755b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop holderct-general of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] For all $\eta<\frac{5}{8}$ and $\varepsilon>0$, there exist $p=p(\eta)$ and $C=C(\eta,\varepsilon)>0$ such that for all $n$,
