{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.309519+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1b97ec86ec4b28143d56caae22ee6a6688755f9bd4468ed9dbb480c9051689a0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 4 of arXiv:2609.02392, 'Large values of cubic and quartic Dirichlet $L$-functions of prime moduli'] Suppose $\chi$ be a primitive Dirichlet character modulo $q$. Let $A$ and $B$ be positive real numbers with $AB = q$.  Then we have
\begin{align*}

