Now, for every $m$ one has $\lambda_m<1$, and the values $\lambda_m$ converge to $2^{-\frac{{\varepsilon}}{2}}<1$ as $m\to\infty$. Hence, there exists $\lambda<1$ such that for all $m$, one has $\lambda_m^{1/(2+{\varepsilon})}<\lambda$. Taking
