{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.506011+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1bd980a98bd9fdee2a43fc5e95592ba1964516f63ce42c327b09c8debfae84cb","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 104 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] A centered Gaussian process $X$ is called a \emph{$Q$-fractional Brownian motion} with Hurst index $H \in (\frac{1}{3},\frac{1}{2}]$ if its covariance function is given by
