{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.635930+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c06ae81c00df689850a45c9630ce57625d4da83818094d8edd8e3b5ca9b4d4d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2506.17109, 'Limit theorems under nonlinear expectations dominated by sublinear expectations'] Let a nonlinear expectation $\mathbb{\tilde{E}}[\cdot]$ be
dominated by a sublinear expectation $\mathbb{\hat{E}}[\cdot]$ on
$(\Omega,\mathcal{H})$, and let $\{(X_{n},Y_{n})\}_{n=1}^{\infty}$ be a
sequence of $2d$-dimensional random vectors such that $(X_{n+1},Y_{n+1}
)\overset{d}{=}(X_{1},Y_{1})$ and $(X_{n+1},Y_{n+1})$ is independent of
$(X_{1}$,$\ldots$,$X_{n}$,$Y_{1}$,$\ldots$,$Y_{n})$ for $n\geq1$ under
$\mathbb{\tilde{E}}[\cdot]$ and $\mathbb{\hat{E}}[\cdot]$ respectively.
Suppose that
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{\hat{E}}[X_{1}]=\mathbb{\hat{E}}[-X_{1}]=0\text{ and }\lim
_{N\rightarrow \infty}\mathbb{\hat{E}}\left[  (|X_{1}|^{2}-N)^{+}
+(|Y_{1}|-N)^{+}\right]  =0, 
\end{equation}
and for each given $(A,p)\in \mathbb{S}_{d}\times \mathbb{R}^{d}$,
\begin{equation}
\tilde{G}(A,p):=\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}n\mathbb{\tilde{E}}\left[  \frac
{1}{n}\left(  \frac{1}{2}\langle AX_{1},X_{1}\rangle+\langle p,Y_{1}
\rangle \right)  \right]  \text{ exists.} 
\end{equation}
Then for each $\phi \in C_{b.Lip}(\mathbb{R}^{2d})$, we have
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}\mathbb{\tilde{E}}\left[  \phi \left(  \frac{1}
{\sqrt{n}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i},\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}Y_{i}\right)  \right]
=u^{\phi}(1,0,0), 
\end{equation}
where $u^{\phi}$ is the unique viscosity solution of the following PDE:
\begin{equation}
