{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.861575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c4b7ee68910788c4d43e66d09d950516537706308eea1c16ed7060e56021e0b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $\varphi_\lambda(x)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\lambda}}e^{-\frac{x^2}{2\lambda}}$ be the density of a Gaussian with mean $0$ and variance 
