{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.774454+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c558b5892aad560c910b0b8a488e93ad74830e57d1473824fb94916732729a9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition D:semiflow of arXiv:2411.01364, 'Global Dynamics of Granular Media Equations via Stochastic Order'] A map $P^*: 
\mathbb{R_+}\times\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)\rightarrow\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$ is said to be a jointly continuous semigroup, or a semiflow on $\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$, if 
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
    \item  $P^*: \mathbb{R_+}\times\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)\rightarrow\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$ is continuous;
    \item $P_0^*\mu=\mu$  for all $\mu\in\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$;
    \item $P_t^*\circ P_s^*=P_{t+s}^*$ for all $t,s\in \mathbb{R_+}$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.953011+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c58e5e3488334a80085d4e79c08744c5754fbab258318e6c95f52f65be0e1f0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2602.08591, 'The Yang--Mills measure on compact surfaces as a \\ universal scaling limit of lattice gau'] Let $\psi\in C^\infty(\mathrm{Cyl},\mathfrak{g})$. Define 
   \[\forall r_1,r_2,\theta_1,\theta_2, \ \ \ K_{r_1,r_2,\theta_1,\theta_2}\psi\coloneq \frac{1}{(r_2-r_1)(\theta_2-\theta_1)}\int_\Sigma \psi(u,\gamma)     1_{[\theta_1,\theta_2]}(\gamma)1_{[r_1,r_2]}(u) \mathrm{d} u\mathrm{d} \gamma .\]
    We have 
        \begin{eqnarray*}
        \mathbb{E}\left[\exp(i\langle \xi_N,\psi \rangle\right)]
        &=&\prod_{\theta\in \Theta^N_-}\left\{\prod_{r\in R^N_-}\left(1-\frac{\vert K_{r,r_+,\theta,\theta_+}\psi\vert ^2}{2}\sigma(\square(r,r_+,\theta,\theta_+))\right)+O_{N,\theta}\right\},
    \end{eqnarray*}
    where 
    $\sum_{\theta \in \Theta^N_-}\vert O_{N,\theta }\vert  \xrightarrow[N\to \infty]{}0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.385373+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c5b8cca8c6114c1af37efc439fa612df83dc4b420e9603c8bc5a8d96665322c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor_join_expectation of arXiv:2411.02046, 'Speed of Convergence and Moderate Deviations of FPP on Random Geometric Graphs'] There exists~$\mathfrak C_1 > 0$ such that the following holds. Let~$x \in \R^d$ be such that~$\|x\|$ is large enough (as required in Lemma~(lem_T_t_and_T of the paper)), and let~$t \in [\mathfrak C_1 \log\big(\|x\|\big),\|x\|]$.  Then,
	\begin{equation}

	\E [ (T(x)- Y_{t,x})^2] \le 2(\mathfrak Ct)^2.
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.539920+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c5e1fa9ca2999ad9bd9b5235eb7dc77e1fcfcbabececc6c67df4ab43cabcd82","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma FejerNew of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] Let $f:[0,1]\rightarrow \lbrack 0,1]$ be continuous and
strictly increasing, with a unique fixed point $p\in (0,1)$ and
single--crossing pattern 
\begin{equation}
f(x)>x\;\text{for }x<p,\qquad f(x)<x\;\text{for }x>p.  
\end{equation}
Then

\begin{enumerate}
\item[(i)] For every $x\in \lbrack 0,1]$, 
\begin{equation}
|f(x)-p|\leq |x-p|,  
\end{equation}
with strict inequality if $x\neq p$;

\item[(ii)] If $x,y$ lie on the same side of $p$ (both $\leq p$ or both $
\geq p$), then 
\begin{equation}
|f(x)-f(y)|\leq |x-y|.  
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.747255+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c5e290f540c1b1286929a5b772bda2d68492709df116aedb64a629169de72e0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 21 of arXiv:2506.10522, 'On the Law of the Iterated Logarithm for $m$-dependent stationary random variables under s'] Let $\{X_n;n=1,2,\cdots\}$ be a sequence of $m$-dependent and linear stationary random variables in a sub-linear space $\sles$ satisfying condition (CC). If there exists $M$ such that 
