{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.864893+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c88b634c0dfe193f04e75dde6398cb3868227a050980c4a2fc8f5efc24f6e4a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 19 of arXiv:2506.10856, 'The space of multifurcating ranked tree shapes: enumeration, lattice structure, and Markov'] The tree $\ddot{T}_N$ with the maximum backwards degree in $\mathcal{MT}_N$ is the multifurcating tree with the following properties 
