{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.209598+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c8c2e926dc6c563d68221fac14a50c39f29987bcb84e8ac1cc94af8cb0545fd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi Def:Weighted-Cap-Prod of arXiv:2608.29013, 'Weighted Homology and Cohomology of Weighted Polyhedra'] Suppose $(X, \lambda)$ is a descending type weighted polyhedron. Define $R$-bilinear \emph{weighted cap product} 
  $$ \Cap:  \mathcal{W}_n(X, \lambda; R)\times \mathcal{W}^p(X, \lambda; R) \rightarrow  \mathcal{W}_{n-p}(X, \lambda; R), \ 0\leqslant p\leqslant n $$ 
  by: for any cochain $\phi\in \mathcal{W}^p(X, \lambda; R)$ and any chain $\theta\in \mathcal{W}_n(X, \lambda; R)$, 
   \begin{equation*} 
   \theta  \,\Cap\, \phi := \frac{\xi\big([ v_0,\cdots, v_{p} ]\big)\xi\big([ v_p,\cdots, v_{n} ]\big)}{\xi\big([ v_0,\cdots, v_{n} ]\big)} \phi\big( \theta|_{  [ v_0,\cdots,v_{p} ]} \big) \theta|_{[ v_{p},\cdots,v_{n} ]}. 
   \end{equation*}
 The coefficient on the right hand side is integral 
  because $\xi$ is a descending weight.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.710768+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c8d3a9c20e1b5673f340dc190add536153a3fb6bfeb8b408b11b47a3cc2af42","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition defi:cLnorm of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] We equip spaces $\cV_\varnothing, \cV_{\sf o},\cV_{\sf x}$ and $\cU_{\sf ox}$ with norm
