{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.758282+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c90e2527507a1e0cbc0481358e917a5a8e88bd3768c26aa6d4a3c25cf74dc6f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_localized_eigenvalue_local_law of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] In the setting of (theorem_localized_eigenvector_localization of the paper), the following estimate holds uniformly in $t\in \left[{0,1}\right]$ for some constant $C>0$ that does not depend on $\varepsilon$:

