weakly with respect to the Gromov-Hausdorff-Prokhorov-function topology as $n\rightarrow\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.519876+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ca5d6ac6655592a79c7459064460c3cfb37c2604565e868647973486b9be895","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:second-largest-in-theorem of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{prop:second_largest}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 1$, and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel satisfying $J(x,y) = \Omega(d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha})$ with $\alpha \in (0,2)$. 

