{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:22:48.865655+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1cba7bf1daa09e28b112820c8891781f898057fc48257edb8302ce69efc2bebc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2 (Exact local selector) of arXiv:2608.29107, 'PathGuide: Dynamic Classifier-Free Guidance via On-Policy Transport Alignment'] Fix $y$, and $\psi \in C_c^\infty(\mathbb{R}^d)$, and a committed past schedule $\vec{\omega}_i$.
Then $\mathcal{L}_i(\omega_i \mid y; \vec{\omega}_i, \psi)$, defined in Equation~\eqref{eq:exact-local-objective} is minimized for
\begin{equation}
\omega_i^\star(y; \vec{\omega}_i, \psi)
=
\frac{
\displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}
\Bigl(
u_{t_i}(x \mid y) - v_{t_i}^\theta(x \mid \varnothing)
\Bigr) \cdot
\nabla_x\psi(x) \,
\hat{p}_{t_i}(x \mid y; \vec{\omega}_i) \,\mathrm{d}x
}{
