{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:44:39.720832+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d24d908a6e3ed5b2390cd61e3e00417182cad90c30294412cee23648685b660","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2608.29747, 'Reduced Khovanov-Rozansky homology'] \cite[attributed to Ocneanu]{Jones1987Hecke}
For each $n \in \N$, there exists a unique $T$-module homomorphism $\mathrm{Tr}_n: \mathrm{H}_n \to \Z[a^{\pm 1}, q^{\pm 1}, \frac{1}{q-q^{-1}}]$ such that
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\mathrm{Tr}_n (BB') = \mathrm{Tr}_n (B'B)$ for all $B, B' \in \mathrm{H}_n$,
    \item $\mathrm{Tr}_{n+1} (i(B)) = \{0\} \mathrm{Tr}_{n}(B)$ and $\mathrm{Tr}_{n+1} (i(B)B_{n}) = \{1\} \mathrm{Tr}_{n}(B)$ for all $B \in \H_n$, and
    \item $\mathrm{Tr}_{1} (1) = 1$,
\end{enumerate}
where $i : H_n \to H_{n+1}$ is the inclusion map that sends $B_j \mapsto B_j$ for all $j \in \{1, \dots, n-1\}$ and $\{n\} = \frac{aq^{-n}-a^{-1}q^n}{q-q^{-1}}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.506517+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d2d4dabc91e1176062c17d4e8fe9ec5db1473e38c600d49bb02487127a019fe","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture Pure partition function- Coulomb gas integral of arXiv:2505.14762, 'Multiple radial SLE($\kappa$) and quantum Calogero-Sutherland system'] For irrational $\kappa \in(0,8)$, the pure partition functions are related to Coulomb gas integrals by affine meander matrix:
