	so that $c_k^{*}=F_k(1)\,F_{k-1}'(1)$ for $k\geq2$ when $m=1$ (type~I). In type~III the marked vertex of $\mathcal{T}^{*}$ is almost surely a leaf, so $\partial(\mathcal{T}^{*})=0$ almost surely, and hence $c_0^{*}=1$ and $c_k^{*}=0$ for every $k\geq1$.","status":"unverified"}

