{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.951492+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d5bf4b40553394179d16ec7436f5c8b3af57151ad7e1af0e2208281ca9318a4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1 ({\cite[Theorem 2.5) of arXiv:2604.05234, 'Quantitative propagation of chaos and universality for asymmetric Langevin spin glass dyna'] {Arous1995-zj}}] There exists a unique weak solution $(Y,B)$ with $\mu=\textup{Law}(Y)$ to the following McKean-Vlasov equation,
