{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.804032+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d6d5479878f16f4cd83f0ab2a443c8054e4fdaf133d43c19a6728a68eb7f4a8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm l:FAFBisFAB of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] For any Borel sets $A,B\in\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}^2)$ and any $X\in L^2(\Xi,\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})$, if $X$ is $\mathcal{F}_B$-measurable, then
