{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.135439+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d823a8213bbd3fb33d815d112154bf9de7622b1a49a1c771cc8d2d03dc2f875","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:contractionMarkov of arXiv:2603.00773, 'Long-time $L^p$ Wasserstein contraction for diffusion processes without global dissipativi'] Under Assumptions~(assum:decomposeYZ of the paper) and (assum:Contract_at_infty of the paper), for any $p\geqslant 1$, there exist $C_p,\lambda_p>0$ (which depend only and explicitly on $p$ and the parameters in $\mathfrak{P}'$) such that for any $\nu,\mu\in\mathcal P_p(\mathbb R^{n+m})$ and $t\geqslant 0$,
