{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.903183+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d85d215e0f7e6bb9f5ad3af45ebeb6195ace23f1a44f5a7995b1fcad5508860","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem T:EWDSHE of arXiv:2511.08479, '\Large From disordered systems to the Critical 2D Stochastic Heat Flow'] Let $u^\varepsilon$ be the solution of the mollified 2D SHE  (equation eq:mollSHE of the paper) with disorder strength $\beta_\varepsilon=(\hat\beta+o(1)) \sqrt{\frac{2\pi}{\log \frac{1}{\varepsilon}}}$ for some $\hat\beta\in (0,1)$. Then for any test function $\phi\in C_c(\mathbb{R}^2)$, we have
\begin{equation} 
\frac{1}{\beta_\varepsilon} \int_{\mathbb{R}^2} \phi(x) \big(u^\varepsilon(t,x)-1\big) {\rm d}x
\xrightarrow[\,\varepsilon\to 0\,]{d} \int_{\mathbb{R}^2} \phi(x) v(t, x) {\rm d}x,
\end{equation}
where $v(t, x)$ is the solution to the Edwards-Wilkinson equation
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
	\partial_t v(t,x) & =\frac{1}{2} \Delta v(t,x) + \sqrt{\frac{1}{1-\hat\beta^2}}\, \tilde\xi(t,x), \qquad v(0, x)\equiv 0\,.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

