{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.627116+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1da64d5584d799393011ca4eea9daf93fdd6916f34014bd7b7b64316100b3558","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:basicboundaryint of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] Let $\vec\ell$ be of convergent type for the face $\cal F$ and $1\leq j_0\leq s$. Then there exists $\epsilon >0$ such that for $0<Y<1$ we have the bounds

