 whenever the integral in the right-hand side makes sense. We call $-\mathcal{I}$ the energy functional.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:32.065398+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1dd313222e4cdaa114032cd80979c531b2d5a60326d3cde08b00197a7477dd4e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l.convex_Phi of arXiv:2411.14105, 'Simultaneous replica-symmetry breaking \\ for vector spin glasses'] Let $(L,\alpha)$ be a decomposition of some $q\in \mathcal Q_\infty$, let $\Phi$ be associated with $(L,\alpha)$, and let $\phi$ be the terminal condition of $\Phi$ given as in~(equation e.phi=initial of the paper).
