{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.350257+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1df7023f72a326907bb278d5beeeb0383bbb72235f9b9c86b18400fdbf7dc3b8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2506.15736, 'Coming down from infinity for coordinated particle systems'] A coordinated particle system on a finite set of sites $V$ started with infinitely many particles at site $v_1 \in V$ will not come down from infinity if the following conditions are met.

