{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.200448+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1dfc7c02a212913b2ec7eb7d6b8e470a7a6f67fe3843c03708ca788ea6e51b10","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lemma reduction conv of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] Fix a symmetric, stochastic $n\times n$ matrix $\ensuremath{\mathcal K}$, and let $\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$ denote its irreducible components. Fix \(m \in (-1,1)^{\mathcal{A}}\). 
