{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.831628+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e0c5ccfbd5352bc3943c3daf1438deb80ed38e4519b71f3a9ec34ab4fcc706d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:monotonicity of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] If $\mathbf{x}_- \preceq \mathbf{x}_+$, $\mathbf{y}_- \preceq \mathbf{y}_+$, $\bm{\lambda}_- \succeq \bm{\lambda}_+$,
$\mathbf{f}_- \preceq \mathbf{f}_+$, and $\mathbf{g}_- \preceq \mathbf{g}_+$, then
