{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:25:49.896010+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e559522d134abc34f2a15937079068d86bec1ccee04c3c6641af6c14924a47d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 49 of arXiv:2609.02065, '\textbf{From Bowditch's question to Goldman's conjecture for type-preserving representatio'] Let $P: \univcover\times \univcover\to \univcover$ be a product map, and let $m, n, l\in \mathbb{Z}, s\in\{+,-\}$.
