{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.747172+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e55e13728305a44364d6a7a11c9c8f03762209443016ed337c0bd1e09916549","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1 of arXiv:2511.19308, 'Universal scaling limits at the spectral singularity of structured random matrices'] Let $H$ be given by \eqref{eq: matrix model definition}.
    Then for all $z \in \C$ with $\Im(z) > 0$ and all $N \in \N$ the expectation of the resolvent has the integral representation
    \begin{equation} 
