        = \frac{\ii N^{K+1}}{(2 \pi \ii)^K} \int_{(0, \infty)^K} \dd a \oint^K \dd b \, \ee^{-N I(a) + N I(b)} \det\s*{ S + \diag_{i = 1}^K\p*{\frac{1}{a_i b_i}} } \sum_{j = 1}^K a_j,
    \end{equation}
    where $\dd a$ is the $K$-dimensional Lebesgue-measure and the $b$-integral is $\oint^K \dd b := \oint \dd b_1 \dots \oint \dd b_K$ where each $\oint \dd b_i$ is a counter-clockwise contour integral over the circle around $0$.
    The function $I: \R^K \to \C$ in the exponent is
    \begin{equation} 
        I(a) := \frac{1}{2} \sum_{i, j = 1}^K s_{ij} a_j a_i - \ii z \sum_{i = 1}^K a_i - \sum_{i = 1}^K \log(a_i).
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.812243+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e58d11e032478ee9e16a65d37674fbe9f920a58746df1ca212d8b42f3186f26","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:main of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] Let $d$, $s$ and $\alpha$ satisfy (hp:main_hp of the paper). There exist constants $\eta_{d,s,\alpha}>0$, $\rho_{d,s,\alpha}\ge 0$, such that for every $M\in \dot H^{-s+1}_{\vee, \div}$,
