{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.075509+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e85bdc231aaa84b233470a7927a3ef36080135fc018d480a7d4c5b0fc75ab67","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:bound-T_n-optimal of arXiv:2509.08928, 'The near critical random bond Ising model via embedding deformation'] Assume that all the variances in $\Lambda_n$ are unitary and all the other variances vanish. Then there exist some small enough universal constants $c_{1}>0$ such that
