{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.573262+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e8bf9ee219e24c47c9a299ac26356209010eb396f8a32c075c696e75e496f91","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2606.14564, 'Upper tails for irregular graphs \\ beyond the mean-field regime'] For every nonempty graph $J$ without isolated vertices and all $0 \le B \le 2A$, the solution to $\mathcal{P}(J;A,B)$ is
