{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.605934+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e91d5f3a86331f798a10cc5bfd93c1305fa558cb9386e6358ab8bc12e4b7595","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2607.08129, '2607.08129'] The rate function $I_\theta$ is convex.  If $I_\theta(f)<\infty$, then $f$ is absolutely continuous and nondecreasing, satisfies $f(0)=0$, and obeys
\begin{equation}
