{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.721730+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ea0ae358e37584eb81de78ce62dfa2e6243463f9aabcd3275b9fb382501dc00","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm2.2 of arXiv:2606.01944, 'Propagation of Chaos for Mean-field Mean Reflected Backward Stochastic Differential Equati'] Under Assumptions (H1)-(H4), the mean-field mean reflected BSDE associated with $(\xi,f,h)$ admits a unique solution $(Y,Z,K)\in \mathcal{S}^2\times\mathcal{H}^2\times I[0,T]$. Moreover, for each $t\in[0,T]$, we have 
