{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.357290+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ecc4cab7275cc80c5965952246a129d8593cd8fb01844b66cfa181a3e53c780","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma limit-points-drift:fixed-path of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] For each $n$, let $\bm{a}^n:[0,1]\to{\mathbb R}^n$ be such that $a_i^n\in H_0^1$ and for almost every $t\in[0,1]$
