{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.079970+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ee6cda8fab9c5a3408cbb801e3bfdb6f7285e31541823810075e27b405c3404","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma D-convege of arXiv:2601.15223, 'Large time behaviour for a class of 2D and 3D stochastic non-Newtonian fluids of different'] Assume that $\boldsymbol{\mathfrak{K}}\in \mathrm{L}^{2}_{\mathrm{loc}}(\mathbb{R};\mathbb{H}^{-1}(\mathbb{Q}))$ and $\{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{Z}}^n_{0}\}_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ be a bounded sequence in $\mathbb{H}$. Then, for every $\omega\in\Omega$ and $\mathfrak{r}\in\mathbb{R}$, there exists $\tilde{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{Z}}} \in \mathrm{L}^{\infty}(\mathfrak{r}, \mathfrak{r}+T; \mathbb{H})\cap\mathrm{L}^{2}(\mathfrak{r}, \mathfrak{r}+T; \mathbb{V})\cap\mathrm{L}^{4}(\mathfrak{r}, \mathfrak{r}+T; \mathbb{W}^{1,4}(\mathbb{Q}))$  such that along a subsequence
