{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.745734+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f063858c532c253841eb63c5e9bf695ca9b84fc369832245a76c33518930c53","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main-circle-endpoint-formula of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Assume that \(W\) is in the minimal Kahane--Peyri\`ere regime. Let \(\mu_{\circ}\) be the dyadic Mandelbrot cascade measure on \(\mathbb{S}^{1}\) generated by \(W\). Then, almost surely on \(\{\mu_{\circ}(\mathbb{S}^{1})>0\}\),
\begin{equation}
\dim_{\mathrm F}(\mu_{\circ})=A_{\mathrm{loc}}(W).
\end{equation}
In particular, if \(A_{\mathrm{loc}}(W)>0\), then for every
\(0<\sigma<A_{\mathrm{loc}}(W)\) there is a finite random constant \(C_{\sigma}\)
such that
\begin{equation}
\lvert\widehat{\mu_{\circ}}(\xi)\rvert
\leq
C_{\sigma}\lvert\xi\rvert^{-\sigma/2}
\end{equation}
for all sufficiently large \(\lvert\xi\rvert\), with
\(\xi\in\mathbb{R}^{2}\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.433034+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f0677ba62d1962ca69db62381c0cb0223c8146607d5d86aa722542b8519a390","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:Jrr-lower of arXiv:2601.07808, 'Supercritical long-range percolation on graphs of polynomial growth: the truncated one-arm'] Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 1$, and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel with $J(x,y) = \Omega(d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha})$ with $\alpha > 1$.

     Then there exists $c = c(G,J) > 0$ such that for all $r \in \mathbf{N}$

     \begin{equation}

        J(B(r), B(r)^c) 
        \geq
        c
        r^{
            \max
            \left(
                d(2-\alpha),
                d-1
            \right)  
        }
        \log(r)^{
            \mathbf{1}
            \left(
                \alpha=1+1/d
            \right)
        }.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.954938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f074317fa23b4afd407708b70d73463702c9589ce0198c5a1df12111f77334b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma esperance of arXiv:2602.08591, 'The Yang--Mills measure on compact surfaces as a \\ universal scaling limit of lattice gau'] Under the $M_\beta$ condition, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for  all $0
