\end{equation} for all $N$ large enough.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.049500+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_206081ba2dfb56ec9fea7705c11cd04d0b6170b8cef29b0437228d4bcacaf9f9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2606.16083, 'Eyring--Kramers asymptotics for infinite-dimensional stochastic gradient systems'] Given $E,\rho>0$, we find a subspace $\mathcal{V}\subseteq B^*\cap A^{-1}(B^*)$ of finite dimension, containing $\{\eta_1,\dots ,\eta_m\}$, such that the corresponding orthogonal projection $\pi:B\longrightarrow H$ satisfies
