{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.682348+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_20ee46576d2fd77306240767d4afc3a4a646a2fe42c83ec476a175985379fdff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Unnumberedtheorem eq:smoothing_formula of arXiv:2412.00279, 'Optimal local storage policy based on stochastic intensities and its large scale behavior'] Let $\Phi$ be a simple point process in $\mathbb{R}$ with history $\mathcal{F}_t,$ and $\lambda(t)$ an $\mathcal{F}_t$-adapted and a.s. integrable process. Then: $\lambda(t)$ is an $\mathcal{F}_t$-stochastic intensity of $\Phi$ if and only if 
