{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.687183+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21075f65c9f1ddba5c550f0a7b007e7cf6fb98adb8ad0c2bbb4000e697664ebd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Riemann Rearrangement Theorem of arXiv:2609.01926, 'On Sum Ranges for $3n$-convergence'] Let $A = (a_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ be a sequence of real numbers and $\sum A$ be its sum.
    \begin{enumerate}
