{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.291951+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_210a62d5c3b8b20719a92e8785cb30ba1cb57d1132dd6724064d3d741b2a3aa0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:mainbound of arXiv:2605.06887, 'Law of large numbers for activated random walk on villages'] For all $a \in \mathbb{R}_+$ and $M \in \mathbb{N}_0^{V}$ we have
