{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.357847+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_210ae0821184af6d4a0d54a557db3bc59dee7a6fda94f4f6f55b95ae2533f492","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition bound on the norm of the limit of arXiv:2411.13062, 'Graphon-Theoretic Approach to Central Limit Theorems for $\epsilon$-Independence'] Let $w$ be a graphon and $\mu_w$ be the measure such that its odd moments vanish, and for any integer $p\ge 1$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \int x^{2p}\, \text{d}\mu_w=\sum_{\pi \in P_2(2p)}\rho(f_\pi,w).
    \end{align*}
Denote
    \begin{align*}
        q:=\sup_{(x,y)\in [0,1]^2}w(x,y),
    \end{align*}
and let $\mu_q$ be the corresponding $q$-Gaussian law (equation eq: q-gaussian def of the paper). Then, for all integers $p\ge 1$, we have that  
\begin{align*}
        \int x^{p}\, \text{d}\mu_w \le \int x^{p}\, \text{d}\mu_q.
    \end{align*}
In particular, if $q<1$, then the measure $\mu_w$ is bounded and its support is contained in $[-2/\sqrt{1-q},2/\sqrt{1-q}]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.239307+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_210f6c5343bfbd27fa9e6f006bf2ec560a5d4a27cf9844270ea6aa7aca5cba17","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop prob: lower bound on event E of arXiv:2411.16398, 'Large Deviations of Cover Time of Tori in Dimensions $d\geq 3$'] For all $\delta, \eta>0$, there exist $K_0(\eta), \varepsilon_0(\eta)>0$ such that the following holds. 
For all $K>K_0$ and $0<\varepsilon<\varepsilon_0$, there exists $M=M(K,\varepsilon)$ such that, 
