{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.574878+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21a26b044f9a22d946be550457fd01ccfb75e7773b3a307d84bd73261b17c9bd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm-Ito-JS-I.4.57 of arXiv:2505.24043, 'Weak solutions of Navier-Stokes Equation with purely discontinuous L\'evy Noise'] Suppose that $\xi$ is  real-valued  semimartingale. Then for every $t\geq 0$, almost surely
