{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.257424+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21d1c6993975a2314b0b9c3e7d32343b2394daea0751be862bfc348e39e7f6ca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma JHJHJH of arXiv:2603.12774, 'Synchronization by noise for stochastic differential equations driven by fractional Browni'] Consider the setting of Proposition~(POINT of the paper). Then there exists a deterministic constant \( \overline{C} > 0 \) such that
