{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:25:35.679750+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21d3288b1f39ce962581ad59673ffa667087d05c13e9b1e686407e0aada8e46a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition discover_nsep_first of arXiv:2603.05491, '\textbf{Local limits of uniform triangulations with boundaries in high genus}'] There exist $m_1,m_2 \ge 0$ and a partial order $i_1,\cdots,i_{m_1+2m_2}$ with $m:=m_1+2m_2 \le \varepsilon p^{-1}|\mathbf{p}|$ such that:
