{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.475220+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21d8ed819308f0b5c7230423f80eaf567bf1480440f89ff6f35c3adce54774ad","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2607.29020, 'Entropic Symmetrization Resistance'] \label[lemma]{lem:d_tr_dominates_oneone_norm}
Let $A \in \mathbb{R}^{d \times d}$ be positive semidefinite. 
Then $d\cdot{\rm tr}(A) \ge \@ifstar{\oldnorm}{\oldnorm*}{A}_{1,1}$, with equality iff every entry of $A$ has the same absolute value. 

\begin{proof}
By (lem:psd_diagonal_dominance of the paper),

\[
\sum_{\{i,j\} \in \binom{[d]}{2}} \@ifstar{\oldabs}{\oldabs*}{a_{ij}} 
\le \frac{1}{2}\sum_{\{i,j\} \in \binom{[d]}{2}} (a_{ii} + a_{jj}) 
= \sum_{\{i,j\} \in \binom{[d]}{2}} a_{ii} 
= \sum_{i=1}^d\sum_{j\ne i} a_{ii} 
= (d-1) \sum_{i=1}^d a_{ii} .
\]
By the same lemma, equality is attained if and only if $\@ifstar{\oldabs}{\oldabs*}{a_{ij}} = a_{ii} = a_{jj}$ for every $\{i,j\} \in \binom{[d]}{2}$. 

Finally, by the nonnegativity of the diagonal entries $a_{ii}$ we have 
\[ \@ifstar{\oldnorm}{\oldnorm*}{A}_{1,1} \le \left( (d-1) \sum a_{ii} \right) + \left(\sum a_{ii} \right) = d\cdot {\rm tr}(A),\]
with equality if and only if $A$ is a nonnegative scalar multiple of $J_d$. 
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:40:59.384647+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21d8f49aa41fcb5e4ac04092b6ed964025ac60c0416e4925393fc4f7d0dd91c2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 28 of arXiv:2609.03962, '$L^p$ isomorphisms for the fractional Laplacian on $\mathbb{R}^n$ and their application'] Let $s,t\in(0,2),~1<p<\infty$. Then $(-\triangle)^{\frac{s+t}{2}}:\Lambda^{s,p}(\R^n)\to\Lambda^{-t,p}(\R^n)$ is bounded. More precisely, it is bounded on $\mathscr{S}(\R^n)$ then extends to $\Lambda^{s,p}(\R^n)$, and equals to $(-\triangle)^{\frac{t}{2}}\circ\flap$. Moreover
