{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.601199+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21f0878bc30cfe1ff3341f5ff25389f413626092fec6b91955c852181286e5af","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 11 of arXiv:2609.01358, 'Regularized spectral expansion of a Rankin--Selberg period and moments'] Let $\phi\in \mathcal{S}([G_n]^1 )$ and $k\in K_n$. Recall $\V$ from \eqref{def-mathcal-V}. For $s,z\in\C$ recall $\lambda_{\mathrm{D}}(s)$ and $\lambda_{\mathrm{C}}(s,z)$ from \eqref{eq:def-lambda-discrete} and \eqref{eq:def-lambda-cont}. Then for $h\in G_2(\A)$ we have
