{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.777536+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_226f03054fcd1841b0e2d164e48de418ba7a73efca41aa4e90d0cd0ebb8ed956","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo 1 (Monotonicity theorem for the $H^{2|2}$ model) of arXiv:2603.25536, 'The $H^{2|2}$ monotonicity theorem revisited'] Fix an integer $N\geq 1$, consider the vertex set $V=\{1,\dots,N,\delta\}$ with a root vertex $\delta$, unoriented edges $(ij)=(ji)$ for $i,j\in V$, and symmetric positive edge weights $W_{ij}=W_{ji}>0$ for $i,j\in V$. Define
\begin{equation}
    \mathcal{D}_W(t_1,\dots,t_N)=\sum_{T\in\mathcal{T}}\prod_{(ij)\in T}W_{ij}e^{t_i+t_j}
\end{equation}
for $t=(t_1,\dots,t_N)$ and $t_{\delta}=0$, where the sum is over the spanning trees $\mathcal{T}$ of the complete graph over $\{1,\dots,N,\delta\}$. Consider the effective $H^{2|2}$ action functional
\begin{equation*}
    S^W_{\text{eff}}(t)=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j\in V}W_{ij}(\cosh(t_i-t_j)-1)-\frac{1}{2}\left(\ln \mathcal{D}_{W}(t_1,\dots,t_N)-2\sum_{i=1}^{N}t_i\right).
\end{equation*}
Then for fixed $p_1,\dots,p_N>0$, the integral
\begin{equation*}
    K=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{N}}f\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_ie^{t_i}\right)e^{-S^W_{\text{eff}}(t)}dt_1\cdots dt_{N}
\end{equation*}
is non-increasing in each of the $(W_{ij})_{i,j\in\{1,\dots,N,\delta\}}$ if $f:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}$ is convex. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.155720+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_227058d3a61b48f48f5d521940082112b824aa69089f944cb45e7cfd87359433","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:unique of arXiv:2607.05671, 'Bi-infinite systems of singularly interacting Brownian particles and the KPZ equation'] Fix $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_0(\mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{Z}})$, and let $x = \{x_i\}_{i \in \mathbb{Z}} \sim \gamma$. Assume that, $\gamma$-almost surely,  
