Consider the following condition on the local times for some solution $(X,L)$ of (equation eq:asym_eq of the paper):
\begin{equation} 
\forall T \in [0,\infty), \quad \limsup_{M \to \infty} \left(\frac{q}{p}\right)^{-M} L_{(-M,-M+1)}(T) = 0 \text{ a.s.}
\end{equation}
Then, solutions to (equation eq:asym_eq of the paper) are pathwise unique for parameter $p$ and initial distribution $\gamma$, among all solutions whose associated local times satisfy (equation eq:aloc of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

