{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.503375+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_228db1512fbf534aa31fd47cc6dbe1aff42e91a2f33e3ad210c24ace7d4045b9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 63 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $A : \bbr^m \to \bbr^{(m \times d) \times d}$ be the linear operator given by
