{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.792548+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_231920e703d93e4338c9e88d893f7e83aea98c51957a3d894ae5bcd2b1b7de4d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo 4 of arXiv:2609.00186, 'Macroscopic scalar curvature bounds on surfaces'] Let $(\Sigma,g)$ be a closed oriented Riemannian surface of genus $k\geq2$, normalized such that $\area_g(\Sigma) = \area_{g_0}(\Sigma)$ where $g_0$ is a metric of constant curvature $-1$. Then, for every $r>0$,
