{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.764921+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2357df3297f1b4ee37ef16584aabddbf70be67d6ad05cf4d0ff6de1057392ca5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2607.09575, 'Probabilistic estimates for a system of\\noisy integrate-and-fire neurons'] Define the transformation $\Upsilon \in \mathcal{C}^{1,\,2}\left([0,\,T]\times\R\right)$ by
	\begin{equation*}
		(t,\,x) \mapsto \Upsilon_t(x) \coloneqq \int_0^x\frac{\diff{y}}{\sigma(t,y)}.
	\end{equation*}
	Fixing an arbitrary index $i \in \{1,\,\ldots,\,N\}$, then 
	\begin{equation*}
		\diff\Upsilon_t\left(X_t^i\right) = \hat{b}_t^i \ind_{\{\Upsilon_t\left(X_t^i\right) < 0\}}\diff{t} + \ind_{\{\Upsilon_t\left(X_t^i\right) < 0\}} \diff{B_t^i} + \diff\sum_{k \ge 1} \Upsilon_{\tau_k^i + \varsigma_k^i}(-\xi_k^i)\ind_{[0,t]}(\tau_k^i + \varsigma_k^i),
	\end{equation*}
	where $B^i$ is a Brownian motion and the (stochastic) drift $\hat{b}_t^{i}$ satisfies the growth condition
	\begin{equation}
		\nnorm{\hat{b}_t^{i}} \le C_{b,\sigma,\mathfrak{K}} \left(1 + \nnnorm{X_t^i} + \langle\nu_t^N,\nnnorm{\cdot}\rangle + \nnnorm{{F}_t^{N}}\right).
	\end{equation}
	Furthermore, the transformed process $\Upsilon_t\left(X_t^i\right)$ satisfies
	\begin{equation}
		\operatorname{sgn}\left(\Upsilon_t\left(X_t^i\right)\right) = \operatorname{sgn}\left(X_t^i\right) \quad \text{and} \quad \nnnorm{\Upsilon_t\left(X_t^i\right)} \le C\nnnorm{X_t^i}.
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.473847+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_235b12b246dc018d540753a3648b719452d5b3fb158aac0c7501d6dd485d66eb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2608.17562, '2608.17562'] Recall that $W_n = a_n^{-1}M_{n-1}$ and $Z_n = a_n^{-1}M_{n}$. Let $h : (0,\infty) \to \R$ be a function such that the derivative of its associated Stein solution $g_{h}'$ exists almost everywhere and satisfies
