with $\widehat{b}_i({\bf x})$ and $\widehat{a}_{ij}({\bf x})$   defined in  ((inf_mom_X_t_hat of the paper)).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.063464+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_23a0e3999b2b3600a0a7d418d7ba3ecd9aa67f0a00b973d4eb1c5b1d4be55b2e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2606.17452, 'Optional Stopping for Superhedging Supermartingales'] Let $\tau$ be a stopping time, $f \in Q$ and fix $T \in \mathbb{N}\cup \{\infty\}$.
The following holds at all $S \in \mathcal{S}$:
\begin{itemize}
\item[i)]
\begin{equation} \nonumber
\overline{\sigma}_{\tau(S)}({\bf 1}_{\{\tau < T\}}~f)(S) \leq {\bf 1}_{\{\tau < T\}}(S)~\overline{\sigma}_{\tau(S)}f(S).
\end{equation}
\item[ii)]
\begin{equation} \nonumber
\overline{\sigma}_{\tau(S)}({\bf 1}_{\{\tau = T\}}~f)(S) \leq {\bf 1}_{\{\tau = T\}}(S)~\overline{\sigma}_{\tau(S)}f(S).
\end{equation}
\end{itemize}
Moreover, the above inequalities are actually equalities if
$\overline{\sigma}_{\tau(S)} 0(S) =0$
(which, as we have mentioned, it is equivalent to the fact that $(L_{(S, \tau(S))})$ holds).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.399680+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_23a44470546bc21146fb58e2b4f80d032ec8c824ba72fa71a924df4ea6866d17","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p:decorrelation setting of arXiv:2605.22803, 'Persistence of asymptotic variance under transport:\\ from hyperfluctuation to stealthy hy'] Let $p\in[-d, 2]$. Suppose that $\Phi$ is a locally absolutely square-integrable invariant random measure, and suppose that $K$ is an invariant transport kernel. Assume that Condition~(c:condition square-integrable general with p of the paper) or Condition~(c:condition square-integrable Markov with p of the paper) is fulfilled. Further, assume that 
