{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:09.091686+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_23dcce3e84a5455bac5b66a88b03dd495b124d4ec449adbc7d104b02ebdd94a6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition the existence of the pairing sigma of arXiv:2411.11341, 'Ultra high order cumulants and quantitative CLT for polynomials in Random Matrices'] Let $r\geq 2$ and $m_1,\dots,m_r\in\mathbb{N}$. Let $m=\sum_{i=1}^r m_i$. Let $\gamma\in \mathcal{P}(m)$ be the partition whose blocks are
