{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:25:41.604783+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_23dd0d8b31123d69603d3cba439193e38030bd29e9b2b1028f8c34512ad3836c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm LDP-RWRS of arXiv:2608.13084, '\bf Branching random walk in random environment'] For any $\varepsilon\in (0, p\wedge (1-p))$, there exist positive constants $c_1(\varepsilon)$ and $c_2(\varepsilon)$ such that for any $x\in{\mathbb Z}^d$,
