{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.600995+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2409da11e8f4e918fca3b2b4101fc6fe1896ad11160471351735f9475fa2c2d6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 10 of arXiv:2609.01358, 'Regularized spectral expansion of a Rankin--Selberg period and moments'] Let $P$ be a standard parabolic of $G$ with Levi $M$ and let $\sigma\in\Pi(M)$. Let $\phi\in \mathcal{S}([\bar{G}])$ and $\lambda\in\a_{P,\C}^\ast/\a^\ast_{G,\C}$ be sufficiently dominant. Then the following sum
		\begin{equation*}
			F_{\sigma,\lambda}(g):=\sum_{\eta\in \B(\sigma)}
			\left(\int_{A_G M(F)\backslash M(\A)}\phi_P(mg)
			e^{\IP{\lambda-\rho_P,H_P(m)}}\overline{\eta}(m)\,dm\right)\eta,
		\end{equation*}
		converges absolutely and we have
		\begin{equation*}
			F_{\sigma,\lambda}(g)=\sum_{\varphi\in\B\left(\mathcal{I}(\sigma)\right)}
			\IP{\phi,\Eis(\varphi, \overline{\lambda})}_{[G]^1 }\varphi_{-\lambda}(g).
		\end{equation*}
		Moreover, the above sums do not depend on the choice of bases.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.827580+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_240f6980d6006fe1de6a9b1c9dadb2816a2065829d029e90c5a8238e43da5f48","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:chen of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] Let $x$ be a bounded-variation path and $s\le u\le t$. Then
