{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:25:49.860609+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24158e884c2bec58cbe4fe3375db3a0a28c4c2363d233209a994419a922f5f76","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2609.02019, '2609.02019'] Let the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{Thm-local-solution} hold. For every $n,R\ge1$ and every $H^s$-valued $\mathcal F_0$-measurable random variable $v_0$, the Cauchy problem \eqref{approximation scheme C} admits a unique global solution
