{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.097186+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_242563ea3df5f0dd3345c55235c726186aaf9a767596bc1f03d4f8d27df56f70","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm lemmZhou of arXiv:2412.08497, 'Time discretization of Quadratic Forward-Backward SDEs with singular drift'] Let $y_i(t) \in L^{2p}(\Omega,\mathbb{R}^m)$ be an $\mathbb{R}^m\text{-valued}$ adapted martingale for all $0\leq i \leq r$ and $p\geq 1$. Then by the martingale representation theorem, there is a square integrable process $z_i(t)$ such that, $y_i(t) = \beta_i + \int_0^t z_i(s)\mathrm{d}W_s$. For any increasing function $\eta:\{0,1,\cdots,N-1\}\rightarrow \{0,\cdots,r\}$, we define $\tilde{\eta}:\{0,\cdots,r\} \rightarrow \{-1,0,1,\cdots,N-1\}$ as $\tilde{\eta}=\sup\{j; \eta(j)\leq i\}$ with the convention $\sup\emptyset = -1.$ Then, there is a constant $C(p,m)$ independent of $r$ such that 
				\begin{align*}
					\mathbb{E}\Big[\Big( \sum_{j=0}^{N-1} \int_{t_j}^{t_{j+1}} \Big| \sum_{i=\eta(j)}^r z_i(s) \Big|^2\mathrm{d}s   \Big)^p\Big] \leq C(p,m)\mathbb{E}\Big[ \Big|\sum_{i=0}^r y_i(t_{\tilde{\eta}(i)+1}) - y_i(0)\Big|^{2p}  \Big] .
				\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:12:46.875814+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2426ad20c9c05d6b2fa8c40bc6ed69cefc66a877e507609c32ff6a84379e0ced","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_hz of arXiv:2608.08532, 'Constrained Maximum Weight Paths in Random Geometric Graphs'] The following properties hold:\\
\((a)\) If there exists~\(z_0 > 0\) such that~\(H(z)\) is strictly increasing for all~\(z > z_0,\) then for any~\(z > z_0\) we have
\begin{equation}
