{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.339245+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_243b260acb8c06a5737e81117a04134f34ce46ab994c34333b845073eafa1a82","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 18 of arXiv:2512.05687, '$L^p$-Boltzmann-Gibbs principle \\ via Littlewood-Paley-Stein inequality'] Assume $V''\ge -\a$ for some $\a>0$ and $\int_\R e^{-V(\eta)} d\eta<\infty$.
Let $p\in (0,\infty)$.  Then, there exist constants $c=c_{p,\a}, C=C_{p,\a}>0$, 
which are uniform in $\ell$ and $m$, such that 
\begin{align} 
c\big\{ \|f\|_{L^p(\bar\mu_{\ell,m})} + \|D_\phi f\|_{L^p(\bar\mu_{\ell,m})} \big\}
&\le \|(1-L_{0,\ell})^{1/2}f\|_{L^p(\bar\mu_{\ell,m})} \\
&\le 
C\big\{ \|f\|_{L^p(\bar\mu_{\ell,m})} + \|D_\phi f\|_{L^p(\bar\mu_{\ell,m})} \big\},
\notag
\end{align}
for $f \in W^{1,p}(\mathcal{Y}_{\ell,m}, \bar\mu_{\ell,m})$, where 
$D_\phi f= (\partial_{\phi(x)}f)_{x=-\ell+1}^{\ell-1]} \in \R^{2\ell-1}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.730506+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24416213fed974fd6c6b462c3248227c2f5574ab86623907f67c2453b5ad340e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:mu-doublePrime of arXiv:2412.09290, 'Asymptotics of Harish-Chandra transform and infinitesimal freeness'] Let $\Psi, \Phi, \mathrm{T}$ be infinitely differentiable functions at $0$ and
