{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.689174+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24ca3adf7e65de638b8ca5030787fd7630c8efb2e23f0a70dacbe13fb120a12b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2605.17328, 'Transportation cost inequalities for mean reflection SPDEs with white noise'] {\rm
The probability measure $\mu$ is said to satisfy the transportation cost inequality $T_p(C)$ on $(E,d)$ if there exists a constant $C>0$ such that, for any probability measure $\nu$ on $\mathcal{M}(E)$,}
