{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.545592+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24d8250e025b867ecb36525cdb0aa13cf6792ad5d4546c3edc6429db2c5d94f5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:cle-gf-to-bubble of arXiv:2603.28161, 'Boundary four-point connectivities of conformal loop ensembles'] Let ${\frak C}$ be the same constant as in Proposition~(prop:touching-equals-bubble of the paper). Then for any $n\ge2$, we have
\begin{equation}
G^\mathrm{Bub}_{x_1}(x_2,...,x_n)dx_1dx_2...dx_n={\frak C}\mathbbm{E}\left[\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{T}(\Gamma)}\prod_{i=1}^n\nu_{\ell\cap\mathbbm{R}}(dx_i)\right].
\end{equation}
When $n=2$, $G^\mathrm{Bub}_{x_1}(x_2)={\frak C}H_{\mathbbm{H}}(x_1,x_2)^h$ (we choose the constant of $H_{\mathbbm{H}}(x_1,x_2)$ such that the coefficient is ${\frak C}$). In particular, for the $\CLE_\kappa$ boundary Green's functions defined in~(equation eq:four-type-gf of the paper), we have
\begin{align}
G^{(1234)}(x_1,x_2,x_3,x_4)&= {\frak C}G^\mathrm{Bub}_{x_1}(x_2,x_3,x_4)\in(0,\infty),\\
G^{(12)(34)}(x_1,x_2,x_3,x_4)&={\frak C}\int H_{\mathcal{U}(\gamma)}(x_3,x_4)^h\mu_{x_1,x_2}^\mathrm{Bub}(d\gamma)\in(0,\infty)
\end{align}
where $\mu_{x_1,x_2}^\mathrm{Bub}$ is defined in~(equation eq:bubble-two-pinned of the paper).
Recall that $\mathcal{U}(A)$ denotes the unbounded connected component of $\mathbbm{H}\setminus A$ for a compact subset $A\subset\ol\mathbbm{H}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.518280+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24dbd627ed01909c0fb89a17edf8eb4db50e9a6e201e035b32a0f8e64308abb4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:erdos_renyi_connectivity of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{prop:erdos_renyi_connectivity}
