{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.384716+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24fdbbe6a2d2ad043864d94eabbc582157af9be2c66217a32ba76ae4f6beca7d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:local_hajek_intro of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] Define
\begin{equation}

    \widehat{\mathsf{N}}_G^{\rho \to v}(x) \coloneqq \mathsf{N}_G^{\rho \to v}(x) - \mathsf{d}_\rho p^{\mathsf{e}-1} n^{\mathsf{v}-2} \mathsf{deg}_v(x).
\end{equation}
Then, for all $\zeta \in (0, \frac{3}{4})$, there is some $c > 0$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P} \mleft[
        \mleft|
            \widehat{\mathsf{N}}_G^{\rho \to v}(X) - \mathbb{E} \mleft[ \widehat{\mathsf{N}}_G^{\rho \to v}(X) \mright]
        \mright| > n^{\mathsf{v} - 1.75 + \zeta}
    \mright] \leq \Exp{- c n^{\frac{4}{3} \zeta}}.
\end{equation}
In particular, for all $\xi > 0$ we have
\begin{equation}
    \operatorname{Var} \mleft[
        \widehat{\mathsf{N}}_G^{\rho \to v}(x)
    \mright] \lesssim n^{2\mathsf{v} - 3.5 + \xi}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.406047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2500aab84ad920a0328d476bb9778a11f4b6c9f50a0cf31dc62bd31a445792bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2604.06516, 'From stochastic individual-based models to free-boundary Hamilton-Jacobi equations'] For any $t>0$ and for any closed $A\subset\mathbb{D}[0,t]$, 
