{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.546121+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2530efd6025744a7bc11a5875610d62ce5f8982704a44dca0c53be116603d509","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:pde-u-v of arXiv:2603.28161, 'Boundary four-point connectivities of conformal loop ensembles'] Let $u=\frac{1}{2}(y_1+y_2)$ and $v=\frac{1}{2}(y_2-y_1)$. Then for $j=1,2$, $F^{(j)}(y_1,y_2,x_1,x_2,x_3)$ satisfies the following pair of second-order PDEs:
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
