{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.346292+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_253ed7d49b993cbc840131cdb5039390bb08e8d4ed187966e26eb2e370434af8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2411.05534, 'Inverse problems for stochastic partial differential equations'] A mild solution $X(\cdot)$  is a strong solution  to (eqSEE of the paper) if the following three conditions hold for all $x \in H$ and $0 \leq s \leq t \leq T$, a.s.,  
