{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.892073+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2542c08384fefdfa04909b7c188c4ffc3d92999a1607ad22853d8a308eccf761","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor Gint2 of arXiv:2510.23430, 'On the Martin boundary for discrete TASEP'] Let $\lambda$ be a partition and $k$ be an integer such that $\lambda_1\leq k$. Let $\mathcal C$ be a positively-oriented simple complex contour encircling both $0$ and $-\mathfrak b$. Then
