{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.712869+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_256932c5301b24660ffe02cead6313d1989da856c552e53df4b6582de916050a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 17 (Deterministic risk, fully overdamped regime) of arXiv:2609.02728, 'Momentum in large-batch training: Polyak enlarges the critical batch size, Nesterov improv'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:diagonal-covariance} and~\ref{ass:power-law}, in the fully overdamped regime $\eta\lesssim (1-\rho)^2$, we have:
