{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.443140+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_25f5695ab6e8b95f3fe134b547251a40425aad162aa050a026464ff2ee7c651c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:XYheightfunction of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] Given a finite subset $\Lambda \subseteq \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^2$, an integer $n \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}^*$, and a collection of conductances $\left( J_{xy,k} \right)_{xy \in E(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^2), 1 \leq k \leq n} \in [0, \infty)^{E(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^2) \times \{1 , \ldots, n \}}$, we define the XY height function to be the probability distribution on the set $\Omega_\Lambda^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}}$ given by the identity
\begin{equation*}
    \mu_{\Lambda , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}} (\left\{ \varphi \right\}) := \frac{1}{Z_{\Lambda,J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}} \prod_{x \sim y} \prod_{1 \leq k \leq n}  I_{\left(\varphi(x) - \varphi(y)\right)} \left( J_{xy,k} \right) .
\end{equation*}
We denote by $\mathrm{Var}_{\Lambda , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}$ the variance with respect to the measure $\mu_{\Lambda , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}$ and write $\mathrm{Var}_{L , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}$ when $\Lambda = \Lambda_L$.","status":"unverified"}

