{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:31.001461+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_26940886f1b780ca39e6d39e95dbc19082b3260f9cdd859b744084631d48d393","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 52 (Triangular canonical extraction) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] Run the stages in the lexicographic order
\begin{equation}
 n\to\mathcal U,\qquad
 J_1\to\infty,\quad J_2\to\infty,\quad\ldots,\quad J_Q\to\infty,

\end{equation}
finishing weight $s$ before starting $s+1$.  Then at every finite internal extraction
level
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb U_s^{-1}M_s^{[J]}\subset\mathscr A_s,

\end{equation}
and at the end of stage $s$
\begin{equation}
 A_{a,s}=y_{a,s},\qquad r_{a,s}=g_{a,s}.

\end{equation}
Quantitatively,
\begin{equation}
 0\le\widehat N_s\le QR^2\Id,\qquad
 \lambda_{\max}(\widehat E_s)\ge\frac{\widehat{\mathfrak H}_s}{d},

\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \sum_a\norm{P_{V_s^\triangle}r_{a,s}}^2
 \ge
 \frac{\widehat{\mathfrak H}_s}{dQR^2}.

\end{equation}
Thus the scale-invariant per-weight capture constant is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\kappa_{Q,d}^\triangle=\frac1{dQ}}.

\end{equation}
With threshold
