{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.315584+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2741d30149ec59228b7586d9462f9935cfacecd9d475a93161ad23300c4e7b85","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:c1 of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] There exist constants $0<b_1=b_1(\lambda), b_2=b_2(\lambda)<\infty$ such that 
