{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.821261+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2745e982ec9c89df35ae503aa14c13d3525c27cc1045787f51fa04acc543deda","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 (Interior H\"older continuity) of arXiv:2604.10142, 'H\MakeLowercase{arnack inequality for} $p$\MakeLowercase{-harmonic functions: \\ improved '] There exist   $C,\gamma>0$, such that for any $p$-harmonic function $u$ on $\overline B_{1}(0)$  and every $0<\delta<1$, we have 
