{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.573728+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_27466c526caec69b0269fec315d9f2f3428f1a14a0bd70668b9fb6cf8d07a583","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 32 (Entropic bound) of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$. There exists $C>0$ such that the following holds. For every $\Lambda\subset \mathbb Z^d$ finite containing $0$, every event $\mathcal A$ measurable with respect to $\mathcal C_e(0)$, and every $\beta_c/2\leq \beta'<\beta\leq \beta_c$, 
