{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.304643+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2756e0ba7c1ae1b22698034336dfa6cbf5ae5120f367b23a1592e4b45e567375","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:entangled of arXiv:2607.18070, 'The Brownian loop-catcher'] For $r\ge1$ and an ordered tuple of directed paths $\omega_i:a_i\to b_i$, $1\le i\le r$, put
\begin{equation}
 H_i=P(\omega_i),\qquad C_0=\varnothing,\qquad
 P_i=\Phi_{C_{i-1}}(H_i),\qquad
 C_i=C_{i-1}\cup\operatorname{supp}(P_i).
\end{equation}
Let $\gamma_i$ be the directed path corresponding to the record $P_i$ (equipped with the time parametrization).  We call $(\gamma_1,\ldots,\gamma_r)$
the entangled multipath loop-erasure of $(\omega_1,\ldots,\omega_r)$, whose range is $C_r$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.027710+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_275a1a23e351059b39526f3b7b8218ff1a7356a7a85dc7852264f40afd919499","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:weak-recovery-S-sgd of arXiv:2609.03858, 'High-Dimensional Learning Dynamics of \\ Attention-Indexed Models'] Consider (equation eq:S-sgd of the paper) with
$\mathcal K=\{1\}$, where $S_1$ is the trainable student and $S_2$ is a fixed teacher. Suppose the
conditions of Theorem (theo:S-sgd-dynamics of the paper) and Assumption (assum:S-initialization of the paper) hold.

\begin{itemize}
\item[1.]If, at initialization,
\begin{equation}
a_+g_+(0)\neq0
\qquad\text{or}\qquad
a_-g_-(0)\neq0,

\end{equation}
then there exist constants
$c>0$ and $0<T_-<T_+<\infty$, independent of $d$, such that
\begin{equation}
\lim_{d\to\infty}\mathbb P\left(\left\lfloor\frac{T_-d}{\alpha_d}\right\rfloor<N_{\mathrm{wr},S}^{(d)}(c)
\le\left\lceil\frac{T_+d}{\alpha_d}\right\rceil\right)
=1.

\end{equation}
In particular, choosing the largest learning-rate scaling $\alpha_d=\Theta\left(\frac1{d\log d}\right)$ covered by Theorem (theo:S-sgd-dynamics of the paper) gives the weak recovery sample complexity
\begin{equation}
N_{\mathrm{wr},S}^{(d)}(c)=\Theta_{\mathbb P}(d^2\log d).
\end{equation}

\item[2.] Let the uninformative manifold be $\mathcal U:=\left\{(t,\Psi,\Omega):t_1=0,\Psi_{12}=0,\Omega_{12}=0\right\}$.
Suppose that
\begin{equation}
[\nabla_\Omega\Phi(\Psi,\Omega)]_{12}=[\nabla_\Psi\Phi(\Psi,\Omega)]_{12}=0
\qquad
\text{for every state in }\mathcal U.

\end{equation}
Then for every fixed $T<\infty$ and every $\epsilon>0$,
\begin{equation}
\lim_{d\to\infty}\mathbb P\left(\sup_{t\in[0,T]}
\max\left(|p_{\Psi,12}^{(d)}(t)|,|p_{\Omega,12}^{(d)}(t)|\right)>\epsilon\right)=0.

\end{equation}
In particular, for any learning-rates covered by
Theorem (theo:S-sgd-dynamics of the paper), $S$-SGD cannot achieve weak
recovery within $\mathcal O(d^2\log d)$ samples.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.874603+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_275bf060efcf535c8aa0f914d44b221b67e6c01e7e32f485ed544808affb270e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro cor:momentstoeps of arXiv:2605.07920, 'Primitive Sequences for Probability Measures on Compact Intervals'] We have
