{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.776077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_275fe355befae35fd1174c61611f8cd1f6fe4cb7e969ded06f46878476f822a7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:mvsde-attractor of arXiv:2411.01364, 'Global Dynamics of Granular Media Equations via Stochastic Order'] Suppose Assumption (asp:potential of the paper) holds.
Let $P_t^*:\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)\to\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$ be the semigroup of the McKean-Vlasov SDE (equation eq:mvsystem of the paper). Then for any $t>0$, $P_t^*$ is a compact map.
