{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.028213+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2761461ce72726a9161cc833a308d8e3168a2025b2c30d22287b563a30abf85f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma untied-one-step-estimates of arXiv:2609.03858, 'High-Dimensional Learning Dynamics of \\ Attention-Indexed Models'] Under the conditions of Theorem (theo:untied-SGD of the paper), let \(J\) be a
stopping time satisfying (equation eq:stopping-time of the paper). Set $g^{(n)}:=\nabla_{m_{\mathcal K}}\Phi\left(m^{(n)},q^{(1,n)},q^{(2,n)}\right)$ and $D^{(n)}:=\operatorname{diag}\left(t_k^{A,(n)}+t_k^{B,(n)}
\right)_{k\in\mathcal K}$, and $\vartheta^{(n)}:=\left(
t^{A,(n)},t^{B,(n)},q^{(1,n)},q^{(2,n)}\right)$.
Then, uniformly on \(\{n<J\}\), 
