{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.455714+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2762bece368159c9f2c98a95ff37355193b95fefae976f37f81949cb7567571d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 8 (Compact critical bubbles) of arXiv:2609.02523, '\bf Strong Ill-Posedness in critical and subcritical regimes for the Hunter--Saxton equati'] There exist two constants $c>0$ and $C>0$ and a family $(\varphi_\varepsilon)_{0<\varepsilon<1}$ of functions in $C_c^\infty(\R)$ with the properties
