{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.124377+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_27d8391175613896f1a3f3d9750903d7cb54f04a80104168754aa0eafe40feab","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:cheegerhyp of arXiv:2510.00748, '\bf On irreducible central limit theorems'] Let ${\ensuremath{\mathcal G}}  =(V,{\ensuremath{\mathcal E}} ,w)$ be a weighted hypergraph as above. Then, for all $k=2,\ldots,N$,
    \begin{equation}
