{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:38:13.632212+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_280d0c2859a6d2574f3ac87484d5e0fecb792c51b702c6a77fbca05f292da9a4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 21 of arXiv:2609.00598, 'Supercritical mean--field limit for magnetized Hamiltonian dynamics'] Suppose that $(X_{N}^{0},\Xi_{N}^{0})\in \mathbb{T}^{2N}\times \mathbb{R}^{2N}$, 
