{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:40:59.378122+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_285fd16a4e555ad0944006671ac1d4ad8d575a1b43c708c63f555a55a3046cd7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2609.03962, '$L^p$ isomorphisms for the fractional Laplacian on $\mathbb{R}^n$ and their application'] Let $s\in(0,2)$, $p\in(1,\infty)$, $m:=[s]$, and set the split (critical)
    index
    \[
      k:=
      \begin{cases}
        s-\dfrac{n}{p}, & s-\dfrac{n}{p}\in\{0,1,\dots,m\},\\[1.0ex]
        -1, & \text{otherwise.}
      \end{cases}
    \]
    Then the weighted fractional Sobolev spaces is 
    \[
    \begin{aligned}
      \Lambda^{s,p}(\R^n):=\Big\{\,u\in L^1_{\mathrm{loc}}(\R^n):\
        & \rho^{\,|\lambda|-s}\,\lg^{-1}\,D^\lambda u\in L^p,\quad 0\le|\lambda|\le k;\\
        & \rho^{\,|\lambda|-s}\,D^\lambda u\in L^p,\quad k+1\le|\lambda|\le m;\\
        & \flap u\in L^p\,\Big\},
    \end{aligned}
    \]
    normed by the sum of the $L^p$-norms of all components, with seminorm
    $|u|_{\Lambda^{s,p}}:=\|\flap u\|_{L^p}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.981576+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2860a88f8c861ec1c1934a4fad23582560439920e9668b78cfe662ec9e6da28c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:stationary-toppling of arXiv:2604.13968, 'Divisible sandpiles via random walks in random scenery'] Let $(G,\rho,\sigma)$ be a stationary random rooted network with $\mathbb{E}[|\sigma(\rho)|/\deg(\rho)] < \infty$. Under parallel toppling, for each $k \geq 0$:
		\begin{itemize}
			\item[\em (a)] The random rooted network $(G,\rho,\sigma_k,u_k)$ is stationary.
