{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.191523+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2916eaf6f060e08a91e0c9f9499ea5d31412f9a02c1bfcbd8e728dfcaac2f1f5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2606.31455, 'Discrete time-multidimensional renewal theory and applications'] Let $a,b:\mathbb{N}^d\to\mathbb{R}$. Their (multi-time) convolution product $c=a*b$ is defined by

\begin{equation}
[a*b](k)
:=\sum_{\ell+\ell'=k} a(\ell)\,b(\ell')
=\sum_{\ell\le_d k} a(\ell)\,b(k-\ell),
\qquad k\in\mathbb{N}^d,
\end{equation}

where $\le_d$ denotes componentwise inequality.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:11:57.336794+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2918001bc4e81bfe8173a2f6519a461c5e0c43411a2ce87a390af8c075de868c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 (Aldous' criterion, \cite{ref7}) of arXiv:2607.23640, '{\sl Non-equilibrium fluctuations of a two-species exclusion process with slow boundary }'] A sequence of real-valued processes $ \left\{X_t^n: 0\le t\le T\right\}_{n\in \mathbb{N}} $
	is tight in \(\mathcal D([0,T];\mathbb R)\) if the following two conditions hold:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item[(i)] $ \lim_{M\to\infty}
		\limsup_{n\to\infty}
		\mathbb P_{\mu^n}^n
		\left(
		\sup_{0\le t\le T}|X_t^n|>M
		\right)
		=0 $.

		\item[(ii)]
		For every \(\varepsilon>0\),
		\[
		\lim_{\delta\to 0}
		\limsup_{n\to\infty}
		\sup_{0<\lambda\le\delta}
		\sup_{\tau\in\mathcal T_T}
		\mathbb P_{\mu^n}^n
		\left(
		|X_{\tau+\lambda}^n-X_\tau^n|>\varepsilon
		\right)
		=0,
		\]
		where \(\mathcal T_T\) denotes the family of stopping times bounded by \(T\).
	\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.511788+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_291c83ccac5bca3da9a50be25f16131e94b77393abccba3f189e076c256221e5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Z-signchanges of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] Let $f$ be a continuous real-valued function on an
interval $(a,b)$. We denote by 
\begin{equation}
Z(f;(a,b))  
\end{equation}
the maximal integer $m\geq 0$ for which there exist points 
\begin{equation}
a<x_{1}<\cdots <x_{m+1}<b  
\end{equation}
such that 
\begin{equation}
f(x_{i})f(x_{i+1})<0,\qquad i=1,\dots ,m.  
\end{equation}
Thus $Z(f;(a,b))$ is the number of strict sign changes of $f$ on $(a,b)$.
Whenever the interval is $(0,\tfrac{1}{2})$ we write simply 
\begin{equation}
Z(f)=Z\!\left( f;\left( 0,\tfrac{1}{2}\right) \right) .  
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.772583+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2921f454c512f7387b4f641cc000699f50127432603f4c89b4681cd9b712f421","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary Application of Ito formula of arXiv:2607.29548, 'Generalized reflected BSDEs with irregular obstacles driven by RCLL increasing processes o'] Let $\left(Y_t\right)_{t \leq T}$ be a one-dimensional adapted process with regulated paths of the form (equation form of the process for Ito of the paper). Then, for every $t \in [0,T]$, we have
		\begin{equation*}
			\begin{split}
				\mathcal{E}(\beta A)_{t} \left| Y_t \right|^2&=  \left| Y_0 \right|^2+ \int_{0}^{t} \dfrac{\beta}{1+\beta \Delta_- A_s} \mathcal{E}(\beta A)_{s} \left| Y_{s-} \right|^2 dA_s+2\int_{0}^{t}  \mathcal{E}(\beta A)_{s} Y_{s-} dY^{\ast}_s+\int_{0}^{t} \mathcal{E}(\beta A)_{s} d \left[Y^{\ast}\right]^c_s\\
				&\quad +\sum_{0 < s \leq t} \mathcal{E}(\beta A)_{s} \left| \Delta_{-} Y_{s} \right|^2+\sum_{0 \leq s < t} \mathcal{E}(\beta A)_{s} \left(\left| \Delta_{+} Y_{s}\right|^2+2Y_{s}\Delta_{+} Y_s \right).
			\end{split}
		\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.247050+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_29227d3e0424dc7fa9f890dd26797ffacb810b6cc069baf7a456625e0a7c6038","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro:asymCell of arXiv:2604.23981, 'Accelerating sampling via asymptotic relaxation enhancing flows'] For $v_n=\nabla^{\perp}\Psi_n$, we have 
