{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.198358+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2936a77d9698a119db2a94e28afbe5705299c13ed91b3677261d0eeaeb445556","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:growth-gadget of arXiv:2509.04333, 'The limiting law of the Discrete Gaussian level lines'] The following holds uniformly over all possible $Q$ as above. Let $\mathfrak{L}_n$ be the (unique) $(H+1-n)$ level line induced by $\xi$. Then, with $\pi^\xi_Q$-probability $1 - e^{-c\log L}$, $\mathfrak{L}_n$ lies below the point $X= (0, Y + \sigma(\log L)^a + \log L)$, where
		\begin{align}
			&Y = -\frac{N_n^{1/3}(\log L)^{2a}}{8(\tau_\beta(\theta) + \tau_\beta''(\theta))\cos(\theta)^3}\,,\\
			&\sigma^2 = \frac{N_n^{2/3}(\log L)^a}{4(\tau_\beta(\theta) + \tau_\beta''(\theta))\cos(\theta)^3}\,.\nonumber
		\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:25.847903+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2936dc8d2241316317f4949d6eff769731814c2566eb75a3c200ae239cc52cae","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 13 of arXiv:2608.29486, 'Cabled braids and their crossing matrices'] An $n \times n$ matrix $M$ is said to {\it admit a cable-block decomposition} if $M$ is in the form of $m \times m$ blocks ($1<m<n$) as 
\begin{align*}
M=\begin{bmatrix}
A_{11} & A_{12} & \dots & A_{1m} \\
A_{21} & A_{22} & \dots & A_{2m} \\
\vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\
A_{m1} & A_{m2} & \dots & A_{mm} 
\end{bmatrix}
\end{align*}
such that the block $A_{ii}$ is a square matrix for each $i \in \{ 1, 2, \dots , m \}$ and all the entries in $A_{i j}$ are equal for each pair $i \neq j \in \{ 1, 2, \dots , m \}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.500749+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_293b9e1e3e816099c71995e10c5e29e4e52a884c95ac0afdf3b4b18aeb2bf5e8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition D:gamma of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] Let $X:\mathbb{Z}^2_\ge \to \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}\cup \{\infty\}$ be a field of independent random variables distributed as follows.
Take real parameters $\alpha$ and $\{\gamma_i\}_{i\in\mathbb{Z}}$.

For any $i\in \mathbb{Z}$, take $X(i,i)\sim \operatorname{Gamma}^{-1}(\alpha+\gamma_i)$ if $\alpha+\gamma_i>0$, and $X(i,i)=\infty$ otherwise.

For any $i > j \in \mathbb{Z}$, take $X(i,j)\sim \operatorname{Gamma}^{-1}(\gamma_i+\gamma_j)$ if $\gamma_i+\gamma_j>0$, and $X(i,j)=\infty$ otherwise. 
We extend the weights $X$ to all of $\mathbb{Z}^2$ by the symmetry condition $X(i,j)=X(j,i)$ for all $i,j$.

For any $u,v\in \mathbb{Z}^2$ with $u \le v$, define the \emph{partition function}
\[
Z_X(u;v)=\sum_{\pi}\prod_{(i,j)\in \pi}X(i,j),
\]
where the sum is over all up-right paths $\pi$ from $u$ to $v$, subject to the following condition:
\begin{equation}

\text{for any $(i,i)\in\pi$, necessarily $(i-1,i)\notin\pi$.}
\end{equation}
In words, paths may cross the diagonal at most once, moving from below the diagonal to above it.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.498968+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_293c811071723ff8df91d928ce9b6dda18c0899fea722ecc69556210feb7fd45","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2605.29608, '2605.29608'] Let $(Y_k)_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^+}$ be the Wolff dynamics with invariant measure $\mu_N$. 
	For any $\hat{J}\in[0,+\infty)$, the log-Sobolev inequality
	\begin{align} 
		E_{\mu_{N}}[f^{2}\log f^{2}]-E_{\mu_{N}}[f^{2}]\log E_{\mu_{N}}[f^{2}]\leq&e^{2\hat{J}}(e^{4\hat{J}}+1)\big(\frac{1}{2}+\hat{J}e^{\frac{e^{2\hat{J}}-1}{2}}\big)N	\mathcal{E}^{\text{W}}_{\mu_{N}}(f),
	\end{align}
	holds for all functions $f:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}$, where
	\begin{align*}	
		\mathcal{E}^{\text{W}}_{\mu_{N}}(f):=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{\sigma,\eta\in\Omega}[f(\sigma)-f(\eta)]^{2}P_{\text{W}}(\eta,\sigma)\mu_{N}(\eta).
	\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.124562+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_293e3f27e0f9fd9de86d67e338e3b134b51a14844f0814deec2308a4193445eb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma def:irreducibility2 of arXiv:2510.00748, '\bf On irreducible central limit theorems'] Let the above assumptions and conventions prevail. Then, the sequence $\{Z_n\}$ is reducible in the sense of Definition (def:irreducibility of the paper) if and only if there exist partitions $\{B_1,\ldots,B_{m_n}\} = \{B^{(n)}_1,\ldots,B^{(n)}_{m_n}\}$ of the vertex sets $V_n$, such that, as $n \to \infty$,
    \begin{enumerate}[label={\rm (\roman*)}]
    \item  $m_n\to \infty$;
    \item  $\sum_{i=1}^{m_n} w_n( {\ensuremath{\mathcal E}} (B_i,B_i)) \sim w_n(\mathcal{E}_n)$;
    \item  $\max_{i=1,...,m_n} w_n( {\ensuremath{\mathcal E}} (B_i,B_i)) = o\big( w_n(\mathcal{E}_n)\big)$.  
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.658618+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2944dbd4cc755856c4db4b9cd7184005ff4f537d132ed09ad9b9fa2539c85a34","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem Lemma: Dimension bound under proper factor condition of arXiv:2605.16921, '${\ASL_n}(\mathbb Z)$ invariant random subsets of $\mathbb Z^n$'] Let $X$ be an ergodic $\mathbb{Z}^{d'}$-system, $f \in L^\infty(X)$, and $\delta > 0$. Let $D \geq 0$ and let $(N_n)_{n \geq 0}$ be nilfactors of $X$, each of dimension at most $D$, satisfying:
    \begin{equation}
        \|\mathbb{E}[f \mid N_n] - \mathbb{E}[f \mid N_n']\|_2 > \delta
    \end{equation}
    for every $n \geq 0$ and every strict nilfactor $N_n' \to N_n$ (i.e.\ of dimension strictly smaller than $\dim N_n$). Then for every finite $I \subset \mathbb{N}$, the joining of $\{N_n\}_{n \in I}$ inside $X$ is a nilsystem of dimension at most $D \|f\|_2^2 \delta^{-2}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.725755+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_29450bc7d0b20f3976da48c5b89ad8beb77a0a04f153fc40660ba2e62c4a42d6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] There exists a constant $C_0>0$ such that 
    \begin{equation}
        \int_0^T\int_0^1 \frac{|\nabla\rho_t(x)|^2}{\sigma(\rho_t(x))}\;dx\;dt\leq C_0\{I_{[0,T]}(\rho)+1\}
    \end{equation}
    for any path $u\in  {\mathcal{D}}_{\mathcal{E}}([0,T],{\mathcalboondox M}_{ac})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

