{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.908172+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2955effa1019e7c4c2e66d5b7a08b29213315078e6e45b1e30ba05d8f6cf4d08","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop energy-est of arXiv:2411.06861, 'Quenched invariance principle for random walks in random environments admitting a cycle de'] Let $B$ be a finite subset of $\mathbb{Z}^d$. 
