{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.317554+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_295cb6521a670beb5777354d96e597235deb522201bdaa87721a53a01be2f06b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem arm_exponents of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] For every $\zeta>0$, $j\geq 1$, there exists $\rho_{\zeta,j}>0$ big enough such that
