{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.696062+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_29dfee7e806b9377fd54ed8a51eab1755c273a302aec97ecd96fd7d1b710403f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:limit_function_upper_bound of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] Let $\Gamma$ be a connected typical diagram. Let   $t=\sum_{i=1}^s t_i$,
   the following upper bounds for limiting diagram functions  hold  for some constant $C>0$.
