{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.256501+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a031a26d7cd7b906f4f3185863d813aaa4afd00dcd9ec3e1ebd63c581b4e4d2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 50 ({\cite[Lemma 3.1) of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] {Cr18}}]
Let $A$ be a non-empty open subset of $F$. 
For any measurable $f:F\to\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}$, it holds that
\begin{equation*}
    G_A f(y)=\int_F g_A(y,z)f(z)\mu(dz), \quad\forall y\in F,
\end{equation*}
where
\begin{equation*}
    g_A(y,z):=\frac{R(y,A)+R(z,A)-R_A(y,z)}{2},
\end{equation*}
with
\begin{equation*}
    R_A(y,z):= \sup\{\calE(f,f)^{-1} : f \in \calF, f(y)=1, f(z)=0, f|_{A}\;\;\rm{constant} \}
\end{equation*}
being the resistance between $y$ and $z$ in the network with $A$  `fused'. 
Note that the function $g_A$ satisfies $0 \le g_A(y,z)=g_A(z,y) \le g_A(y,y) = R(y,A)$ and
\begin{equation}
    |g_A(y,z)-g_A(y,w)|\leq R(w,z), \quad \forall y, z, w \in F.
\end{equation}
Furthermore, $g_{x}$ is given by
\begin{equation*}
    g_{x}(y,z):=\frac{R(x,y)+R(x,z)-R(y,z)}{2}.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

