{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.844542+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ad45c00f956480b3cc2d51fc45ba8f745ab7fe30ddf6bac0a4e855fb59ba8e8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm: Taylor Lipschitz of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] For $m\ge 0$ and $\tau_0\in{\mathcal T}$, let $H_{z_1z_2}$ be the expression defined in (equation Eq: def H of the paper). In addition let $\mathbb X:{\mathcal F}^{\le m}\to\mathbb{R}$ be a multiplicative functional. Then
