{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.573948+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ae5cd0f86bee561b360db9bdf1534855a31468bf5b4d7f1a5c51d56a19aaa21","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 35 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d = 6$. There exist $K>0$ and $k_0 \geq 1$ such that the following holds. 
