{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.499691+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ae71c638d5af9360e1e590c51af2e01199e78e0f12ce9d1daf239c12bfcf2d1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2608.05185, '\large\bf ON THE HEAT FLOW CONJECTURE FOR RANDOM MATRICES'] For \(z=x+\mathrm{i}y\), write
\(\dd A(z)=\dd x\,\dd y\) for planar Lebesgue measure.
We use the notation
\[
 \D=\{z\in\C:|z|<1\},
 \qquad
 \mathscr{D}(z,r)=\{w\in\C:|w-z|<r\}
 \quad (z\in\C,\ r>0).
\]
For \(S>0\) and \(c\in\C\) with \(\left|c\right|<S\), define
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr{E}_{S,c}
 \overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}
 \left\{\sqrt{S}\,u+\frac{c}{\sqrt{S}}\overline{u}:
                 u\in\C,\ \left|u\right|\leq1\right\},
\end{equation}
If \(c=\left|c\right|\mathrm{e}^{2\mathrm{i}\theta}\), this ellipse has
semiaxes \(\sqrt{S}\pm\left|c\right|/\sqrt{S}\) and is rotated through
\(\theta\).  Let \(\mu_{S,c}\) be its normalised planar area measure.
Equivalently,
\begin{equation}
 \dd\mu_{S,c}(z)
 =\frac{S}{\pi(S^2-\left|c\right|^2)}
 \mathbf{1}_{\mathscr{E}_{S,c}}(z)\dd A(z).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.284196+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ae7baa3654e491e9b3a311b9c2170727f86b375ca99247cd6ab01194bf5768a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 11 (Constructive endpoint-resolution bounds) of arXiv:2608.21496, '2608.21496'] Let $d=\lfloor(m-1)/2\rfloor$, let $\xi_{d+1}$ be the largest zero on $[0,1]$ of the shifted Legendre polynomial of degree $d+1$, and put
\begin{equation}
A_{m,L}=\min\left\{\frac1{m+1},\frac{L}{m(m+1)}\right\},\quad
D_{m,N}=\prod_{j=1}^m\frac{N-j}{N+j}.

\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
A_{m,L}D_{m,N}&\le\Delta^{\uparrow,L}_{m,N},\\
\Delta^{\uparrow,L}_{m,N}
&\le\min\left\{B_{m,N},
L\left(1-\xi_{d+1}+\frac1{N+1}\right),1\right\}.
\end{aligned}

\end{equation}
If $L$ is fixed and $m^2/N\to\tau\in(0,\infty)$, then
\begin{equation}
e^{-\tau}\le\liminf\frac{m^2\Delta^{\uparrow,L}_{m,N}}L
\le\limsup\frac{m^2\Delta^{\uparrow,L}_{m,N}}L
\le j_{0,1}^2+\tau,

\end{equation}
where $j_{0,1}\simeq2.4048$ is the first positive zero of $J_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.352205+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ae9a94c251f6a93c802c2eb4c26c3ab3bfa53c1c43cfd2940d50bbadb8da69f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 9 of arXiv:2606.17472, '2606.17472'] Let $n\ge 2$ and $a_1<\cdots <a_n$. Then the following statements hold:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item If $h(x)=0$ for $x<0$, then
