{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:49:21.124465+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b024fff85c3a2525a5c888c6e3817ed98af8e85fa3dcc5d14d9ef8740bfe674","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2608.26662, 'Boundary–Moment Universality and Curvature Corrections in Random Geometric Graphs on Riema'] There are $C<\infty$ and $r_0>0$ such that, for
