{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.596682+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b0736642e8dc554b544dd12563b2591e8d2740ea2c8315a95656d47dc8ea234","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] Let $\alpha$ be a probability measure on $(\X,\calX)$. A process $(J_n,S_n)_{n\geq0}$ with values in $\X\times\N^d$ is a discrete multi-time Markov renewal chain with initial law $\alpha$ and semi-Markov kernel $q$ if $J_0$ has law $\alpha$, $S_0=\zerod$, and

