{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.940837+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b15ba940d15d404f3fd14415fd8cb108cabf3696928d52145fae644b38a50f7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LemmaFiniteOccurrenceTimes of arXiv:2606.13615, 'Data-Driven Subsampling Rates for Diffusion Parameter Estimation of SDEs'] Suppose that Assumption~(Assumptions of the paper) holds and that (equation eqGenSDEIntro of the paper) admits an invariant measure $\mu$. Let $\mathbf{X}_0 \sim \mu$ be independent of $\mathbf{W}$, let $\mathbf{X} = (\mathbf{X}_t)_{t \geq 0}$ be the corresponding solution process to (equation eqGenSDEIntro of the paper) with $d$-th component $X = (X_t)_{t \geq 0}$, and assume that the ergodicity condition (equation eqErgoCond of the paper) is fulfilled. Then there exists a $\tilde{\delta} > 0$ such that 
