\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.327480+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2bdf732cc12b988cbdc4a279cb86602ba01751330eeb50756391dc6cbd609633","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:invariantmeasures of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] For any $\rho\in [0,1]$ and any $\mathcal{E}\in [\rho ,\kappa\rho]$, the measure $\mu_{\rho ,\mathcal{E}}$ is reversible for the symmetric generator $\mathcal{L}_S$, and invariant for the generator $\mathcal{L}$. Moreover, for all~$x\in\mathbb{Z}$, it satisfies
