{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.588976+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2bdfc4b43d4978f618d79a7e3864f02e32fa9fee897c4e9a4ab1242dc2a92d1e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor consequences of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Assume that $D(\mathcal F_{\beta})\cap X^{a,b}_{p,p'}\neq \emptyset$ and  let $\mathsf{P}^*\in X^{a,b}_{p,p'}$ be the unique minimizer of $\mathcal F_{\beta}$ on $X^{a,b}_{p,p'}$. Then for any $\mathsf{P}\in X^{a,b}_{p,p'}\cap D(\mathcal F_{\beta})$
   \begin{align}
       \frac{\beta }{2a^{\frac{2-p}{p}}} \mathscr W_p^2(\mathsf{P},\mathsf{P}^*)\leq \mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P})-\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}^*)\leq \frac{a^{\frac{2-p}{p}}}{2\beta } \abs{\partial \mathcal F_{\beta}}^2(\mathsf{P}).
    \end{align}
    Moreover, for any curve of maximal slope $(\mathsf{P}_t)_{t>0}$ w.r.t. $\abs{\partial \mathcal F_{\beta}}$ in $X^{a,b}_{p,p'}$ satisfies for every $t\geq t_0>0$
    \begin{align}
        \frac{\beta }{2a^{\frac{2-p}{p}}}\mathscr W_p^2(\mathsf{P}_t,\mathsf{P}^*)\leq \mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_t)-\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}^*)\leq (\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{t_0})-\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}^*))e^{-2\beta a^{\frac{p-2}{p}}(t-t_0)}.
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.740388+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2be0f6c6edd79285ace233f9f349d73e795d2af8dc31daeec63bc952d667cdba","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2506.10494, 'Geometric Jensen-Shannon Divergence Between Gaussian Measures On Hilbert Space'] [\cite{Minh:2020regularizedDiv}, Lemma 24]

