{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.362438+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2bf4fde7bb8fa65bce8f0fba6f52f11af2e37568abe5511cae01e6d55ac30384","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary thm:PF-log-lower of arXiv:2605.16244, 'Analysis of a twisted Bose--Einstein Markov chain with applications to sampling Catalan st'] For $n\ge2$ and $t\ge1$,
