{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.189554+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2bf7d3ba6059096bd40767d3a82420ed4252fce9e88b8c5c9d9fcf6db410e113","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 31 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$, there exist $C,c>0$ such that for any $T>0$, $D\subset \widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^d$ and $z_1,z_2,z_3\in \widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^d\setminus D$ with $\min_{i\neq j}|z_i-z_j|\ge d$, 
