Let $k = \sup_{F\in\mathcal{F}}\{|F|\}$ and $q$ be the Holder conjugate of $p$. Then $||T_\mathcal{F}|| = k^\frac{1}{q}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.366721+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c12ad63131bcf84b6f34b3db541b1e20366cee85a3d0aee66325a96ddea64f6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:SPDE:reg of arXiv:2607.20956, 'Sharp moduli of continuity for Gaussian fields and stochastic PDEs via correlation bounds'] Fix a compact rectangle $I \times J \subset (0\,,\infty) \times \mathbb{R}^d$.
    Then, under (equation ns:cond:sol of the paper), we have 
    \begin{align*}
        \|u(t\,,x)-u(s\,,y)\|_2 \asymp \phi((t\,,x)\,,(s\,,y)) := \phi_1(|t-s|) \vee \phi_2(|x-y|),
    \end{align*}
    uniformly for all $(t\,,x),(s\,,y) \in I\times J$, where
    \begin{align*}
        &\phi_1(|t-s|) := |t-s|^{\theta_1} \quad \text{and}\\
        &\phi_2(|x-y|) := \begin{cases}
            |x-y|^{\theta_2}, & 0<\theta_2<1,\\
            |x-y|\sqrt{\log_+(1/|x-y|)},& \theta_2 = 1,\\
            |x-y|, & \theta_2>1.
        \end{cases}
    \end{align*}
    Moreover, $t \mapsto u(t\,,x)$ is a.s.~H\"older continuous on $I$ of order $\theta_1^-$; $x \mapsto u(t\,,x)$ is a.s.~H\"older continuous on $J$ of order $\theta_2^-$ when $0<\theta_2<1$, and a.s.~continuously differentiable when $\theta_2>1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

