{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.647594+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c50467a184b278e01900b1289ad9dd222fa3f0f7a88f239f8ebc731e02f3f48","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem partitions approx of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] Let $\beta >0$ such that $\beta \not\in \Xi$. For every $\varepsilon, \delta > 0$, there exists $\ell$ large enough such that
