{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.582736+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c7e06e1a4d8cf0d964a39c5c6928b60e5bbd9d241bc8a38af4f1a896eee0e2d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2609.01333, '2609.01333'] Let $ e_1= (1,0)$ and $\gamma > 0$.  For a $C^2$ function $\varphi: \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R} \setminus \{0\}$, the map $$\varphi \mapsto \cF(\varphi) := \cH_{\Omega_\varphi}$$
is defined for every $(t, \varphi(t)z) \in \partial \Omega_\varphi$ with $z \in \mathbb{S}^1 = \partial B_1$, by
\begin{align*}
 \cF(\varphi)(t)= \cH_{\Omega_\varphi} ((t, \varphi(t) z))= \cF_0(\varphi)(t)+ \gamma \cF_1(\varphi)(t)
\end{align*}

where the Yukawa interaction takes the form,
\begin{align}
\int_{\Omega_\varphi} \hspace{-1.5ex}G_\kappa(|(t, \varphi(t) z)  -\xi|)\mathrm{d}\xi =\hspace{-1.5ex}\int_\mathbb{R}\int_{B_1} \hspace{-1.5ex} \varphi^2(s) G_\kappa(|(t, \varphi(t)e_1)-(s,\varphi(s)y)|)\mathrm{d} y \mathrm{d}s=:\mathcal{F}_1(\varphi)(t).
\end{align}
While, the mean curvature of $\partial\Omega_\varphi$  at $(t, \varphi(t) z)  \in\partial \Omega_\varphi$ is given by
\begin{align}
\begin{split}
H_{\partial\Omega_\varphi}((t, \varphi(t)z) )
&=\frac{-\varphi''}{(1+\varphi'^2)^{\frac{3}{2}}}+\frac{1}{\varphi(1+\varphi'^2)^{\frac{1}{2}}}. =: \mathcal{F}_0(\varphi)(t).
\end{split}
\end{align}
Moreover,  for $\lambda \in (0,\infty)$ the function $t\mapsto \cF(\lambda)(t) = C_{\lambda,\kappa}$ is constant, where
\begin{align*}
C_{\lambda,\kappa} &=H_{\partial\Omega_{\lambda}}((0,\lambda e_1))+\gamma \int_{\Omega_{\lambda}}G_\kappa(|(0,\lambda e_1)-z|) \mathrm{d}z=\frac{1}{\lambda} + 2 \gamma\lambda^2 \int_{B_1} K_0(\lambda\kappa|e_1-y|)\mathrm{d}y.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.060072+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c8a88ec8997a00ad861dff0379a112eb19c4178787909e357f343b4c36fb0ae","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 (Branching process started at time $n$) of arXiv:2607.02019, 'Critical branching processes in random environment with immigration and an application to '] A \emph{branching process in the random environment} $(\mathcal E_k)_{k\in\mathbb Z}$ \emph{with immigration} started at time $n\in\mathbb Z$ is a process $(Z^{(n)}_{n+k})_{k\ge0}$, with  $Z^{(n)}_n\in\mathbb Z_{\ge0}$ and defined recursively by
\begin{equation}
	Z^{(n)}_{n+k+1}=\sum_{i=1}^{Z^{(n)}_{n+k}} \xi_{n+k,i}+M_{n+k+1},\qquad k\ge0.
\end{equation}
A \emph{branching process in the random environment} $(\mathcal E_k)_{k\in\mathbb Z}$ is defined using \eqref{eq:BP1}  but with $M_{n+k+1}=0$ a.s. for all $k\ge 0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.357833+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c8d7da49961bafad7ac03d2ac59046307394d41ab4560f8961ff7235b888550","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.vn.1lip of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] For each $n \in {\mathbb N}$ and $k \in \{0,1,\dots,n\}$, $\mathcal{V}^n(k,\cdot)$ is $1$-Lipschitz with respect to $|\cdot|_{\infty}$, i.e., for all $\bm{x},\bm{y}\in{\mathbb R}^n$
    \begin{align*}
        |\mathcal{V}^n(k,\bm{x}) - \mathcal{V}^n(k,\bm{y})| \leq |\bm{x} - \bm{y}|_{\infty}.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.331352+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c9227b08010ac9b82e1317126e092ba143eac6fa2604e79fc61c63f1162668a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:unif_prob_bound of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $(B_t)_{t\geqslant 0}$ denote the hypoelliptic Brownian motion on $\mathbb{G}$. If $\Omega\subset \mathbb{G}$ is a bounded, open set satisfying the intrinsic exterior cone condition, there exists a constant $c=c(\Omega)\in (0,1)$ such that 
