{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.985121+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2cf033bb0e45f0b7829cc7187dbf613107c52535a4af7c5a0c1648abf972b4b0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma continuite de T_eta of arXiv:2412.00865, 'On the spectral problem and fractional diffusion limit for Fokker-Planck with(-out) drift '] Let $\eta_0, \lambda_0>0$ small enough. Let $\eta \in [0,\eta_0]$ and $\lambda \in \mathbb{C}$ such that $|\lambda|\leqslant\lambda_0$. Then,  \\
\noindent 1.  The map $\mathcal{T}_{\lambda,\eta} : \mathcal{H}_0 \longrightarrow \mathcal{H}_\eta$ is continuous.  Moreover, there exists a constant $C>0$, independent of $\lambda$ and $\eta$ such that
\begin{equation}
