{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.695556+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d2d69646608058562520a4b18fb7351a5f4183edd367a670bda9458ae9f058b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:asy_theta of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] The $\alpha$-stable theta function $\theta_{\alpha}(x, \tau)$ defined in (equation theta of the paper) satisfies the following asymptotic properties for $x \in \mathbb{T}^d$ and $\tau > 0$.
