{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.854309+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d33b8435fd816da1969f137543ee03c8f622eeda43e2bf7bf1d198c4cdee954","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:f-g of arXiv:2410.23944, 'Hitting time mixing for the random transposition walk'] Let $M \in \mathbb{N}$ and $T \subseteq [n]$ such that $M \leq T = n^{o(1)}$. Then,
