{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.245445+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d6fecef6490f0f1b8c6fa188989a7ed4d315a6bfdcfae3536789164dc49011b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 68 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Fix some $M,K\in \N$ and let  $n\in \N$. Assume that for all $i\in \lbr M\rbr$ and $\varepsilon>0$, we have some $\hfix^{\per,(i),\varepsilon}_0$ in $\UCp$ so that the associated particle configurations satisfy \eqref{eq:DominationAssumption} at time $0$, and such that the rescaled height functions $\hfix^{\textup{patch},n^{-1},\varepsilon}(\hfix^{\per,(i),\varepsilon}_0;\cdot,0)$ of the $(n^{-1},N)$-patched ASEP at time $0$ converge to $\hfix^{\per,(i)}_0 \colon \mathbb{T}\rightarrow \R$ as $\varepsilon \rightarrow 0$ with respect to the UC topology. 
