        \item [(b)] $Y'_j$ is continuous and non-decreasing, 
        \item [(c)] $Y'_j(t)$ can increase only on $F_{f(j)}$, i.e., 
        \begin{align*}
            \int_0^{t}\mathbf{1}{F_{f(j)}}(W'(s))dY'_j(s)=Y'_j(t) \quad \text{for all } t \ge 0
        \end{align*}


    \end{itemize}
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:30:50.729690+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d7b58782ee105b778aac885ac5bd5b3ad339c9ad6f89a47e64268eff9b36307","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem nah-an-opt of arXiv:2503.22334, 'Probabilistic analysis of optimal multi-pivot QuickSort'] The additional cost of the algorithm compared to always using $t_{\mathrm{opt}}$ is of sub-polynomial order:
