{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.590969+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d7f1a1ff315fa6d8cf10648a3f672c5d5d2ba3992ebad4b320aada5056fb186","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary YA of arXiv:2411.09976, 'Occupation times on the legs of a diffusion spider'] For  $r\in\{1,2,\dotsc, R\}$ and $z_i>0,\, i=1,2,\dotsc,r,$ 
\begin{equation} 
\mathbf{E}_\mathbf{0}\left(\mathrm{exp}\bigg(- \sum_{i=1}^r z_i A_T^{(i)}\bigg)\right) 
= \frac{\displaystyle 1 -\sum_{j=1}^r \beta_j +\sum_{j=1}^r  \frac{\lambda\,\beta_j}{\lambda + z_j} \frac{c_{\lambda+z_j}}{c_\lambda}}
{\displaystyle 1 -\sum_{j=1}^r \beta_j +\sum_{j=1}^r \beta_j \frac{c_{\lambda+z_j}}{c_\lambda}},
\end{equation}
where (cf. (equation cr1 of the paper)) 
\begin{equation*}
c_\lambda:=-\frac{d}{dS}\varphi_\lambda(0+)>0.
