{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.198259+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d9a65f25808a2f3fc5127014c8e13c4696259cc1ffc0af0fc9d444897cf8576","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2604.26549, 'Existence and uniqueness results of a stochastic nonlinear heat equation with a constraint'] Let $T>0$ be fixed and $u_0\in \Vp\cap\bM$ be given. Then, there exists a pathwise unique strong solution $u$, in the sense of Definition \ref{Def-Strong-Soln}, of the SPDE \eqref{eqn-main-prob-Ito} such that
