{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.525823+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2e619913acc41418693f2c55d645bbf7e39e6444f05bfa2460c1e89ba70454a4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Def:alpha-mixing of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] A sequence $\{X_k\}_{k\geq 1}$ of $d$-dimensional random vectors on a sublinear expectation space $(\Omega, \mathcal{H}, \hat{\mathbb{E}})$ is called $\alpha$-mixing if there exist $c_X>0,\alpha>0$ such that for any non-empty finite subset $\Lambda^1,\Lambda^2\subset \mathbb{N}$ with $\Lambda^1_{max}:=\max_{u_1\in \Lambda^1}u_1\leq \min_{u_2\in \Lambda^2}u_2=:\Lambda^2_{min}$ and $\phi\in C_{lip}(\mathbb{R}^{2d})$ with Lipschitz constant $l_{\phi}>0$,
		\begin{equation*}
			\begin{split}
				|\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\phi(\bar{X}_{\Lambda^1}, \bar{X}_{\Lambda^2})] - \hat{\mathbb{E}}[\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\phi(x, \bar{X}_{\Lambda^2})]|_{x=\bar{X}_{\Lambda^1}}]| \leq c_X l_{\phi} e^{-\alpha |\Lambda^2_{min}-\Lambda^1_{max}|},
			\end{split}
		\end{equation*}
		where $\bar{X}_{\Lambda^i}=\frac{1}{|\Lambda^i|}\sum_{u_i\in \Lambda^i}X_{u_i}$  and $|\Lambda^i|$ is the number of elements in $\Lambda^i$, $i=1,2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.955947+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2e61b58c161f031531176b1e906771956d496a3942aaa1eb22e9feb07a019a89","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2606.25501, 'An RDT based approach to large deviations of Wishart and Wigner matrices spectral edges'] (\cite{Gordon85})
 Assume the setup of Theorem \ref{thm:minGordonpos1}. Let $\psi_q(\cdot)$ be an increasing function on the real axis. Then
