{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.955880+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2e62f4970429ef32271aa8cab0fd0bc9803a8006004fc6220c24da93667b749b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:h_inverse of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] The characteristic sub-gamma function $h(u) = 1 + u - \sqrt{1+2u}$ 
is a strictly increasing
function from $[0,\infty)$ onto $[0,\infty)$ with inverse
\begin{align}
  h^{-1}(v) = v + \sqrt{2v},
  \qquad 
  v\geq 0.

\end{align}
Consequently, for any $v \geq 0$,
$h(u) \geq v$ if and only if $u \geq v + \sqrt{2v}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:19:42.467684+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2e6c19df4197d5e1223fc7ff9b3f05ff829beed142a756ea443d2219a907aee9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 (Exact reflection) of arXiv:2609.03466, 'Least-Favorable Location for Binomial Top-$t$ Selection'] Let $T(p)=1-\delta-p$. Then, for every $n,k,t$ and $p\in[0,1-\delta]$,
