{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.473432+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ed2c7990fb8bf6db67f2ce44752f6940f3b4456eebd110b3074915cdf1275af","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:uniquefixed of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Let $\mathcal{L}_S$ be defined in (equation def:lsbip of the paper), where $\mathcal{L}^A$ is a primitive QMS generator on the subsystem $A$ with invariant state $\sigma^A \in \mathcal{D}_+(\mathcal{M}_A)$. Suppose that (asspA2 of the paper) holds. Then, 
\begin{itemize}
