\end{equation}
Here $\chi^G$ is a standard Gaussian random variable (real if $\chi$ is real and complex otherwise) which is independent of~$\chi_\alpha$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.350667+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ef013a744ce8121e85359ce829263139ca5ca01b1bc871c496c9d9271a247e2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:two-point-TASEP of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] Fix $\alpha_0 \in \mathbb{R}$. 
