{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.805116+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f7a370261d56af9d3936b111d4964c70ce9d56b6a600477c57dc40c3ad4e221","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:K5 of arXiv:2606.23865, 'Uniform-in-time Gaussian fluctuations for multiscale nonlinear stochastic systems via Mall'] Let the term $\mathsf{K}_5(t, r_1 \vee r_2; \varepsilon, \eta)$ be defined in equation (equation E:Second-der-X-W2W2 of the paper). Then, for any $p \in \mathbb{N}$ and $t \ge r_1 \vee r_2,$ there exists a time-independent positive constant $K$ such that 
