{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.338272+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f7fecd062716a8ef65a602af60edde6333de25c8fcfdada61508310fda55d06","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2607.14948, 'Graph alignment in sparse inhomogeneous models via self-overlap'] Let $(G^\uparrow, G, H)$ be an inhomogeneous correlated graph system, and assume that $G^\uparrow$ is weakly inhomogeneous. Define

    \begin{equation}
    x_{sparse} = \lim_{\eps \to 0} \operatorname*{pliminf}_{n \to +\infty} \frac{|V_{\leq (1-\eps)}|}{n}.
\end{equation}
    Furthermore, assume that for some $r \geq 0$,
    \begin{equation} 
        \min_{e \in E} p_e \geq \frac{1}{n (\log n)^r} \qquad \text{whp.}
    \end{equation}
    Then, if $\hat{\pi}$ is an estimator of $\pi^*$, there exist at least $x_{sparse}(n - o_\Proba(n))$ vertices $v \in [n]$ such that $\hat{\pi}(v) \neq \pi^*(v)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.283281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f825bb730c3d334d31fb1bdc451e9995e90055c7eac9a70bffb875599dc5ffb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2606.22940, 'From smooth to discontinuous kernels: a variance transfer principle for hyperuniform proce'] Let  $ x_{ N}\in  \Sigma $ such that  $ d(x_{ N},\partial  \Sigma ) \to \infty $,    and a limit point $ \P = \lim_{ N_{ j}\to \infty } \tau _{- x_{ N_{ j}}} \X _{ N_{ j}}$.   

 Let $ \alpha \geqslant 0.$ Let $ R_{ N}\to \infty .$ Assume that for some non-negative  non-degenerate $ f\in \B_{ c}^{}(B_{ 1})$ there is $ C_{ f}$ such that  for all $ N\geqslant 1,R\in [1,R_{ N}]  $,
\begin{align*}
\sup_{ x\in \Sigma ^{ R}} \mathbf E \left[\;\overline{\X_{ N}}(\tau _{ x}f_{ R })^{ 2}
\right]\leqslant C_{ f}R^{ d-\alpha }.
\end{align*}
Then for $\gamma >0,\varphi \in \F_{ \gamma }$ continuous $ \Leb$-a.e.,   $R\geqslant R_{ f}^{\circ }, L \geqslant  { R^{ d + 2}},$  
\begin{align}

\sup_{ x_{ 0}\in \mathbb{R}^{ d}}\displaystyle\int_{ [-L/2,L/2 ]^{ d}}  \textrm{Var}\left(\P(\tau _{ x_{ 0} + x}\varphi _{ R})\right)\frac{ dx}{L^{ d}}\leqslant C_{ \varphi,f }V_{ \alpha ,\gamma }(R)
 \end{align}
 where $ R^\circ _{ f},C_{ \varphi ,f}$ depend explicitly   on $ f,\varphi ,d,C_{ f}$. 

If $ \P$ is furthermore assumed to be stationary,  we have the result for all $   x\in \mathbb{R}^{ d}, R\geqslant R_{ f}^{\circ }$ 
\begin{align}

  \textrm{Var}\left(\P(\tau _{ x}\varphi _{ R})\right)\leqslant C_{ \varphi,f }V_{ \alpha ,\gamma }(R),
\end{align}
which means that $ \P$ is $ \alpha $-hyperuniform. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.223438+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f881ceefb8c3e1ce103ec74e1c43a2a8dccc3d354467623bdd5115439f240f9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 (Anchored constant-speed estimate for normal families) of arXiv:2609.00501, 'Uniqueness of Finite-Time Varifold Limits for the M\"obius-Invariant Willmore Flow'] Let \(I\subset\R\) be an interval and let
