{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.588680+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f954d06b3427ef1f1eb9abcf93f578d4038f581fb54c21fcb54bf60fda9cb50","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Col cor_global_energy of arXiv:2608.30548, 'Finite speed of propagation and waiting time phenomena for stochastic porous media equatio'] The unique kinetic solution to (equation Eq_SPME_intro of the paper) with initial value $u_0$ { satisfying (equation assumption_m_plus_one of the paper) admits the estimate} 
    \begin{align}
        \begin{split}
&
 \mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(
        \sup_{t\le {T}} \int_{\mathbb{T}^d}  u^{\alpha+1 }\,\mathrm{d} x \,+\, \int_0^{T} \int_{\mathbb{T}^d}   | \nabla (u^{(\alpha+m )/2 })|^2\,\mathrm{d} x\, \mathrm{d} t \biggr)^p
        \biggr]^{1/p}
        \\&\quad \lesssim_{(\alpha,m,n,p,\psi)} \,\int_{\mathbb{T}^d}  u_0^{\alpha+1 }\,\mathrm{d} x \,+\,T\bigl(\|u_0\|_{L^1(\mathbb{T}^d)} \,+\,
