{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.052168+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2fb54415ece96d4382d95b69f0608aaa91bacd6c20ae3dcae22c1c360979b2af","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:fourier of arXiv:2607.12564, 'Power-law and log-periodic degree tails for a family of probability generating function eq'] Let $\chi:=2\pi/\log\lambda$, $s_m:=\rho+1+i\chi m$, and
