{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.943424+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3031c0e230bfc2bb2fb209d28e7451e9301f4c23991907390a6333edf8836f52","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 8 of arXiv:2606.24584, '2606.24584'] Let $D$ be an $n\times n$ irreducible doubly stochastic matrix. Then $D$ is cyclic  if and only if there exists a permutation matrix $P$ such that
