and
\begin{equation}
\liminf_{s\to 0+}\Big(\frac{1}{\log 1/s\, \log\log\log 1/s}\Big)^{1/2}\sum_{k\ge 2}\frac{(\log k)^{-1/2}}{k^{1/2+s}}\eta_k=-(2\sigma^2)^{1/2}\quad\text{\rm a.s.}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.216298+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_304631344dbbd4fbea9c2a5f4782d204d604ab9815b76acc38dcbf81787d8301","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:zerobd of arXiv:2607.05671, 'Bi-infinite systems of singularly interacting Brownian particles and the KPZ equation'] Fix $r \in [1, \infty)$. 
