{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.446399+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3046a659c32d510206297077da7bcfc2cdb2a1f9d743ea24e10af3b111afaa9b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:domstochdisorder of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] For any $L \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$ and any $\beta \geq 0$, one has the stochastic domination
