{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.356649+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3055491b67c51ef902af6b0ab6a67c8e4f3b0759c5fd1b62869ccec33b3cd4d0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:local of arXiv:2608.23638, 'Replicable Conformal Prediction'] Let $F$ be continuous, let $S_1,\ldots,S_n$ be i.i.d.\ with cdf $F$,
let $k_n=\lceil(1-\alpha)(n+1)\rceil\le n$, and put
$\widetilde{\tau}=S_{(k_n)}$.  Under Assumption~(ass:margin of the paper),
$|F(\widetilde{\tau})-p|<f_{\min}\Delta$ implies $\widetilde{\tau}\in I$, and for every
$a,b\in I$,
