{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.021038+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_30848bc6fce454cace1314fff747620be518923543b090d22e4e19b6e1428942","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2605.06556, 'Probability of Quota Violations in Divisor Apportionment Methods with Nonzero Allocations'] (Asymptotic Apportionment) Let $(1,x,y_1(x,\tau_1),\ldots,y_{n-2}(x,\tau_{n-2}))$ be a reduced population vector with $\bm\tau=(\tau_1,\ldots,\tau_{n-2})$. Let $A$ be a divisor method that guarantees nonzero allocations on $M$ seats. Then for almost every $\bm\tau$ satisfying $-\tfrac13 < \tau_1 < \cdots < \tau_{n-2} < \tfrac13,$

