{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.114341+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_309e8202470cecb70d481feaca3555bedbd13a18c88307e6397933c0e7930ddf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theorem_spin_correlations of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $D \subset \mathbb{C}$ be a bounded and simply connected domain and $a, b \in \partial D$ be two prime ends of $\partial D$. Let $(D_{\delta};a_{\delta}, b_{\delta})_{\delta}$ be discrete approximations of $(D;a,b)$ satisfying the assumptions of Section (sec_assumptions_domain of the paper). Then, for any $\eta >0$ and any $k \geq 1$, we have that
\begin{align*}
    &\delta^{-\frac{k}{8}} \mu_{\delta}^{\pm}[\sigma_{x_1}\dots \sigma_{x_{k}}] = C_{\sigma}^k f_{D}^{(\pm, k)}(x_1,\dots ,x_k) + o(1) \\
    &\delta^{-\frac{k}{8}} \mu_{\delta}^{+}[\sigma_{x_1}\dots \sigma_{x_{k}}] = C_{\sigma}^k f_{D}^{(+,k)}(x_1,\dots ,x_k) + o(1) \\
    &\delta^{-\frac{k}{8}} \mu_{\delta}^{-}[\sigma_{x_1}\dots \sigma_{x_{k}}] = C_{\sigma}^k f_{D}^{(-,k)}(x_1,\dots ,x_k) + o(1)
\end{align*}
as $\delta \to 0$, uniformly over all $x_1, \dots, x_k \in D$ at distance at least $\eta$ from $\partial D$ and from each other. Here, $C_{\sigma}>0$ is a constant that corresponds to the fact that we are working on the square lattice. The functions $f_{D}^{(\pm,k)}$, $f_{D}^{(+,k)}$ and $f_{D}^{(-,k)}$ are explicit and satisfy the following conformal covariance property. If $\psi: D \to \tilde D$ is a conformal map, then for any $k \geq 1$ and any $x_1, \dots , x_k \in D$, with $\xi \in \{\pm,-,+\}$,
\begin{align*}
    &f_{D}^{(\xi, k)}(x_1,\dots ,x_k) = \prod_{j=1}^{k} \vert \psi'(x_j) \vert^{1/8} f_{\tilde D}^{(\xi,k)}(\psi(x_1),\dots ,\psi(x_k)).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.965613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_30a4f0baa39d1ed74d852b7e972e6a092b2986ea379c201ee252f61a3f21305b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {ATE for Gaussians}


