{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:25:41.654611+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31285005d891a13667a9bfcd8e0cd401eaec3a743961444b0d5f0fc81ffb01e4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:countable-dense-regular-families of arXiv:2608.15923, 'Universality of two-dimensional Markovian holonomy fields'] There exists a countable collection $\mathscr D$ of finite regular based loop families with the following property. For every finite regular based loop family $L=(\ell_1,\ldots,\ell_r)$ and every $\varepsilon>0$, there exists $L'=(\ell'_1,\ldots,\ell'_r)\in\mathscr D$ such that:
