{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:35:56.812281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31310368026e3a5573671dfb9e0a9bf65189c61079eff178b56b0fd97f89371d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma G_A_decoupling_lemma of arXiv:2603.28520, 'The Supercritical Loop O(1) and Random Current Models: Uniqueness and Mixing'] For $A \subseteq \Lambda_r$, with $\abs{A}$ odd, the following localization identity holds
