where $L^2_{\langle v\rangle^2}$ denote the weighted $L^2$ space: $\displaystyle L^2_{\langle v\rangle^2}:=\left\{f: \mathbb{R}^d \longrightarrow \mathbb{C} \ ; \ \int_{\mathbb{R}^d} |f|^2 \langle v\rangle^2 \mathrm{d}v < \infty \right\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.774109+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31511473a35a3aca24d5f60079d7343cf565ddd942abe05ab95b9c3172f1da66","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:order-bounded-equivalent of arXiv:2411.01364, 'Global Dynamics of Granular Media Equations via Stochastic Order'] Let $M$ be a subset of $\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$.
Then the following statements are true.
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textnormal{(\roman*)}]
\item $M$ is bounded from above in $\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$ with respect to the stochastic order if and only if
\begin{equation}
\int_0^{\8}\bigg(\sup_{\mu\in M}\mu\big((u,\8)\big)\bigg)u\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} u<\8.
