{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.829846+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31954df1407496b560ffc4a57609d89f9d2f17530714e4e18443839c6a74332e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:cross-area-leading of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] Consider a two-channel Hawkes process with equal baselines $\mu$, common decay $\beta$, zero self-excitation, and cross-kernels
\begin{equation}
