	\end{equation}
	Then $\{(\varphi^{k},{{\boldsymbol{ {\Pi}}}}^{k})\}_{k\in\mathbb{N}}$ is pre-compact.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.709618+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31ae8eff854e58ca8ee2221d9ba811999049826bd235e1ce7a7603f9fc1b3176","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thrm:examples of arXiv:2411.18749, 'A star is born: Explosive Crump--Mode--Jagers branching processes'] Consider the four examples $(i)$-$(iv)$. The infinite tree $T_\infty$ almost surely contains a unique infinite star and no infinite path when
