{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.705406+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31b14c72b44c4b87e70421843b9e93e700525c5fcf5f5cd307f419818d33206e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm t:thm_q of arXiv:2504.07255, 'A Tail-Respecting Splitting Numerical Scheme\\ for L\'evy-Driven SDEs With Superlinear Dri'] Let assumptions
$\mathbf{H}^{\mathrm{Lip}_+}_A$,
$\mathbf{H}_{A_x,A_{xx}}$,
$\mathbf{H}_{a,b,c}^{\mathrm{Lip}_b}$, and
$\mathbf{H}_{\nu,p}$
 hold. Then,
 for any $T\in[0,\infty)$ and $q\in (0,p)$ there is convergence
\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}
\sup_{t\in[0, T]} \mathbf{E} \|X_t^n-X_t\|^q \leq_C h_n^{\bar \delta}(1+\|x\|^p),\quad x\in\mathbb{R}^d,
\end{aligned}\end{equation}
with the convergence rate
\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}
