{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.459462+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31ba845d7298a56241e60e2127f4c849a033f0391ad7eb83662f650c2e380d76","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 46 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] For every $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$, let $\mathcal{X}^{1,n},\mathcal{X}^{2,n}$ be two time-dependent fields taking values in $ \mathcal{D} \big( [0, T],  { \color{orange} L^2 (\mathbb{R})}' \; \big)$ and defined on the same probability space. Let $(\alpha^{(i)}_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$, $i=1,2$, be two sequences of constants such that 
\begin{equation} 
 \lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{|u \alpha^{(1)}_n + v  \alpha^{(2)}_n|}{n}= \infty,
\end{equation}
for all $(u, v) \in A$ and $A$ a subset of $\mathbb{R}^2$ whose complement has 
$0$-Lebesque measure. 
Assume that there exists $\delta >0$ such that for every $f,g \in C_c^r(\mathbb{R})$ for some $r \in \mathbb{N}$,
there are finite constants $C_1(f,g), C_2(f,g)>0$ non-decreasing in $T$ and independent of $n$ for which 
\begin{align}
\sup_{0 \leq s \leq T}\mathbb{E} \Big[ \big|  \mathcal{X}_s^{1,n} (f) \mathcal{X}_s^{2,n} (g) \big|   \Big] &\leq C_1(f,g)\,,  \\
 \mathbb{E} \Big[ \big|  \mathcal{X}_t^{1,n} (f) \mathcal{X}_t^{2,n} (g) - \mathcal{X}_s^{1,n} (f) \mathcal{X}_s^{2,n} (g) \big|   \Big] &\leq C_2(f,g) (t-s)^{\delta}  \,,\qquad \text{for all $s,t\in[0,T]$.}  
\end{align}
Further, assume that $C_1$ depends bilinearly only on the $L^2(\R)$-norms of $f,g$ of their first $1<r<\infty$ derivatives 
and that $C_2$ is invariant under translations of $f$ and $g$, i.e. for any $u,v\in\R$, $C_2(f,g)=C_2(f^u,g^v)$. 

Then, for any $t \in [0, T]$, any $f \in \mathcal{S}( \mathbb{R} )$ and any $h_1, h_2 \in C_c^{\infty}(\mathbb{R})$, 
\begin{equation}   
\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty }   \mathbb{E}\Bigg[ \Bigg| \int_0^t {\rm d} s \frac{1}{n} \sum_{w}   \nabla f ( \tfrac{ w }{n}  ) \, \mathcal{X}_s^{1,n} \Big( h_1^{ \frac{w + \alpha^{(1)}_n s }{n} } \Big)   \mathcal{X}_s^{2,n} \Big( h_2^{ \frac{w + \alpha^{(2)}_n s}{n} } \Big)  \Bigg|  \Bigg] = 0,
\end{equation}
where for $w \in \mathbb{Z}$ and $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$, $h_1^{ \frac{w + \alpha^{(1)}_n }{n} }$ and $h_2^{ \frac{w + \alpha^{(2)}_n }{n} }$ are given by \eqref{smoothshift}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.337294+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31c8584544e503e14f64d1b56a091b1022f6e4860f05b375d627371a8d0078ab","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:admissible of arXiv:2601.19630, 'Mass generation for the two dimensional O(N) Linear Sigma Model in the large N limit'] We will say that a cylindrical functional $F$ is \textit{admissible} provided at least one of the following holds:
