{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:08.981577+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31d3bb38eb9a249fe44759a22a512f852e751eacbc4d934cec4fee88a6f19c41","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def_stationaryIncr of arXiv:2608.17463, 'Persistence probabilities of fractional L\'evy fields indexed by hyperbolic space and othe'] A real valued field $(X_\eta)_{\eta\in\mathcal{M}}$ indexed by a homogeneous Riemannian manifold $\mathcal{M}$ is said to possess \emph{strong} stationary increments if for all $\zeta\in\mathcal{M}$ we have
    \begin{align*}
        (X_\eta - X_\zeta)_{\eta\in\mathcal{M}} {~\stackrel{(d)}{=}~} (X_{\psi_\zeta^{-1}(\eta)})_{\eta\in\mathcal{M}},
    \end{align*}
    where the equality is in finite dimensional distribution.

    A real valued field $(X_\eta)_{\eta\in\mathcal{M}}$ indexed by a Riemannian manifold $\mathcal{M}$ is said to possess \emph{weak} stationary increments if for all $\eta,\zeta\in\mathcal{M}$ the distribution of the increments is a function of the distance $d(\eta,\zeta)$, i.e.\
    \begin{align*}
        \expec{e^{i \lambda (X_\eta - X_\zeta)}} = f(\lambda, d(\eta,\zeta))
    \end{align*}
    for some function $f:\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \to \mathbb{C}$, any $\eta,\zeta\in\mathcal{M}$ and $\lambda\in\mathbb{R}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.359887+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31d5070b96542d1b56d3d7346274e12c246df830b611605b6d249f953f14c81e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:connection_two_Malliavin of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] It holds that $\mathbb{D}^{1,2}_W=\mathbb{D}^{1,2}$ and that for any $F \in \mathbb{D}^{1,2}$ we have 
