{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:32:58.357869+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31e645d25a2a23d92e2fdf42f550e525b92670d1ad06620963f0b17f7325b36d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Union of diagrammatic graphs of arXiv:2506.06559, 'Bi-infinite incipient cluster in high dimensions'] Let ${\bf G}=(G,S,\ell)$ be a diagrammatic graph and $x,y\in \mathbb{Z}^d$. We will denote ${\bf G}\uplus \{x,y\}$ the diagrammatic graph $(G’,S’,\ell’)$ defined as follows
\begin{enumerate}
\item if $x,y\in \{\ell(s), s\in S\}$, then 
\begin{itemize}
 \item $V(G’)=V(G)$ 
 \item $E(G’)=E(G)\cup e_{\{x,y\}}$ where an edge $e_{\{x,y\}}$ is added between the vertices $s,s’\in S$ such that $x=\ell(s)$ and $y=\ell(s’)$ 
  \item $S=S’$ and $\ell=\ell’$.
\end{itemize}
\item if $x\in \{\ell(s), s\in S\}$ and $y\notin  \{\ell(s), s\in S\}$,
\begin{itemize}
 \item $V(G’)=V(G)\cup\{y_*\}$ 
 \item $E(G’)=E(G)\cup e_{\{x,y\}}$ where an edge $e_{\{x,y\}}$ is added between $y_*$ and the vertex $s\in S$ such that $x=\ell(s)$
  \item $S’=S \cup \{y_*\}$, $\ell(s)=\ell’(s)$ if $s\in S$ and $\ell’(y_*)=y$.
\end{itemize}
\item if $x,y\notin \{\ell(s), s\in S\}$
\begin{itemize}
 \item $V(G’)=V(G)\cup\{x_*,y_*\}$ 
 \item $E(G’)=E(G)\cup e_{\{x,y\}}$ where an edge $e_{\{x,y\}}$ is added between $x_*$ and $y_*$.
  \item $S’=S \cup \{x_*,y_*\}$, $\ell(s)=\ell’(s)$ if $s\in S$, $\ell’(x_*)=x$ and $\ell’(y_*)=y$.
\end{itemize}
\end{enumerate}

We will extend this notation to ${\bf G}\uplus {\bf G}'$ when ${\bf G}$ is a diagrammatic graph and ${\bf G}'$ a fully labeled graph simply, by successively adding to ${\bf G}$ the finite number of labeled edges composing ${\bf G}'$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.547905+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31e8e8c4f5ea0f2b9e53319986b777dab2db8536aa29601b56c0eb71756ba881","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 32 (The dimension of the support and the range of SBM) of arXiv:2604.01852, 'The on/off Brownian snake'] Let $\mu \in \mathcal{M}_F(\mathbb{R}^d)$ be a non-zero finite measure, let $\gamma > 0$ and let $(\mathcal{X}_s, s \geq 0)$ be an $\text{SBM}(\gamma)$ started from $\mu$. Then we have that for $y>0$, that
\begin{equation*}
