{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:36.157094+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31f6da03863b202e2b7b0ff6cd5aa2f45c8f96aec8e2ca144e0bc632b8928207","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 23 of arXiv:2609.01574, 'A linear bound for Fujita's freeness conjecture'] For every positive integer $n$, there exists $\delta_n>0$ with the following property. Let $k$ be a positive integer with $k\leq n$, and let $n=b_0\geq b_1\geq\cdots\geq b_k=0$ be real numbers. For every $0\leq i<k$, let $d_i>0$, set $a_i:=(d_i-b_i)/2\geq0$, and let $0\leq c_i\leq n-d_i$. Then
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{i=0}^{k-1}(b_i-b_{i+1})
 \left(
 \frac{(a_i+c_i)^{a_i+c_i}}{a_i^{a_i}c_i^{c_i}}
 \right)^{1/d_i}
 \leq (C_0-\delta_n)n.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.793009+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31fd0d2765f03df7c998fccbb60ef911c648d45bb348e1398122f6f75f71454c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:characterizeRinfty of arXiv:2411.08295, 'Improving the convergence of Markov chains via permutations and projections'] Let $\pi$ be the discrete uniform distribution on $\mathcal{X}$ and $P = P^T \in \mathcal{L}(\pi)$. Denote the sequence of isometric involution transition matrices to be $Q_{1,j}$ as in this subsection, and define the sequence of projections $(R_l)_{l \in \mathbb{N}}$ as in (equation eq:Rndef of the paper). The limit $R_\infty$ is given by
	\begin{align}
		R_\infty = (nb) \Pi + (a-b) I = \begin{bmatrix}
			a & b & \ldots & b \\
			b & a & \ddots & \vdots \\
			\vdots & \ddots & \ddots & b \\
			b & \ldots & b & a
		\end{bmatrix},
	\end{align}
	where $a = a(Q_{1,2},\ldots,Q_{1,n},P), b = b(Q_{1,2},\ldots,Q_{1,n},P) \in [0,1]$ satisfy $nb + a-b = 1$. In particular, $R_\infty = \Pi$ if and only if $\mathrm{Tr}(P) = 1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.972537+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32011ad14b67b218e6aa6cd025fb8d588a40542816bfb66df7e9cac3781bdd55","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2606.10313, '\textbf{Invariance principles for additive functionals of voter models}'] There exists $C_7<+\infty$ independent of $a, b, B^{\vec{s}}$ such that
