{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.613495+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_322c47c3d2e2d5538bd5dcacbb4049b7fb094b72af7d2cda13c0fce586e83204","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 ($\ell^p$ matrix deviation inequality) of arXiv:2506.09333, 'On the Dimension-Free Concentration of Simple Tensors via Matrix Deviation'] Let $p\ge 2$. Let $A \in \R^{N\times d}$ be a random matrix whose rows are i.i.d. copies of a mean-zero isotropic subgaussian random vector $Z \in \mathbb{R}^d$. Consider the stochastic process
