{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.649169+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32323344116000182643352369529ad56ad1c030551fc9ea34546bd008f60851","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:billingsley of arXiv:2607.04002, 'Collisions of random walks in unimodular random graphs: applications to the random geometr'] Let~$\{N_i: i \in \mathbb{N}\}$ be an i.i.d. family of Poisson random variables with mean~$\lambda > 0$. There exists~$c_\mathrm{pois} = c_\mathrm{pois}(\lambda) > 0$ such that 
