{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.959105+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_323f48955d87ee2fa3b57578afbdda148fd6b906d5a64ebdeecda2620abefd9c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 19 (Pathwise centered operator and full cutoff convergence) of arXiv:2606.26065, 'Localized Centered Second-Chaos Operators'] Assume the Galerkin-state finite-state condition in Assumption~\ref{ass:time} and
\[
 \mathfrak S_H^{(\eps)}(\beta,\sigma)
 +\mathfrak S_B^{(\eps)}(\zeta,\sigma)<\infty.
\]
Then on the full-probability event $\Omega_*$ of Lemma~\ref{lem:BC}, for every cutoff $\Lambda$ the series~\eqref{eq:assembled} defines a bounded operator
\[
 \cB^\circ_\Lambda(\omega):\Xspace_T^\sigma\to\Yspace_T^{\beta,\zeta},
\]
and
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{\Lambda\in\Dyd\cup\{\infty\}}
 \norm{\cB^\circ_\Lambda(\omega)}_{\Xspace_T^\sigma\to\Yspace_T^{\beta,\zeta}}
 \le C_*(\omega)
 \left[\mathfrak S_H^{(\eps)}+\mathfrak S_B^{(\eps)}\right].
\end{equation}
Moreover the entire Galerkin sequence, not merely a subsequence, satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \cB^\circ_\Lambda(\omega)\to\cB^\circ(\omega)
 \quad\text{in }\cL(\Xspace_T^\sigma,\Yspace_T^{\beta,\zeta}).
\end{equation}
For every fixed input and output test vector, the limiting scalar pairing belongs to the centered second Wiener chaos.","status":"unverified"}

