{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.830039+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_325e37543c513adb27e1ab2b550b0825b83c2155df9f0263c8ba80c1721fe2ae","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2606.24385, 'Gradient Mean-Field Dynamics with Measure-Valued States: Well-Posedness, Chaos, and Long-T'] Let $\gamma$ be a Gaussian measure on $(E,\mathscr{B}(E))$. We define the mean $a_{\gamma}$, and the covariance $B_{\gamma}$ of $\gamma$ by
