{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.655780+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32645eecb2d31b1c75547d9ce5ffd493b52814d8fae4ce00a77d911ecef40e77","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:main of arXiv:2411.04690, 'Asymptotic distribution of the derivative of the taut string accompanying Wiener process'] If a convex function $\varphi$ satisfies
\begin{equation} 
\int\limits_{\mathbb{R}}  \varphi(u) e^{-2\lambda|u|} du <\infty
\quad \textrm{for some } \lambda\in (0,r)
\end{equation}
or
\begin{equation} 
     \int\limits_{\mathbb{R}}  \varphi(u) \, p_{\infty,r}(u) du =\infty
