{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.719074+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_328bd86ee01cc00afaab9b77a32ffd36d427af66a838b6f7a34f54513e7e5f16","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2608.17449, 'Spectral Simplicity and Joint Eigenvalue Densities\\ for a Non-Gaussian Brownian Time Chan'] There exists $\Omega_*\in\Borel(\Omega)$ such that
