{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:49.833604+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32a4fb1201942b3dec01ef81de65e7a42a92d26051b40d2520a6c0cf86173d40","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 11 (Deterministic profile joint factorial moments) of arXiv:2506.12632, 'Point process convergence of extremes in $K$-symmetric exclusion'] Suppose that $A_k = (a_k,b_k]$, $1 \le k \le m$, are finite and disjoint, and define $A \subset \R$ by
