{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:41.028271+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32edbcbcbcd57b53002319f0b8df503cda0b4323c5f1cd2945ace2b390c7ae64","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t01 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] Fix a bounded function $F\colon {\mathbb R}_+ \times {\mathbb T}^d_N \to {\mathbb R}$, and
a cylinder function $f$.  Then, there exists a finite constant
${\mathfrak c}({\boldsymbol u}^N)$, uniformly bounded in $N$, such that
\begin{align*}
& {\mathbb E}_{\nu^N} \Big[\, \Big|\,
\int_0^t \, \sum_{x\in {\mathbb T}^d_N} F (s,x)\,
(\Xi_{{\boldsymbol u}^N(\cdot), x} f) (\eta^N(s))
\, ds \, \Big| \,\Big]
\\
& \quad \;\le\;
{\mathfrak c}({\boldsymbol u}^N) \, \Big\{ \frac{1}{K_N} \;+\;
K_N\,  \int_0^t (\, 1 + \Vert F(s)\Vert^2_\infty\,)\, \big[ \,
H_N(f^N_s)  + (N/\ell_N)^d \,\big] \, ds\; \Big\} 
\end{align*}
for all $t> 0$.  In this equation, $f^N_s$ is given by (equation 2-34c of the paper),
and $(\ell_N : N\ge 1)$ is the sequence introduced in the statement of
Theorem (mt1 of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.794588+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32f1d2177e290571898592ca12410bda4b3f4dddb5544193e266eb9657ad26f1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 80 (Bell polynomials) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] The Wick map $\W(t,x)$ is the generating function of Bell polynomials, 
in the sense that 
\begin{equation}
 \W(t,x) = \sum_{n\geqs0} B_n(x, -y_2, \dots, -y_n) \frac{t^n}{n!}\;.
\end{equation} 
$B_n$ is called the \emph{$n$th complete Bell polynomial}. It can be decomposed 
as 
\begin{equation}
 B_n(x, -y_2, \dots, -y_n)
 = \sum_{k=1}^n B_{n,k}(x, -y_2, \dots, -y_{n-k+1})\;,
\end{equation} 
where each $B_{n,k}$ is the homogeneous part of degree $k$ of $B_n$, and 
is called \emph{incomplete Bell polynomial} of order $(n,k)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.008424+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32f637774f91c7e331ec00e5426688550a8b2e08ed5d35e70bddd81c1750e04b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma keyI2 of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Under the same assumption as in the previous lemma, for any $s\in\left[s_0,\frac{e_0\tilde{\mu}_{n,N}}{\tilde{\sigma}_{n,N}}\right]$, when $N$ is large enough,
