{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:20:15.584469+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_33035a755f81c5d69baaf6138d180e3610a8d5445d00240bc87b9c2dd6977b90","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition propLinearIncrement of arXiv:2609.00777, 'Universal murmuration and Hecke augmentation'] Let $L$, $\mathbf X$, and $\mathbf Z$ have finite second moments, with $L$ centered.  Let $\mathbf Z^\perp$ be the residual after the best affine linear projection of $\mathbf Z$ on $\mathbf X$.
