{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.888383+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_334c7ed47df65b2a0bc16e6dfacb031bb9134afab002be4629c669a8e7586c9d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] Let the hypotheses of (thm:dragoverkill of the paper) hold for each $\ell$, with respect to $r=r_\ell, \lambda=\lambda_\ell,\delta=\delta_\ell,\sigma=\sigma_\ell$. If moreover, the field satisfies an analogous of the Weyl law, meaning that (eq:pseudoweyl of the paper) holds for some sequence $w_\ell$,
