{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.188876+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_33a597390b79bb9cfa432d4e60813a75f02fa830fd5111cc376fc96865dcc65b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 25 of arXiv:2604.18871, 'Quantitative approximation of the Vlasov(--Fokker--Planck)--Navier--Stokes system by stoch'] Let Assumptions~\ref{assump-PDE} and \ref{assump-particles} hold, with $\sigma=0$. Let us further assume that $F \in L^\infty([0,T]; H^\gamma_{2}(\T^d\times \R^d))$ for some $\gamma>0$, and that $\langle v\rangle^k \nabla_{v} F \in L^2([0,T];L^2(\T^d\times\R^d))$.
