{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.337094+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_33cb4b51ff19ccaafa2ceec4634996303701d53fadbfcba29d1db79f58ba1f59","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2607.27150, 'Modelling Anomalous Diffusion: The Role of CTRWs and Non-Local Dynamics'] Let $r_0>0$. For every multi-index $\beta=(\beta_1,\dots,\beta_d)\ge0$, there exist constants $c_1,c_2,c_3>0$ such that for all $t>0$ and all $x,y\in \mathbb{R}^d$ such that $|x-y|>r_0$ it holds that
