{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.164442+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3465ceb1c7b91e506b4f6fd662b2398020ed97dfb731bb84ffbc31b73a109576","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] (Local) chiral residue conditions can be imposed in families as follows:
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item
    A \defined{family of chiral residue conditions} $(B,f,{\mathbf{R}}^\pm)$ consists of:
    \begin{enumerate}
