{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.862751+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3486e87bf0380bb447133b10d52ea9f3b40e8210149c2e847994285105a83702","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $t\in[0,T)$, $Y^{t,x}$ be the solution of \eqref{Eq:target} started at time $t$ with $Y_t^{t,x}=x$. Assume that $\sigma$ is four times continuously differentiable with bounded derivatives and uniformly elliptic. Then the law of $Y_T^{t,x}$ admits a density $p(y;t,x)$ with respect to the Lebesgue measure. Furthermore, if $0\le n+m \le 4$ there are constants $0<C<\infty$ such that
