{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:43:45.397497+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_350806fe73ad2ed695d9676e909c0129d24766ea2c423c2490b9f616cc279e5b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mainresulta 1 (Growth determined by the diameter) of arXiv:2609.04143, 'The Geometry of Real Anisotropic Bohnenblust--Hille Constants'] Let $(\mathbf q^{(m)})_{m\ge2}$ be a sequence of Bohnenblust--Hille exponents and put $d_m=d(\mathbf q^{(m)})$.
