{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.840163+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_351abb1e35c59fa4757e3ac61e4278959ff21723413696e787f79194cab58044","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Def: reduction chain of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] For any $k\in\mathbb{N}$ and $\rho\in{\mathcal T} _b$ with $k+1$ leaves we define a \emph{reduction chain} as a collection of $k$ binary trees $(\rho^0,\rho^1,\ldots \rho^k)$ such that 
