{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.732076+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_35261624a1ca676af3c75e6ed26494c3546c238f3585dd99c573732a1cf559dc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma expintest of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] For $\beta \in (0,1)$,  $a, c, t,\mu \ge 0$,  there exists $c' > 0$ such that
