    \begin{equation}
        \P\left(\lim_{q'\to\infty} X_1^{\kappa_{2q'}} (x, \omega)=y\neq y'=\lim_{q'\to\infty} X_1^{\kappa_{2q'+1}} (x, \omega)\right)=1.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.254551+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_355429b02903a6098c4f066f9df8996ed772e37fa5d30c270be36d6ac2aa12f0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 20 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] For $\calX=(X,d^X,\mu_X),\;\calY=(Y,d^Y,\mu_Y)\in\frK(\tau)$, we define
\begin{align*}
  d^{\tau,\BL^{\kappa}}_{\frK}(\calX,\calY):=\inf_{f,g,Z}\Big\{ d^Z_{\mathrm{H}}(f(X),g(Y))\vee d^Z_{\BL^{\kappa}}(\mu_X\circ f^{-1},\mu_Y\circ g^{-1})\Big\},
\end{align*}
where the infimum is taken over all compact metric spaces $(Z,d^Z)$ and isometric embeddings $f:X\to Z$ and 
$g:Y\to Z$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:33:21.443883+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_35557bd18746d177456c4b5d61878f3aa07baa67511443efbca1ae19f259010a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Power-law bounds of arXiv:2606.19583, 'Power-law hypothesis and (un)fairness of PageRank on undirected multi-type PAMs'] Consider the undirected multi-type PAM $(G_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ with finite set of colors $S=\{1,2,\ldots,q\}$ with $q \in \mathbb{N}$. Further, for any $n \in \mathbb{N}$, let $\phi_n$ denote a vertex that is chosen uniformly at random from $G_n$, and let $c \in (0,1)$.
Then there exists a constant $\gamma \in (1,\infty)$ that does not depend on the color $k$ such that, as $r \rightarrow \infty$, the graph-normalized PageRank with damping factor $c$ satisfies
\begin{align}
&\liminf_{n \rightarrow \infty} \mathbb{P}(R_{\phi_n}(G_n)>r \mid X_{\phi_n}=k) \geq (1+o(1))\frac{2\Gamma(m_k+\frac{2}{\varphi_k^{\boldsymbol{m}}})}{\varphi_k^{\boldsymbol{m}} \Gamma(m_k)}\sum_{s=\lceil \gamma r \rceil}^\infty\frac{\Gamma(s)}{\Gamma(s+\frac{2} {\varphi_k^{\boldsymbol{m}}}+1)} \cr
&\limsup_{n \rightarrow \infty} \mathbb{P}(R_{\phi_n}(G_n)>r \mid X_{\phi_n}=k) \leq \frac{2\Gamma(m_k+\frac{2}{\varphi_k^{\boldsymbol{m}}})}{\varphi_k^{\boldsymbol{m}} \Gamma(m_k)}\sum_{s=\lceil r \rceil}^\infty\frac{\Gamma(s)}{\Gamma(s+\frac{2} {\varphi_k^{\boldsymbol{m}}}+1)}.  
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.976112+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3559201d6d1e18d7b70c6953f2bdad4a3da4807edbd14c28db716759273a7a61","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:expdecay of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] Fix $t_0\in[0,1]$, $N\in\N$, and consider $\lambda\in C^\infty(\R)$ with $\mathrm{supp} \,\lambda\subset[t_0-c\mu,t_0]$ for some universal constant $c>0$. Then, the following holds uniformly in $t_0\in[0,1]$ and $\mu\in[0,1]$:
   \begin{equs}
         \norm{K_{N,\mu}\lambda}_{L^p}&\lesssim_c  \mu^{1/p} \norm{K_{N,\mu}\lambda}_{L^\infty}\;\;\text{for every}\;p\in[1,\infty]\,,\\         
       \norm{(t_0-)K_{N,\mu}\lambda}_{L^1}&\lesssim_c  \mu \norm{K_{N,\mu}\lambda}_{L^1}\,. 
   \end{equs} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:18.993358+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_355c185b524ae0d582154164650f4395d26b1289201fe9bf2e68fa02be62ba12","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main-1 of arXiv:2609.02552, 'Resolvent Estimates for the Stokes Operator \\ in a Three-Dimensional Lipschitz Domain'] Let $\Omega$ be a bounded Lipchitz domain   in $\mathbb{R}^3$.
