{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.505453+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_35b8df08681be34f56eabee95647a60a188a8b49537519a3cccc3e07dfb5c7a3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 95 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] The rough convolution operator
\begin{align*}
\mathscr{J} : \big( \scrd_X^{2 \alpha}([0,T],L(V,D(A^2))), \interleave \cdot \interleave_{X,2\alpha} \big) \to \big( \scrd_X^{2 \alpha}([0,T],W), \interleave \cdot \interleave_{X,2\alpha} \big)
\end{align*}
given by
\begin{align*}
(Y,Y') \mapsto \bigg( \int_0^{\cdot} S_{\cdot - s} Y_s \, d \bfx_s, Y \bigg)
\end{align*}
is a continuous linear operator between Banach spaces with operator norm bounded by
\begin{align*}
\| \mathscr{J} \| \leq C (  \interleave \mathbf{X} \interleave_{\alpha} + T^{\alpha} ),
\end{align*}
where the constant $C > 0$ depends on $\alpha$, $T$, $\mathbf{X}$ and $M$, $\omega$, but does not depend on $T \leq 1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:26:02.532639+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_35bf4f20c29a942bed032b1437dfda33d518307a45f94c766b1cec63e320e72a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem special_classification of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Taut foliations on $S^1\times D^2$ and $\mathbb{T}^2\times I$ transverse to the boundary are classified as follows:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item If $\mathcal{F}$ is a taut $C^0$-foliation on $S^1 \times D^2$ transverse to the boundary, then $\mathcal{F}$ is isotopic to the standard foliation by disks.

        \item If $\mathcal{F}$ is a taut $C^0$-foliation on $\mathbb{T}^2 \times I$ transverse to the boundary, then $\mathcal{F}$ is isotopic to a product of a foliation on $\mathbb{T}^2$ with $I$.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.808064+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_35c035c64d33674c573e007b3d993c8d2e73c3ccd7fc08201b9bf28595855f9f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:noise_series of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] Given any orthonormal basis $\{e_k\}_{k\ge 1}$ of $L^2_{\div} (\mathbb{R}^d)$,  or, equivalently, any orthonormal basis $\{\sigma_k = \mathcal{Q}^\frac 12 e_k\}_{k\ge 1}$ of $U_0$, there exists a sequence $\{W^k\}_{k\ge 1}$ of independent one-dimensional $(\mathcal{F}_t)_{t}$-Brownian motions such that
	\begin{equation*}
		W^\mathcal{K}_t 
		= \sum_{k\ge1} \sigma_k W^k_t 
		=\sum_{k\ge1} \mathcal{Q}^\frac 12 e_k W^k_t.
	\end{equation*}
	In particular, if $U_0$ embeds in a Hilbert space $U_1$ with a Hilbert-Schmidt embedding, the series is convergent and defines an $U_1$-valued Wiener process.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.192613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_35c53a7897ab9e6a6751087bed7d5ea0ba777d70bda9136f61402e9b61db45b4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2606.31455, 'Discrete time-multidimensional renewal theory and applications'] If $f(0_d)<1$, then $(\ez-f)$ is convolutionally invertible and \eqref{eq:renewal-equation}
