{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:25:40.139856+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3618bb226339c016cf4681f270e5c79811fcc90e67087b71233a073662ca0c62","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2609.00425, 'Individual and Uniform Eventual Positivity of Self-Adjoint Semigroups'] The space $H$ decomposes as $H = H_{\mathrm{even}} \oplus H_{\mathrm{odd}}$, where
    \begin{align*}
        H_{\mathrm{even}}
        &\coloneqq
        \set{x\in\ell^2(\mathbb{Z}) : x_n=x_{-n}\text{ for all }n\in\mathbb{Z}}, \\
        H_{\mathrm{odd}}
        &\coloneqq
        \set{x\in\ell^2(\mathbb{Z}) : x_n=-x_{-n}\text{ for all }n\in\mathbb{Z}}.
    \end{align*}
    Moreover, the following assertions hold:
    \begin{enumerate}[\upshape (i)]
