{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.362885+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_363746bfe35c2bb53dd9d072a1e690553ec0be03abb993e4451952af2cda38d3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 72 (Size of $k_i$ at the $\sqrt{n}$ threshold) of arXiv:2511.09517, 'From Cannings model to Brownian motion conditioned on local time profile'] Let $i_* := \inf \{1 \le i \le S : k_i > \sqrt{n}\}$. Then there exists $c=c(\varepsilon)>0$ such that for all $n\ge 1$,
