{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.332251+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36530288418f1626ba5e05c6e512be18029fa4c454604bcece7cfb742d6a8857","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:changingMass of arXiv:2601.19630, 'Mass generation for the two dimensional O(N) Linear Sigma Model in the large N limit'] For any $\lambda>0$, $\beta \geq 0$, there exists a unique $m \in (0,1)$, which arises as the solution to the gap equation
