\end{align}
Furthermore, if $H \in C_c^2(\mathbb{R})$, the role of $\widehat{C}$ is fulfilled by some constant $C(H)$ satisfying \eqref{Cinvshift}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.518118+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_368f1e222b33ade5cb09966ff9dbde7984a4ae86aca1074918488901a86f4f63","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem mininf of arXiv:2411.16651, 'On a problem of optimal mixing'] Let $X$ and $Y$ be compact Souslin spaces and let cost function  $c: X\times Y \to [0,+\infty)$ be continuous. Let $\mu_1,\dots,\mu_n,$ and $\nu$ be atomless probability measures on $X$ and $Y$ respectively, then 
