{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.622815+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36926978ea91bf221d74e879f103a71f375bd58a5bd794c9859a7f96c71bb241","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 192 (Top order commutation identities in the first order formulation) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] The following identities hold for $i = 1,2,3$:
	\begin{subequations}
		\begin{align}
