{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:23:25.637824+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_369d7fd8c20594d61ad588163c58e180388979b3e8cedad4f49acc91672d4b13","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2609.01458, 'Confluence relations for $q$-analogues of multiple zeta values'] For $n\in\mathbb{Z}$, we denote by $\mathcal{F}^{n}$ the subset
of $\hat{\mathcal{F}}$ consisting of the elements 
