{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.636518+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36ae5bd058834bcf9f9602af08f4c7706bb61e7e9f0f593b3f82f5c36bc841b0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 27 of arXiv:2609.01362, '{Double cluster swapping for spin models: \\Pfaffian relations and sharpness}'] Let $P \in \Ec$ and $\eps > 0$. There exists $c = c(\eps) > 0$ such that for every $\beta \in (0,1/\eps)$, $h > 0$ and $n \geq 1$,
