{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.059409+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36feb0a08d0775c8fb0ab0de3896851f5f18e87bec6cde0cbfa94a0b31bde816","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Key1 of arXiv:2606.19313, 'Stability of Khintchine-type inequalities via log-monotonicity'] Let $r_k=r_k(X)$ for a random variable $X$. Let $\alpha=(\alpha_1, \alpha_2, \ldots )$ be a weak partition of $q$ with at least two nonzero parts. The following bounds hold.

