{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.732620+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_37017685f56983bc51f10d2ac70adebf9560696c254497e753c51413a7fb80fd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Langevin-to-Laplacian of arXiv:2604.20008, 'Mixing times of Langevin dynamics for \\ spiked matrix models'] For any $f\in C^\infty(\mathbf{S}_N)$, let $\tilde f=f\circ p \in C^{\infty}(\mathcal M)$ be the pullback of $f$ to $\mathcal M$. Then for any $(x,\theta)\in\mathcal M$, and any $H_0$, 
