{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.925147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_37132168b7f8133a6a1617935b5f2611b78d0a56a9ba70684b255b5eaf6032a9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma3.3 of arXiv:2412.05706, 'Quasi-multiplicativity and regularity for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$, $x\in \mathbb{Z}^d$ and $A,D\subset  \widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^d\setminus \widetilde{B}_x(1)$, and any increasing event $\mathsf{F}\subset \{x\xleftrightarrow{\le 0} A\}^{c}$ that is measurable with respect to $\mathcal{F}_{\widehat{\mathcal{C}}_A^{-}}$, we have 
