Here, $\Phi(x):=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\int_{-\infty}^x\exp(-y^2/2)dy$ denotes the cumulative distribution function of the normal distribution $\mathcal{N}(0,1)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

