{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.974794+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3764f2eae3cb1013707999c284a80d455f6dae6eb722a141c9473a1349502300","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2606.11142, 'Strong invariance principles for diffusions, Markov chains and their perturbations.'] (Theorem 1.1 from \cite{Kozhina}). Fix $T > 0$ and let us define a time-grid $\mathbb{T}_N := \{t_i\}_{i=1}^N$ for $N \in \mathbb{N}$. Under assumptions A1, A2, AD3, for $q \in (4d+1, \infty)$, there exist constants $C := C(q) \ge 1$ and $c \in (0, 1]$ such that for all $0 < t_i < t_j \le T$ and all $((x, y), (x', y')) \in (\mathbb{R}^{2d})^2$:
