where $p_\epsilon(t, (x, y), \cdot)$ and $p(t, (x, y), \cdot)$ denote the transition densities at time $t$ of the perturbed and original SDEs respectively, starting from $(x, y)$ at time $0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.824275+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_376522e96ce1d0955b221cbe7d57eebad0a8f821525ada7ff0048318b8d09b8f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo thm2zero of arXiv:2605.06488, 'Continuous-state branching processes with L\'evy-Khintchine drift-interaction: Laplace dua'] Assume $\neg \Htwo$,\ $\Hone$ and $\mathrm{a}=0$ in (equation branchingmechanism of the paper) (no diffusive part in $\Sigma$). There exists a $[0,\infty]$-valued càdlàg Markov process  $X^{\mathrm{e}0}$, such that
\begin{equation*}
\forall x\in [0,\infty],\ \mathbb{P}_x-\text{a.s., } \underset {n\rightarrow \infty}{\lim}\! \downarrow X^{\mathrm{e}0, (n)}_t  =X^{\mathrm{e}0}_t,\ \forall t\in [0,\infty)\text{, and }
X^{\mathrm{e}0, (n)} \underset{n\rightarrow \infty}{\Longrightarrow} X^{\mathrm{e}0} \text{ in } \mathbb{D}_{[0,\infty]}.\end{equation*}
The process $X^{\mathrm{e}0}$ is a Fellerian continuous extension of $X^{\mathrm{m}}$ at $0$, absorbed at $\infty$. It satisfied under $0^+\cdot \infty, \infty^- \cdot 0$, 
