{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.654249+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_376899df26b0f3e09d6ef66885bc23aeedf3a766f22d547b71bcbe474d15bd80","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 14 of arXiv:2605.07184, 'Convergence of Stochastic Gradient Descent with mini-batching and infinite variance'] A random vector $\zeta$ is regularly varying if the sequence of measures $\{\mu_n\}_{n\geq 1}$ defined
  on $\Rset^d\setminus\{0\}$ by
