{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.719219+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_37d4404c243348aeaca52e7fec37ae1e7f4bfcfdcf87059571da08ddc44f1405","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2511.13404, 'Asymptotic stability and mean ergodicity of Feller processes on Polish spaces'] Let $\mathfrak{F}=\{f\in B(\X):\Vert f\Vert_\infty\le1\}$. Then the following three statements are equivalent: 
		\begin{itemize}
			\item [(\runum{1})] There exists unique invariant probability measure $\mu$ for $\Phi$ such that $\forall\,\nu\in\mathcal{P}(\X)$, 
        \begin{equation*}
            \lim\limits_{t\to\infty}\|P_t^*\nu-\mu\|_{TV}=0.
        \end{equation*}
			\item[(\runum{2})] $\Phi$ is uniformly eventually continuous with respect to $\mathfrak{F}$ on $\X$, and there exists $z\in\X$ such that $\Phi$ satisfies the lower bound condition \eqref{eq:LBC_P} at $z$.
            \item[(\runum{3})] There exists $z\in\X$ such that $\Phi$ is uniformly eventually continuous with respect to $\mathfrak{F}$ at $z$ and satisfies the lower bound condition \eqref{eq:LBC_P} at $z$.
