{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.743699+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_38014a1dc0b3b75fa0bbbae3a26daeff607d280265defed831be53a7de9737d4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defin 6 of arXiv:2604.03548, 'Degree-preserving conservative processes and a unified approach for their hydrodynamics'] Let $\rho_0\in L^2(\mathbb T)$. A measurable function $\rho: [0,T] \times \mathbb{T} \to \mathbb R$ is a weak solution to the heat equation with initial profile $\rho_0$
