{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.020050+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_38174898c413dd7d008389031b4fee40332e96e7e4873d94970d75646594d0c6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2605.06556, 'Probability of Quota Violations in Divisor Apportionment Methods with Nonzero Allocations'] Let $A$ be a divisor method that guarantees nonzero allocations on $M$ seats and suppose the populations are ordered such that $p_1 < \cdots < p_n$. The apportionment $A(p_1, \dots, p_n)$ exhibits a \emph{quota violation caused by nonzero allocations} if the following conditions hold:
