{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.773378+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_38292070c836eb7bbe93721e0bdfc78f281446fad9d072f8f755b4ec9c9aaa28","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:locally dissipative of arXiv:2411.01364, 'Global Dynamics of Granular Media Equations via Stochastic Order'] The equation (equation eq:mvsystem of the paper) is called locally dissipative at $a\in\mathbb R$ with configuration $(r,g)$, if
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item the function $g:\mathbb R_+\times\mathbb R_+\to\mathbb R$ satisfies, for all $x\in\mathbb R$, $\mu\in\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$,
\begin{equation*}
-2xV'(x+a)-2x(W'*\mu)(x)+\sigma^2(x+a)\leq -g(x^2,\|\mu\|_2^2);
\end{equation*}
\item the number $r>0$ and the function $g$ satisfy
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
&g(\cdot,r^2) \text{ is continuous and convex};\\
&\inf_{0\leq w\leq r^2}g(z,w)=g(z,r^2);\\
&\inf_{z\geq r^2}g(z,r^2)>0.
\end{split}
\end{equation*}
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:27:14.874015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_383048abe82d1009e2e3195433776f68846adc8f4eb46834f91cdcfb3fcea54c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2608.23462, '2608.23462'] Suppose that Assumption~\ref{assu:frozenLipschitz} is satisfied, that $(\hat Y^x_t)_{t \geq 0}$ is $2$-dissipative and that $f$ is $L_f$-Lipschitz. Then,
