{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.802141+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_383d6ea97ef6eea413ca8dc4084f6ddeeb138b09011418676763925bd000b36f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition P:CQCLT of arXiv:2606.23865, 'Uniform-in-time Gaussian fluctuations for multiscale nonlinear stochastic systems via Mall'] [bour_spilio_2025]
Let $T>0$ be fixed, $\theta_t^\varepsilon \triangleq \frac{X_t^\varepsilon-\bar{X}_t}{\sqrt{\varepsilon}}$ and $N \sim \mathscr{N}(0, \sigma_t^2).$ For sufficiently small $\varepsilon$ and $\eta,$ and $0<\xi < \frac{1}{2},$ there exists a time-dependent positive constant $C$ such that
\begin{multline*}
\sup_{t \in [0,T]}d_W \left( \theta_t^\varepsilon,N \right) \le C \left[ \eta^{\frac{1}{4}} + \varepsilon^{\frac{1}{4}} + \left( \frac{\eta}{\varepsilon}- \frac{1}{\gamma^2} \right)^{\frac{1}{2}}  + \left( \frac{\eta}{\varepsilon} \right)^{\frac{1}{2}} \eta^{\frac{1}{2}-\xi} + \varepsilon^{\frac{1}{2}-\xi} \right]\\
+ C \left( \left( \frac{\eta}{\varepsilon} \right)^{\frac{1}{2}} \eta^{\frac{1}{4}} + \left( \frac{\eta}{\varepsilon} \right) \eta^{\frac{1}{4}} + \left( 1+ \frac{\eta}{\varepsilon} \right)e^{-\frac{CT}{\eta}} \right).
\end{multline*}
where, $\sigma_t^2$ represents the limiting variance and is defined in equation (equation E:Limiting-Variance of the paper) below. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.126616+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_383f7857b580be989c34153ad67d280985b2aea9218a3f60a46c517a93a06d9b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:int-2 of arXiv:2510.06891, 'Multivariate CLT for L\'evy processes: convergence rates without moment assumptions'] Let $\bm{X}$ and $\bm{Z}$ be as in Theorem~(thm:int-0 of the paper) and assume $\mathds{E}[|\bm{X}_1|^2]<\infty$. Suppose $\mathscr{A}\subset\mathscr{C}$ and that
there exists $U\in\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R})$ such that 
$U^d\in\mathscr{A}$ and $\mathds{P}(Z\in U)^d\ne\mathds{E}[Z^2\1_U(Z)]$ for  a standard Gaussian random variable $Z$ in $\mathbb{R}$. Then $\mathds{E}[|\bm{X}_1|^2\max\{0,\log(|\bm{X}_1|)\}]<\infty$ if and only if
\begin{equation}

t \mapsto t^{-1}d_\mathscr{A}\big((\bm{X}_t-t\mathds{E}\bm{X}_1)/\sqrt{t},\bm{\sigma}\bm{Z}\big)\in L^1_{\mathrm{loc}}(+\infty).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:33:12.355575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3848f84eb297c57bdca552db5d49bbff6cdbce8130a7803ff7538777124c537f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 224 of arXiv:2608.29416, 'Algorithmic threshold for high-dimensional projection pursuit I: general theory'] In the spherical (resp.\ Ising) projection pursuit problem, we say that an algorithm $\cA$ (as in \eqref{eq:algorithms-as-maps}) \textbf{$(\ioeps,\gamma)$-attains} a target measure $\mu\in \cP_2(\bbR)$ if the output $\bx = \cA(\bG,\bg^{\aux})$ satisfies, with probability at least $\gamma$, \emph{both} of the following properties:
    \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
         \item  
         $\bx \in S_N(\iota)$ (resp.\ $\Sigma_N(\iota)$);
         \item 
         $\bbW_2(\mu,\mu_{\bG}(\bx)) \le \ioeps$.
    \end{enumerate}
For $\fq \in [1,2)$, we say that $\cA$ is \textbf{$(\fq,\iotamsr,\iotasol,\gamma)$-confined} to a subset $\cM\subseteq \cP_2(\bbR)$ if the output $\bx$ satisfies, with probability at least $\gamma$, \emph{either} of the following properties:
    \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
        \item  $\bx \notin S_N(\iotasol)$ (resp.\ $\Sigma_N(\iotasol)$);
        \item  $\bbW_\fq(\mu_{\bG}(\bx),\cM) \le \iotamsr$.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.634143+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_384a666a9875907553c2e8501703f93e09f6f0f38c72f81d7be97c58c1564e2b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:secondhalfsumgeneral of arXiv:2412.09145, 'Asymptotic expansions for normal deviations of random walks conditioned to stay positive'] For all $a, b>0$, $a\notin \mathbb{Z}$ and $t \in (0,1)$ there exist numbers $c_{i,\nu}$ such that, uniformly in $z$,
\begin{multline*}
    \sum_{k=2}^{\lfloor n/2\rfloor} 
        \frac{z^m}{(n-k+t)^{b}(k-t)^a}
        e^{-\frac{z^2}{2 (n-k+t)}}
\\
=
    \frac{z^m}{n^b}
    e^{-\frac{z^2}{2 n}}
    \sum_{\nu=0}^{\lfloor a \rfloor-1}
        \frac{z^{2\nu}}{n^{\nu}}
        \sum_{i=\nu}^{\lfloor a \rfloor-1}
            \frac{c_{i,\nu}g_{a-i}(t)}{n^{i}}
+
    O\left(\frac{1}{n^{a+b-m/2-1}}\right),
\end{multline*}
where
\begin{align*}
    g_{\lambda}(t) 
=
    \sum_{k=2}^{\infty}
        \frac{1}{(k-t)^{\lambda}}.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.548450+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3853b40874b376d500b175c4855285001c2b80850421888c888d56e36a6f65bf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 38 of arXiv:2604.01852, 'The on/off Brownian snake'] Let $x=(b,0) \in E=\mathbb{R}^d \times [0,\infty)$ and let $\varepsilon>0$. Let $h \coloneqq \varepsilon /2$ and let $X=(W,V)$ be a snake with distribution $\mathbb{N}_x(\cdot | T_h < \infty)$. Then the process $(\Tilde{\mathcal{Z}}^{(\varepsilon, \rm d)}_s, \Tilde{\mathcal{Z}}^{(\varepsilon, \rm a)}_s)_{s \geq 0}$ defined by
    \begin{equation}
        (\Tilde{\mathcal{Z}}^{(\varepsilon, \rm d)}_s, \Tilde{\mathcal{Z}}^{(\varepsilon, \rm a)}_s) \coloneqq \Big(\sum_{\substack{p: A^X_{\gamma^{(h)}_p}(s)=0,\\ H^X_{\gamma^{(h)}_p}(s) \in [Y_p^{(h)}, Z_p^{(h)}),}} \delta_{W_{\gamma^{(h)}_p}(H^X_{\gamma^{(h)}_p}(s))}, \sum_{\substack{p: A^X_{\gamma^{(h)}_p}(s) = 1 \\ H^X_{\gamma^{(h)}_p}(s) \in [Y_p^{(h)}, Z_p^{(h)}),}} \delta_{W_{\gamma^{(h)}_p}(H^X_{\gamma^{(h)}_p}(s))}\Big)
    \end{equation}
    is an $\text{ooBBM}(4/\varepsilon, c, \Tilde{c})$ and with initial state $(0,\delta_b)$, i.e. starting from a single active particle at spatial location $b$.
    \begin{proof}
