{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.068100+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3876b3f001f84abde809a2318742d6bd88e36bca635c567bced50495eb9cbb20","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:dissipation of arXiv:2606.28575, 'Global smooth solutions by high mode Lie-Transport noise for Logarithmically Hyperdissipat'] Let $M\ge 1$ and $r_0, \gamma$ satisfying $-\frac{1}{2} < r_0 < \gamma < 0$. There exists $\nu_0>0$ depending only on $M$ such that for all $\nu>\nu_0$ and all $\|\omega_0\|_{H^{\gamma}_g}\le M $, there exists a unique global solution $\omega^{{\operatorname{det}}} $ of 
    \begin{equation}
\begin{cases}
    \partial_t\omega^{{\operatorname{det}}} + \mathcal{L}_u \omega^{{\operatorname{det}}} + A\omega^{{\operatorname{det}}} - \nu\Delta \omega^{{\operatorname{det}}}   =0 \\
    u= K[ \omega^{{\operatorname{det}}}].
    \end{cases}
\end{equation}
Moreover, it holds, for some $\eta_0 >0$  
    \begin{align}
    \sup_{t>0}\|\omega^{\operatorname{det}}_t\|_{H_g^\gamma}^2 + \|\omega^{\operatorname{det}} \|_{L^2(0, +\infty; H^{\gamma+1}_g)}^2 &\lesssim \|\omega_0\|_{H_g^\gamma}^2 \\
        \|\omega^{\operatorname{det}}_t\|_{H^{r_0}_g} &\lesssim  e^{-\eta_0 t} \|\omega_0\|_{H^\gamma_g} .
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

