{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.361276+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3897d6a41a19b38f14ac8ab61c53654454d8d16fcfac96bbaaec8e8e9dc3f4bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 (Change of variables) of arXiv:2604.21389, 'Existence and uniqueness for \\ singular stochastic differential equations \\ with piecewi'] Let Hypothesis~\hypref{hyp:nu} and assume that $b$ and $\sigma$ are measurable and locally bounded.

For every $(X,B)$, weak non-explosive solution to~\eqref{eqn:SDE_general}, let $I$ denote the smallest interval such that~$X_t\in I$ for all $t\geq 0$ $\mathbb{P}$-a.s.. Then $(\Phi_\nu(X),B)$ is a weak non-explosive solution to the classical SDE
