{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.501923+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_38a994a036fe99568e0f74a686887e68150782843b19532b39d70f6c939ceb09","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def : LDP/ContinuousMetric of arXiv:2412.03320, 'Large deviation principle at speed $n$ for the random metric in first-passage percolation'] Let $n \ge 1$. We extend $\BoxPT^{(b)}$ to $\intervalleff0n^d$ as follows. For all edges $(x^-, x^+), (y^-,y^+) \in \edges{\intint0n^d}$ and all $x\in \intervalleff{x^-}{x^+}$, $y\in \intervalleff{y^-}{y^+}$, we define
	\begin{equation}
		\TightBoxPT(x,y) \coloneqq \min_{\substack{x' \in \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\{ x^-,x^+ \aftergroup\egroup\originalright\} \\ y' \in \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\{ y^-,y^+ \aftergroup\egroup\originalright\}  } } \p{ \norme[1]{x-x'}\tau_{(x^-, x^+)} + \TightBoxPT(x',y') + \norme[1]{y-y'}\tau_{(y^-, y^+)} }.
	\end{equation}
	We then define, for all $x,y\in \intervalleff0n^d$,
	\begin{equation}

		\TightBoxPT(x,y) \coloneqq \p{ b\norme[1]{x-y} } \wedge  \min_{x', y'} \p{ b\norme[1]{x-x'} + \TightBoxPT(x',y') + b\norme[1]{y' - y}  },
	\end{equation}
	where the minimum is taken on all pairs of points, belonging to a pair of (maybe equal) edges in $\edges{\intint0n^d}$. For all $x,y\in X$, we define
	\begin{equation}

		\TightSPT(x,y) \coloneqq \frac1n \TightBoxPT(nx,ny).
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.360502+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_38b39ddc1380577bdb50445bf9d3fb93109976b4fa20b507427fd1c5407f2bcd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:crossing of arXiv:2606.11503, 'Percolation on hierarchical lattices'] For any directed graph $G_{1}$ satisfying (e:hypothesis of the paper), we have
