{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.734722+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_38e39e5aff91f346af3ec4825089eca8166d5af0597bde2da25c913e3670bc65","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 10 of arXiv:2609.02197, '2609.02197'] Let $f \in \mathscr{S}'$ and $h:\mathbb{Z}^d\longrightarrow\mathbb{C}$ be a function such that $$\exists \left(\mu,r\right) \in \mathbb{R}_+\times \mathbb{N},\forall x \in \mathbb{Z}^d,\left|h\left(x\right)\right|\leq \mu\left(1+\left|x\right|\right)^r.$$
