{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.417410+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_38e53976943abaae1fddbabe2760d7e9fa6e25de109aeb6278d88ff373f4efaf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 104 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] In the setting of Lemma~\ref{Lemma_continuity_varyinf_ff}, there exists $\varepsilon > 0$ depending only on the constants in the assumptions with the following property. If $\boldsymbol{\mu}^{\textnormal{I}}$ satisfies the off-criticality Assumption~\ref{Assumptions_offcrit} and for any $g,h \in [H]$ and $e \in [\mathfrak{e}]$
