{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.630996+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_390f8e2760a073add37f42e3462163d5df827e757edd379d6bfd5979002c5bde","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:scaling limit of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] Let $\mu=\mu_n$ satisfy $\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty}\mu\sqrt{n}=\alpha\in\mathbb R$.
    Let $\mathbf{T}_n=\mathbf T^\mu$ be a $\mu$-height-biased tree of size $n$, let $d_n$ denote the graph distance on $\mathbf{T}_n$ with each edge having length 1, and let $\sigma_n$ denote the uniform measure on the  vertices of ~$\mathbf T_n$. Then
    \begin{align*}
        \left(\mathbf{T}_n,\frac{d_n}{\sqrt{2n}}, {\sigma_n}\right) \overset d\longrightarrow \big(\mathbfcal{T}_{\alpha},d_{\alpha}\,, \sigma_{\alpha}\big),
    \end{align*}
    where the convergence in distribution above is with respect to the Gromov-Hausdorff-Prokhorov (GHP) topology. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:53.447345+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_39105fa62429fa61ea3d032f1d8613087660993b11ad317e7b5e68780e597306","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2606.15843, 'Long-time behaviour of DLRA for SDEs'] Suppose Assumptions (H3), (H7) and (H8) hold.
			Moreover, suppose  Assumption~\ref{AS:relation2} holds. Furthermore, suppose the initial condition $(\zeta,\xi)\in L^p(\Omega,V_r(\bb R^d)\times\bb R^r)$. Then, there exists a constant $C(b,\sigma,p)>0$, one has
             \begin{align}
