{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:07.835188+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_39304daba1db91a6bd89852981a9aa4d51c7f69c0ae3bd161d27a7ae0ff3fc21","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm_limit_curves of arXiv:2608.09105, 'Longest convex chains with i.i.d.\ points'] Assume (equation p_cont of the paper) and (equation p_lower of the paper).
Then for every $\varepsilon>0$, there exists $\delta=\delta(\varepsilon,\mathfrak{p})>0$ such that
