{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:09.088922+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_39350e098166ec805e939a09b1a837e3e9b209102f74ddff70ae6af0c3f2758c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Upper bound of cumulants Wigner of arXiv:2411.11341, 'Ultra high order cumulants and quantitative CLT for polynomials in Random Matrices'] Let $\mathcal{X}\sim Wigner$.  Consider the polynomial $P(\mathcal{X},\mathcal{D})$ in ((def of P of the paper)) and the random variable $\mathbf{X}$ defined in ((object of the paper)).  Suppose that $\mathbf{C}_1$ is satisfied. 
