{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.605116+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3952865851eb1874e14d2433a4ebc6976c953bedbc2ae430ef745840d15acedd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition CH1 of arXiv:2412.05142, 'Strong convergence of the Euler scheme for singular kinetic SDEs driven by $\alpha$-stable'] For $s>0$, $q\in[1,\infty]$ and ${\boldsymbol{p}}\in[1,\infty]^2$, an equivalent norm of ${\mathbb B}^{s,q}_{{\boldsymbol{p}};{\boldsymbol{a}}}$ is given by
