are satisfied. Then, there exists a constant $\mathfrak L>0$, depending only on the structural data $\alpha,\beta,\delta,\theta,T,C$, such that, for every weak mild solutions $(X,W)$ and $(Y,W)$ to \eqref{abstract_formulation} with initial data $x,y\in H$, respectively, in the sense of Definition \ref{def:mild-sol}, defined on the same probability space, it holds that 
