 \end{equation}
In particular, pathwise uniqueness holds for \eqref{abstract_formulation}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.013718+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_39afd2e1556923ef940f8d3492737260d2955d4965341a8a00bdd1974c3e7007","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 70 of arXiv:2609.02850, 'Canonical-row Chern flow on Bott--Samelson towers:\\ realizable-volume models for Schubert'] For every $w\in S_n$, the support of $G_w$ is $M^\natural$-convex.  In
