{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.354521+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_39cf5dba63e09e6374094ab374f0ffe43c1ad49110debc350dad7cfe646c323b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.randommeasures of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] Let $(m^n)_{n\in{\mathbb N}}$ be a sequence of random elements of $\mathcal{P}_p({\mathbb R})$, and let $m \in \mathcal{P}_p({\mathbb R})$. Suppose that the following properties hold:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item for every test function $\phi \in C_b({\mathbb R})$, $\langle \phi, m^n \rangle \to \langle \phi, m \rangle$ in probability,
        \item for all $\varepsilon > 0$, there exist $R > 0$ and $N \in {\mathbb N}$ such that
        \begin{align*}\mathbb{P} \bigg[ \int_{{\mathbb R}} |x|^p \mathbf{1}_{\{|x| > R\}} dm^n > \varepsilon \bigg] < \varepsilon,\qquad \text{ for all } n \geq N.
        \end{align*}
    \end{enumerate}
    Then,
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbf{d}_p(m^n,m) \longrightarrow 0\quad \text{in probability.}
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.328919+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_39d3397ddd956bd5c2299535198b0ffb42f702aa4123f934c502d50118ddf825","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:oriented_cone_horiz of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $X$ be a unit vector in $V_1$. For $p\in\mathbb G$ and $\beta,\rho>0$, the \emph{oriented intrinsic horizontal cone} in the direction of $X$ is defined as
