{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.431332+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a043e45f68f19d537aecab5825596e3398ec0f27b63afd66bbb91db540d92e1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma whatislemma2 of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] For any $B>0$, and any $\zeta\in\Gamma_B$, consider the random matrix $A_n\sim\operatorname{Sym}_n(\zeta)$. For any 
