{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.194251+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a27775051845c47089acfd7d1189d2427d83046798ab16129812e162a18a348","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 7 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] Let $\delta\in (0,1/2),\mathsf C>0$, $X\sim \Hyp(n_1,n,m)$ with $\mathbb EX=\frac{n_1m}{n}\leq  \mathsf CN^\delta$. There exists constants $C,c$ depending on $\mathsf C$ such that
