{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.588763+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a297b2adf308cbc05f3c5e20647d3dc1e5db5985cf9e2420bd269056858b32f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:time-reversed-detailed of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] Let $p(s,x;t,y)$ denote the transition density of the forward process. If:
\begin{enumerate}
\item The coefficients $b_i$ and $\sigma_{ij}$ are bounded and Lipschitz continuous
\item The diffusion matrix $a_{ij} = \sum_k \sigma_{ik}\sigma_{jk}$ is uniformly elliptic
\item The transition density satisfies $\int p(0,x;t_*,y)\mu_0(dx) = \mu_{t_*}(dy)$
\end{enumerate}
Then the time-reversed process $\tilde{X}_i(s) = X_i(t_* - s)$ satisfies:
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{d} \tilde{X}_i(s) = \tilde{b}_i(s,\tilde{\mathbf{X}}(s))\mathrm{d} s + \sum_{j=1}^K \sigma_{ij}(t_*-s,\tilde{\mathbf{X}}(s))\mathrm{d} \tilde{B}_j(s)
\end{equation}
where $\tilde{B}_j$ are independent Brownian motions and
\begin{equation}
\tilde{b}_i(s,x) = -b_i(t_*-s,x) + \sum_{j=1}^K \sum_{k=1}^K \frac{\partial}{\partial x_k}[a_{ij}(t_*-s,x)] + 2\sum_{j=1}^K a_{ij}(t_*-s,x)\frac{\partial \log \rho_{t_*-s}}{\partial x_j}(x)
\end{equation}
with $\rho_t$ the marginal density at time $t$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.617359+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a2c45e9c523b7b734e23446b3ee3c288b125111b9e15cfc0dedad29e0bc6f90","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Let~$\{T_k\}_{k\ge0}$ be as defined in Corollary~\ref{cor-1.3}. Then for all $n\ge1$,
