{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.795411+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a305967a657cc75f636780296f7b069c35cfb60fa82aa38eeb1dc41c742818e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:tailrl-binary-recovery of arXiv:2609.02987, 'Tail Likelihood Reinforcement Learning'] Suppose $r_i\in\{0,1\}$ and let
$M:=\sum_{i=1}^N\mathbf 1\{r_i=1\}$. If $M>0$, then every successful
rollout receives weight $1/M$ and every unsuccessful rollout receives weight
zero. Hence the uncentered TailRL{} estimator reduces to
\begin{equation}
g_{\mathrm{TailRL}}^{(N)}(x)
=
\frac{1}{M}
\sum_{i:r_i=1}S_i,

\end{equation}
which is the MaxRL estimator. After mean-centering, successful rollouts have
weight $1/M-1/N$ and unsuccessful rollouts have weight $-1/N$. If $M=0$,
all uncentered and centered weights are zero.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.861488+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a323983726b6871c3dfaa9361069bdb1e103c18bdc3cf0f5e954dd3aeba8f78","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] For $h$ such that $\frac Th\in \mathbb{N}$ and $j\in \{0,\dots,\frac Th\}$ let $(\hX_{jh}^{h,\delta},\xi_{jh})_{0\le j\le T/h}$ be defined in \eqref{eq_Xhdelta} and $(\tiX_{jh}^{h,\delta},\xi_{jh})_{0\le j\le T/h}$ be defined in \eqref{Eq:Half_step}. 

