    In particular their joint laws are equal, i.e.\ it holds that $\mathcal{L}\bigl( (\hX_{jh}^{h,\delta},\xi_{jh})_{j\le T/h}\bigr) =\mathcal{L}\bigl((\tiX_{jh}^{h,\delta},\xi_{jh})_{j\le T/h}\bigr)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.593661+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a3240d287ad19b52339621a823be3a704cb8d85d7432ccd12d869e1fca5286b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 (Exact three-summand representation of $\MAX_7$) of arXiv:2608.25221, 'Representing MAX functions using two-hidden-layer ReLU networks'] We have the following identity
