{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.626426+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a9edb5ceea132aa66ac6392c872a50a261cb06089ad0166a5add2553f60a7dc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Kolmogorov criterion of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] Let $\{(X^n_{t})_{t\in \mathbb R}\}_{n\geq 1}$ be a sequence of $\mathbb R^d$-valued continuous processes defined on  probability spaces $(\Omega^n,\mathcal{F}^n,P^n)$ such that
