{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.360157+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ac9346b58889844ba37e73c251ccfce9e65114aeba06b86fb71be15d6d0f470","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 32 of arXiv:2511.09517, 'From Cannings model to Brownian motion conditioned on local time profile'] If $T_{\lfloor (\log n)^{\frac{3+2\varepsilon}{6}}\rfloor}-T_M=\sum_{m=M+1}^{\lfloor(\log n)^{\frac{3+2\varepsilon}{6}}\rfloor}\zeta_m\ge\tfrac{1}{3}\delta n$, then
