{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.993303+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ae3e8878333ecdfc5547cf5d3ac99cdde2ad98735f593298791b9d429012624","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem polynomial theorem of arXiv:2412.01086, 'Spectral radii of sparse non-Hermitian random matrices'] Suppose $Z$ has Weibull entries with shape parameter $\alpha >0$ and $p_n\gg (\log n)^{\frac{2}{\alpha}}/n$. Then 
