{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.944446+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3aeece95fd6c727eea3b1f54755c0a423e9858a37f04af834ba5107bb64e363c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor other_approximation of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] The discrete approximations $\omega_n,\omega_{\mathrm{black},n}$, $\omega_{\mathrm{white},n}$ satisfy
