{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:49.833403+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3b1f15e9252807391aa714088e549ad8604ec9f7e4f4acab88cbbbe20cb3fb01","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 8 of arXiv:2506.12632, 'Point process convergence of extremes in $K$-symmetric exclusion'] Suppose $p$ satisfies Condition \ref{lighttail}, $\nu$ satisfies Condition \ref{initialprofilecond}, and $\eta_0 \sim \nu_L$, where $L \uparrow \infty$ as $t \to \infty$. If $\lim_{t\to\infty} L\big(\frac{\log t}{t}\big)^{1/2} > 0$, then for any $m \ge 1$, 
