{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.473114+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3bc4799e998be0004ccd00f811641a5f8f260776a9b504e6398868f3a83b5eb4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma divergencelemma of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Let $P_{t,O} = \exp(t \mathsf{L}_O)$ be a symmetric contraction $C_0$-semigroup satisfying (assp:locoercive of the paper). For any $T > 0$ and $x_t \in L^2_\perp([0,T]; \mathcal{H}_O)$, there exists a solution $(z_t, y_t) \in H^1_{\mathsf{L}_O} \times H^2_{\mathsf{L}_O}$ to the abstract divergence equation:
