{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.420286+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3bc5f3e9acdab8824a16738cb7de96fc53267ea974f000fd21a791879e6d6215","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 127 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Given these data, the master problem asks to find an $H$-tuple of functions $\boldsymbol{F}(z)=(F_h(z))_{h=1}^H$ having the following properties for any $h \in [H]$.
