{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.781481+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c2918f1ab248ef01137763b35921b007d220ac8918d04dca14091ea5d138944","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lm Concentration for specific functionals of theta of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] There is a $C=C(T,k)>0$ such that on a set $A_k$ with $\mathbb{P}(A_k)>1-C'(T,k)n^{-2}$, the following holds. 
