{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.097918+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c2f5c8374a88c2401bc4783fae2880eec1d07c429ab3124ac4166a8f9c44cab","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm Lemm6.4 of arXiv:2412.08497, 'Time discretization of Quadratic Forward-Backward SDEs with singular drift'] Let $(Y_{i}^1, Z_{i}^1)$ and $(Y_{i}^2, Z_{i}^2)$ be two solutions to the scheme (equation linBTZ1 of the paper), respectively, such that $(G_i^1,\xi^1)$ and $(G_i^2,\xi^2)$ satisfy Assumption (assum56 of the paper). For $0\leq i\leq n$, let
				\begin{align*}
					\Upsilon_i:= \prod_{j=i}^{N-1}(1+\delta t_j\Gamma_j +\delta t_j\Pi_j \cdot {H}_j),
				\end{align*}
				where 
				\begin{align*}
					\Gamma_j:&= \frac{G_j^1(\mathbb{E}[{Y}_{j+1}^1/\mathfrak{F}_{t_j}],{Z}_j^{1})-G_j^1(\mathbb{E}[{Y}_{j+1}^{2}/\mathfrak{F}_{t_j}],{Z}_j^{1})}{\mathbb{E}[\delta{Y}_{j+1}/\mathfrak{F}_{t_j}]}{\bf 1}_{\{\mathbb{E}[\delta{Y}_{j+1}/\mathfrak{F}_{t_j}]\neq 0\}},\\
					\Pi_j:&= \frac{G_j^1(\mathbb{E}[{Y}_{j+1}^{2}/\mathfrak{F}_{t_j}],{Z}_j^{1})-G_j^1(\mathbb{E}[{Y}_{j+1}^{2}/\mathfrak{F}_{t_j}],{Z}_j^{2})}{|\delta{Z}_{j}|^2}\delta{Z}_{j}{\bf 1}_{\{\delta{Z}_{j}\neq 0\}}.
				\end{align*}
				Then the following representation holds
				\begin{align}
					\delta Y_i = \mathbb{E}\Big[\Upsilon_i\delta Y_{t_N} + \sum_{k=i}^{N-1}\delta t_k\delta G_k \frac{\Upsilon_i}{\Upsilon_k}\Big/\mathfrak{F}_{t_i}\Big].
				\end{align}
				Moreover, the following comparison principle holds true: $ Y_i^1\geq Y_i^2$,
				whenever $Y_N^1 \geq Y_N^2$ and $G_j^1(Y_i^2, Z_i^2)\geq G_j^2( Y_i^2, Z_i^2)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.361607+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c2ff53531735b33bd856835b6fcec100ba57bd6e87e6c6425c58de1c4dfd4b7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 53 (Uniform selection pair) of arXiv:2511.09517, 'From Cannings model to Brownian motion conditioned on local time profile'] Fix a base height $h^*$. For $0\le h\le h^*$, $1\le p\le q_n(h^*)$ and $1\le k\le q_n(h)$, let $(A,\mathcal{V})$ be a pair consisting of
\begin{itemize}
    \item an event $A$ measurable with respect to $\mathcal{G}_{h}^{(p)}\vee \sigma(\Lambda_h)$, and
    \item a random vector $\mathcal{V}$ of $k$ vertices taking values in $\{x^{h}_1,\ldots, x^{h}_{q_n(h)}\}$.
\end{itemize}
We say that $(A,\mathcal{V})$ is a $(p,h,k)$-uniform selection pair if, under $\mathbb{P}_n$,
\[
(\mathcal{V}\mid A)\,\overset{d}{=}\,\{u^{h}_1,\ldots,u^{h}_k\},
\]
that is, conditionally on $A$, the vector $\mathcal{V}$ has the same distribution as a uniformly chosen $k$-tuple of distinct vertices at height $h$. When \(p=q_n(h^*)\), we abbreviate this as an \((h,k)\)-uniform selection pair.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.666248+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c3cb00324e98331b6232f3665f8f5071b269e08411ff7afed05c77d7ba139ea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:2s5c-taylor of arXiv:2411.00930, '\bf \Large Asymptotic Product-form Steady-state for Multiclass Queueing Networks: A Reentr'] Let $\theta(r)\in\mathbb{R}^5$ be given for each $r\in(0,1)$, satisfying $|\theta(r)|\leq cr$. Denoting $\theta=\theta(r)$, as $r\to0$, we have
