{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.856425+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c404b0f6ced3c0786f055f6ec4fdbf04c6620ad3d761a6c6a987668b60651f3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2607.17030, 'Stationary measures for log-gamma polymer on a strip and in half-space'] If $-\alpha<u<0$ and $v>u$ then,   as $N\to\infty$, we have
 \begin{equation}

     \GG_N(\alpha,u,v)\sim \Gamma(\alpha-u)^{N}\Gamma(\alpha+u)^N \tfrac{\Gamma(\alpha+v)}{\Gamma(\alpha-u)}\EE[R^{-u-v}],
 \end{equation}
 where $R$ is  given by \eqref{Rseries}.

If $-\alpha<v<0$ and $u>v$, then, as $N\to\infty$, we have
\begin{equation}
  \GG_N(\alpha,u,v)\sim
  \Gamma(\alpha+v)^N\Gamma(\alpha-v)^N
  \tfrac{\Gamma(\alpha+u)}{\Gamma(\alpha-v)}
  \EE[(R')^{-u-v}],
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
  R'  =1+\zeta_1'+\zeta_1'\zeta_2'
  +\ldots+\zeta_1'\dots\zeta_n'+\dots,
\end{equation}
and $(\zeta_i')_{i\ge1}$ are i.i.d.\ $\mathrm{Beta}_{II}(\alpha+v,\alpha-v)$ random variables. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.740896+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c472319df296c0a8ac00995adf329a6fca8c4f2d13bd85571504acd08b44a56","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Let $\Phi = (\varphi_t)$ be a nonwandering flow on $M$ tangent to a continuous nonvanishing vector field $X$.
