{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.966033+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c6741c92b4be080f57b386410291ed34d9830342c563734ae41e3349e6f3deb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm cokernel distribution theorem 1_intro of arXiv:2505.11700, 'Distribution of the cokernels of determinantal row-sparse matrices'] (Theorem (thm: cokernel distribution theorem 1 of the paper)) Let $G$ be a finite abelian group and $\mathcal{P}$ be a finite set of primes including those dividing $|G|$. 
Assume that a sequence $(k_n)_{n=1}^{\infty}$ satisfies the following:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item for every prime $p$ in $\mathcal{P}$, $p \nmid k_n$ for all sufficiently large $n$;
    \item for every $\epsilon>0$, $k_n < n^{\epsilon}$ for all sufficiently large $n$;
    \item  if $2 \in \mathcal{P}$, then for every $\delta>0$, $\delta \log\log n < k_n$ for all sufficiently large $n$.
\end{enumerate}
Then
$$
\lim_{n\to \infty} \mathbb{P}\left(\bigoplus_{p \in \mathcal{P}} \mathrm{cok}(A_n)_p \cong G\right) = \frac{1}{|\mathrm{Aut}(G)|}\prod_{p\in \mathcal{P}} \prod_{i=1}^\infty (1-p^{-i})
= \prod_{p \in \mathcal{P}} \nu_{\mathrm{CL}, p}(G_p).
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.958451+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c6aaf6e5d4685bc5f6ba30233e71d8c72b3850992502577238a5c21d463dfeb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 (Normalized Fourier expansion) of arXiv:2606.26065, 'Localized Centered Second-Chaos Operators'] Let $K>4d$.  On the support of the four dyadic cutoffs, every amplitude $m$ with finite norm~\eqref{eq:symbol-norm} admits an expansion
