{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.669835+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c85e0fa31a2bed5fd1e5be6065eb6aed6d6f8cbe7e170b79fbc8b69dd2a8ef5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2604.24390, 'Weak solutions to distribution-dependent stochastic Volterra equations'] Suppose Assumption~\ref{ass:volatility} and~\ref{ass:kernel}. Let $(A^m)_{m \in \bN}$, $(M^m)_{m \in \bN}$ and $(X^m)_{m \in \bN}$ be as in \eqref{eq:Am}, \eqref{eq:Mm} and \eqref{eq:Euler_approx_process}, respectively. Then, there is a subsequence $(X^{m_k},A^{m_k},M^{m_k})_{k \in \bN}$ of $(X^m,A^m,M^m)_{m \in \bN}$ and a probability space $(\tilde{\Omega}, \tilde{\mathcal{F}},\tilde{\bP})$ with stochastic processes $\hat{X}^k,\hat{A}^k,\hat{M}^k$, $k \in \bN$, $\tilde{X}, \tilde{A}, \tilde{M}$ and a Brownian motion $(\tilde{B}_t)_{t\in [0,T]}$ on it with $(\hat{X}^k, \hat{A}^k, \hat{M}^k) \stackrel{\mathscr{D}}{\sim} (X^{m_k},A^{m_k},M^{m_k})$, $k \in \bN$, such that $(\hat{X}^k, \hat{A}^k, \hat{M}^k) \to (\tilde{X},\tilde{A},\tilde{M})$ in $C([0,T]; \bR^d \times \bR^d \times \bR^d)$ as $k \to \infty$ $\tilde{\bP}$-a.s., where $\tilde{M}$ is a local martingale with representation
  \begin{equation*}
    \tilde{M}_t=\int_0^t \sigma(s,\tilde{X}_s, \L(\tilde{X}_s)) \dd \tilde{B}_s, \qquad t \in [0,T].
  \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:02:34.822202+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c89b966e7f1ce6efbcc1dbbd789adb50e77fc1065c2542b3da53a92c5fffae1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 (Finite-time reduction for first-hit decisions) of arXiv:2607.19752, 'Weak Equilibrium Measures and Capacity--Hitting Identities\\ for the Hypoelliptic Third-Or'] Suppose Assumptions~\ref{ass:U} and~\ref{ass:controlled-coefficients} hold,
