{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.775683+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3cb544d4f92fd17ca18cc19f08fc7a97181d8363f3acd168c3976a853715c975","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:reversal of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] There is some $\lambda_0 > 1$ and $C, c > 0$ such that for all $\lambda \geqslant \lambda_0$,
