where $\mathcal{X}_i$ are i.i.d. random variable with the same  Tracy-Widom distribution $F_1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.337554+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d1c0eb4715170d6629fb41f50d5babe6c13b8bbdfa980cec261c2a8caf42e32","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2607.14948, 'Graph alignment in sparse inhomogeneous models via self-overlap'] Let $K$ be a weakly inhomogeneous random graph, with associated edge probabilities $(p_e)_{e \in E}$. Then, for any sequence $\lambda_n \to +\infty$ with $\lambda_n \leq n$,
