{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.970271+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d3d706427d3a30b9d105ac54d56884586eaf9e88fd2f9eb73d9e4601e3d54c5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 of arXiv:2608.03273, 'On the Asymptotic of Coupled Spherical Integrals: An Operator-Valued Extension of the Free'] An RV $X$ with mean $\mu=\mathbb E[X]$ is sub-exponential if there are non-negative parameters $(\nu, \chi)$ such that
