{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.299263+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d477f731d56232e90d90c53bf5d6ada032d12aabd12da4b483535c7d268c44f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop prop_iii of arXiv:2608.30382, 'Convergence rates for the RMSprop optimizer with full control of the hyperparameters'] Let $\beta\in[ \nicefrac{1}{2}, 1 ) $,
$ \varepsilon \in [0,\infty) $,
$ i \in \{ 1, 2, \dots, d \} $,
$ n \in {\mathbb N} \backslash \{ 1 \} $,
let $ A_n \in \mathcal F_{ n - 1 } $,
and let $ C_X^{ (3) } , C_v^{ (-3) } \in (0,\infty) $.
Assume that
\bas{
  {\mathbb E}\bigl[
    | X^{(i)}(\theta_{n-1},U_n) |^3
    |
    \mathcal F_{ n - 1 }
  \bigr]
  \le C_X^{ (3) }
\qquad\text{on }A_n
}
and
\bas{

  {\mathbb E}[ \1_{ A_n }( v_{ n - 1 }^{ (i) } )^{ - 3 } ]
  \le C_v^{ ( - 3 ) }
  .
}
The negative-moment assumption implies that $v_{n-1}^{(i)}>0$ almost surely
on $A_n$. If $\varepsilon=0$, the conditional covariances in the conclusion are
therefore evaluated on $A_n$ and extended by zero to $ \Omega \backslash A_n $.
Then one has
\bas{

  {\mathbb E}\Bigl[
    \1_{A_n}\mathrm{cov}((\sqrt{v_n^{(i)}}+\varepsilon)^{-1},
    X^{(i)}(\theta_{n-1},U_n)|\mathcal F_{n-1})^2
  \Bigr]^{1/2}
  \le
  4 C_X^{(3)} (C_v^{(-3)})^{1/2}\,\frac{1-\beta}{1-\beta^{n-1}}.
}","status":"unverified"}

