{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:47:04.949316+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d6a3f7f5a3d92a9f8f39f04ba8519d0d5e687e63fe20fd7c7f5bc1dd0c8dfcc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-effbt of arXiv:2412.03067, 'Geodesic Trees and Exceptional Directions in FPP on Hyperbolic Groups'] Let $C>0, o \in \Gamma$ be as in Proposition~(prop-effbt of the paper).

	Suppose Assumption~(assume-subexp of the paper) holds. Then, given $c>0$, there exists $R_0=R_0(c,C) >0$ such that for $R \geq R_0$ the following holds.\\

Let $A=A(o,C)$ denote the event that there exist $u, v, w \in \Gamma$ such that
	\begin{enumerate}

