{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:33:11.959384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d701d27cca71bc0b7faa54853ed62d91cd3e72d631d95e686a749c0a2625f23","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:strict-tilted-product of arXiv:2607.14087, 'Stochastic Domination of Gaussian Maxima: A Resolution of the Weak Simplex Conjecture'] \label[proposition]{prop:strict-tilted-product}
Let $R$ be an $m\times m$ correlation matrix with $R\neq I_m$, and let
$X\sim\mathcal N(0,R)$.  For each $i$, let
\[
  f_i(z)=e^{a_i z}\mathbf 1_{(-\infty,b_i]}(z),
  \qquad a_i>0,\quad b_i>0,
\]
and suppose that $\int zf_i(z)\,d\gamma_1(z)=0$.  Then
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb E\prod_{i=1}^m f_i(X_i)
  >\prod_{i=1}^m\int f_i\,d\gamma_1.
\end{equation}
The matrix $R$ may be singular.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.975321+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d7295831cf18aeab6ac5a22302f67a3c3bc833c330ec0f3951001edfafffae2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_1 of arXiv:2412.03774, '{ Refining Concentration for \\Gaussian Quadratic Chaos with\\ Applications in Sonar and C'] For $0< b<1$  and integer $m\geq1$ define the sequence of functions  

  \begin{eqnarray}

