{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.812807+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d7884644b5d347b12edae3b654396b4a1df9b3b07ed50a2d1b9a32a855c686f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:integral of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] The Mellin transform of the function
    \begin{align*}
        f_{a,b,s}(t)=t^a \int_0^\pi \frac{(\sin\theta)^b }{(1-2t \cos \theta+t^2)^s} \,\mathrm{d} \theta,
        \quad a\in\mathbb{R},\,b,s>0,
    \end{align*}
    is absolutely convergent for $-a<\re z<2s-a$ and it is given by
    \begin{align}
        M[f_{a,b,s},z] =\frac{\sqrt\pi \Gamma\left(\frac{b-2s+2}{2}\right)\Gamma\left(\frac{b+1}{2}\right)}{2\Gamma(s)}
        \cdot \frac{\Gamma\left(\frac{2s-z-a}{2}\right)\Gamma\left(\frac{z+a}{2}\right)}{\Gamma\left(\frac{b-a-z+2}{2}\right)\Gamma\left(\frac{b+a-2s+2+z}{2}\right)}.
    \end{align}
    The analytic continuation of $M[f_{a,b,s},z]$ is a meromorphic function with only simple poles, which are contained in the set
    \begin{align*}
        (2s-a+2\mathbb{N}) \cup (-a-2\mathbb{N})
    \end{align*}
    of zeros of the denominator of (equation eq:mellinf of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.724188+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d7ad4fc15e061cf24e0e9145a40fa72ca4c373dd1dc6041caa4de41b82402cb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop.localtimesBRW of arXiv:2411.19145, 'On the intersection of critical percolation clusters and other tree-like random graphs'] There exists $C>0$, such that for any $n\ge 1$, and any $x_1,\dots,x_n,z \in \mathbb Z^d$ (possibly with repetition), with $d\ge 5$, 
