In particular, if $Y$ is reflexive, then $\operatorname{QNA}(X,Y)=\operatorname{NA}_1(X,Y) = \operatorname{NA}_2(X,Y)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.290159+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d94be0ea6cf3ff7ccf436a887152426b6bb76406a510517131fd586c8bae16c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def_conditional_convergence_in_probability of arXiv:2411.08846, 'On the Number of Crossings and Bouncings\\ of a Diffusion at a Sticky Threshold'] We say that the sequence of random variables $(X_{n})_{n\ge 1} $ converges to the random variable $X_{0}$ in probability, conditionally on the event $\mathcal H $ with positive probability, 
	if $X_{n} \longrightarrow  X_{0} $ in $\Prob^{\mathcal H}$-probability.
	We denote this convergence with
	\begin{equation}
		X_{n} \convergence{\Prob^{\mathcal H}} X_{0}.
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.331645+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d94c0eb031b665611515efe07870953ab1d51c0d761f819db8ad6016faf42f2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma thm:equivs for Schervish of arXiv:2412.06420, 'Accuracy, Estimates, and Representation Results'] The following are equivalent:
		\begin{enumerate}
		\item Schervish form: for $v\in\set{0,1}$ and any $x\in[0,1]$, 
		\begin{align}
		&			\mathsf{acc}_v(v)-\mathsf{acc}_v(x)=\int_{x}^{v}{v-t}\;\;\lambda(\dd{t}).&&\text{(eq:Scherv of the paper)}\nonumber
		\end{align}
		\item For all $x,y\in[0,1]$, (i.e., replacing $v\in\set{0,1}$ by a general $y\in[0,1]$)
				\begin{align}
						&			\mathsf{acc}_v(y)-\mathsf{acc}_v(x)=\int_{x}^{y}{v-t}\;\;\lambda(\dd{t}).
				\end{align}
		\item For all $x,p\in[0,1]$,
				\begin{align}
				&\mathrm{Exp}_p\mathsf{acc}(p)-\mathrm{Exp}_p\mathsf{acc}(x)=\int_x^p (p-t)\;\lambda(\dd{t})
				\end{align}
		\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.233752+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d96cc7b30582b38a35bc85a1fb826991f4f437efafae7e0b716c10c9f015e09","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 9 of arXiv:2609.00567, 'Hodge--Tate splitting and Akizuki--Nakano vanishing in positive characteristic'] Let \(\mcalG\) be a flat affine group scheme over an fpqc algebraic stack \(\mcalX\). A morphism \(f\colon\mcalY\to\mcalX\) of stacks is called a \emph{\(B\mcalG\)-torsor} if there exists a representable fpqc cover \(U\to\mcalX\) by a scheme and an equivalence
  \begin{equation*}
    \mcalY\times_{\mcalX}U\simeq B_U\mcalG_U
  \end{equation*}
  of stacks over \(U\), where \(\mcalG_U\defeq\mcalG\times_{\mcalX}U\). We use the expression \(B\mcalG\)-torsor only in this sense.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.611338+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d972ee7e3116bbf2bc5b94f74745910eec0e9d4fbd9734aaf8e524f8364fea6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 (Proposition 4.1 in \cite{DLV}) of arXiv:2607.08536, 'Soft edge limit of the Laguerre beta-ensemble at the lower edge'] There exists a.s.~finite random time $\mathfrak{t}<\infty$ such that 
\begin{align}
    |\mathfrak{p}(t)-\sqrt{t}|\le t^{-1/4}\log t,\qquad \text{ for all $t\ge \mathfrak{t}$.}
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.954003+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d9f9a77d74085e9ab2cd1fe34458a9939071e550165c0264b41f84b3994fdaf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:Lambda of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] For $A \in \{\rho, J\}$ and $k \in \mathbb{R}$ define
\begin{align}
  \Lambda^A(k)
  \equiv
  \sup\left\{
    \bigl\langle 
    \mathcal{L}_k^A f, f \bigr\rangle_{\mu}
    \mathrel{\Big|} f \in D(\mathcal{L}_k^A),\|f\|_{L^2(\mu)} = 1
  \right\},

\end{align}
where the supremum is over the real Hilbert space $L^2(\mu)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.660871+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3da230e711fe01d726710e46542780ba4548cc3d96e41bc36fa54e2463f3f162","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 (Section 2.2 in \cite{Taki05}) of arXiv:2604.23572, '2604.23572'] In any work-conserving single-server queue 
satisfying Assumptions~\ref{assumption-1} to \ref{assumption-3}, 
the mean amount $\E[U]$ of unfinished work in steady state is given by

\begin{equation}
\E[U] =
\rho 
+ \frac{\ds\sum_{k \in \K} \rho_k \E[\tilde{H}_k]}{1-\rho} 
+ \frac{\ds\sum_{k \in \K} \rho_k(\rho -\rho_k)}{2(1-\rho)} 
+ \frac{\ds\sum_{k \in \K} \E[H_k]^2 \delta_k^{(2)}}{2(1-\rho)} 
+ \sum_{k \in \K} \E[H_k] v_{k,0}^{(1)} ,

\end{equation}

where $\delta_k^{(2)}$ and $v_{k,0}^{(1)}$ are given 
by (\ref{delta_k^2}) and (\ref{v_{k,0}^1}). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:07.028334+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3db3177217f60dc6815e4b25383472a12a41a46ecd2e87564146a8605ce81988","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:legendre of arXiv:2607.29330, 'Large deviations for the maximum of\\ the generalized TAP free energy'] Fix a regular \(f\in(f_{\mathrm{eq}},f_1)\). Let \(\theta_f\in(0,1)\) be the
		unique minimizer defining \(\Sigma(f)\), let \(\zeta_f\) be the
		corresponding constrained Parisi minimizer, and let \(q_f\) be its first
		positive contact point. Let \(X^f\) be the Auffinger--Chen process
		associated with \(\zeta_f\). Assume the strict Plefka condition
		\begin{equation}
			1-\xi''(q_f)\mathbb{E}\left[
			\left(
			\partial_{xx}\Phi_{\zeta_f}(q_f,X^f_{q_f})
			\right)^2
			\right]>0.
		\end{equation}
		Then
		\begin{equation}
			\begin{aligned}
				\lim_{\varepsilon\downarrow0}\liminf_{N\to\infty}
				\frac1N\log\mathbb{P}\bigl(\mathcal E_{N,\varepsilon}(f)\bigr)
				&=
				\lim_{\varepsilon\downarrow0}\limsup_{N\to\infty}
				\frac1N\log\mathbb{P}\bigl(\mathcal E_{N,\varepsilon}(f)\bigr)\\
				&=
				\Sigma(f)
				=
				\inf_{\theta\in(0,1)}
				\bigl[\Lambda(\theta)-\theta f\bigr].
			\end{aligned}
		\end{equation}
		Moreover,
		\begin{equation}
			\lim_{N\to\infty}
			\frac1N
			\log
			\mathbb{E}\exp\left\{
			\theta_f\max_{\mathbf{m}\in[-1,1]^N}F_{\mathrm{TAP}}(\mathbf{m})
			\right\}
			=
