{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.491829+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3dbc0e2dba35257316ce31e8242a0fa0914d0d2e29eb34c59eeca17aea448446","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2607.04012, 'Hölder regularity for backward stochastic Volterra integral equations and applications to '] Let $0\leq r\leq s\leq v\leq T$, and define $\delta_j(r,s)\coloneqq |[r,s]\cap[t_j,t_{j+1})|$, where $|\cdot|$ denotes Lebesgue measure. Then there exists a constant $C>0$, independent of $\pi$, $r$, $s$ and $v$, such that, for every $0 \leq k \leq N-1$,
