{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.338010+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3dbfc9dfbb134d126ce4f19ad7767e94292ddbbfbc4ef08bf125350c21756ca9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 3 of arXiv:2512.05687, '$L^p$-Boltzmann-Gibbs principle \\ via Littlewood-Paley-Stein inequality'] Let $u\in \R$. 
For functions $F=F(\eta)$ and $G=G(\eta) \in C^2(\R^N)$, if all integrals
in the following converge, we have
\begin{align*} 
 \int_{\R^N} GL_0F d\mu_u & = \int_{\R^N} FL_0G d\mu_u  \\
& = -\frac12 \int_{\R^N} \sum_{x\in \T_N} \big( \partial_{\eta(x)} -\partial_{\eta(x-1)} \big) F \cdot
\big( \partial_{\eta(x)} -\partial_{\eta(x-1)} \big) G\, d\mu_u, \\
\int_{\R^N} G L_1 F d\mu_u &= -\int_{\R^N} F L_1 G d\mu_u.
\end{align*}
For the carr\'e du champ of the $\eta$-process, we have
\begin{align} 
\Ga(F)  = \sum_{x\in \T_N} \big( \partial_{\eta(x)} F -\partial_{\eta(x-1)} F \big)^2 
= \sum_{x\in \T_N} \big( \nabla^*D_\eta F(x) \big)^2 
=: |\nabla_{\T_N}^* D_\eta F|^2,
\end{align}
recall Remark \ref{rem:1.3} for $\nabla^*$ and $D_\eta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

