    where $C=C(p,q)$ is a constant depending only on $p$ and $q$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:28.055829+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3df2dad0ed5c77775922dfc1e74288aff0361c882369667a1b600e3a27ad6e2f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:generic_bound of arXiv:2608.12056, 'Deviation inequalities for U-processes of growing order, with applications to half-space d'] Let $j\in N$ and assume that $\{X_t, t \in T\}$ is a $\psi_{2/j}$ process. Then for any $t_0 \in T$ and integer $p \geq 2$, \begin{multline}

        \left(\mathbb E \sup_{t \in T} \lvert X_t - X_{t_0} \rvert^p \right)^{1/p} \\
        \leq  2^{j}(p-1)^{j/2} \sup_{t \in T}\|X_t - X_{t_0}\|_2+C2^{j}\gamma_{2/j, \left\lfloor \log_2 (pj) \right\rfloor}(T, d)
         \,. 
