{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.702415+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e1cf7310f8274f3cd0b909e6f9545bc4e6172a4808d1da55d6109df7a2398e7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:Rsub of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] The \textbf{subcritical 1-point measure} $R_{1}^{\mathrm{(Sub)}}(dx)$ is the unique Radon measure on $\mathbb{R}$ determined by its sinc transform: for any $t > 0$,
\begin{equation}
    \int_{-\infty}^{\infty} \frac{\sin^{m} (t\sqrt{-x})}{(t\sqrt{-x})^{m}} \, R_{1}^{\mathrm{(Sub)}}(dx) = \sum_{\Gamma \in \mathcal{T}_{1}} \int_{0}^{1} \mathcal{Q}_m(\xi) \mathcal{F}^{\mathrm{(Sub)}}_{\Gamma}(\xi t) \, d\xi.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:11:44.390613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e22e26b151fc90bae36f3da1710f068935adc89fef1d50bba9f821c08541dd8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2609.03171, 'Factorization patterns and fields of definition of $\ell$-torsion points on the Jacobians '] \cite[Theorem 5.76]{2005ehcc}
Let \(\alpha_1,\ldots,\alpha_6\) be the roots of $P$. 
\begin{itemize}
