{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.617886+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e33e926019cda414dccb1a52a0ac2d74710c48c8ad2d66a5ba43fec94a9b310","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 155 (Divergence identity on the characteristic diamond) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $\mathcal{J}$ be a spacetime vectorfield on  $\characteristicdiamondtwoarg{[\leftubar,\ubar)}{[\moreinterestingu_1,u]}$, and let $\mathcal{J} = \mathcal{J}^{\ubar} \nullgeop{\ubar} + \mathcal{J}^u \nullgeop{u} + \mathcal{J}^A \nullgeop{x^A}$ be its decomposition relative to the double-null coordinate vectorfields. Then the following identity holds:
	\begin{equation} 
