{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.818615+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e53d3b60dced5deaa8b3832a4ceaee167c5cc834825dab5655887f8cc61ef6f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma r:whitenoise-multiplication of arXiv:2607.24640, 'The Yang-Mills measure on surfaces via Morse theory'] Let $\psi,\widetilde{\psi}\in L^\infty(\Sigma)$. For every sequence $(\widetilde{\psi}_n)_{n\geq 1}\in \mathcal{C}^\infty(\Sigma)$ that converges to $\widetilde{\psi}$ in $L^p$ (for every $p<\infty$), $(\xi_\psi\widetilde{\psi}_n)_{n\geq 1}$ also converges to $\xi_{\psi\widetilde{\psi}}$. In particular, the $\sigma$-algebra $\sigma(\xi_{\psi\widetilde{\psi}})$ generated by
$$
\left\{\langle\xi_{\psi\widetilde{\psi}},\phi\rangle^{-1}(B):\ \phi\in\mathcal{C}^\infty\left(\Sigma\right),\ B\ \text{Borel set of}\ \Sigma\right\}
$$
is contained in $\sigma(\xi_{\psi})$, i.e. the same $\sigma$-algebra with $\psi$ replacing $\psi\widetilde{\psi}$ in the definition.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.853799+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e53ed3b2ae183eac4319222396f39029b2679764a8f542ec18cb3514ce3f990","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem lem:recursiveLemmaFormula of arXiv:2509.16694, 'A central limit theorem for two-dimensional directed polymers with critical spatial correl'] For all $a>-1$, $z\in \big[\,0,\,(a+2)z_a/2\,\big)$ and $x\in [0,1]$,
