{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.234693+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e6545079018885243c225e28743242ccaf750ceff542889291c000798d958b0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theo1 of arXiv:2604.22510, 'Asymptotics of Multi-Scale McKean--Vlasov Diffusions with Super-Linear Kernels: a Lifted S'] Suppose that the assumptions $(\mathbf{A}_{\text{slow}})$ and $(\mathbf{A}_{\text{fast}})$  hold. Then for any initial values $\xi\in L^p(\Omega;\mathbb{R}^n)$, $\zeta\in L^p(\Omega;\mathbb{R}^m)$ with $p>\kappa$, it holds that
