{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.582440+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e861b210eaadc0089af9891b045ad114e9e8b6a92556166c3fae0cd82f86d6a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem many balls of arXiv:2411.09640, 'Random Lipschitz functions on graphs with weak expansion'] For any $r \in \mathbb N$ the following holds. Let $m=m(G,r)$ be the maximum size of a ball of radius $r$ in $G$. For any $W \subseteq V(G)$, there exists $U \subseteq W$ of size $|U| \geq \left\lfloor \frac{|W|}{m^2} \right\rfloor$ such that 
