{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.086133+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f2886e25f0e48763329e3a65ab63368ec3ecfc79c055cd85f460f65e22d22a3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition merging-block of arXiv:2412.08400, '\vspace{-1.0cm} Characterization of Exponential Families of \\ Lumpable Stochastic Matrice'] Let $(x, x') \in \mathcal{D} = \kappa_2(\mathcal{E})$ be such that for some $y \in \mathcal{S}_x$ it holds that
\begin{equation}

    \abs{\set{(y,y') \in \mathcal{E} \colon y' \in \mathcal{S}_{x'}}} > 1.
\end{equation}
Then we say that $(x,x')$ is a merging block of $(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E})$ with respect to $\kappa$.
Furthermore, when 
$\left| \mathcal{S}_x \right| \geq 2$, we say that the merging block is multi-row (note that (equation eq:merging-block-condition of the paper) need not hold for every $y \in \mathcal{S}_x$).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.243062+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f3505893076c029c829dda74399dd4a04a688dcef77fd6da7a3f1eadf07fda2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem inf of arXiv:2604.23751, 'Large deviation principles for pattern-avoiding permutations, and limit shapes for constra'] Let us consider two sets $A$ and $B$ and a function $h$ on $A \cup B$.
It holds that
\begin{equation}
\inf_{z \in A \cup B} h(z) +\inf_{z \in A \cap B} h(z)
\ge \inf_{z \in A} h(z) + \inf_{z \in B} h(z).
\end{equation}
Moreover, if the inequality is strict, then
\begin{equation}
    \inf_{z \in A} h(z) = \inf_{z \in A \backslash B} h(z) < \inf_{z \in A \cap B} h(z),
\end{equation}
and the same holds if we switch the roles of $A$ and $B$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.309675+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f42efeb47bb42352523177dc2b2489c8f2402a88d43becb30beba7e9ba757b6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_irreducible:CPPdrift:infinite of arXiv:2411.14876, 'Limit theorems for stochastic exponentials of matrix-valued L\'evy processes \\'] Assume $L$ is a Lévy process in $\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}$ fulfilling (equation eq-nonsingular of the paper) with characteristic triplet $(\Sigma_L, \gamma_L, \nu_L)$ such that $\Sigma_L=0$. 
