{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:48:30.910360+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f4c6e12a5e3fbaf7bc4063ddac080c97dfffa035bc925e1e7abdb2e616c596d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 5 (Kronecker theorem ++) of arXiv:2609.00974, 'On Algebraic Integrability\\ of Vector Fields \\ with Rational Function Coefficients\\ tha'] Let $P\in \mathbb{Q}(t_1,\ldots,t_r)[X]$ be an irreducible polynomial. 
    If modulo all maximal primes $q$ from an open dense subset of an integral model of $\mathbb{Q}(t_1,\ldots,t_r)$ it has a root in $\mathbb{F}_p$, where $p>0$ is the characteristic of $\kappa(q)$, then $P$ is linear, and its root is a rational number.

    Consequently, if $K$ is a field of characteristic zero, $f\in K$, and $f$ modulo $q$ for all maximal ideal $q$, in an open dense subset of a suitable integral finite-type model of a subfield $f\in K'\subset K$, satisfies $X^p=X$, where $p>0$ is the characteristic of $\kappa(q)$, then $f\in \mathbb{Q}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.278497+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f4d7c82d689f261244387e6ae0dafe61fdc27d6ac0a26dc9996817862dcfd8a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq: decomposition of W of arXiv:2411.05924, 'Non-negative Martingale Solutions to the Stochastic Porous Medium Equation with Sticky Beh'] $\widetilde W$ and $\widetilde W_n$ are $Q$--Wiener processes adapted to the filtrations $\widetilde{\mathbb F}$ and $\widetilde{\mathbb F}_n$, respectively, which can be rewritten as
