{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:56.353905+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f79530019edb8eb6a95bde445c62f6c19dcbf9e09748866a719b41fefb83b15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Problem 34 of arXiv:2608.26628, 'Open Problems in Mathematical Logic'] Let $L_x=\{z : z \leq_K^+ x\}$ and $U_x=\{z : z \geq_K x\}$. Are the following true?
