{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.922550+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f7e022d8c42db94422a1fd002ed67c1913318778302a47b2fa8d4cca5c48727","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture conj_QM of arXiv:2412.05706, 'Quasi-multiplicativity and regularity for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] {basu2017kesten}}] For any $3\le d\le 5$ and $\delta>0$, there exists a constant $c=c(d,\delta)>0$ such that for any $p\in [p_c(d),p_c(d)+\delta]$, $N\ge 1$, $Z\subset \mathbb{Z}^d$ with $B(4N)\setminus B(N) \subset Z$, $X\subset Z\cap B(N)$ and $Y\subset Z\setminus B(4N)$,  
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb{P}_p\big(X\xleftrightarrow{} Y\ \text{in}\ Z\big)\ge c\cdot  \mathbb{P}_p\big(X\xleftrightarrow{} \partial B(2N)\ \text{in}\ Z\big)\mathbb{P}_p\big(Y\xleftrightarrow{} \partial B(2N)\ \text{in}\ Z\big).
	\end{equation}	
	Here ``$A\xleftrightarrow{} A'$ in $Z$'' means that there exists a path within $Z$ that connects $A$ and $A'$ and consists of open edges. (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:43:45.388699+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f810455e93e5b5d5cf21500fce9f7e793f30d080b7278ebc2e98499485ec61e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2609.04139, 'The conformally invariant metric on CLE$_4$ II:\\ existence of geodesics'] Let $U \subsetneq \BC$ be a simply connected domain. Let $z \in U$ be deterministic, and let $V \subset U$ be a deterministic simply connected domain. Write $\{V_j\}_j$ for the connected components of $V^\star$ (recall~\eqref{eq:def-V-star} for the definition of $V^\star$). Let $(\Gamma_U, D_{\Gamma_U}^U, \{D_{\Gamma_U|_{V_j}}^{V_j}\}_j)$ be coupled as in \Cref{def:weak_axioms}, Axiom~\eqref{it:weak_axiom_locality} (locality). Let $\tau$ be a stopping time for the filtration $\{\mathcal{F}_t\}_{t \ge 0}$, where
\begin{equation*}
	\mathcal{F}_t \defeq \sigma\left(\SCB_s(\SCL(z); D_{\Gamma_U}^U), \Gamma_U|_{\SCB_s(\SCL(z); D_{\Gamma_U}^U)} : s \le t\right).
\end{equation*}
Then, conditionally on the $\sigma$-algebra generated by~\eqref{eq:weak_axiom_locality} and by $\SCB_\tau(\SCL(z); D_{\Gamma_U}^U)$, on the event that $\SCB_\tau(\SCL(z); D_{\Gamma_U}^U) \cap V^\star = \emptyset$, the pairs $(\Gamma_U|_{V_j}, D_{\Gamma_U|_{V_j}}^{V_j})$ are independent and their conditional laws are those of $(\Gamma_{V_j}, D_{\Gamma_{V_j}}^{V_j})$, respectively.

The same is true with a deterministic connected arc of $\partial U$ in place of $\SCL(z)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.593079+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f81356c75778a052aee3e917f5a6d26aa3171d7460f045b94784299bea1e57a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] The following hold.
 \begin{enumerate}
 \item[(1)]  For any $\lambda \geq 0$ and $g\in L^\infty(\mathbb{R}_+;\mathbb{R}_+)$, the generalized Volterra-Riccati equation (??) has a unique global solution $V^\lambda_g \in C(\mathbb{R}_+;\mathbb{R}_+)\cap C^2\big((0,\infty);\mathbb{R}_+\big)$.

 \item[(2)] For any $K_1,K_2>0$ and $T\geq 0$, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $\lambda_1,\lambda_2\in[0,K_1]$ and $g_1,g_2 \in L^\infty(\mathbb{R}_+;\mathbb{R}_+) $ with $\big\|g_1\big\|_{L^\infty_T}, \big\|g_2\big\|_{L^\infty_T}\in[0,K_2]$,
 \begin{eqnarray*}
 \sup_{t\in[0,T]} \big| V^{g_1}_{\lambda_1} (t) -V^{g_2}_{\lambda_2} (t)\big|
 \leq C\cdot \Big(\big| \lambda_1-\lambda_2 \big| + \big\|g_1-g_2\big\|_{L^\infty_T}\Big).
 \end{eqnarray*}
 \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.239571+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f83f0202f508c00358db204f245a48b9a4ae2ba3518e84828d37e0acc1878eb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 60 of arXiv:2609.00567, 'Hodge--Tate splitting and Akizuki--Nakano vanishing in positive characteristic'] Let \(\Perf\) be the category of perfect \(\setF_p\)-algebras.
