{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.307032+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f849d135ff0e01d11fbd3a55462cbf0864218a1fdeee69adb02be833807ac22","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:shift_NM of arXiv:2411.14818, 'Scaling limits of solitons in the Box-Ball system'] {Assume that $\eta \in \Omega$.} For any $k, \ell, h \in {\mathbb{N}}$, $i \in {\mathbb{Z}}$ and $n \in {\mathbb{N}}$, we have 
