{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.968036+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f991225da7e56ee41dc4165edc28ded9d0eddc96b5ea8e0b3dd9296235bf717","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2606.09904, 'Non-explosion principles for branched rough differential equations with unbounded coeffici'] Assuming \(\phi\) is such that \(\|D^k\phi(x)\| \le l(\|x\|)^{\alpha_k}\) for all \(k = 0, 1, \dots, N\), 
  we have for any \(f \in \CF_{N - 1}\), 
  \begin{equation}
    \|\partial^f_X \phi(\mathbf{Y}_t)\| = \|\partial^{[f]}_X Y_t\|
      \le \frac{1}{\Pi(f)} l(\|Y_t\|)^{\sum_{k = 0}^{N - 1} \Lambda_k([f]) \alpha_k}.
  \end{equation}
  Moreover, if \(\alpha_k = (1 - \beta k)\alpha\) for some constants \(\alpha\) and \(\beta\), then 
  \begin{equation}
    \|D^n \partial^f_X \phi(\mathbf{Y}_t)\| \le \frac{(1 + |f|)^n}{\Pi(f)} 
      l(\|Y_t\|)^{((1 + |f|) - (n + |f|)\beta)\alpha}
  \end{equation}
  for any \(n \in \mathbb{N} \cup \{0\}\), \(n \le N - |f|\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.653693+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f99907ff67e641012d31e35ed731a6f59a2cb3f5c70053a7e59dea7afcf9ce7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2605.07184, 'Convergence of Stochastic Gradient Descent with mini-batching and infinite variance'] The drift $\tilde\gamma$ in \eqref{eq:drift} can be expressed as 
