{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.441880+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3fb594a841296d73478398a4890a7d771ba05534fe9945427c781a388c6a9fc6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2604.07478, 'Mixing Times and Cutoff for the Rook's Walk'] For any $n\in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 3}$ and $d\in \mathbb{Z}_{ \geq 2}$, let   $\Omega,\Omega_*$, $P,P_*$ and $\pi,\pi_*$ be the state space, transition matrix and stationary distribution of the standard Rook's walk and the RWBD chains resp. each with parameters $n$ and $d$. Also, let $x\in \Omega_*$. Then,
  \[\Vert P_*^t(x,\cdot) - \pi_*(\cdot) \Vert_\text{TV} = \Vert (P^t \mu_x)(\cdot) - \pi(\cdot) \Vert_\text{TV}\]
  where $\mu_x$ is a distribution of $\Omega$ with probabilities uniformly distributed over $H_x$. That is,
   \[\mu_x(h) = \begin{cases}
      \frac{1}{\varphi(x)}, \quad &h\in H_x\\
      0, \quad &h\not\in H_x
   \end{cases}\]
   for all $h\in \Omega$, where $\varphi(x) = {d \choose i}(n-1)^i$ as in Definition \ref{defphi}.
   \begin{proof}
      \begin{align*}
         \Vert P_*^t(x,\cdot) - \pi_*(\cdot) \Vert_\text{TV} &= \frac{1}{2}\sum_{y\in \Omega_*}|P^t_*(x,y) -\pi_*(y)|\\
         &= \frac{1}{2}\sum_{y\in \Omega_*}|(P^t \mu_x)(H_y) -\pi(H_y)| \tag{By Def. \ref{BDRW}}\\
         &= \frac{1}{2}\sum_{y\in \Omega_*}\sum_{h_y\in H_y}|(P^t \mu_x)(h_y) -\pi(h_y)|\\
         &= \frac{1}{2}\sum_{z\in \Omega}|(P^t \mu_x)(z) -\pi(z)|\\
         &= \Vert (P^t \mu_x)(\cdot) - \pi(\cdot) \Vert_\text{TV}
      \end{align*}
   \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

