{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.162144+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4028a291e9c2c8c532bcaf117f5c389f4193e45fcf97a71f17e0de546c140e60","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:concentreGp* of arXiv:2603.00773, 'Long-time $L^p$ Wasserstein contraction for diffusion processes without global dissipativi'] Under Assumptions~(Assum:basic of the paper) and~(Assum:PointwiseContractInfty of the paper), assume moreover that $\eta$ is Lipschitz continuous with constant $L_\eta$ and that the contraction~(equation eq:contraction_def of the paper) holds with $p=1$ for some $C_1,\lambda_1>0$. Denote by $\mu_\infty$ the invariant measure of the diffusion process~(equation eq:EDS_X of the paper). Then, for all $p\geqslant 1$ and $t\geqslant 0$,
\[G_p^*(t) \leqslant A e^{- \min(\rho,\rho') t }\]
 with
