{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.606707+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_407df97f0432e8f9783bb2292feb59eb6fcad347f399f120112cbaa4f70bc1e1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2506.08775, 'Markovian multivariate Hawkes population processes: Efficient evaluation of moments'] A \textrm{Markovian multivariate Hawkes process} is a point process $\bm{N}(\cdot)$, with $\bm{N}(0)=\bm{0}$, whose components $N_i(\cdot)$ satisfy
\begin{align}

\begin{split}
    \pp(N_i(t+\Delta) - N_i(t) = 0 \, | \, \cF_t ) &= 1 - \lambda_i(t)\Delta + o(\Delta),\\
    \pp(N_i(t+\Delta) - N_i(t) = 1 \, | \, \cF_t ) &= \lambda_i(t)\Delta + o(\Delta), \\
    \pp(N_i(t+\Delta) - N_i(t) > 1 \, | \, \cF_t ) &= o(\Delta),
\end{split}
\end{align}
as $\Delta \downarrow 0$, with $\cF_t = \sigma(\bm{N}(s) \, : \, s \leqslant t)$ denoting the natural filtration generated by $\bm{N}(\cdot)$.
Here, each component $\lambda_i(t)$ of the intensity function satisfies the mean-reverting dynamics
\begin{align}

    \ddiff\lambda_i(t) = \alpha_{i}(\overline{\lambda}_i -\lambda_i(t))\,\ddiff t + \sum_{j=1}^d B_{ij}(t) \,\ddiff N_j(t),
\end{align}
where $\lambda_i(0) = \overline{\lambda}_i \geqslant 0$, $\alpha_i \geqslant 0$, and for each $i,j\in[d]$, $(B_{ij}(t))_t$ is a sequence of independent random variables, distributed as the generic non-negative random variable $B_{ij}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.445636+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_407f58e8bad9796da3af360974aabde3e6049c94fde82e67930ea82b0145ad06","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:integervaluedXYwithlambda of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] We fix a sidelength $L \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, a parameter $\lambda >0$, a collection of non-negative conductances $\left( J_{xy,k} \right)_{\{x,y\} \in E(\Lambda_L), 1 \leq k \leq n}$, and define the probability distribution on the set $\Omega_{\Lambda_L}^\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}$
\begin{equation*}
    \mu_{\Lambda_L , J, \lambda}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}\mathrm{-XY}} (\left\{ \varphi \right\}) := \frac{1}{Z_{\Lambda_L , n , J, \lambda}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}\mathrm{-XY}}}  I_{\left(\varphi(0)\right)} \left( \lambda \right)\prod_{x \sim y} \prod_{1 \leq k \leq  n} I_{\left(\varphi(x) - \varphi(y)\right)} \left( J_{xy, k} \right) .
\end{equation*}
We denote by $\mathrm{Var}_{L , J , \lambda}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}$ the variance with respect to the measure $\mu_{\Lambda_L , J, \lambda}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}\mathrm{-XY}}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-09T06:55:03+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4084a35d50541a58d62cc7e012776cec3619aaf056e2cde9a72bd73fbf625d5d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2512.19517, 'Spiking and Resetting'] The process $({\bar X}^\varepsilon_t)_{t \ge 0}$ with state space $\{0,1\}$ and c\`adl\`ag  trajectories defined by 
