{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.446858+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4084a7062702b065b781a4c21d2d822eb38806d5fad1ac7641eeaf525d16f282","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:path_expansion_H_plus_A of arXiv:2508.17838, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices'] Let \(U_n(x)\) be the Chebyshev polynomial of the second kind, 
and let \(V_n,\Phi_2,\Phi_3,\underline{\Phi_2V_n},\underline{\Phi_3V_n}\) be as in Definition~(def:nonbacktracking of the paper).  Introduce
\begin{equation}
\underline{\Phi_A V_n}\;\equiv\;\sum_{i=1}^n A^i\,V_{n-i},
\end{equation}
recording that each insertion of \(A\) of total multiplicity \(i\) carries no backtracking constraint, then
\begin{equation}
U_n\bigl((H+A)/2\bigr)
=
\sum_{k\ge0}\;\sum_{\alpha\in\{2,3,A\}^k}\;\sum_{\substack{\ell_0+\cdots+\ell_k=n}} 
V_{\ell_0}
\;\underline{\Phi_{\alpha_1} V_{\ell_1}}\;\cdots\;\underline{\Phi_{\alpha_k} V_{\ell_k}},
\end{equation}
where each symbol \(\alpha_i\in\{2,3,A\}\) indicates an insertion of \(\Phi_2,\Phi_3,\Phi_A\) respectively, and the summation   runs over all nonnegative integers \(\ell_i\ge0\).","status":"unverified"}

