{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.463912+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_40a86cd73c112d018e59eb11f165d2ee6de882f12706043e0de46a449247a5a3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 36 (\cite{abbrescia2022emergence}*{Lemma 6.6}; Relationship between $\{\p_t,\p_1,\p_2,\p_3\}$ and $\{\Lunit,X, \Yvf{2},\Yvf{3}\}$) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] The following identities hold:
