{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.308774+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4157a825a412d01c7f71eaa84a8f29817a4ef9ebd0f8827043086b9fcf96930d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 5 (Matrix Freedman) of arXiv:2606.24323, 'Conditioning of incoherent sub-dictionaries sampled from a coherent dictionary'] Let $(Y_\ell)_{\ell}$ with $Y_0=0$ be a matrix martingale adapted to the filtration $(\mathcal F_\ell)_\ell$, whose values are symmetric (self-adjoint) $d\times d$ matrices.
Assume that the difference sequence $X_\ell = Y_\ell-Y_{\ell-1}$ is almost surely bounded by $R$ and that the quadratic variation process is almost surely bounded by $\sigma^2$, meaning 
\begin{align*}
    \|X_\ell\| \leq R \quad  \mbox{and} \quad & \| \sum_{\ell=1}^L \E[X_\ell^2\mid \mathcal F_{\ell-1}]\| \leq \sigma^2 \quad \mbox{(a.s.), then}\\
\P(\| Y_L \|\geq t) = \P\Big(\| \sum_{\ell=1}^L X_\ell \| &\geq t \Big)\leq d \cdot \exp\left(\frac{-t^2/2}{\sigma^2+ Rt/3}\right)\leq d \cdot \exp\left(\frac{-t^2}{2\sigma^2+ Rt}\right).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

