{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.800326+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4168bd6bf6be12db279520442dd41964d77ad177ede3b8f2efe5525b380574d1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:connectivity of arXiv:2510.05850, 'Three-point connectivity constant for $q$-state Potts spin clusters'] For $q\in(1,4)$ and $r=1/q$, assume Conjecture~(conj of the paper) holds, and $P_n(z_1,\ldots,z_n)$ is defined as in~(equation eq:gf-0 of the paper). Then 
