{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.833068+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4168c6722e1ed350b9225e6790b988a81494b653591b22945239f8b081179f7f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop eq:ST0_OP of arXiv:2609.01751, 'Orthogonal polynomials which are eigenfunctions of a partial differential operator'] For ${\gamma} > - d_1$, let ${\alpha} = {\gamma} + d_1 -1$. Define 

\begin{equation} 
 {\mathsf Q}_{\bm j, \ell, m}^n(\bm x,\bm y) = \bm T_{\bm j, n-m}^{({\boldsymbol{\kappa}}, \alpha+2m)}(\bm y) (1-|\bm y|)^m 
