{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.500796+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4169d6fc30710ac2676e4e36a4939061e4a43011bfcb0080c7e75e2c8acfd3ea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 (Mixing property) of arXiv:2605.30030, 'Critical exponents for planar random-cluster model with cluster-weight~$q=4$'] There exist~$c_{\rm mix},C_{\rm mix}\in(0,\infty)$ such that for every~$r\le R/2$ and every two events~$A$ and~$B$ depending on edges in~$\Lambda_r$ and outside~$\Lambda_R$, respectively, 
