{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.871011+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_416c1786f2cfdfdefabb9fee67465ae759ac3696a278481480343490d55f9ed9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition spine-decomposition of arXiv:2504.20963, 'Exponential moments of truncated branching random walk martingales'] Fix $x \ge 0$. For every $n \ge 0$,  $ \widehat{\mathbb{P}}^*_{x}  \big|_{ \mathcal{F}_{n}} =  \widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{x}   \big|_{ \mathcal{F}_{n}}  $. Moreover, 
