where $\delta$ is given in Eq.\ ((delta of the paper)), and where $c\in (0,+\infty)$ if $\delta=0$, and $c\in (-1,0)\cup (0,1)$ if $\delta=1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.564652+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_417859174cf1db08b6bade45be353296493bca80ecff64ef70f7e87a8b16a682","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2608.27249, 'Torus actions, almost non-negative curvature and fundamental groups'] For all \(m\in \mathbb{N}\), there is a constant \(0<C(m)<\infty\), such that the fundamental group of every almost non-negatively curved closed manifold \(M\) of dimension \(m\), which is homotopy equivalent to a closed manifold \(N\) such that \(N\) admits an action of a torus \(T\) which has a minimal stratum consisting of a single orbit, contains a abelian subgroup of index \(<C(m)\).

  Moreover, there is a finite index abelian subgroup of \(\pi_1(M)\) which acts trivially on \(\pi_2(M)\).
  If the torus action on \(N\) is slice-maximal then the action of \(\pi_1(M)\) on \(\pi_2(M)\) is \(C(m)\)-trivial. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.371646+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4179bfe20cdf27d53b46e6325a02e90a82b745068d9957d03ce0661e93044a0d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2512.08595, 'Small time asymptotics of spectral heat content of isotropic processes'] For any $\varepsilon>0$,
		\begin{align*}
