{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.202808+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_41a7dfcf8f3d18671ca991569c2923aa7ee4c1d1491062338a8f3b1c8abf9be7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition nonlinear log sobolev of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] We say the reversible quadratic system associated to \(\ensuremath{\mathcal Q}_J^{\ensuremath{\mathcal K}}\) satisfies a \textbf{Nonlinear-Modified Log-Sobolev Inequality} of rate \(\alpha\), abbreviated as \(NMLSI(\alpha)\), if  for all 
