{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.367335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_41ac8c3a1d5b1630b1307ae80cf5e505b0b1bf8fe26a26b1175f119bd1993d92","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:main square-integrable of arXiv:2605.22803, 'Persistence of asymptotic variance under transport:\\ from hyperfluctuation to stealthy hy'] Suppose that $\Phi$ is a locally absolutely square-integrable invariant random complex measure, and that $K$ is an invariant transport kernel. Further, assume that either Condition~(c:condition square-integrable general of the paper) or Condition~(c:condition square-integrable Markov of the paper) holds.
Then $K\Phi$ is locally absolutely square-integrable.
\begin{proof}
If Condition~(c:condition square-integrable general of the paper) holds, the assertion follows from Lemma~(l:remainder2case1 of the paper). If Condition~(c:condition square-integrable Markov of the paper) holds, the assertion follows from Lemma~(l:remainder2case2 of the paper). In both cases, we apply the lemmas with $p=0$. The lemmas each actually include a stronger statement, which we do not need here but in the following subsection. Also, while Lemmas~(l:remainder2case1 of the paper) and~(l:remainder2case2 of the paper) make the same statements under different conditions, the proofs differ completely. The proof of Lemma~(l:remainder2case2 of the paper) follows a technique that is adapted from a proof in~[Dereudre_Flimmel_Huesmann_Leblé_2024].
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.364889+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_41b14b057fe43b223de148b78644e075e3c7d6e513ce3ced3b60c30d611c0a0f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 13 of arXiv:2506.20146, 'Parabolic Anderson Model in the Hyperbolic Space. Part I: Annealed Asymptotics'] Let $R,\varepsilon>0$ be given fixed. Then the
