{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.733027+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_41d65f75e9a162469cbbc7f990452ef64f38edccfb501bdd6c18a08c5c994396","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 13 of arXiv:2609.02755, 'The Sharp Rate of Probabilistically Strong Convergence to the KPZ Equation'] Given a rooted tree $\tau$, we say that $C \subset E_+(\tau)$ is a cut of $\tau$ if any path in $E(\tau)$ with the root of $\tau$ as an endpoint contains at most one edge in $C$. We denote by $\mathbb{C}[\tau]$ the set of all cuts of $\tau$.
	We recall that for a rooted tree $\tau$, there is a natural partial ordering on $E(\tau)$ in which $e \ge e^\prime$ iff $e^\prime$ lies on the unique path from $e$ to the root.

	 We write $\tau_{\ng C}$ for the subgraph consisting of those edges $e \in E(\tau)$ such that there does not exist $\tilde{e} \in C$ with $e \ge \tilde{e}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.504163+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_41dda3e47c3c57d30cee01fa313e3d4e9807d1d01fd17a1b7872ff31424adb82","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 75 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $\xi \in \bbr^m$ be arbitrary. An $\bbr^m$-valued continuous, adapted process $Y = (Y_t)_{t \in [0,T_0]}$ for some $T_0 \in (0,T]$ is called a \emph{local solution} to the Stratonovich SDE \eqref{SDE-Strat} with $Y_0 = \xi$ if
\begin{align*}
Y_t = \xi + \int_0^t f_0(s,Y_s) ds + \int_0^t f(s,Y_s) \circ dB_s, \quad t \in [0,T_0].
\end{align*}
If we can choose $T_0 = T$, then we also call $Y$ a \emph{(global) solution} to the Stratonovich SDE \eqref{SDE-Strat} with $Y_0 = \xi$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:32:20.720559+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_41e03c75e06818262964becf93113b33196ecd95daf83781d728573e8f8dba81","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 21 of arXiv:2609.00285, 'Multicrossing complex of knot and secant classes'] Let $A$ be an abelian group. Then
