{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.025537+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_41e04fc3d46875c5b7e86479785d68161ff70cb0ccbd12ea3ace17531d72f5ac","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Def:Orey of arXiv:2512.06984, 'Infinite Dimensional Multifractal Analysis of the Wiener measure'] For $q \in ( 0  , 1) $, let $C_q^{\mathrm{crit}} $  be the set of \emph{critical $q$-Hölder functions} that is the set of $\bar{\omega} \in \Omega$ such that:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item  the function $ \bar{\omega} $ is $\alpha$-Hölder  for every $\alpha < q $, 
    \item the Hölder exponent of $ \bar{\omega}$ is at most $q$ in the sense that the following limit exists and equals $q$:
    \begin{equation} 
    \lim_{ n \to + \infty } \frac{ - \log \left\{  \sum_{i =1}^n \left[ \bar{\omega} \left(\frac{i}{n}  \right) - \bar{\omega} \left( \frac{i-1}{n} \right) \right]^2 \right\} }{2 \log n } = q \; . 
    \end{equation}
\end{enumerate}
We then introduce the set of \emph{critical Hölder functions} as 
\begin{equation*}
    \Omega^\mathrm{crit} := \bigcup_{ q \in (0,1) }  C_q^{\mathrm{crit}} \;. 
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.774486+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_41e534a2e9336d4bc17c5f955cc3b19471287ac7b9d07e2017d211722e621443","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thmhit of arXiv:2411.09257, 'Iterated Generalized Counting Process and its Extensions'] Let $T_n\coloneqq\inf\{s>0:\hat{M}(s)=n\}$ be the first-passage time of IGCP for any state $n\ge1$. Then, its distribution is given by
