{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.085295+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_421834b1ea73ec1864a830e53dcf4249f44183b31d135a9d9d8c81d27974d447","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition s-normalization of arXiv:2412.08400, '\vspace{-1.0cm} Characterization of Exponential Families of \\ Lumpable Stochastic Matrice'] When $(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E})$ is strongly connected we define the mapping
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
    {\mathfrak{s}} \colon \mathcal{F}^+(\mathcal{Y},\mathcal{E}) &\to \mathcal{W}(\mathcal{Y},\mathcal{E}) \\
    F &\mapsto P \colon \mathcal{E} \to \mathbb{R}_+, (y,y') \mapsto P(y,y') = \frac{F(y,y') v_F(y')}{\rho_F v_F(y)},
