{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.486998+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4220b52976b91f63215f13ac30ab91cc39d18caa9c28df09a1c8adf83b6ad4c3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 5 of arXiv:2607.03360, 'Smoluchowski-Kramers Approximation Meets Khasminskii Averaging Principles in Nonequilibriu'] Suppose that \assmref{ass:mom-bdd} and \assmref{ass:gd-lip} hold. For each $t\in [0,T]$, the quantity $\sqrt{m} |v_t^m|$ is bounded in $L^2(\Omega)$. More precisely, there exists a constant $C_{T,\la_0,|v_0|}>0$, independent of $m$, such that 
\beq{bdd-mvs}
\EE\Big[m|v_t^m|^2\Big] \leq C_{T,\la_0,|v_0|}.
\eeq
Consequently,
\beq{0-mvs}
\EE\Big[|mv_t^m|^2\Big] \leq C_{T,\la_0,|v_0|}m.
