{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.474591+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42458b1445b4536ce732c7182d3ba9f213ddc7fdd6d0675bc98634f5b5694cc0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Theo1 of arXiv:2511.19391, 'Central limit theorem for supercritical Crump-Mode-Jagers processes counted with non-indiv'] Suppose that assumptions (A1 of the paper)-(A7 of the paper) hold and  let $\varphi$ be an $h$-dependent descendant characteristic, for some $h \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$, satisfying (C1 of the paper)-(C5 of the paper). Then, as $t \rightarrow \infty$, $t \in \mathbb{G}$, 
