{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.160920+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_424e8a43d111b2e3d495ed264c62b71b5b1d2f0d6bbb49ca80c72d6bc07c1356","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor eq:right-derived-rep of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $\textbf{\textup{C}}$ be a locally fibrant simplicial model category, and let $G\colon\textbf{\textup{C}}\to\textbf{\textup{SSet}}$ be a functor that is corepresented (in the enriched sense) by a cofibrant $X\in\textbf{\textup{C}}$. Then $G$ is right Quillen and
    \begin{equation}
        \textbf{\textup{C}}[{\mathcal{W}}^{-1}]\xrightarrow{\;\textbf{\textup{R}}G\;}\textbf{\textup{SSet}}[{\mathcal{W}}_\textup{Quillen}^{-1}]\simeq\Spc
    \end{equation}
    is corepresented (in the $\infty$-categorical sense) by the same $X$; here the unlabelled equivalence in $(\textup{(eq:right-derived-rep of the paper)})$ is the unique one.
    \begin{proof}
        As the mapping space functor for $\textbf{\textup{C}}$ is a right Quillen bifunctor, $G$ is indeed right Quillen. It then suffices to show that the two functors $\textbf{\textup{C}}[{\mathcal{W}}^{-1}]$ agree after restriction to the full subcategory of $\textbf{\textup{C}}$ spanned by the cofibrant-fibrant objects, where this follows by the same argument as in the previous lemma.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.454591+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4255d1277a57f94e52356be9bee42dc3dfb2b4dc9cc1d41aa93be1ce0aa14e28","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 (Proposition 2.2 in \cite{Guan-Ma2003}) of arXiv:2609.02516, 'Power convexity of the torsion function on horo-convex domains in hyperbolic space'] Suppose that $W=(w_{\alpha\beta})$ is diagonal. For $k=1,2,\cdots,n$, we have
\begin{equation}}
\frac{\partial\sigma_k(W)}{\partial w_{\alpha\beta}}=\begin{cases}
