{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.256134+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4276518e3765c2ad98bc3913b3c79f28560a5c8c7e3faaf5839b69454722dfaa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:delta_explicit of arXiv:2609.04092, 'Short character sums of inhomogeneous polynomials'] Fix an integer $\kappa\geq 1$. Let $\underline{s}=(s_1,...,s_\kappa)\in \{1,2\}^\kappa$, and for $i=1, 2$, define 
        \begin{align*}
    \sigma_{\kappa,\underline{s}}^i = |\{s\in \{s_1,...,s_\kappa\}:s= i\}|.
        \end{align*}      
    Fix tuples ${\bf h}_1,...,{\bf h}_{\kappa}$ with ${\bf h}_i\in [-\mathbf{L}_{s_i},\mathbf{L}_{s_i}]$.  Let $1\leq j\leq k$ and $0\leq \xi_{0}^1,\xi_{0}^2\leq j$ be integers satisfying $\xi_{0}^1 + \xi_{0}^2=j$.  Then,  if $\xi_{0}^1 <\sigma_{\kappa,\underline{s}}^1$ or $\xi_{0}^2 <\sigma_{\kappa,\underline{s}}^2$, then $\Delta_{\underline{s},\underline{{\bf h}}}^{\kappa}\tilde{\Phi}_{j,(\xi^{1}_{0},\xi^{2}_{0})}({\bf x}_1,{\bf x}_2)$ vanishes.
    Otherwise,
 upon recalling the definition (equation def:tilde_phi of the paper),
    \begin{align}
\Delta_{\underline{s},\underline{{\bf h}}}^{\kappa}\tilde{\Phi}_{j,(\xi^{1}_0,\xi^{2}_0)}({\bf x}_1,{\bf x}_2)
                = \sum_{\iota_\kappa=0}^{\xi_{\kappa-1}^{s_\kappa}-1}\cdots \sum_{\iota_1=0}^{\xi_{0}^{s_1}-1}\binom{\xi_{\kappa-1}^{s_\kappa}}{\iota_\kappa}\cdots \binom{\xi_{0}^{s_1}}{\iota_1} \tilde{\Phi}_{j,(\xi_\kappa^{1},\xi_\kappa^{2},\eta_\kappa^{1},...,\eta_\kappa^{\kappa})}({\bf x}_1,{\bf x}_2,{\bf h}_1,...,{\bf h}_{\kappa}),
            \end{align}
        where
            \begin{align*}
                (\xi^1_{\kappa},\xi^2_{\kappa},\eta^1_{\kappa},...,\eta^{\kappa}_{\kappa})=
                \begin{cases}
                    (\xi^1_{\kappa-1},\iota_\kappa,\eta^1_{\kappa-1},...,\eta_{\kappa-1}^{\kappa-1},\xi_{\kappa-1}^{2}-\iota_\kappa), &s_\kappa=1\\
                     (\iota_\kappa,\xi_{\kappa-1}^{2},\eta_{\kappa-1}^{1},...,\eta_{\kappa-1}^{\kappa-1},\xi_{\kappa-1}^{1}-\iota_\kappa), &s_\kappa=2,
                \end{cases}
            \end{align*}
       and $\eta_\kappa^{i}\geq 1$ for all $1\leq i \leq \kappa-1$.
       In particular, $\Delta_{\underline{s},\underline{{\bf h}}}^{\kappa}\tilde{\Phi}_{j,(\xi^{1}_0,\xi^{2}_0)}({\bf x}_1,{\bf x}_2)$ has bihomogeneous degree $(\xi^{1}_0-\sigma^{1}_{\kappa,\underline{s}},\xi^{2}_0-\sigma^{2}_{\kappa,\underline{s}})$ in the variables $({\bf x}_1,{\bf x}_2)$.","status":"unverified"}

