{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.353052+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_427e699bf0a7fee4714c8b362d2e834a2e4410ebbccf2f88a0465c152e24ca5d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition defi2.3 of arXiv:2608.22945, 'A Momentum-Based Variance-Reduced Algorithm for Federated Multiobjective Optimization'] An iterate $x^t$ generated by a stochastic algorithm is said to be an \emph{$\epsilon$-Pareto stationary solution in expectation} if
