{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.256129+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_428eb570ea888e0cf3f7f504085bc79d8131a521c45f0821806eb319fa126e39","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem RDS_SDS_MEAU of arXiv:2603.12774, 'Synchronization by noise for stochastic differential equations driven by fractional Browni'] Under the assumptions of Lemma~(RR_TT of the paper), for every $\omega = (\omega^-, \omega^+) \in \mathcal{B}_H \times \mathcal{B}_H$ and $x \in \mathbb{R}^d$, 
