{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.365758+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42c3d68cd1b2346147fc1d9d8db806627d3626af9e09b2b7644ea4c693897911","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def solution for NBC of arXiv:2504.06238, 'Infinite Boundary Friction Limit for Weak Solutions of the Stochastic Navier-Stokes Equati'] Let  $u_0: \Omega \rightarrow L^2_{\sigma}$ be $\mathcal{F}_0-$measurable and $\alpha_n \in C^2(\partial \mathscr{O}; \mathbb{R})$. A process $u^n$ which is progressively measurable in $\bar{W}^{1,2}_{\sigma}$ such that for $\mathbbm{P}-a.e.$ $\omega$, $u^n_{\cdot}(\omega) \in C\left([0,T];L^2_{\sigma}\right) \cap L^2\left([0,T];\bar{W}^{1,2}_{\sigma}\right)$, is said to be a weak solution of the equation ((NSalphan of the paper)) if it satisfies the identity
\begin{align} \nonumber
     \inner{u^n_t}{\psi} = \inner{u_0}{\psi} - \int_0^{t}\inner{\mathcal{L}_{u^n_s}u^n_s}{\psi}ds &- \nu\int_0^{t} \inner{u^n_s}{\psi}_1 ds + \nu\int_0^t \inner{(\kappa - \alpha_n)u^n_s}{\psi}_{L^2(\partial \mathscr{O}; \mathbb{R}^2)}ds\\ &+ \frac{1}{2}\int_0^{t}\sum_{i=1}^\infty \inner{B_iu^n_s}{B_i^*\psi} ds - \int_0^{t} \inner{Bu^n_s}{\psi} d\mathcal{W}_s
\end{align}
for every $\psi \in \bar{W}^{1,2}_{\sigma}$, $\mathbbm{P}-a.s.$ in $\mathbb{R}$ for all $t\in[0,T]$. Moreover $u^n$ is said to be unique if for any other such process $v^n$, $u^n$ and $v^n$ are indistinguishable.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.258347+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42cb52604989cad4972f4d1b635824a9bd5c1fdd16167f484aa3658bbe160dcd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2604.19308, '\textbf{On McKean--Vlasov SDEs with polynomial drifts for SIS epidemic models}'] Assume that~\eqref{co:3},~\eqref{co:6} and~\eqref{co:7} are satisfied. Then
