\end{equation*}
for all $n\in\N$, $j\in\{0,\dots,k_{n}-1\}$ and $t\in [t_{j,n},t_{j+1,n}]$ with the two non-negative constants
\begin{align*}
k_{p,j,n} &:= \max_{i=0,\dots,j} \big((p-1)\hat{b}_{0} + p(\hat{b}_{k+3} + c_{p}l^{2})\big)(t_{i,n},N(t_{i,n})),
\\
l_{p,j,n} &:= \max_{i=0,\dots,j} \big(2(p-1)\big(\hat{b}_{0} + c_{p}l^{2}\big) + (2p-1)\hat{b}_{k+3}\big)(t_{i,n},N(t_{i,n})).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.502745+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42cb738cb0883d6a8685327d1bee42bfcfeef88ff1fe2a2f9582265c7426e6ee","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:mu-mixture of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[proposition]{prop:moment-law}
Fix an integer \(q\ge1\) and \(\sigma>1\).  There exists \(\varepsilon_0>0\) such that, for every \(0<\varepsilon<\varepsilon_0\), one can find a symmetric compactly supported \(C^\infty\) density \(\nu\) for which
