{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:52:32.335117+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42fe0888ea617dc74369e6fb37bef227d2ae136b6f8e4ca09c22c777641f0089","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:GGCpolynomrate of arXiv:2609.03980, 'Decay Rates and Domain Dependence of a Coupled Wave-Heat System with Spatially Dependant H'] Let $(\Omega,\Omega_w,\Omega_h)$ be a Lipschitz interface triple in $\mathbb{R}^n$ with $\Omega_h$ controlling $\Omega_w$ in time, and let $S \in L^\infty(\Omega_h,\mathbb{C}^{n\times n})$ be accretive.
