{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.678992+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43384128b69298425c78e6a0f072063923f1c5d9423312615907c58deb1f17e1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2609.02699, '\vspace{-0.5 cm}Gauge theory and symplectic structures'] There exists a constant $C>0$ depending only on $r$ and the geometry of $M$ such that if $(\phi,A,\beta)$ solves equations \eqref{Dirac 6d}, \eqref{Curvature 6d} then
