{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.324954+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_433dc3775fa63154abb5d1fcdde94a476707ccb734cfdcf5ac15fc0061451dce","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:finitecollision of arXiv:2601.10624, 'Source localisation in simple random walks'] Suppose $\mathbb{H}$ is an infinite, connected, vertex-transitive, recurrent graph of finite degree. Further, let $a$, $b \in \mathbb{H}$ be such that the transition probability $p_{2j}(a, b)$ is positive for some $j \geqslant 0$, and consider two independent simple random walks $X_t$, $Y_t$ on $\mathbb{H}$. Then, we have
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{P}(\exists t > 0 \colon X_t = Y_t \mid X_0 = a, Y_0 = b) = 1.
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

