{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.252133+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43751eaf94ce3f1ee230aff0447bbd9aeb03ddbc0b40f9a2617afdad3d26d9d0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 23 of arXiv:2604.15226, '\bfseries Nonlinear Schrödinger equations with spatial white noise potential on full space'] There exists distributions $\Wick{\nabla X_1\cdot\nabla X_2}\in\CC_{-\delta}^{-\frac{1}{2}-\kappa}(\IR^3)$ and $\Wick{|\nabla X_2|^2}\in\CC_{-\delta}^{-\kappa}(\IR^3)$ such that
\begin{equation}
