in probability in the space $\CC_{-\delta}^{-\kappa}(\IR^3)$ for any $\kappa,\delta>0$ with $c_\eps^2=\IE\big[|\nabla X_{2,\eps}|^2\big]$ a diverging quantity. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.130689+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43761109ff4fb5be316dde0e64cae50dac18bd3f7b07b5b5e080895a6948284b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma E:dg of arXiv:2510.09818, 'On the Fourier dimension of fractional Brownian graphs'] [LL25]
	Let $H \in (0,1)$.
	Let $0<s_1<\cdots<s_I$ and $a = (a_1,\dots,a_I) \in \mathbb R^I$ with $\sum_{i=1}^I a_i = 0$. Then:
	\begin{enumerate}
	\item[(i)] For any $i \in \{1,\dots, I\}$,
	\begin{align}
		\partial_{s_i} g_a(s) = 2H \sum_{j=1}^{i-1} a_i a_j (s_i-s_j)^{2H-1} - 2H \sum_{j=i+1}^I a_i a_j (s_j-s_i)^{2H-1}.
	\end{align}
	\item[(ii)] For any $i<j$ in $\{1,\dots, I\}$,
	\begin{align}
		\partial_{s_i} \partial_{s_j} g_a(s) = 2H(1-2H) a_i a_j (s_j-s_i)^{2H-2}.
	\end{align}
	\item[(iii)] If $k \ge 3$, then for all $i_1<\cdots<i_k$ in $\{1,\dots, I\}$,
	\begin{align}
		\partial_{s_{i_1}} \cdots \partial_{s_{i_k}} g_a(s) = 0.
	\end{align}
	\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.738657+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4377fd4991aef3742e6f9bec7f6e948918144cea286752445eb880b7705ef86d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 40 of arXiv:2609.02755, 'The Sharp Rate of Probabilistically Strong Convergence to the KPZ Equation'] Let $\tilde{E}, E, F$ be metric spaces. Let $\iota : \tilde{E} \to E$ be a compact embedding. Let $E_{\mathrm{sol}} \subset E$ be open and let $f : E_{\mathrm{sol}} \to F$ be continuous. Suppose that $(X_\lambda)_{\lambda \in \Lambda}$ is a collection of $\tilde{E}$-valued random variables such that:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item there exist $e \in \tilde{E}$ and $p > 0$ such that $\sup_{\lambda \in \Lambda} \mathbb{E}[ d_{\tilde{E}}(X_\lambda, e)^p ] < \infty$;
		\item for every $\lambda \in \Lambda$, $\iota(X_\lambda) \in E_{\mathrm{sol}}$ almost surely;
		\item every subsequential limit $\mu$ of the laws $(\iota(X_{\lambda}))_{\lambda \in \Lambda}$ satisfies $\mu(E_{\mathrm{sol}}) = 1$.
	\end{enumerate}
	Then for all $y_0 \in F$,
	\begin{equ}
		\limsup_{M \to \infty} \sup_{\lambda \in \Lambda} \mathbb{P}( d_F( f(\iota(X_\lambda)), y_0) > M) = 0\;.
	\end{equ}","status":"unverified"}

