{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.364653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43c21ed4e4658a6bdb28531a95e7b6343354a821ddfd1ba56e01aaba59872711","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem crossingbubble of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] There exists $\beta>0$ that is independent of $\alpha$ such that for all $\zeta>0$, there exists $R_0=R_0(\zeta)$ such that for all $R\geq R_0$, all $p$ sufficiently small depending on $R$, there exists a constant $C=C(R,\alpha, \zeta)$ such that 
