\end{equation}for all $n{,k}$ and all levels $d\geq k$ with $R^{-d}n\geq 1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.110277+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43c572ab2097ee3a710374cfe85968ea5a5087c5e60ee7e4ca3c909d726d7277","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma heat0 of arXiv:2411.15881, 'Stable Approximation for Call Function Via Stein's method'] Let the random variable $Y\sim S_\alpha(1,0)$ and denote the density function of $Y$ by $p_{1,0}$. Then for any $y\in(-\infty,\infty)$, we have
