{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.733425+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43d72d5b643e0801b60c66964edca589c3966a51db2be56f4a5e5fcbe2f95855","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Greenasymp of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] Let $\eta \in [0,1)$ and $\vec{\textbf{a}} \in \operatorname{HB}_{\epsilon_p}$ be such that $\textbf{a}^{(\emptyset)} = 0$. 
