{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.246004+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_443bbb66476143868e9a5f3591c5cb1f29f9797db8379b0cea2f18e01874e2db","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2609.01098, 'Gaussian upper bounds for averaged heat semigroups on graphs'] Let  $C,r_0>0$ and $n>2$ and assume that, for all $B(r)\subset  X$, $r\geq r_0$, and all $U\subset B(r)$, we have the Faber-Krahn inequality
