{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.449502+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_44f73933552e962f7dc329b8cf6dea10e22567bb75ca701f5154bd857a3bb981","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma convsubs of arXiv:2609.02213, 'Invariant subspaces for free linearizations of Lipschitz maps'] Let $(M,e)$ be a pointed metric space. Let $p\in\mathbb{N}$ and let $a_1,\ldots,a_p\in\mathbb{K}$ be such that $\sum_{i=1}^p a_i = 0$ and
		\begin{equation} 
			\sum_{i\in J}a_i\neq 0,
			\qquad \forall J\subset\{1,\ldots,p\},\; \emptyset \neq J \subsetneq \{1,\ldots, p\}.
		\end{equation}
		For $1\leq k\leq p$, let $(x_k(n))_n$ be sequences in $M$, and set $\gamma_n:=\sum_{k=1}^p a_k\delta(x_k(n))$.
		If $(\gamma_n)_n$ has a weakly convergent subsequence with limit $\gamma=\sum_{k=1}^q b_k\delta(y_k) \neq 0$,
