		In particular, the subsequence converge to $\gamma$ in norm.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:08.985147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_44f81392214d907b9473430facc90fc2c445e5f295da96ba1ba67e731b22d5ae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:multil of arXiv:2411.10829, 'Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble and its Laplace transform'] Choose $m\in \mathbb N$, $\vec \mathbf k \in \mathbb R^m_+ $, and $\vec \boldsymbol{\tau}\in \mathbb R_{\ge 0}^m$ such that $\boldsymbol{\tau}_1\le \cdots \le \boldsymbol{\tau}_m$, any real $C_1>0$, and a large enough $N\in \mathbb N$. We take the rank $N$ G$\beta$E corners process $\{y^n_i\}_{1\leq i\leq n\leq N}$, with variance $\tau=2N/\beta$; and $\vec k \in \mathbb Z^m$, and integers $N\ge N_1\ge \cdots \ge N_m$,  such that
