{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.216292+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4500d833986d218cabddb362b23530f0a0634fea9370c71001e72a396b78504a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition sq_holder of arXiv:2412.07690, 'A law of large numbers concerning the distribution of critical points of random Fourier se'] For any $\mu>0$ and $\forall A,B\in \Sym_{\geq 0}({\boldsymbol{V}})$,  such that $A^{1/2}+B^{1/2}\geq \mu{\mathbbm{1}}$ we have
