{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.216016+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_456ca7d4fad05376ce872e0b427883b08f67a985040024be6364cf302bd48046","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Eprocess of arXiv:2607.05671, 'Bi-infinite systems of singularly interacting Brownian particles and the KPZ equation'] Fix $(t,x) \in [0,\infty)\times \mathbb{R}$ and $\delta, \varepsilon>0$.
