{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.137640+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45739c54b80ae0a0611d0ecedb5c12088412678015fa0662d04fb2138b2e9d57","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2608.27569, 'Laplace and Dolbeault operators on Sasakian manifolds'] Let $(M^{2n+1},g,\xi)$ be a compact Sasakian manifold. Let  $m\in \{0,\ldots, 2n+1\}$. Then, 
