in terms of the pure and mixed Palm probability measures $\mathbb E_{{\mathcal V }_l}^0$, for $l\in\{1,2\}$, and $\mathbb{E}_{{\mathcal V }^{(k)}_{l,r}}^0$, for $l\neq r, k\in\{1,2\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.866414+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45ac8aff95f34dbd99d42424b2fbcc37d4c787363abb71116894508b4aedf892","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:eid-dirstructure of arXiv:2510.13659, 'On the energy image density conjecture of Bouleau and Hirsch'] Let $(X,\mathcal{X},\mu,\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$ be a Dirichlet structure with the associated carr\'e du champ operator $\gamma: \mathcal{F} \times \mathcal{F} \to L^1(\mu)$. For any $n \in \mathbb{N}$, $\bphi \in \mathcal{F}^n$, we have
