        \int f \, d\mu = \int f \, d\nu 
    \end{align*}
    for all $f \in D$ then $\mu = \nu$. That is, $D$ is sufficiently large that measures agreeing on $D$ must agree on the whole space.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.955864+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45b180203ba77f5ba9fbfa33340c0335a5c7bbd41c02c8e560d7025399946e15","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:non-overlap of arXiv:2608.23135, 'Graph distance and effective resistance of the random walk trace in four and five dimensio'] There exist $C=C_{\varepsilon,
