{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.826339+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45bf771244dfeaf601d1b23aeb146b07b6df082ae336f9d2096b36e0a6437fba","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition d:law-random-holonomy of arXiv:2607.24640, 'The Yang-Mills measure on surfaces via Morse theory'] Let $\gamma$ be an admissible curve. Then, one defines the law of the random holonomy along $\gamma$ as follows:
