{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:43:45.398415+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45c03479af1c0ca7419804567dee8e9070e4d5faa3d73b38c1ca1844ca44fc05","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2609.04143, 'The Geometry of Real Anisotropic Bohnenblust--Hille Constants'] If $\sigma(\mathbf q)=0$, then $C_{\mathbf q}^{(m)}=1$. If $\sigma(\mathbf q)>0$, then
