{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.304625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45c6fc35e3f6d8715acb0a7d865c6a9e83c6d5bb36e1d6eccd53ccb051fea207","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:IPLDP of arXiv:2411.14818, 'Scaling limits of solitons in the Box-Ball system'] Assume that the initial distribution ${\mu}$ is a {space-homogeneous} Bernoulli product measure or two-sided  Markov distribution supported on $\Omega$ {and that $\mu\left(\eta\left(0\right) = \eta\left(1\right) = 1\right) > 0$}. {Let $\nu$ be the conditional probability measure such that ${\mu}$ is conditioned on $\Omega_{0}$.} Then, for any $k \in {\mathbb{N}}$, we have the following. 
