{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.951105+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45deceed13373b46e78bfd943570a751351da8389e3970d28fa8d08f70dac7ea","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 259 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] In the situation of Theorem~\ref{thm:spcurvenonbip}, define the even Green function as $\textnormal{Gr}^+(p_1,p_2) = \textnormal{Gr}(p_1,p_2) + \textnormal{Gr}(p_1,\overline{\varsigma}(p_2))$, where $\textnormal{Gr}$ is the usual Green function on $\Sigma_{\boldsymbol{v}}^{\textnormal{half}}$ with Dirichlet boundary conditions. We have
