{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.365117+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45e93113ee1fbd9a43d585e1cebacd99dcddfdfe864721d99ac182bc43d5515d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor subpolynomialconc of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] For all $\alpha,\zeta>0$, $R$ sufficiently large depending on $\zeta$, and all $p$ sufficiently small depending on $R,\zeta$, there exists $C=C(\alpha,\zeta,R,p)>0$ such that for all $k\geq 1$, $n>R^k$  
