{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:36:12.196808+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_46456a95e8e630d9bac66ffbe9bd4666f59f68dd0a22b9769575b38910f5b15b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2609.03932, 'Khovanov monodromy groups via motions'] Let~$(C_1,d_1)$,~$(C_2,d_2)$ be chain complexes of finitely generated free~$\Z$-modules,~$f_i, g_i:C_i\rightarrow C_i$ chain maps for~$i\in\{1,2\}$ such that 
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
    \item~$(\id \otimes \; \varepsilon_2 g_2)$ and~$(\varepsilon_1 g_1 \otimes \id)$ induce isomorphisms on the homology~$H_\ast(C_1 \otimes C_2)$; 
    \item~$(f_i)_* = \varepsilon_i (g_i)_* \colon H_*(C_i)\rightarrow H_*(C_i)$, with~$\varepsilon_i \in \{\pm 1\}$; 
    \item~$(f_1\otimes f_2)_* = \varepsilon_1\varepsilon_2 (g_1\otimes g_2)_* \colon H_*(C_1\otimes C_2) \rightarrow H_*(C_1\otimes C_2)$. 
\end{enumerate}

Then~$(f_1\otimes \id)_* = \varepsilon_1 (g_1\otimes \id)_*$ and~$(\id\otimes f_2)_* = \varepsilon_2 (\id\otimes g_2)_*$ on~$H_*(C_1\otimes C_2)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.766844+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_46459f44f39a1b0b8de86ddbe69b92a4c083fb7678377942f1993707e674918f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Fix $q \in (0,1)$, $c \in [0, q^{-1})$, $N \in \mathbb{N}$ and let $\lpplen = \{\lpplinen_{i}\}_{i \geq 1}$ be as in (\ref{Eq.Deflpplen}). We define the constants
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&\sigma = \frac{q^{1/2}}{1- q}, \hspace{2mm} f = \frac{q^{1/3}}{2 (1 + q)^{2/3}},
\end{split}
\end{equation}
and the rescaled processes
\begin{equation}
\lpplenc_i(t) = \sigma^{-1} N^{-1/3} \cdot \left(\lpplinen_i(tN^{2/3}) - \frac{2qN}{1-q} - \frac{qtN^{2/3}}{1-q}\right) \mbox{ for } i \in \mathbb{N}, t \in [0,\infty).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.727121+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_464849973df45f84c46fe14c00b72d8413649fbb27f9c477f740645866df6b31","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop normalitycriterion of arXiv:2606.08325, 'Digit Mixing under Polynomial Maps'] Let \(Y\) be a real-valued random variable.  Let \(\alpha>0\), let \((B_s)_{s\ge1}\) be a nonnegative sequence, and let \(c>0\) be some constant.  Assume that for every real \(u\) with \(S_\alpha(|u|)\ge1\),
			\begin{equation}
				|\mathbb E e(uY)|\le \exp(-cB_{S_\alpha(|u|)}).
			\end{equation}
			Assume also that
			\begin{equation}
				\sum_{s\ge1}s\exp(-cB_s)<\infty.
			\end{equation}
			Then \(Y\) is almost surely absolutely normal. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.095910+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_464d52c7c3c8b33e9a05e2bc417fc3d2e5ab3b00faa373201386a2e872c1a10a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm John-Nirenberg inequality of arXiv:2412.08497, 'Time discretization of Quadratic Forward-Backward SDEs with singular drift'] Given $V$ a $\operatorname{BMO}\text{-process}$ and let $r$ be a fixed number in $[0,\tau]$. Then, for every integer $p\geq 1$
				\begin{align*}
					\|\mathbb{E}[\sup_{r\leq t\leq \tau}|V_t-V_r|^p/\mathfrak{F}_{r}]\|_{\infty} \leq p!(11\varrho_{r,\tau}(V))^p.
				\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.976710+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_464eb71fad0e3c8befd374e7d5f1b127380057fa9630f245c9582a6517fc7fec","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:1052a of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] For any $N\in\N$, $p\in[1,\infty]$ and $\mu\in(0,1]$, we denote by $\mathcal{W}^p_{N,\mu}$ the set of all time weights $u_\mu\in \mathcal{D}(\R)$ verifying
\begin{equs}
  \max_{i\leqslant N} 
    \mu^{-1/p+i}
    {\| \d^i_t u_\mu 
    \|}_{L^p((-\infty,1])}< \infty\,.
\end{equs}
Then, for every $\psi\in \mathcal{D}(\R)$, $M\geqslant N$ and $q\in[1,\infty]$, uniform in $\mu\in(0,1]$ we have
    \begin{equs}      \norm{K_{M,\mu}\big(u_\mu\psi)}_{L^{q}}&\lesssim \norm{K_{M,\mu}\psi}_{L^{q}}\,,\;\text{provided} \; u_\mu \in\mathcal{W}^\infty_{N,\mu}\,,\\
          \norm{K_{M,\mu}\big(u_\mu\psi)}_{L^{1}}&\lesssim\mu \norm{K_{M,\mu}\psi}_{L^\infty}\,,\;\text{provided} \; u_\mu \in\mathcal{W}^1_{N,\mu}\,.
    \end{equs}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.943765+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4650c2c54c63a2d2fca32593f7070210959102d7917b10ca28764131a39144e1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:semicontinuity of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Fix $(R,b)$ as above. The function $I:\text{AF}(\Lambda,R,b)\to [0,\infty)$ given by 
