{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.653947+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_467160fa12ee04bd4a9bc77f54668d607ebf863c1ada145f3998337bcbd4ed5e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 (When upward jumps are admissible) of arXiv:2608.30859, 'Conservation Laws with Discontinuous Flux:\\ A First Application to Traffic Flow'] Let $u^-<u^+$ and $\theta^-\ne\theta^+$. According to \eqref{eq:LaxCond}, upward jumps are Lax-admissible in the following two situations:
