{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.329145+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_46b908ea58785db892766814f4e9f38d6aeb1e50e3a5bd7a3b79eb5a2541c012","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:spectralgap of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] There exists a universal constant $C_5=C_5(\kappa )>0$ such that for any local function $f$ supported in $\{0,\hdots ,\ell -1\}$ for some $\ell\ge 1$, with $\psi_f(\rho ,\mathcal{E})=0$ for any $\rho \in [0,1]$ and $\mathcal{E}\in [\rho ,\kappa\rho]$, we have 
