{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:53:39.213367+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4711ae201a58dc8c626ca42b164618fc6e3d5761aacffec3658587828edbfd76","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 12 of arXiv:2608.27022, 'On LCK Geometry of Gauduchon Connections'] Let $(M,J,\omega)$ be a non-K\"ahler lcK manifold. Suppose that $\omega$ is Gauduchon, $\|\theta\|$ is constant and $dRic^{t,2}=0$, then there only are two possibilities 
