= \mathcal{L}^{(d)}\bigl[\iota_d(\mathfrak{q})\bigr]\bigl(\iota_d(f)\bigr) 
\qquad f \in \mathbb{R}[x]_d,
\end{align*}
where $\iota_d(\mathfrak{q}) \coloneqq \{\iota_d(q_s)\}_{s\ge0} \subset \operatorname{Im}\iota_{d}$ is a $\boxplus^d$-semigroup.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.333692+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4724600176968fec4e916f6c65c7da7fa611e59e0c692e29e3a7f51e91883803","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2511.06196, 'Central limit theorem for high temperature spin models via martingale embedding'] We have
