{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.292078+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4749c23221875db32a5a531f311058e44a2c0c9334c71bffe571f7d4275d7840","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:UV_int of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Let the test functions $f_1,f_2$ satisfy the assumptions of Theorem~(theo:main of the paper) and let $K$ be defined as in (equation eq:def_K of the paper). For any $x_1,x_2\in (0,1]$ with $x_1<x_2$ it holds that
