{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.429573+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4782ce538221aab8709732866d7c161dd1f21dd1ba46c93625f1b1aac28d61d4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma alpha_quantile_properties of arXiv:2605.20471, 'Note on the Weak Convergence of Hyperplane $α$-Quantile Functionals and Their Continuity i'] Let $t>0,\alpha \in (0,1),\gamma \in \mathbb{R}^d$. Define the hyperplane $\alpha$-quantile functional $\mathcal{D}_{\mathbb{R}^d}[0,\infty) \ni x\mapsto M_{t,\alpha}(x)$ by
	\begin{equation}
	M_{t,\alpha}(x)=\inf\bigg\{y:\frac{1}{t}\int_0^t\mathbf{1}_{\{z\in \mathbb{R}^d:\gamma \cdot z \leq y\}}(x_s)ds\geq \alpha\bigg\}
