{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:11:57.318376+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4796d9276e0c07e26f3619ec71ba2a917cc34994db670c52477e58021ae24868","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2607.23526, 'Equivalence of Canonical and Microcanonical Ensembles for Euclidean Lattices'] The functions $Z$, $\psi$, $m$, and $\sigma^2$ are real analytic on $(0,+\infty)$, and
