{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.053167+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_47b9fdedb850a0e1fef412239e160ebfbfdec4cf0cd5db69019be1e466a7df29","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 37 of arXiv:2606.16164, 'A Low-Regularity Semigroup Sewing Lemma via Quotient Structures'] Let $0<\sigma<1$, $\beta>0$, and define $N_h:=h^{-\sigma/2}$ for $0<h\le1$.  Then there are constants $C,c>0$ such that for all $x\in H^{\alpha+\beta}$,
