{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.830066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_47f5618ea69f56510907265cfe26b5763ad718027c083b765ff652c957e1230f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:stable-threshold of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] Let $X$ be a one-dimensional symmetric $\gamma$-stable Levy process with $\gamma\in(0,2)$ and let $\mathrm{Sig}^M(X)$ be its geometric Marcus lift. For every integer $k\ge1$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}\left[\left|\inner{\mathrm{Sig}^M(X)_{0,T}}{1^k}\right|\right]<\infty
\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
k<\gamma.
