{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:47:07.722702+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4861c4f273dc455812112fde34b0c85412e355c738f22086f7477650fbe3ece4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 (Orientation of the coupling) of arXiv:2608.06523, 'On the Gardner Transition in the Ising Pure $p$-Spin Glass II'] At the marginal base point,
\begin{equation}
 \frac{\partial\beta^2}{\partial m}
 =-(p-1)\frac{\beta^2}{\Gamma_\mu(q)}
 \frac{\partial\Gamma_\mu(q)}{\partial m}<0,

\end{equation}
and
\begin{align}
 \frac{\partial\beta^2}{\partial\xi'(q)}
 ={}&\frac{\beta^2(1-m)}{
 \xi'(q)\E[\cosh^{-4}(M(q))e^{W_\mu(q)}]}
 \Big[2\{\E[\cosh^{-2}(M(q))e^{W_\mu(q)}]
          -\E[\cosh^{-4}(M(q))e^{W_\mu(q)}]\}\notag\\
 &\hspace{25mm}+\frac m2\{\E[\cosh^{-4}(M(q))e^{W_\mu(q)}]
          -\E[\cosh^{-2}(M(q))e^{W_\mu(q)}]^2\}\Big]>0.

\end{align}
At the marginal base point, the derivative along the stationary level
curve satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \frac{d\beta^2}{dm}
 =\frac{\partial\beta^2}{\partial m}
 +\frac{\partial\beta^2}{\partial\xi'(q)}
   \frac{d\,\xi'(q)}{dm}<0.

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

