{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.324169+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4884336eaf826be7b2351a8d9090005e761da0c7b2168020fc39a50f750e7e91","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:deformed-moment-convergence of arXiv:2609.03532, 'Airy limit for the Jack process and topological expansion'] For every $\theta>0$, $\boldsymbol k\in\mathbb R_{>0}^m$, and
