{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.644558+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_489c33765413a11dbd27ba538d716c2a0b4d6ccf4fbd80994551be5d36ba7a31","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:contour_random_narrow_exc_pos of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] For any sequence of events $(A_n)_{n \geq 1}$, and any $\epsilon>0$, we can choose $\delta=\delta(\epsilon)>0$ such that 
