    \|\<\mathbf{X}, [f]\>\|_{(|f| + 1)\gamma}.\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.200947+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48c976bcff2b9c1af845c18afecfc36602b4dc5bd7d5c6bf3c818d51686ac60f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem MLSI DOWN UP of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] Suppose that \(\Lambda\) is a nonnegative definite matrix with largest eigenvalue \(\lambda(\Lambda) < 1/2\). Then 
