{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:35:57.365538+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48d57813d447a8ded51b855f654aa2e0e86e681cb1b9c10f8d5216096e464613","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2604.10446, 'Least singular values of shifted sparse random combinatorial matrices'] For a random vector $X\in \mathbb{R}^n$ and $\varepsilon\ge 0$, the L\'evy concentration of $X$ of width $\varepsilon$ is 
