{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:52:32.331740+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48e24c72d70fdb2af8aa0a03055a17a770eb76eeb31e39200939dfe7cd51213a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq: expression-psi of arXiv:2609.03959, 'The combinatorial Hopf algebra of signed graphs'] Let $\Psi$ be the unique morphism of combinatorial Hopf algebras between the combinatorial Hopf algebra of signed graphs $(\mathcal{S},\zeta)$ and $(QSym, \zeta_{Q})$. Then for any signed graph $\Sigma$
