\end{equation}
and consequently, for all $k\in \Nbb_{\leq n}$,
\begin{equation}
    \left|\grad^k \Pop_t f\right| \leq \upe^{-kt}\Pop_t \left|\grad^k f\right|.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.903918+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48e8fe73f3c88278a0e7d5bef4035e1a3169240ff051bb2294455bf5c0b3bcef","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def GIIA of arXiv:2607.19511, 'A Conditional Probability Hierarchy for Stochastic Choice\footnote{We thank Samson Abramsk'] A stochastic choice rule $c: {\cal G} \to \Delta(\Omega)$ satisfies \textbf{Generalized Independence of Irrelevant Alternatives} (\textbf{GIIA}) if for every $G, H \in \cal G$, and every $E, F \in \cal F$ with $E, F \subseteq G \cap H$, we have:
\begin{equation} 
c_G(E) \times c_H(F) = c_H(E) \times c_G(F).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.589008+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48eb15ad66e46981121c84398b6438bbfda3306312a446a4b57e6cb4cc446f30","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem: OP-continuous-M of arXiv:2605.16963, 'Stochastic Euler Equations with Pseudo-differential Noise: Continuous and Discontinuous Pe'] If $s\ge0$, and $\mathscr{p}\in \mathfrak{M}^s$, then  there
		is $\widetilde \alpha \in \mathbb N_{0}^{d}$ and a constant
		$C=C(s,q)>0$ such that
		\begin{align*}
			\|{\mathrm{OP}}(\mathscr{p})\|_{\mathscr L(H^{q+s};H^{q})}\leq C(s,q)|\mathscr{p}|^{\widetilde \alpha ; s}.
