{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.308853+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4940f694520d4b6704090eae3c262de45f1940522843535a2d7a2d62b7fdcf75","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2606.24323, 'Conditioning of incoherent sub-dictionaries sampled from a coherent dictionary'] Let $H$ be a real $K\times K$ matrix with zero diagonal, $M$ a symmetric $K\times K$ matrix with zero diagonal and entries in $\{0,1\}$ and $p\in (0,1)^K$. 
Further, let $\wm$ be the diagonal matrix with $\wm_{ii} = \sqrt{p_i}$, $\bar M$ be the complement matrix to $M$, ie. $\bar M_{ij}: = 1- M_{ij}$, and $\hat H$ be any matrix that coincides with $H$ on $\bar M$, that is for the Hadamard (entry-wise) product we have $\bar M \odot \hat H = \bar M \odot H$. Denoting with $\P_\mu$ the coherence rejective sampling measure associated with $M$ and $p$ from Definition~\ref{coh_rej_sampling}, we then have for any $r\geq 6 \|\wm \hat H \wm \|$ 
\begin{align*}
\P_\mu(\|D_I H D_I\| \geq r) \leq 108 K \exp\left( - \min\left\{ \frac{r}{6 \|\bar M \odot\hat H\|_{\infty,1}}, \frac{r^2}{36\|\wm \hat H\|_{2,1}^2 },\frac{r^2}{36\| \hat H \wm \|_{\infty,2}^2 }\right\} \right).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.562158+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_494460478f8ad8c4333332ab231907f7f06c7bd12d300a0e469ddfddccfdc3b8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3.2 of arXiv:2603.13873, '{Solvability of BSDEs with possibly unbounded stochastic coefficients \\ on a general weig'] Let $\xi, \xi'\in L_\tau^p(\rho_\cdot;{\mathbb R}^k)$, both $g$ and $g'$ be the generator of BSDEs satisfying assumptions (A:H4 of the paper) and (A:H5 of the paper), and $(Y_\cdot,Z_\cdot)$ and $(Y_\cdot',Z_\cdot')$ be the weighted $L^p$ solution of BSDE$(\xi,\tau,g)$ and BSDE$(\xi',\tau,g')$, respectively, in the space of $H_\tau^p(\rho_\cdot;{\mathbb R}^{k}\times{\mathbb R}^{k\times d})$.
Then there exists a constant $C_{p,\theta}>0$ depending only on $p$ and $\theta$ such that
\begin{align*}
\begin{split}
&\mathbb{E}\left[\sup_{s\in[0,\tau]}\left(e^{p \int_{0}^{s}\rho_r{\rm d}r}|Y_s-Y_s'|^p\right)\right]+\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\int_0^{\tau} e^{2\int_0^s \rho_r{\rm d}r}|Z_s-Z_s'|^2{\rm d}s\right)^{\frac{p}{2}}\right]\\
&\ \ \leq  C_{p,\theta}\left(\mathbb{E}\left[e^{p \int_{0}^{\tau}\rho_r{\rm d}r}|\xi-\xi'|^p\right]+\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\int_0^\tau e^{\int_0^s\rho_r{\rm d}r}\left|g(t,Y'_t,Z'_t)-g'(t,Y'_t,Z'_t)\right|{\rm d}s\right)^p\right]\right).
\end{split}
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.599673+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_49470ff050600a678e2fba9b57717fb90063ba7ae22009bc903e94faa62084f5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:cavityscaling of arXiv:2606.11248, 'Persistent Homology of the Planar Wiener Sausage: Brownian Scaling and a Logarithmic Expec'] Let $A\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}$ be compact and connected, and let $a>0$. Then
