{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.076490+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_494742219d9951ae2a4f06aa53ba8d2ee3d644bdb728d906865d0397aa9b814d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo excha-D of arXiv:2507.00737, 'Dispersion models on a circle: universal properties and asymptotic results'] Let $n\geq 1$ be an integer. Consider a valid DDM\xspace $A$, and some deterministic masses $m[k]=(m_0,\cdots,m_{k-1})$ all non-negative multiples of $1/n$, satisfying the total weight condition  $W(m[k])<1$. Let $R_k=1- W(m[k])$.
