	where $nC[b]$ follows the ${{\sf DDirichlet}}(nR_k,b)$ distribution.
	\end{itemize}\vspace{-2em}~ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:47:07.722151+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4948b2a996bee13b361ad381328ea6e5e222688cb81748d58fc2fcfb659dfd99","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 (Differentiation of the endpoint law) of arXiv:2608.06523, 'On the Gardner Transition in the Ising Pure $p$-Spin Glass II'] For every test function $\varphi$ as in
