{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.728574+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4960a33367056f6e596b2e61161ca3c338c79935557ee2985d6d9bc7565a0445","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-energy-ineq-on-C of arXiv:2411.04500, '\LARGE Probabilistic Approaches to The Energy Equality in Forced Surface Quasi-Geostrophic'] Let $ \mathcal{C}_0\subset \mathbb{X}_{\alpha,\beta} $ be a weak-strong uniqueness class of (equation PDE-SQG of the paper) and let $\mathcal{C}=\overline{\mathcal{C}_0}^{\mathcal{I}}$. Suppose that $ \theta\in \mathcal{C} $ is  a weak solution of (equation PDE-SQG of the paper) for some $g \in L^2([0, T];H)$ in the sense of Definition (def-weak-solution-skeleton-equation of the paper). Then the $ H^{\alpha-2\beta} $-energy inequality holds:
