{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.367172+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4986e729411df00f2078cecb92abae8fe1e418996604d52d0f8aa1dae28e2da0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem one-arm-measure-concentration of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Consider critical percolation on $\Lambda_n$. Let $N_n$ be the number of open sites $z\in \Lambda_n$ such that $z$ has an open arm that goes Euclidean distance at least $1/2$. Then for any $\alpha>0$ and $\nu>0$, there exists $C=C(\alpha,\nu)$ such that for all $n$, we have
