{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.808212+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_49874bb1461ba5f04a0fb8c3ce3fc1e9d05396581d085974c5b7b8d6598a8079","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:sigma_k of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] Let $\{\sigma_k\}_{k\ge1}$ be any orthonormal basis of $U_0=H^{\frac d2 +\alpha}_{\div}$. Then, for every $x,y \in \mathbb{R}^d$ we have
