    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.439831+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_499902a85bf9b4c032d46c9a7872738cd33064aa9d1882b647b2936bb297af22","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition \bf Ribbon graph of arXiv:2508.17838, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices'] Let $\Sigma$ be a compact surface (with or without boundary). A (punctured) ribbon graph $\Upsilon$ with $s$ faces and perimeters $(m_1,\dots,m_s)$ is a quadruple $(\mathcal{V}(\Upsilon), \mathcal{E}(\Upsilon), \iota, \phi)$, where
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[(1)] $(\mathcal{V}, \mathcal{E})$ is a graph;
    \item[(2)] $\iota: (\mathcal{V}, \mathcal{E}) \hookrightarrow \Sigma$ is an embedding;
    \item[(3)] $\phi: [s] \to \mathcal{V}$ assigns a marked vertex to each face;
\end{enumerate}
such that 
\begin{itemize}
    \item The boundary of the surface lies in the graph: $\partial \Sigma \subset \iota(\Upsilon)$;
    \item The complement $\Sigma \setminus \iota(\Upsilon) = \bigsqcup_{i=1}^{s} D_i$, where each $D_i$ is an oriented $m_i$-gon and $\phi(i) \in \partial D_i$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.155815+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_499982c8be4e3551ee1b37c17e33ada59b8b01d6c358dd73c92e2ca24a7a4d81","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:exist of arXiv:2607.05671, 'Bi-infinite systems of singularly interacting Brownian particles and the KPZ equation'] Fix  $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_0(\mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{Z}})$. Assume that for some $\chi > 1/2$, 
