{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:52:32.333264+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_49e8cffef1bf496c9501a29823c483266ce5a7d524697385037460cf54ccc903","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:ofh1/2 of arXiv:2609.03980, 'Decay Rates and Domain Dependence of a Coupled Wave-Heat System with Spatially Dependant H'] Let $\Gamma$ be a relatively open subset of the boundary $\partial \Omega$ of some bounded Lipschitz domain $\Omega \subset \mathbb{R}^n, n\geq 2$.
    We then define the space
    \begin{alignat}{2}
        H^{1/2}(\Gamma)& \coloneq  \left\{v\in L^2(\Gamma)~\middle|~ \|v\|_{H^{1/2}(\Gamma)}^2 <\infty \right\},  \textnormal{ where }\nonumber\\
        \|v\|_{H^{1/2}(\Gamma)}^2& \coloneq  \|v\|_{L^2(\Gamma)}^2\nonumber
        + \int_\Gamma \int_\Gamma \frac{|u(x)-u(y)|^2}{|x-y|^{n}}\;\mathrm{d}\sigma(x,y).
    \end{alignat}   
