{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.759635+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_49ff2993ebdaad3627f9d8f4a592ff0c36672f8b7f281eccf645198d3c6ed9fa","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 8 of arXiv:2604.12233, 'An upper bound on the smallest singular value of dense random combinatorial matrices'] For a vector $v\in \R^n$, and parameters $\gamma\in (0,1)$, $\alpha>0$, the combinatorial Least Common Denominator (CLCD) is defined as
