{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.161149+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4a4b9978f0bd4f7e8daa0fa21cc83e30129b8a0f4881931913ad3e93dab18fb0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Def_SliceDerivative of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] The \defined{slice distribution} $\mathscr{F}^\mathbf{Sl} \subseteq T\paren{\mathbf{Dir}\times\mathbf{Ram}}$ is the distribution induced by the slices foliating $\mathbf{Dir} \times \mathbf{Ram}$;
