{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.532160+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4a8270f5fcd59d7b5740e8b3db993c023416d4a3970b208997949afcc3e7adb0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def.pyramid of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] Given $k \in \mathbb{N}_+$ and $N \in \mathbb{N}$, for every ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}} \in \mathcal{G}^{(N)}_k$, we can construct a sequence partition of good cubes $(\mathcal{P}^{(N,k)}_{h})_{0 \leqslant h \leqslant k-1}$ as follows. 
