{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.194326+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4a8d9e18c87be84a2095a5a7ffeb6f4c3c111e91ae7ecf0c4bff95e2a0b77eef","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 8 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] For $K=O(\log N)$, let $Y_x$ denote the number of strings with prefix $x$ in $S_K$. Let $T_q$ be the set of all strings $x$ such that $\mathbb EY_x\geq N^q$.
