{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.686163+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4b497f75e27e7ee8e48d4b60ab43e4e85f416d12fdd2bb6d84e34b473fa89731","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition defsDF of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] For each diagram $\Gamma$, we define its associated diagram function as
\begin{equation}
F_{\Gamma}(\{n_j\}) := F_{\Gamma,\Sigma}(\{n_j\}) =
