{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.491649+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ba8992b72d8b5359d9dfc59a21b021601794a00068b52da0a04bf6f88ea226b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 (Recentering of $\Pi^-$, Step 2.c) of arXiv:2605.28677, 'Weak universality for stochastic reaction-diffusion models\\ with long-range correlated no'] Let $[\beta]\geq0$ and assume that $(\Gamma_{xy}\Pi_y)_{\beta'}=\Pi_{x\beta'}$ for all populated $\beta'\prec\beta$.
Then for every $c^{(k')}\in\RR[\![z_k]\!]$, we have

\begin{align}
(\Gamma_{xy}\Pi_y^-)_\beta 
&= \Pi_{x\beta}^- 
+ \Big( 
\sum_{k \geqslant \kk} \ve^{(\kk-k)\alpha} T_x^{<|\cdot|-2}\big(z_k W_{k, \varepsilon}(\Pi_x)\big)\Big)_\beta  \\
&\hphantom{= \Pi_{x\beta}^-\ }
- \Big(\Gamma_{xy} 
