{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:27.967146+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4bb5a2d922cfc8f02d63293fa40bc98905ab564247eba1954680e3ae1807109b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 (Component sizes and susceptibility) of arXiv:2607.13210, 'Punctured Wilson--Evolving Sets and Root Identities for Massive Kirchhoff Forests'] For every $x\in V$,
\begin{equation}
  \Ee[\pi(C_q(x))]
  \leq
  \sum_{z\in V}h_q(x,z)
  \sum_{y\in V}\pi(y)h_q(y,z).
\end{equation}
Define $ \chi_q
  :=\sum_{x,y\in V}\pi(x)\pi(y)\Pp(x\leftrightarrow_q y).$
Then, it comes
\begin{equation}
  \chi_q
  \leq
  \sum_{z\in V}
  \left(\sum_{x\in V}\pi(x)h_q(x,z)\right)^2.
\end{equation}
If $M_q:=\max\{\pi(C) \mid C\text{ component of }F_q\}$
then, for every $a>0$, we get:
\begin{equation}
  \Pp(M_q\geq a)
  \leq\frac{\chi_q}{a^2}
  \leq
  \frac{1}{a^2}
  \sum_{z\in V}
  \left(\sum_{x\in V}\pi(x)h_q(x,z)\right)^2.
\end{equation}
Finally, for $U\subset V$, it results:

\begin{equation}
  \Pp(C_q(x)\cap U\neq\emptyset)
  \leq
  \sum_{y\in U}\sum_{z\in V}h_q(x,z)h_q(y,z).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

