{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.971637+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c1b8e85d8e047017b15150c84f5de5099a2eb6fac500a943cae8d4aa859194c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:iso_action of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] Given $\underline{\tau}, \underline{\sigma} \in \boldsymbol{\mathfrak{T}}$ and $f\in\mathrm{Iso}(\underline{\tau},\underline{\sigma})$, we define an induced linear isomorphism $\hat f: \mathcal{H}^{\underline{\tau}} \rightarrow \mathcal{H}^{\underline{\sigma}}$ and, for any $k \in \{1,{\mcb{n}}\}$, a bijection $\tilde f^{[k]}: (\R^k)^{N(\underline{\tau})} \rightarrow (\R^k)^{N(\underline{\sigma})}$ by setting
\begin{equs}
\hat f:\mathcal{H}^{\underline{\tau}} 
\ni
\bigotimes_{n \in N(\underline{\tau})}
e_{n}
&\mapsto 
\bigotimes_{m \in N(\underline{\sigma})} e_{f^{-1}(m)} \in \mathcal{H}^{\underline{\sigma}}\;,\\
\tilde f^{[k]}:(\R^{k})^{N(\underline{\tau})} 
