		\mathbb{P} \Big( \big\{ \sqrt{\widehat{T}_{(v)}(1)} = u\big\} \setminus \mathcal{T}^{\eta,(T)}_{(v)} \Big)=r_{k,T}(\widehat{u},\widehat{v})(1+o_k(1))
	\end{equation} holds uniformly over all $u \in \mathcal{R}_k^{\eta'}(1)$ and $v \in \mathcal{R}_k^{\eta'}(T)$, where $r_{k,T}$ is as in~(equation eq:funcfg of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:25.848359+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c581d70e5e86455aaf4735b20474a068df6d6cb0a5c0f42434e25749babc2d8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 of arXiv:2608.29486, 'Cabled braids and their crossing matrices'] Let $p, q$ be non-negative integers with $q \leq n-1$. 
