{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.744884+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c5ba442a92d6111f9b2791f19312a47a96f39aa43708e8720bac42b943cfa26","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 3 of arXiv:2511.14757, 'A weak convergence approach to the large deviations of the dynamic Schr\"odinger problem'] Let $R _\eta$ be the path measure associated with an $\sqrt{\eta}$-scaled Brownian motion. Then, the associated Schr\"odinger bridges satisfy the LDP of Theorem \ref{thm:LDP_dSB} with rate function given by 
