{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.414651+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c5eea400cdc22224aac112c41356dddff9c70917e598fb050847db99c35495b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: continuity of period of arXiv:2609.02073, 'Existence of closed non-planar $p$-elasticae'] Let $(\lambda_n,C^2_n) \to (\lambda, C^2) \in \overline {S^0}$ such that $(\lambda,C^2) \neq (\frac{p-1}{2},0)$.
