{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.578798+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c6607f819c7aa53e7a3806c56ea5abf64d4a353c94770c2b30212a7bb2a1649","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 53 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$, $\beta\geq 0$, and $n\geq 1$. Let $G=(V,E)$ be a subgraph of $\mathbb Z^d$ which contains $\Lambda_{2n}$. Let $S\subset \Lambda_{n-1}$ containing $0$. Then,
