{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.291440+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c7650ac1e0e360c362b896291cd75a343d11e1f3c15b6cd8b0b8beb8cef2213","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:general_testfn of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Let $X$ and $\Omega$ be as in Theorem~(theo:main of the paper). For test functions $F_1,F_2:[c_0,1]\times\mathbf{C}\to \mathbf{C}$ assume that $F_j(x,\cdot)$, $j=1,2$, satisfy the assumptions of Theorem~(theo:main of the paper) uniformly in $x\in[c_0,1]$. Assume additionally that $F_1,F_2$ are $\alpha$-H{\"o}lder continuous in the first variable for some fixed $\alpha>0$. Then we have
\begin{equation}
N^{-2}\mathrm{Cov}\left(L_N(F_1),L_N(F_2)\right)=\int_{c_0}^1\mathrm{d} x_1\int_{c_0}^1\mathrm{d} x_2 C_\beta\Big(\big(x_1,F_1(x_1,\cdot)\big),\big(x_2,F_2(x_2,\cdot)\big)\Big)+\mathcal{O}(N^{-c}),

\end{equation} 
for some $N$-independent $c>0$. The implicit constant in $\mathcal{O}(\cdot)$ may depend only on $c_0$, $\sup_x \|F(x,\cdot)\|_{H^{2+\delta}(\Omega)}$, on the constant in the H{\"o}lder regularity condition and on model parameters from Assumption~(ass:chi of the paper). We also have that $N^{-1}L_N(F_1)$ and $N^{-1}L_N(F_2)$ are asymptotically jointly Gaussian distributed in the sense of (equation eq:main_macro of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

