{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:22:01.678729+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4cf36846d4007d484e06b43a2fbce24301a3d36ffa75e6c319cdb7434124fb9c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Question of arXiv:2605.02226, 'Finitely Dependent Processes on Subshifts'] \begin{enumerate}
\item A $d-$dimensional domino is a $ d$-dimensional box whose one side has length $2$ and all other sides have length 1 with its vertices in $\mathbb{Z}^d$. Does there exist a strongly irreducible subshift contained in the space of domino tilings of $\mathbb{R}^d$ for $d\geq 3$?
