{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.588503+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4d5d1485a49d48fb7f2d09d1c99472273cf3a60445ec8cb9507163e5603c081e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm-(u P)-long-time of arXiv:2605.16963, 'Stochastic Euler Equations with Pseudo-differential Noise: Continuous and Discontinuous Pe'] Let the conditions of Theorem (Thm-(u P)-local of the paper) hold and
		$$\theta\in\left(\frac{d}{2}+p,{s-\max \{3\zeta,1\}}\right).$$
