{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:32:18.836845+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4d88a6f00bfbc9057bcb97ff1e3adfdfc0dd6e6d27e4810d06c9edd51106168e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 23 of arXiv:2609.03830, 'Parabolic Poincar\'e inequalities and maximal function estimates for systems of partial di'] Let $1< p<\infty$ and $\max\{1,p-1\}<q<\infty$.
    Assume that $|F|\in L^{\frac{pq}{2}}_{\loc}(\Omega_T)$ and that $u\in  L^\frac{pq}{2}_{\loc}(0,T;W^{1,\frac{pq}{2}}_{\loc} (\Om;\mathbb{R}^N))$ satisfies \eqref{p_weak_sol}
