{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.355643+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4db851f052d0122c42cea90d25212f7eda705e7a033b7ee0eb9480c8fa9015bb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem SupremumInequalityUnderMixing-geometric of arXiv:2412.01635, 'On the Weak Convergence of the Function-Indexed Sequential Empirical Process and its Smoot'] (Geometric mixing conditions)\\

	Let $\mathcal F$ be a set of Borel maps $\mathcal X \to \mathbb R$ that satisfies $\sup_{f \in \mathcal F} |f(x)| \leq 1$. Furthermore, suppose there exists $\beta \in (0,1)$ and $C_\beta \geq 0$ with $ \alpha^X(t) \leq C_\beta \beta^t, t \in \mathbb N_0, $ 	
	and that it holds 
	\begin{equation}
		\int_0^1 \log^2 N_{[]}(\varepsilon, \mathcal F, \rho_\nu) d\varepsilon < \infty
	\end{equation}  
	for some $\nu > 2.$ Then there exists $\kappa > 0$, a constant $C \geq 0$ that only depends on $\nu$ and the mixing coefficients and $\lambda,\Lambda: (0,\infty) \to [0,\infty)$ with $\Lambda(\delta) \to 0$ as $\delta \downarrow 0$ such that for each $\delta > 0$, $n \in \mathbb N$ and $1 \leq i \leq j \leq n$, with $m = j-i+1$, we have 
	\begin{align*}
		& \EOuter{ \sup_{\rho_\nu(f-g) \leq \delta} \left|S_{n,i,j}(f) - S_{n,i,j}(g)\right|^\nu} \leq C \left[ m \left( \Lambda(\delta) + \lambda(\delta) m^{-\kappa} \right)^2 \right]^{\frac{\nu}{2}}.
	\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.821626+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4dbbe79e8da75dd9c9401be4f8ebf23011b31910b15f82f42933ef9d3536c115","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Wanted inequality of arXiv:2607.18531, 'Doubly reflected BSDEs driven by Inhomogeneous simple Lévy processes: Applications to gene'] Let $\big(Y_t,Z_t,V_t,K^{+}_t,K^{-}_t\big)_{t \leq T}$ be the unique solution of the DRBSDE ((basic equation Finance of the paper)). For any $\theta \in \mathcal{T}_{0}^T$, the $\mathcal{E}^f$-value of our game option at any time $\theta$ is given by:
	\begin{equation*}
		\essinf_{\eta_2 \in \mathcal{T}_{\theta}^T} \esssup_{\eta_1 \in \mathcal{T}_{\theta}^T} \mathcal{E}^f_{\theta,\eta_1 \wedge \eta_2}(\mathcal{P}(\eta_1,\eta_2))=Y_{\theta}=\esssup_{\eta_1 \in \mathcal{T}_{\theta}^T} \essinf_{\eta_2 \in \mathcal{T}_{\theta}^T} \mathcal{E}^f_{\theta,\eta_1 \wedge \eta_2}(\mathcal{P}(\eta_1,\eta_2)).

	\end{equation*}
	In particular $\mathbf{V}=Y_0$, i.e. the initial value $Y_0$ represents the $\mathcal{E}^f$-value of the game option.

	Assume moreover, that $L(S_{\cdot})$ and $-U(S_{\cdot})$ are l.u.s.c.  along stopping times, then the pair $(	\eta^{\theta,\star}_1,	\eta^{\theta,\star}_2)$ given by
	$$
	\eta^{\theta,\star}_1=\inf\{t \geq \theta:Y_t=L(S_t)\} \text{ and } \eta^{\theta,\star}_2=\inf\{t \geq \theta:Y_t=U(S_t)\},
	$$
	defines a $\theta$-saddle point for the game option.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.574133+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4dbd989438203ad659c6ce298cedcc6e236538291ea00377c849ed84f806fba2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem THm-eps-nocut of arXiv:2605.15742, 'Turbulent stretching of FENE dumbbell polymer model via special stochastic scaling and sin'] (Removing of the cut-off)
