{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.449480+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4de2d1312d2987f3476e70f64974a0eee47b93e8333c2b90663c12a5b7c6f878","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition corollary.identification of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] Let $y , z \in W$ be two vertices of $G$ and $J \in (0 , \infty)^E$ be a collection of conductances. Denote by $\bar G$ the graph $G$ in which the vertices $y$ and $z$ have been identified and by $\bar J$ the induced collection of conductances (see Figure~(fig:identificationvertices of the paper)). Then
