{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.539621+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4de525135824af3b72e69b24360615d4a629555748660625d0f22827259fa7bc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] For every $\mathbf{a}\in \{0,1\}^{E({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m)}$ and $G\subseteq F\subseteq E({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m)$, we have 
