for any fixed $\xi>0$, uniformly in $z\in\mathcal{D}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.571119+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4dff44df31b8753f939b4992437c5f26ff71b7e80df0815b85d182722c5c8ee6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:joint-system of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] The vector process $\mathbf{X}(t)$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{d}\mathbf{X}(t) = A(t)\mathbf{X}(t)\mathrm{d} t + \Sigma(t)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}(t) + \boldsymbol{\mathcal{E}}(t)\mathrm{d} t
\end{equation}
where:
\begin{itemize}
\item $A(t)$ is the drift matrix with entries $A_{ij} = -\frac{1}{2}\delta_{ij} + (1-\delta_{ij})(\lambda_i - \lambda_j)^{-1}$
\item $\Sigma(t)$ is the diffusion matrix with $\Sigma\Sigma^* = \text{Cov}(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{X}/\mathrm{d} t)$
\item $\mathbf{B}(t)$ is a $K$-dimensional Brownian motion
\item $\|\boldsymbol{\mathcal{E}}(t)\| \leq C_1 K^{1/2} N^{-5/6+\varepsilon}$
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

