{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.952105+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e47d06f2e6bb45265e276e2fc2e838ad90bf82fe48fb32836215996476b4c2b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 45 (Cubic stability inequality) of arXiv:2606.24887, '2606.24887'] For $0 < \eta_{\ast} < \eta^{\ast} < \infty$, let $\xi_1, \xi_2 : [\eta_{\ast}, \eta^{\ast}] \rightarrow \CC$ be complex-valued functions and $\tilde{\xi},\varphi: [\eta_{\ast},\eta^{\ast}] \rightarrow \RR_{+}$ be continuous. Suppose that some continuous function $\Delta : [\eta_{\ast}, \eta^{\ast}] \rightarrow \CC$ satisfies the cubic inequality 
		\begin{equation*}
			\big| \Delta^3 + \xi_2 \Delta^2 + \xi_1 \Delta \big| \le \varphi 
		\end{equation*}
		on $[\eta_{\ast}, \eta^{\ast}]$ as well as 
		\begin{equation*}
			\abs{\Delta} \lesssim \min \left\{ \varphi^{1/3}, \frac{\varphi^{1/2}}{\tilde{\xi}^{1/2}}, \frac{\varphi}{\tilde{\xi}}\right\}
		\end{equation*}
		at $\eta^{\ast}$. If the following holds
		\begin{enumerate}
			\item $\tilde{\xi}^3/\varphi^{2}$ is a monotonically increasing function,
			\item $|\xi_1| \asymp \tilde{\xi}$ and $|\xi_2| \lesssim \tilde{\xi}^{1/2}$,
		\end{enumerate}
		then, on $[\eta_{\ast}, \eta^{\ast}]$ we have 
		\begin{equation*}
			\abs{\Delta} \lesssim  \min\left\{ \varphi^{1/3}, \frac{\varphi^{1/2}}{\tilde{\xi}^{1/2}}, \frac{\varphi}{\tilde{\xi}}\right\}.
		\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.352275+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e48968d2c3220e5d187d7c85835fa3a6539531445104521e957b9143cc46604","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:cm of arXiv:2506.03999, 'Large deviations for scaled families of Schr\"odinger bridges with reflection'] A subset $\Gamma \subseteq \calX \times \calY$ is called \textit{$c$-cyclically monotone} if
    \begin{equation}
        \sum_{i=1}^k c(x_i, y_i) \leq \sum_{i=1}^k c(x_i, y_{i+1}),
    \end{equation}
    for all $k \in \bN$, $\{ (x_i, y_i ) \} _{i=1} ^k \subseteq \Gamma$, where $y_{k+1}$ is interpreted as $y_1$. 
    Correspondingly, a transport plan $\pi \in \Pi (\mu, \nu)$ is called cyclically monotone if $\pi(\Gamma) = 1$ for some cyclically monotone set $\Gamma$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.671469+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e49c789f945853929a38083b8fb8806bc41d694bbee68cb404a09b98d80cd1f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 15 of arXiv:2604.24392, 'Numerical approximation of Markovian BSDEs in infinite horizon and elliptic PDEs'] We construct a sequence of random functions $v^{n}_M : \Omega \times \Pi \rightarrow \bR^{d'}\times \bR^{d' \times d}$, $n \in \bN$ such that $v^0_M=0$ and, for all $n \in \bN$, $z\in \Pi$,
