{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.759162+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e55118b1483990ec0319b1c6c74ccfe1062843532b49d18ab9d788312bb8dbd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn vhypergraphon of arXiv:2609.02682, 'LDP for tensor forms'] Let $\mathcal{W}_{v}$ be the space of all real-valued symmetric functions in $L^1([0,1]^v)$. We will refer to $\mathcal{W}_v$ as the space of \emph{``$v$-hypergraphon"}s, or simply, the space of hypergraphons. 
\\

For a symmetric and zero-diagonal $v$-tensor $Q_n$, we define the corresponding hypergraphon $W_{Q_n}\in \mathcal{W}_v$ by setting
\begin{align}
W_{Q_n}(x_1,x_2,\ldots,x_v):=Q_n(i_1,i_2,\ldots,i_v)\quad\text{ if }\,\max\{\lceil nx_r\rceil ,1\}=i_r\text{ for all }r\in   [v]. 
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

