{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.120177+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e5bb2e9b09c601aba92bcf5a37eec802a297ea96f1e020a0a1a8a76355fc0c2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma logmoment of arXiv:2608.17031, 'A shape theorem for periodic branching diffusion'] Fix $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$ and $e\in S^{d-1}$. Let $\lambda_e>0$ be the minimizer in (equation eq:prelimCriticalSpeed of the paper), and recall that $\zeta_e = \lambda_e e$. Let $(Y_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be the solution of (equation eq:SDETiling2.0 of the paper) under the measure $\mathbb{P}_x^{\zeta_e}$. Let $\hat{Y}_t:=(1/t)e\cdot(Y_t-Y_0)$. For every $\eta \in \mathbb{R}$ and $e\in S^{d-1}$, there exist $\theta_1,\theta_2\in \mathbb{R}$ such that, for every $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$, 
