Let $\mathcal L_P$ denote the set of probability measures $\mu$ on $\mathcal{F}_S$ 
that are consistent with $P\in\mathcal{P}_S$.  \hfill $\blacktriangleleft$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.008022+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ea1fc2aafafe3569d88d346092201866fe05d969d0a84dabd28185a608db48f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem LUE soft left2 of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Consider an LUE $L_{a,N}$. Suppose there exist $\Theta_1,~\Theta_2\in \mathbb{R}$ such that $0<\Theta_1\le\frac{N}{n}\le \Theta_2<1$ and $\lim\limits_{N\rightarrow\infty}\frac{N}{n}=\gamma\in(0,1)$ where $n=N+a$. Then on any $A\subset[s,+\infty)$ for $s>-\infty$, with the same parameters as in Theorem (LUE left soft of the paper), for $N\in\mathbb{N}$ large enough,
    \begin{equation}
W_1\left(\mathcal{N}_{L_{a,N}}^{LS},\mathcal{N}_{Ai}\right)\le\frac{g(s,\Theta_1,\Theta_2)e^{-s}}{N^{\frac{2}{3}}}
