 where $g$ is nonincreasing with respect to $s$ for any fixed $\Theta_1$ and $\Theta_2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.168578+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ea253f51543eb3e43eef39a390858e5b4334a64e0a8f65eeb781501b7bdb9d9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor_g_kCM of arXiv:2412.07258, 'Permuton limit of a generalization of the Mallows and $k$-card-minimum models'] The $k$CM [Travers] arises as the special case of Definition (def_gen_perm_model of the paper) if we choose
