{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.521675+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ea94eb72f9ff6719495d672285c59b11c0edceba6e5b1ba0e3f0006399bb18e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:lcft-H-conf-infty of arXiv:2411.19810, 'Radial conformal welding in Liouville quantum gravity'] Suppose $\beta_1,\beta_2,\beta_3\in\mathbb{R}$ and $f:\mathbb{H}\to\mathbb{H}$ is the conformal map with $f(0) = 1$, $f(1)=\infty$ and $f(\infty) = 0$. Then 
