{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:09.912492+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4fa60d94d30fbc7718b65ee7b80dfad0267b24de872d99e0537cc0be03ded7ad","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2603.26936, 'Sharp Riemannian heat kernel estimates on the cut locus and the Parabolic Anderson model'] For any $\alpha> 0$, we have $$\abs{\bm{G}_{\alpha}(x,y)}\leq \begin{cases}
