\end{equation}
with zero initial conditions.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:41.037992+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_50072152bdd90ee56cd0f0ac8644d504defff769df16023b7e95b443fbb0ec6b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l38 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] The sequence of measures ${\mathbb Q}^M_N = {\mathbb P}_{\nu^N} \circ (M^N)^{-1}$
on $D([0,T], {\mathscr D}'({\mathbb R} \times {\mathbb T}^{d-1}))$ converges, as
