{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.340799+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_505046e2fb442088da038559336187125596ec7390a4ea03c4176fff78ef145f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture conj: WalkMatrixSquareFree of arXiv:2603.26932, 'On the satisfaction frequency of spectral characterization conditions'] Suppose that $\bM$ is chosen uniformly at random from all symmetric $n\times n$ matrices with $\{0,1 \}$-valued entries and consider an independent random vector $\zeta$ that is uniform on $\{0,1 \}^n$.   
