{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.713274+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_505514345ecf4ca07c83cb0ea2608fa129338bdcc05a074781f74ea2d90da415","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition The:main_result_finite of arXiv:2411.04778, 'Coupling between Brownian motion and random walks on the infinite percolation cluster'] For almost every configuration $\omega\in \Omega$, we can construct a version of $(S_t)_{t \in[0,T]}$
