{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.346010+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_50a633a3465fc0a94f805cc7757ef8359ed8efd5678c9c571a894846a45a4577","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 (General Hoeffding inequality) of arXiv:2604.21113, 'Tail Bounds via Southwest Boundary'] Let \(X_1, \dots, X_N\) be independent mean-zero sub-gaussian r.v.'s (with the same $c$), and let \(a = (a_1, \dots, a_n) \in \mathbb{R}^N\). Then, for any 
