{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.888570+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_50abdaf71a14fcb65b749f1dc3236fb1cb888768e5ef447251f3cb5e420a6925","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:eta-entropy of arXiv:2606.29557, 'Propagation of chaos for Belavkin equations beyond pure states'] For every \(T>0\),  it holds that
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
  \frac1N
