{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.537506+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_50ae4c3d38d279952a2c65a70c9be16acc62b5e69b382ba24fe1a295113e87c1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:LGJ-seed-linear of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] Let $H = \ell^2(\mathbb{Z})$.  The seed functions
$\psi_{t,r,n}$ and $\phi_{t,r,n}$ satisfy the linear
problem (equation eq:Linear-Psi-3 of the paper) and the adjoint
linear problem (equation eq:Linear-Phi-Prob of the paper) on
$\mathcal{V}$ with edge weights
$(c_k, \lambda_k)$.  Explicitly, for each fixed
$r \in \mathbb{Z}$:
\begin{align}
\psi_{t,r,n+1}
&= (1{-}\theta)^{-1} \psi_{t,r+1,n}
   - (1{-}\theta)^{-1}\theta \psi_{t,r,n},
 \\
\psi_{t-1,r,n}
&= -q(p\theta)^{-1} \psi_{t,r+1,n}
   + p^{-1} \psi_{t,r,n},

\end{align}
and
\begin{align}
\phi_{t,r+1,n}
&= (1{-}\theta)^{-1} \phi_{t,r,n+1}
   - (1{-}\theta)^{-1}\theta \phi_{t,r+1,n+1},
 \\
\phi_{t,r+1,n}
&= -q(p\theta)^{-1} \phi_{t-1,r,n}
   + p^{-1} \phi_{t-1,r+1,n}.

\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.597785+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_50b00a7fb544cbeb5c8015c13c2ddf60193c6e77ba97f2fd8a2437468d5b33c5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] For $x\in C$, $A\in\calX$ and $k\in\N^d$,

\begin{equation*}
\psi_k(x,A)=\psi^C_k(x,A\cap C)+\sum_{r\leqd k}\int_D g_D(r)(x,\dd y)\psi_{k-r}(y,A).
\end{equation*}

Consequently,

\begin{equation*}
\Psi_k(x,A)=\Psi^C_k(x,A\cap C)+\sum_{r\leqd k}\int_D g_D(r)(x,\dd y)\Psi_{k-r}(y,A),
\end{equation*}

where $\Psi^C=s_0*\psi^C$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.472040+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_50b5b238ff1e42b0a1ed5ed414cd963551c0f97b6282eef5f907079722d006c1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 37 of arXiv:2609.02561, 'NON-NEF LOCI IN MIXED CHARACTERISTIC'] With notation as above, let $D$ be an $f$-big $\Q$-Cartier $\Q$-divisor on $X$.
We define the numerical vanishing order of $D$ along $v$ as
\begin{equation*}
v_{\num}(D/S)=
\inf_{S^0 \subset S} 
\inf \left\{ v(D') \middle|
\begin{gathered}
 \text{$D'$ is a $\Q$-Cartier $\Q$-divisor on $f^{-1}(S^0)$} \\
 \text{such that $D|_{f^{-1}(S^0)} \equiv_{S^0} D' \geq 0$}
\end{gathered} 
\right\}, 
\end{equation*}
where $S^0$ runs through all open neighborhoods of $c_{X}(v)$ in $S$.
By definition, $v_{\num}(D/S)$ only depends on the $f$-numerical equivalence class of $D$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.800464+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_50b74d431ac862f595a9e4ff2c407643a2afd4038cd1b91ea358d21d9ef88481","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemme 79 of arXiv:2604.00635, 'Large deviations of the periodic Toda chain'] Let $\bs{x}_N\in \R^N$ have pairwise distinct entries. The matrix $\op{A}(\boldsymbol{x}_N)$ introduced in \eqref{definition matrice A2}
