{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:10.190395+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_50b9a5d691fcc3537cb2cf2ed667b984e4b97507faa2c585daedea7ef3b35804","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 176 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] Let $n\in\{ 1,2,...\}, \lambda\geq 0$.
Then there
