{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.632209+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_50cec049c131e5364ac06617a60abfa90d3c4bf77fa97e121b1f7815fb7e24b1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:rescaledescapeprob of arXiv:2411.13505, 'Capacity of loop-erased random walk'] There exists a nontrivial random variable $X_\infty$ such that
