{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.280810+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_51293afadef1884c7d981a6cc10969074b6b889e491b7a3b3ba950e0dca84e02","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 19 of arXiv:2606.22611, 'Upper and Lower Bounds on Expected Soft Maxima\\of Gaussian Processes'] Let $X = (X_t)_{t \in T}$ be a centered  Gaussian process with a finite index set $T$. Let a subset $A \subset T$ with $\diam(A) \le a$ be given, and let $\cA = \set{ A_1,\ldots,A_n}$ be a partition of $A$. For any $\mu \in \eP(T)$ supported on $A$, let  $\mu^i \deq \mu(\cdot|A_i)$ be the 
