{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.616419+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_51391a82ca12180f832337933a1a68cc2fe86f1e45f8f3c1c2d6327674a9c1ad","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:AFEbds of arXiv:2412.05491, 'Near-critical and finite-size scaling for \\ high-dimensional lattice trees and animals'] Let $d>8$ and $L \ge L_3$.
Suppose that $m \in [0, \frac{1}{2} m(p) \wedge \frac{1}{2} m_S({\mu_p})]$,
that $\tilde{b}(m) \le 3$,
and that $m(p) L$ and $m_S({\mu_p})L$ are sufficiently small.
Then the functions $\hat F_p ^{(m)}, \hat A_{\mu_p} ^{(m)}, \hat E_p ^{(m)}$ are $d-2$ times weakly differentiable.
In addition, there exists $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$ such that,
for any multi-index $\gamma$ with $\abs \gamma \le d-2$
and any choice of $q_1, q_2$ satisfying
\begin{equation} 
    \frac{ \abs \gamma } d < q_1^{-1} < 1,
    \qquad
    \frac{ 2 - \varepsilon + \abs \gamma } d < q_2^{-1} < 1 ,
\end{equation}
the following hold with constants independent of $p,m,L$:
\begin{align} 
\biggnorm{ \frac{ \nabla^\gamma \hat A_{\mu_p} ^{(m)} }{ \hat A_{\mu_p} ^{(m)} } }_{q_1}, \;
\biggnorm{ \frac{ \nabla^\gamma \hat F_p ^{(m)} }{ \hat F_p ^{(m)} } }_{q_1}
	\lesssim 1 , \qquad
\biggnorm{ \frac{ \nabla^\gamma \hat E_p ^{(m)} }{ \hat A_{\mu_p} ^{(m)} \hat F_p ^{(m)}} }_{q_2}
\lesssim \beta ,
\end{align}
If $\abs \gamma \ne 0$, the estimates are improved to
\begin{align} 
\biggnorm{ \frac{ \nabla^\gamma \hat A_{\mu_p} ^{(m)} }{ \hat A_{\mu_p} ^{(m)} } }_{q_1}, \;
\biggnorm{ \frac{ \nabla^\gamma \hat F_p ^{(m)} }{ \hat F_p ^{(m)} } }_{q_1}
	\lesssim L^{ \abs \gamma - d/q_1 } 	, \quad
\biggnorm{ \frac{ \nabla^\gamma \hat E_p ^{(m)} }{ \hat A_{\mu_p} ^{(m)} \hat F_p ^{(m)}} }_{q_2}
	\lesssim \beta ( L^{\abs \gamma - d/q_2} + \beta ),
\end{align}
with constants independent of $p,m,L$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.196047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_513f97de0263f24aac292cf679c8b8b00e00b1d94ea57a67d00277d1c0b932ff","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:CE-law of arXiv:2509.04333, 'The limiting law of the Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Let $V\subset \mathbb Z^2$ be a connected domain, and consider the \ensuremath{\mathbb Z\textsc{gff}}\xspace model ${\widehat\pi}_V^\xi$ with boundary conditions $\xi$ that are $1$ on a $*$-connected path in $\partial_{\mathtt v} V$ and $0$ elsewhere so that they induce a unique disagreement polymer $(\gamma,\{D_i\},\{h_i\})$ in $V\cup \partial_{\mathtt v} V$ that contains boundary disagreements. Then for $\beta\geq \beta_0$, the law of this unique disagreement polymer is given by 
