\end{equation*}
for every tangent block $T\subset T_{\theta_0}\Theta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:29:35.086580+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_51742bb1129b3330195e8c62c54ef87a2ddaa36a317b287ed4204b16b5a59907","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 8 of arXiv:2609.03819, 'Stochastic damped wave and Euler-Bernoulli equations with singular locally H\"older contin'] {\cite[Theorem 6.2.2 and Proposition 6.2.9]{Dap-Zab2002}}
Assume that Hypotheses \ref{H0}, \ref{H0.5} and \ref{H1} hold. Then, for every $n\in\N$, $\varphi\in B_b(H_n)$, $t>0$ and $x,h,k\in H_n$ we have
\begin{align}
&|\scal{\nabla(R_n(t)\varphi)(x)}{h}_{H_n}|\leq \|\Gamma_{t,n}h\|_{H_n}\|\varphi\|_{\infty},\\
&|D^2(R_n(t)\varphi)(x)(h,k)|\leq \sqrt{2}\|\Gamma_{t,n}h\|_{H_n}\|\Gamma_{t,n}k\|_{H_n}\|\varphi\|_{\infty}.
