{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.458464+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5198f2048e980b315130be7b7993cab099c419d5a27b214d481b7c6859f93112","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_meta of arXiv:2411.16572, 'Optimal decay of eigenvector overlap for non-Hermitian random matrices'] For any matrices $A_1,A_2\in{\mathbb C}^{2N\times 2N}$ and vectors ${\bm x}, {\bm y}\in {\mathbb C}^{2N}$, we have
		\begin{equation}
			\begin{split}

