{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.512358+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_51b00a7dee7450da43243032afe317db531b3fe063981c829829eb33f9278cd7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary two-lobe of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] Assume that $Q$ is continuous and strictly increasing on $
[0,1]$. Assume that $H_{F}$ has exactly one zero 
\begin{equation}
