{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.252482+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_51b31e9e05d2b724041ecbbae1e8321560eff5f1bcdae9817bf055fb2382878d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 7 of arXiv:2605.23292, 'Second-order Poincaré inequalities and localization on the Poisson space'] Let $h \in L^1(\mathbf{N} \times \WW)$ and $G$ be a measurable function of $\eta$ bounded by $c_G<\infty$. Then
