{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.872606+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_520b2ed0dd6016d7240b37613576d70c6d960ab70463b91f981ee5f858bd9743","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2605.07832, 'A Bismut -Elworthy formula for BSDEs with degenerate noise'] Assume that condition (equation cond_traccia_gamma of the paper) is verified and let $T>0$ and $\alpha\in(0,1)$ be fixed. Hence, there exists a positive constant $c$, which only depends on $T$, such that
