{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.792230+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_52b48edec602aaaa18b9c97aa6e54fa6bbbdc6e84d449114005868c6cc8adf5e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem propchaosbissansbruitindiv of arXiv:2605.11785, 'Regularization of a mean-field SDE by an additive common noise: the conditional expectatio'] Let ${\mathcal L}(\overline X^{N},X^{1,N},\cdots,X^{k,N})$ denote the distribution of the empirical mean and $k$ components in the particle system (equation eq:part1 of the paper) and ${\mathcal L}(X^0,X^1,\cdots,X^k)$ the distribution of the $X^0$ component of the weak solution to (equation eq.barXsigma=0BIS of the paper) given by Theorem (thm.existenceNIN of the paper) together with $k$ conditionally independent copies $(X^1,\cdots,X^k)$ distributed according to the conditional law of the $X$ component given $X^0$.  Under Assumption (equation Hyp.noCN of the paper), for each $\epsilon\in(0,1/2)$, there exists a finite constant $C_\epsilon$ such that, for any $N\ge k\ge 1$, 
