{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.501231+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_52f3e79a35d8000959f56999055a5ce6cc04fd52081ef5e1896afdd264e98331","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 37 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] We denote by $\Lip([0,T] \times W, \bar{W})$ the space of all continuous functions $f_0 : [0,T] \times W \to \bar{W}$ such that for some constant $L > 0$ we have
