{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.300698+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_53310a2cf371a2ecca2503e875f4797557caca3c3ecbfa9010b75c5b2036e110","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:laplace-tail-bound2 of arXiv:2608.30382, 'Convergence rates for the RMSprop optimizer with full control of the hyperparameters'] Let $ c, q \in (0,\infty) $, $ \beta \in (0, 1) $, $ n_0, n \in {\mathbb N} $ with $ n_0 < n $.
Let $ V_n^* $ be a nonnegative random variable which satisfies for all $ \lambda \in [0,\infty) $ that
\bas{
  - \ln
  \mathbb{E}\bigl[
    e^{ - \lambda V_n^* }
  \bigr]
  \ge
  \sum_{ k = n_0 + 1 }^n
  \min\Bigl\{ q, c \frac{1-\beta}{1-\beta^n} \beta^{n-k} \lambda \Bigr\} .
