{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.476316+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_53566b718d3a4259012dc90fa391fbc9d160130503ae7d5158bf9ef522b2ef89","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma resolve-pt of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $V$ be a faithful representation of the compact Lie group $G$.\footnote{Such a representation always exists as a consequence of the Peter--Weyl Theorem, see e.g.\ [broecker-tom-dieck]*{Theorem III.4.1}.} Then $\textbf{\textup{L}}(V,-)\to1$ is a cofibrant replacement in the $G$-global model structure.
    \begin{proof}
        It is clear that $\textbf{\textup{L}}(V,-)$ is cofibrant. Moreover, if $\varphi\colon H\to G$ is any homomorphism of compact Lie groups, and ${\mathcal{U}}_H$ is any complete $H$-universe, then $\textbf{\textup{L}}(V,-)({\mathcal{U}}_H)^\varphi=\textbf{\textup{L}}(\varphi^*V,{\mathcal{U}}_H)^H$ is weakly contractible by [schwede2018global]*{Proposition~1.1.21}, i.e. $\textbf{\textup{L}}(V,-)\to1$ is a $G$-global weak equivalence.
    \end{proof}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.952498+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5357cdf440746c5c0dcf9b0c31aec10b70b9e5e68366d4b8e01270e1c42c7eee","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 50 of arXiv:2606.24887, '2606.24887'] For all $N\times N$-matrices $M$, $B \subset [N]$ and $z \in B $ and $y \notin B$, we have
		\begin{equation}
			G_{zy} = - \sum_{b \in B} \sum_{a}^{(B)} G_{zb} M_{ba} G_{ay}^{(B)}.
		\end{equation}
		The previous equality holds replacing $G$ by $G^{(C)}$ and $G^{(B)}$ by $G^{(C \cup B)}$ for any $C\subset [N]$ such that $C \cap B = \emptyset$ and $y \notin C \cup B$. In particular, if $M \in \C^{2N \times 2N}$, $T \subset [N]$, $x \in [N]\backslash T$ and $y\in [2N]\setminus (T \cup \ubarr{T} \cup \{ x, \ubarr{x}\})$,  we have
		\begin{align}
		G^{\bset{T}}_{xy} &= - \sum_{b \in [2N]\setminus (T \cup \ubarr{T} \cup \{ x, \ubarr{x}\})}  \Big( G_{xx}^{\bset{T}} M_{xb} G^{\bset{Tx}}_{by} + G^{\bset{T}}_{x \ubarr{x}}  M_{\ubarr{x} b} G^{\bset{Tx}}_{by} \Big), \\ 
			G^{\bset{T}}_{\ubarr{x}y} &= - \sum_{b \in [2N]\setminus (T \cup \ubarr{T} \cup \{ x, \ubarr{x}\})}  \Big( G_{\ubarr{x}\ubarr{x}}^{\bset{T}} M_{\ubarr{x}b} G^{\bset{Tx}}_{by} + G^{\bset{T}}_{\ubarr{x}x }  M_{x b} G^{\bset{Tx}}_{by} \Big). 
		\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:33:12.356218+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_535bd33535d43127f9e00fcb3538d9fa0b4e2602c8f7c0506f787af555c83cbf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 231 (row-spliced matrix) of arXiv:2608.29416, 'Algorithmic threshold for high-dimensional projection pursuit I: general theory'] For $S\subseteq [M]$ and matrices $\bG, \hbG \in \R^{M\times N}$ with rows $(\bg^a : a\in [M])$ and $(\hat\bg^a : a\in [M])$, let $\tbG = \tbG(\bG,\hbG;S) \in \R^{M\times N}$ be the matrix with rows $(\tbg^a : a\in [M])$, where 
	\[
		\tbg^a = \begin{cases}
			\bg^a & a \not\in S\,, \\
			\hat\bg^a & a\in S\,.
