{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.281849+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5393386f6feb9c4be8b52a18af0f359ba0a31c349c7dc6c61996ef4fd9b1e0fd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 31 of arXiv:2606.22611, 'Upper and Lower Bounds on Expected Soft Maxima\\of Gaussian Processes'] Let $X = (X_t)_{t\in T}$ be a centered Gaussian process with a finite index set $T$.
