{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.590980+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_53a6072b9604bb0579c195606f99411c33a199b5107f0061edfde2c8fca2de1e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition StoFubiniThm of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] Let $T\geq 0$, $m(dt)$ be a $\sigma$-finite measure on $\mathbb{R}_+$ and $h$ be a measurable function on $\mathbb{R}_+$ satisfying that 
 	\begin{eqnarray*}
 	\int_0^T \big|h(T-t)\big| \cdot \bigg( \int_0^t |f(s)|^2\, ds +\int_0^t  \int_0^\infty \big| g(s,y) \big|^2\, \mu(dy)\,ds \bigg)\,m(dt)  <\infty .
 	\end{eqnarray*}
 	If $\sup_{t\in[0,T]}  X(t)  <\infty$ a.s., we have
 	\begin{eqnarray}
 	\lefteqn{\int_0^T h(T-t)\cdot \bigg( \int_0^t \int_0^{X(s)} f(t-s)\, B(ds,dz)\bigg)\, m(dt)}\!\!\!&\!\!\!&\cr
 	\!\!\!&=\!\!\!&  \int_0^T \int_0^{X(s)} \bigg( \int_s^{T} h(T-t)f(t-s)\, m(dt) \bigg)B(ds,dz) 
 	\end{eqnarray}
 	and 
 	\begin{eqnarray}
 	\lefteqn{\int_0^T h(T-t) \cdot \bigg(\int_0^t  \int_0^{X(s)}\int_0^\infty g(t-s,y)\, \widetilde{N}(ds,dz,dy) \bigg)\, m(dt) }\!\!\!&\!\!\!&\cr
 	\!\!\!&=\!\!\!& \int_0^T  \int_0^{X(s)}\int_0^\infty \bigg(\int_s^{T}h(T-t) g(t-s,y)\, m(dt) \bigg) \widetilde{N}(ds,dz,dy).
 	\end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:53.443389+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_53a62e17139a801733056df22c83b74490a2631a50905f28cb89ac48c9e04caf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 53 of arXiv:2606.15425, 'Well-posedness of stochastic parabolic equations with gradient nonlinearities and applicat'] Let $G, H$ satisfy the conditions of Proposition \ref{prop:randomcommutator}, where $G$ is $\mathcal F_t$-progressive and $H$ is $\mathcal F^\sigma_t$-progressive. Again, let $\sigma$ be a stopping time. Then the progressively measurable process 
\begin{equation} 
P(t-t \wedge \sigma)\int_0^{t \wedge \sigma}P(t\wedge \sigma-s) G_s \d {W}_s + \mathds{1}_{t \geq \sigma}\int_0^{(t-\sigma)_+} P((t-\sigma)_+ -s)H_s \d \widetilde {W}_s
\end{equation} 
is a modification of 
$$\int_0^t P(t-s)\left(\mathds1_{\{s \leq \sigma\}}G_s + \mathds1_{\{s \geq \sigma\}}H_{(s-\sigma)_+}\right) \d {W}_s.
$$ 
In particular, continuous modifications of these processes are indistinguishable.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.711724+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_53a7574b167f615011f55ba9fc3f662c80f0be4342c99fb2e5b9246fac8ebb38","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem MixEV of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] In the setting of (mix of the paper), let $O \in C_c^{\infty}\left(\mathbb{R}^n\right)$ be an arbitrary smooth, compactly supported function. If (equation eq:condA1 of the paper) holds for $k=1$, then for any fixed $n\in \mathbb{N}$, there exists a constant $c>0$ so that 
\begin{align}
 &\left|	\mathbb{E} O\pa{\gamma_+ \left({D N}\right)^{2/3}\left({E^+-\lambda_1}\right),\ldots,\gamma_+ \left({D N}\right)^{2/3}\left({E^+-\lambda_n}\right)}\right.\nonumber \\
 &\left.-\mathbb{E} O\pa{ \left({D N}\right)^{2/3}\left({2-\mu_1}\right),\ldots, \left({D N}\right)^{2/3}\left({2-\mu_n}\right)}   \right|\le N^{-c} ,
