\noindent then for each $t \in[0,\tau]$, we have $Y_{t} \leq Y_{t}^{\prime}.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.769442+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_53ce015ab8bd6570795b75db5636820ff6883de5cdff17fc3c17eb82804a5b3f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Fix $b > 0$, $\vec{y} \in \weyl_2$, and let $f,g \in C([0,b])$ be such that $f(b) > y_1 > y_2 > g(b)$. Then 
