{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.800845+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_53d0139ef1db5212c44d5ee8930417bbacf041e48e339c5562a3c982705e22c0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:dissipation-closure of arXiv:2605.17082, 'Spectral Purification in Reversible Markov Chains: Hidden Parameters, Observable Equivalen'] Under the assumptions of (thm:sharp-rigidity of the paper), for all $k \ge T_{\mathrm{rigid}}(\delta)$,
\begin{equation}
