{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.355714+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_53dd819a9bdaf7c5a5cd79b4d1ac68a18f6dfe383f8d81dd40c00dc8086d0fd9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 36 of arXiv:2606.17501, 'Critical spectral behavior and large deviations for geometric $\alpha$-stable processes'] For any $\theta \in \mathbb{R}$, the $L^{p}$-spectral radii $\lambda_{p}(\theta\mu)$ are independent of $p \in [1, \infty]$. That is, we have
