 where the summation  is over all nontrivial partitions $\Pi$  of $[s]$ (i.e., excluding the partition $[s]$ itself).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.465425+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_53e4758611c3aed9c77d75ca4fee5c8c34a51b6e9c0adc0265f2dea28411b9fe","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma simplify-q3-eq-zeta-ind of arXiv:2608.27904, 'Instantons, indefinite 4-manifolds, and Dehn surgery'] Fix $k > 0$. Let $\zeta$, $\eta$ satisfy $d_1 \zeta = 0$ and $d_2 \zeta = d_1 \eta$, and suppose $\delta_1 d_3^i \zeta = 0$ for $i < k-1$. Let $\zeta^\#$ be defined as in (equation zeta-eta-sharp of the paper). Then for any $0\leq j \le i \le k$ with $j < k$, we have
	\begin{equation}
