{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.285172+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_540612d76d3a945effff06c979e56ed6ae85ee6b0353ed8ee40d7c421255e5c2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:zetam of arXiv:2604.20660, 'The Legendre structure of the TAP complexity\\ for the Ising spin glass'] The TAP free energy is the random function $F_{\mathrm{TAP}}: [-1,1]^N \to \mathbb{R}$ defined by
		\begin{equation}
			F_{\mathrm{TAP}}(\mathbf{m}) =  \inf_{\zeta\in \mathcal{P}([q,1]) } F_{\mathrm{TAP}, \zeta}(\mathbf{m})
		\end{equation}
		where 
		\begin{equation}
			F_{\mathrm{TAP},\zeta}(\mathbf{m}) = H(\mathbf{m})-\sum_{i=1}^N \Phi_\zeta^*(q_\mathbf{m},\cdot)(m_i)-\frac{1}{2}N\int_{q_\mathbf{m}}^1 t\xi''(t)\zeta([0,t])\mathrm{d} t \, ,
		\end{equation}
		where $q_\mathbf{m}:=\frac{1}{N}\Vert \mathbf{m}\Vert^2$, $\Phi_\zeta^*(q,\cdot)$ denotes the Legendre transform of $\Phi_\zeta(q,\cdot)$, as defined in (equation eq:PPDE of the paper), and $\zeta([0,t])$ stands with an abuse of notation for $\zeta([q,t])$. We denote by $\zeta_\mathbf{m}\in \mathcal{P}([q_\mathbf{m},1])$ the minimizer (unique by [chen2018generalized]) achieving the infimum above.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.676997+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_540a7e1a003d228f6ddfa86121e9f7727c29d71c08bc88749fbd8e235d6d0628","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 20 (Associated local system to a covering map) of arXiv:2608.30875, 'A Decomposition Theorem for Topological Semi-small Maps'] Let $f:X \longrightarrow Y$ be a covering map of Hausdorff, path-connected, locally contractible 
