{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.185309+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54259ee733ca514398ce9888fba55239f32064f3e6129aca8e1a27c3a181c1f7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$ with $d\neq 6$, there exist constants $\Cl(d), \cl(d)>0$ such that the following hold for all $N\ge \Cref{const_thm1_1}$ and $v,v'\in \widetilde{B}(\cref{const_thm1_2}N)$: 
