	\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.775335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_549b18a9baacc9eae5e3e5bfea9a36dad6111138134ad4b7b0125574e9468867","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm: LowerBound_Smaller_d of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Let $d \geq 1$, $\lambda > 0$, $\ell \in \mathbb N^+$, $\alpha \in (0, d)$, and $Q \in \mathcal{H}_{\alpha, K}$. 
