{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:08.999269+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54a1abad1e7428ae5a951a344e30b387f9f29b43e0024335f3ccadc5a8cc4dac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop mbdc of arXiv:2411.10829, 'Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble and its Laplace transform'] For any $C_1>0$, there exist $C_2=C_2(C_1)>0$ and $C_3=C_3(C_1)>0$, such that if $|N-N_\ell|<C_1N^{2/3}$ for all $\ell\in\llbracket 1, m \rrbracket$, 
