{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.244156+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54a32b105183bf34472693a8869f2cdb04d1126750dd6ffc7e0ee92f92a5d5db","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi construction of mu of arXiv:2604.23890, 'The Cutoff Profile for Random Transpositions on Repeated Cards in the Full Range of Parame'] Suppose $t\in\mathbb{Z}$. Set $t':=t-\lfloor\frac{n\log n}{2}\rfloor$, and $\gamma_t:=\exp(-2t'/n)$, which is the same as in (defi: construction of nu of the paper). Let $\mu_n^t$ denote the measure on $\mathfrak{S}_n$ defined by the following sampling process: first, sample $M_t\in\{0,1,\ldots,n\}$ according to the distribution 
$$\mathbf{P}[M_t=k]=\begin{cases}\mathbf{P}(\Pois(\gamma_t)=k)/\mathbf{P}(\gamma_t-l^{1/3}\le\Pois(\gamma_t)\le \gamma_t+l^{1/3})&\gamma_t-l^{1/3}\le k\le \gamma_t+l^{1/3}\\
0 & \text{else}
\end{cases},$$ 
then sample a uniformly random subset $S_t$ of size $M_t$ in $[n]$. Finally, sample a uniformly random element of $\mathfrak{S}_{[n]\backslash S_t}$ and view it as an element of $\mathfrak{S}_n$ by fixing all of the elements in $S_t$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.394094+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54af74a47d56b584dcb65ede67cd0f6dfe094d38cf59f34e83abb048a1899023","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:h of arXiv:2607.22333, '\large \bf COLLISION AND NON-COLLISION FOR DIFFUSIONS ON CONFIGURATION SPACE'] There exists a family  of even functions $h_\varepsilon\in C_c^\infty(\mathbb{R})$, $0<\varepsilon<1/4$, such that
\begin{equation}
0\le h_\varepsilon\le 1,
\qquad
h_\varepsilon(t)=1\ \text{for }|t|\le \varepsilon/2,
\qquad
\mathrm{supp} h_\varepsilon\subset \{|t|<\sqrt\varepsilon\},
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
|h_\varepsilon'(t)|\le \frac{c_h}{|\log\varepsilon|\,(|t|\vee \varepsilon)}
\qquad (t\in\mathbb{R}),
\end{equation}
with $c_h>0$ independent of $\varepsilon$.","status":"unverified"}

