{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.331733+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54b2a9bd663a7e7569d96bc6aaf801aa9be0c11a030078f4437094762df6923e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm1 of arXiv:2601.19630, 'Mass generation for the two dimensional O(N) Linear Sigma Model in the large N limit'] For any $\lambda \geq0$, $m>0$, there exists a constant $C(m,\lambda,L)$ independent of $N$ such that
