	where $N(h) = \E h(Z)$ with $Z \sim \mathcal{N}(0,1)$, $h \in \mathcal{H}_1$ and $f_h$ is the solution to the Stein's equation. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.476050+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54bf630e530f20365df491d78ade5d06f6132cb82222e678ff9884f186f5d54b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma box-product-vs-product of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] There exists a natural $G$-global weak equivalence $X\boxtimes Y\to X\times Y$ for any $X,Y\in\cat{$\bm G$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top}$.
