{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.542902+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_551707dce2f6ac8b1380dea3c5f1669ecaf4e65c41aa37f7dbd7e905e09ca69d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:matrix_local of arXiv:2603.27906, 'Marked GUE-corners process in doubly periodic dimer models'] For $(z_1,w_1)$ and $(z_2,w_2)$ in a neighbourhood of $q_{\infty}$, let
~$z_i=1+\frac{Z_i}{N^\frac{1}{2}}$,~$i=1,2$, and set
\begin{equation}
\tilde g(\ell x+i,2y+j)=\prod_{m=1}^i(1+\alpha_m^{-1}\beta_m)(1+\alpha_{m+1}\beta_m^{-1})\alpha_{i+1}^{-j},
\end{equation}
and let~$\nu$ be given in~(equation eq:period_function of the paper). Then, as~$N\to \infty$, 
\begin{multline} 
