    \\
    \Ll|\partial_q\psi\Ll(q+t\nabla\xi(p)\Rr)-\partial_q\psi\Ll(q'+t'\nabla\xi(p')\Rr)\Rr|_{L^1}\leq C\Ll(\Ll|t-t'\Rr|+\Ll|p-p'\Rr|_{L^1}+\Ll|q-q'\Rr|_{L^1}\Rr).
\end{gather*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.475836+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_55a566152596041841fe65e8c7c03533cab62feb269efbcc0db3f356faada2dd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop quotient-we-global of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $\alpha\colon G\to G'$ be any homomorphism of compact Lie groups, and let $f\colon X\to Y$ be a $G$-global weak equivalence in $\cat{$\bm G$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top}$ such that $X(V)$ and $V$ are $\ker(\alpha)$-free and Hausdorff for every $V\in\textbf{\textup{L}}$. Then $\alpha_!f$ is a $G'$-global weak equivalence.
    \begin{proof}
        Picking functorial cofibrant replacements in the $G$-global level model structure yields a commutative diagram
        \[
            \begin{tikzcd}
                X'\arrow[r,"f'"]\arrow[d] & Y'\arrow[d]\\
                X\arrow[r,"f"'] & Y
            \end{tikzcd}
        \]
        where $X'$ and $Y'$ are cofibrant and the vertical maps are $G$-global level weak equivalences. By 2-out-of-3, $f'$ is again a $G$-global weak equivalence, and hence $\alpha_!f'$ is a $G'$-global weak equivalence by Lemma~(lemma:restr-right-Quillen of the paper). To complete the proof we will show that $\alpha_!$ sends the vertical maps to $G'$-global level weak equivalences; it will then follow by 2-out-of-3, that $\alpha_!f$ is a $G'$-global weak equivalences.

        We argue for the left-hand map, the argument for the right-hand one being analogous. By Lemma~(lemma:orth-spc-ev-lrQ of the paper) each $X'(V)$ is $\mathcal G_{{\textup{O}}(V),G}$-cofibrant, and hence in particular $\ker(\alpha)$-free and Hausdorff by Lemma~(lemma:G-CW-Hausdorff of the paper). Applying the previous lemma levelwise therefore shows that $\alpha_!(X'\to X)$ is a $G$-global level weak equivalence, as desired.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:48:43.581585+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_55a7eafe46eaaa07b1905505fbeee04627fa1482400534a060715ee235de8f17","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 49 of arXiv:2608.07239, 'Unified framework for asymptotically uniform iterative construction of generalised random '] Let $0<\delta<1$ with $\delta=O(\tfrac{\log\log\alpha}{\log\alpha})$, such that there exist $\mu_1,\mu_2>0$ with $\mu_2=\Omega(1)$, $\mu_1+\mu_2=1$, and
