{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.366688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_55d84a2ab8c7ccb345db956ae93286792567c8838f0fdffa2321718385ff561d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem closeness-projections of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] For every $\delta>0$, there exists $n_0=n_0(\delta)$ such that for all $n\geq n_0$ and measurable $A\subset Y$,
