{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.237896+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_55e70b5712ea55cb8f43bf7f439c4a654d070cbbbf40c2a7e166d9c91e047ea5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:iterated_psi of arXiv:2604.22528, 'Malliavin calculus for signatures with applications to finance'] Let $X = (X_t)_{t \in [0, T]}$ be an $\mathbb{R}^d$-valued continuous semimartingale and let $\sigX[]$ denote its signature. Then,
    \begin{equation}
        \int_{0 \le s_1 \le \ldots \le s_n \le t} 
