\end{equation}
is verified at time \( t = 0 \), then it is verified for all \( t \ge 0 \). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.359047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_55f938a6108ba07e90b42980dd9dec96ba148342e886a5218e572cab20e3e881","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 17 of arXiv:2511.09517, 'From Cannings model to Brownian motion conditioned on local time profile'] For $n \ge 1$, $1 \le s < h(q_n)$, and $f \in M^{s}$ with $N_f=(N_1,\ldots,N_m)$ and $\#\mathrm{Dom}(f) :=\sum_{i=1}^m N_i$, we have
