{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.251397+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5620c0fc8a9e214b9cc5a317e0002a4d04aa5bb8dae49d8264fa3c421cfe7382","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 14 of arXiv:2604.15226, '\bfseries Nonlinear Schrödinger equations with spatial white noise potential on full space'] Let $0<\mu\le 1$ and $m\ge1$. For $u_0\in e^X(H^1(\IR^2)\cap L_\mu^2(\IR^2))$, consider the unique solution $u_\eps$ to the regularized equation associated to \eqref{NLS}. Then there exists a unique function $u\in\CC(\IR,e^X(H^1(\IR^2)\cap L_\mu^2(\IR^2)))$ such that
