{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.540384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5623ead6df95744afcee75dd573ea1828d8a591e302bc27ef4f7eaab92289b62","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] For each $e'$ such that $\partial e' \subseteq \mathscr{C}^*_{\mathbf{a}}({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m)$, we have $\|D_{e'}(\nabla v_m(\mathbf{a}))\|_{\mathcal{L}_{\mathbf{a}}^2} \leqslant \mathcal{O}_s(C)$, thus
