G_{10, 10}^{5, 5} \left(
1 \middle| \begin{matrix}
	1-a,\,1-a,\,1-a,\,\frac{5-d}{4},\,\frac{3-d}{4},\,a+\frac{d+1}{2},\,a+\frac{d+1}{2},\,a+\frac{d+1}{2},\,0,\,\frac{1}{2} \\
	a,\,a,\,a,\,\frac{d-1}{4},\,\frac{d+1}{4},\,\frac{1-d}{2}-a,\,\frac{1-d}{2}-a,\,\frac{1-d}{2}-a,\,1,\,\frac{1}{2}
\end{matrix}
\right)\!,
\]
where $a = \frac{1}{4} \big( \frac{\gamma}{\sqrt{\pi}} \frac{\Gamma\left(\frac{d}{2}\right)}{\Gamma\left(\frac{d+1}{2}\right)} - d + 1 \big)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.748279+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56271ed5579d2987d70381439c8d74d907ee8efa5d633ea476aa28c809ed5ac4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 15 (Strict positivity of variances) of arXiv:2607.28865, 'First-Passage Percolation on Spread-out line graphs: Microscopic Regime'] Assume that $\ell\ge2$ and $\go$ is not deterministic.
\begin{enumeratei}
