{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.590694+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56fa7cea27957297bd9f11977db3170dd1822a6bb07a991311ec7700eda57064","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm_singlerec of arXiv:2411.09976, 'Occupation times on the legs of a diffusion spider'] For $n \geq1$, 
\begin{align} 

\nonumber
\mathcal{L}_t\Bigg\{ \mathbf{E}_\mathbf{0}\left((A_t^{(i)})^{n}\right) \Bigg\}(\lambda) = \sum_{k=1}^{n}& \frac{n! D_k^{(i)}(\lambda)}{(n-k)! \lambda^k} \mathcal{L}_t\Bigg\{ \mathbf{E}_\mathbf{0}\left( (A_t^{(i)})^{n-k} \right) \Bigg\}(\lambda)\\ 
&+ \frac{n!}{\lambda^{n-1}} \mathcal{L}_t\Bigg\{ \mathbf{E}_\mathbf{0}(A_t^{(i)}) \Bigg\}(\lambda)
