\mathbf{E}_\mathbf{0}\left((A_1^{(i)})^{n}\right) = \mathbf{E}_\mathbf{0}\left(A_1^{(i)}\right) - \sum_{k=1}^{n} D_k^{(i)}(\lambda) \left( 1 - \mathbf{E}_\mathbf{0}\left( (A_1^{(i)})^{n-k} \right) \right), 
\end{equation}
and, in particular, $D_k^{(i)}(\lambda)$ does not depend on $\lambda$ for any $i=1,\dotsc,R$ and $k=1,2,\dotsc$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.743275+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56fb14f2ba2604ff13c0b28dd7fc375adf3909e5274a8db7be1df75b0ece65d4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 45 of arXiv:2605.02430, '\textbf{Scaling limit of the range of tree-valued branching random walks in random environ'] We fix $\alpha \ino (1, 2]$. Let $\mu$ satisfy (\ref{hypostaintro}). Let $\tau_\infty$ be a GW($\mu$)-forest  (Definition \ref{GWfordef} $(\textbf{b})$). Let $\nu$ be a supercritical offspring distribution whose mean is denoted by $\ttm_\nu$. We assume that there is  $\ttb\ino ( \frac{2\alpha}{\alpha-1}, \infty)$ such that $\sum_{k\in \bbN} k^{1+2\ttb} \nu(k)\leko \infty$. Let $(\bT, \boo)$ be an invariant GW($\nu$)-tree (Definition \ref{definvRW}) that is independent from $\tau_\infty$. 
