a.s.~holds weakly on $\bbR^2\! \times \bD(\bbR_+, \bbR) \! \times \! \bC^0 (\bbR_+, \bbR)^6 $ equipped with the product topology. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.988781+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56fb50cde620750f6a8bb69882d85cb238154a2a9c3f83dd42410281ca659e91","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2609.03386, 'Twisted Gradient Flow Approach to Vegetation-Rainfall-Bushfire Interactions Model'] We have the following convergence as $m \to \infty$:

\begin{equation}
S_{\text{{\tiny $1,\!\delta,\!\nu$}}}(\tilde{z}_m,\tilde{g}_m) \longrightarrow S_{\text{{\tiny $1,\!\delta,\!\nu$}}}(\tilde{z},\tilde{g}) \quad \left\{
\begin{array}{l}
\text{in} \quad C([0,T]\,;L^2(\Omega)),\\[0.1cm]
\text{weakly in} \quad W^{1,2}(0,T\,;L^2(\Omega)),\\[0.1cm]
\text{weakly$^*$ in} \quad L^\infty (0,T\,;H^1(\Omega)),\\[0.1cm]
\text{weakly in} \quad L^2(0,T\,;H^2(\Omega)),
\end{array}
\right.
\end{equation}

