{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.624821+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5702f6a3b15ee1c74b4d53804b6ced2e5f8471adb34b3602e8848a14cc529807","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem:Indep-Increments-augmentation of arXiv:2505.24043, 'Weak solutions of Navier-Stokes Equation with purely discontinuous L\'evy Noise'] Assume that  $(\Omega, \mathscr{F}, \mathbb{P})$ is a probability space 
 with the family  of all $\mathbb{P}$-null sets of $\mathscr{F}$ denoted by $\mathscr{N}$, i.e. 
	\begin{equation}
\mathscr{N}\coloneqq\bigl\{ A \subset \Omega: \exists B \in \mathscr{F}: A\subset B \mbox{  and } \mathbb{P}(B)=0 \bigr\}.
