{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:22:01.670972+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_572df849f641557be4ff6cab179636849c23c63ddc95d275bcbbee9baf24395d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2605.02226, 'Finitely Dependent Processes on Subshifts'] For $ m \in \mathbb{N}$, an element $x \in \{ 0,1\}^{G}$ is called an $ \mathbf{m}$-\textbf{net} (with respect to distance $d$ on $G$) if the set $ \{ g \in G: x_g =1\}$ is a maximal $m$-separated set. In other words, it is
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $m$-covering i.e. for every $ g \in G$ there exists $h\in G$ such that $ d(g,h) \leq m$ and $x_h= 1$, and
    \item $ m$-separated i.e. for every $ g $ with $x_g = 1 $ and $ h $ such that $ d(g, h) \leq m$ we have $ x_{h}=0$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.731221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_572e2d96288a536d04f63555cafb6bbd5468204327f32380cf682b848ecbdff3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lA1Delta of arXiv:2504.07255, 'A Tail-Respecting Splitting Numerical Scheme\\ for L\'evy-Driven SDEs With Superlinear Dri'] Let $r\in[2,\infty)$. Then, for any $\gamma\in [0,1]$
\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}
\sup_{t\in[t_k,t_{k+1})}\mathbf{E}^{(N)}_{t_1,\dots,t_N}\Big[\|\Delta_t^n\|^r\Big|\mathcal{F}_{t_k}\Big]
\leq_C \|\Delta_{t_k}^n\|^r
&+h_n^{r\gamma +1}(1+\|X_{t_k}^{(n)}\|^{r\gamma\chi+r}) +h_n^{r\gamma }(1 + \|X^n_{t_k}\|^{r\gamma\chi+r})\\
&+h_n  (U_{t_k}^n)^r
+ h_n^{r\gamma+1} (U_{t_k}^n)^{r\gamma\chi}  + h_n
