{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.494501+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_573d5121d024b8942845bcbd75e9916b778aef4f11da3608b274cd8f4e0138a1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2605.09459, 'Multipoint connectivity in the branching interlacement process'] Let $R > 0$, and let $X$ be a random walk on $\mathbb{Z}^d$ indexed by an infinite critical tree starting from the origin, whose reproduction law $\mu$ has finite third moment.
