where $T$ is the unit tangent vector field and $k$ is the geodesic curvature  of $X$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.999602+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_574dc2a4dbf3ac49e8546d1eb18f83320e3f32bff35f78ce036e6f4d1734fbda","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:eude of arXiv:2604.17253, 'Large Deviations for the Nonlinear Schrödinger Equation with Randomized Quasi-Periodic Ini'] Consider the randomized quasi-periodic Cauchy problem (equation eq:nls of the paper)--(equation eq:initialdata of the paper) together with (cor:polynomial_decay of the paper). 
