{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:55:57.008110+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57544da4e0e294c2ee19b9007dd7c864fcd31ab9afb7dd7f3e2ff7257c71bc09","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 8 (\cite{BGP}; see also \cite{AKP}) of arXiv:2609.02808, 'Minimizers of Laplace eigenvalues under a lower curvature bound'] A geodesic metric space $(X,d)$ has \emph{curvature $\ge1$ in the sense of Alexandrov}
if every point has a neighborhood $U$ such that, for every geodesic triangle
$\triangle abc\subset U$ of perimeter $<2\pi$, every vertex $a$, and every point $x$ on
the opposite side $[b,c]$,
\begin{equation}
d(a,x)\ \ge\ d_{\Sph^2}(\bar a,\bar x),
\end{equation}
$\triangle\bar a\bar b\bar c$ being the comparison triangle and $\bar x$ the point
matched to $x$. A two-dimensional such space is an \emph{Alexandrov surface of curvature
$\ge1$}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.578924+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5759c6237bf46eafc04255c6073f8934a6fe9c2cc45e43fac08b1713ae5ea226","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 (Janssen test) of arXiv:2609.01296, 'Asymptotic safety regions for Gabor frames generated by Hermite functions'] Let $g\in L^2(\mathbb R)$, $\|g\|_2=1,$ and let $\Lambda \subset \R^2$ be a lattice.
    The Gabor system $\G(g,\Lambda)$ is a frame for $L^2(\R)$ if
    \begin{equation}
        \sum_{\lambda^\circ \in \Lambda^\circ} |V_g g(\lambda^\circ)| < 2,
    \end{equation}
    where the notation $\Lambda^\circ$ stands for the adjoint lattice. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.580435+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_575accd47699513929ff2ebbb9dc5aa83bc5226e5bc4a91b6f925b994b2da252","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2609.01296, 'Asymptotic safety regions for Gabor frames generated by Hermite functions'] For every $\varepsilon>0$ and $0<\rho<\frac{1}{2}$, there exists $n_{\varepsilon, \rho} \in \N$ such that, whenever $n\geq n_{\varepsilon, \rho}$ and a pair of parameters $a,b>0$ satisfies
    \begin{equation}
        \min\{a,b\} \leq n^{-\frac{1}{2}- \varepsilon}, \quad ab \leq \frac{1}{2}-\rho,
    \end{equation}
     the Gabor system $\mathcal{G}_n(a,b)$ forms a frame for $L^2(\R)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.754506+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_576203bab2f97779f8f4a564e80c28e7cf058e5a568e42ad3b90c10b181a0126","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 32 of arXiv:2604.11682, 'Semilocalization for inhomogeneous random graphs'] Let $\nu > 0$. There exists a constant $C_{\nu} > 0$ such that with
