{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.231977+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57d0402b01ef6fd0d5ff892a1c0e9c313fb6f24daa89bff1e335523974f1b1d5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] For $\delta>0$ and $N\in \N$, let $(u;v) = (u_1,u_2;v_1,v_2) \in D_{\delta^{1/4}}^N \cap \big(\mathbb{X}^{N}_{\delta^{1/4}} \times \mathbb{X}^{N}_{\delta^{1/4}}\big)$ be such that $v_2-u_2 \geq 3\delta^{1/2}N^{3/2}$.  There exist $c,C>0$, which do not depend on $\delta>0$ or $N\in \N$, such that 
the events
\begin{equation*}
    \hat{D}_{N,\delta}^{u,v} := \Big\{\gamma^{\per}_{u',v}(u_2+z) \in [u_1-5\delta^{3/5}N,u_1+5\delta^{3/5}N] \, \forall \, u' \in \bar{B}^N_{\delta}(u) , z\in [\delta N^{3/2},3\delta N^{3/2}] \Big\}
