{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.472121+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57e8d349320505d0579b0d01991ab6d193366944711c0e5b7882c62501b63c01","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2608.17562, '2608.17562'] Let $(X_{i})_{i \ge 1}$ be a sequence of \iid random variables with common distribution function $F$. Assume that
  $\widebar{F} \in \SRV{\alpha}{\rho}$, with $\alpha > 0$, $\rho < 0$,
  and auxiliary function~$A$.
  Set
  $$Z_n \coloneq a_n^{-1}
  \max(X_{1},\dots,X_{n}),
  $$
  where   
  $a_n \coloneq F^{\leftarrow}(1 - 1/n)$,
  $n\geq 1$. Let $\mathcal{H}$ be a set of functions $h : \R \to \R$ such that the associated Stein solution $g_{h}$ exists, belongs to $\mathcal{C}^{1}((0,\infty))$, where $x \mapsto xg_{h}'(x)$ is absolutely continuous and satisfies 
\begin{align}
x\vert g_{h}'(x) \vert \leq C_{1}x^{\beta} 
\end{align}
 and 
\begin{align}
\vert (xg_{h}'(x))'\vert \leq C_{2}x^{\gamma} 
\end{align}
for almost every $x >0 $, some $\beta \in (-\infty, \alpha),\ \gamma \in (-\infty, \alpha - 1)$,
 $C_{1}, C_{2} > 0$ independent of $h$. Then,
 there exists $C_{\alpha} > 0$ such that 
\begin{align}
  \underset{h \in \mathcal{H}}{\sup}\ \big\vert \esp[h(Z_{n})] - \esp[h(Z)]\big\vert \leq C_{\alpha}\Big(\frac{1}{n} + A(a_n)\Big) + \underset{h \in \mathcal{H}}{\sup}\ \big\vert\esp\big[h(Z_{n})\ind_{U^{c}_{n}}\big] - \esp[h(Z)]\prob(U_{n}^{c})\big\vert,
