{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.993635+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57eba3c81e583a4ac30784dd873e6d4280df2878c330991b7a1b6bc9fc23f1c2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem digraph of arXiv:2412.01086, 'Spectral radii of sparse non-Hermitian random matrices'] {l90}}] 
Let $d>0$ be a positive constant and $\omega$ be a function such that $\omega (n)\to \infty$ as $n\to\infty$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item If $d<1$, then with high probability, each nontrivial (i.e., containing more than one vertex) strongly connected component of $\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{d}}(n,d/n)$ is a directed cycle with length smaller than $\omega (n)$.
\item If $d>1$, there exists a positive constant $\alpha =\alpha (d)$ such that with high probability, $\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{d}}(n,d/n)$ contains a strongly connected component larger than $\alpha n$, and every other nontrivial strongly connected component is a directed cycle with length smaller than $\omega (n)$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:23:25.626520+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57eba6a3991c0d496eef0f7289f2d7b217574dd22cb3d10b5fc50f5bd5e57b1b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem point-absorption of arXiv:2609.01300, 'Virasoro Constraints for Orbifold Curves'] Let \(L\) be a finite totally ordered set of identity labels with variables
\(\{w_i\}_{i\in L}\), and let \(*\) be a distinguished point label with
variable \(x\).  For a set partition
\(\pi=(B_1,\ldots,B_{q(\pi)})\in \mathrm{Part}(L)\), write its blocks in increasing order
of their maximal labels and set
\[
  X_0=x,
  \qquad
  X_\alpha=x+\sum_{\beta=1}^{\alpha}W_{B_\beta}.
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
  \sum_{\pi\in\mathrm{Part}(L)}
  \prod_{\alpha=1}^{q(\pi)}
  X_{\alpha-1}\,w_{b(B_\alpha)}\,T_{B_\alpha}
  =
  \left(x\prod_{i\in L}w_i\right)
  \left(x+\sum_{i\in L}w_i\right)^{|L|-1}.

\end{equation}
For \(L=\varnothing\), both sides are understood to be \(1\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.526201+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57ee63ffcd86ec098cc95552c5bce4f57bdb30a7212c1aedbf4f8cec6e1f4b58","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma tp-preservation of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] Let $h(u_{1},u_{2})$ be a $TP_{2}$ density on $
[0,1]^{2}$ and let $A,B:[0,1]\rightarrow \lbrack 0,1]$ be two non-decreasing
differentiable bijections. Define 
