{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.306740+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57f397d284da8ec77d6b3219b043a75cdefff267eb442cc803ce11441c9bfd8a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2609.03755, 'The Scramble Number of Outerplanar Graphs'] A \emph{bramble} $\mathcal{B} = \{B_1, \ldots, B_m\}$ is a collection of connected subgraphs of $G$ that all pairwise ``touch". We say two subgraphs $B_i$ and $B_j$ ``touch" if either:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $B_i\cap B_j \neq \emptyset$
        \item There exists an edge in $G$ between a vertex in $B_i$ and a vertex in $B_j$.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:44.961010+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57f6f4c45bf6d8960a7cd459cf77914b4943ed821d86187102a189d62bed5682","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 (Traveling Wave) of arXiv:2605.11279, 'Flocking with Multiple Types: Competition, Fluid Limits and Traveling Waves'] We call a $\CCC^2$ function $H = \parens*{H_+, H_-}\!: \real \to [0, 1]^2$ a \textbf{traveling wave} with mass partition $(\rho^+, \rho^-)$, for some $\rho^\pm \in [0,1]$ with $\rho^+ + \rho^- = 1$, and speed $\gamma > 0$, if
    \begin{enumerate}[label = \arabic*.]
        \item $H$ is coordinate-wise non-decreasing;

        \item $\lim_{t\to-\infty} H(t) = (0, 0)$ and $\lim_{t\to\infty} H(t) = (1, 1)$; and

        \item the measure-valued process $\curlbr*{\mu_\pm(s)\! : s\geq 0}$, induced by the (extended) cumulative distribution function processes $\curlbr*{\rho^\pm H_\pm(\cdot - \gamma s)\!: s\geq 0}$, solves the mean-field equation \eqref{originalFluid}.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:22:48.897727+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57fafb845c4ce2e127a6d466f33a2ec3700b864a4cca6c2449dddecc50e04e55","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 61 ($\Delta_0$-Separation) of arXiv:2608.29157, 'Dilator-based analysis of $\KP$'] If $A(x,y_0,\cdots,y_{n-1})$ is a $\Delta_0$-formula with all free variables expressed, and $s,t_0,\cdots,t_{n-1}\in \bfL(u)_\ttX$, then 
    \begin{equation*}
        H[\ttX]\Vdash \exists y\in \ttL(u)_\ttOmega \bigl[ \forall x\in y \bigl(x\in s\land A(x,t_0,\cdots,t_{n-1})\bigr) \land \forall x\in s \bigl(\lnot A(x,t_0,\cdots,t_{n-1})\lor x\in y\bigr)\bigr].
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.735753+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57fd66ab0f26916b5e2f2f5c5aefad19b721a5f82788b10f9c690f0300c47a28","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:asep-seed-linear of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The seed functions (equation eq:asep-seed-def of the paper) satisfy the
