{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:32:20.749532+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5801124a6a9d3dda88ea1de5a5bcfcb5520b4e034fd0490d5b01f5ae89505bb0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Exact CNN representation of the directional classifiers) of arXiv:2609.00402, '2609.00402'] Let \(T\geq2\), \(B=T-1\), $\bm L=(1,\ldots,1)$, $\bm k=\{k_{h,1}=h+1:h=1,\ldots,T-1\}$, $\bm{\mathcal P}=
\{(\operatorname{Pool}_{h,1},w_{h,1},s_{h,1})
