{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.095678+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_589596501553983c44de5a939db96be38990427efee6adb97025edc3881158f2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lemma:subordinadoNblack of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] Fix $r\geq 0$. Under $\mathbf{N}_{x,r}$ and outside of a negligible set, the  convergence 
