{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.184576+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58d99a3734f54e80d87cc8ceaa146359c9bd22281dbe0c9a9639acfab0e9ed13","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2606.30349, 'Attenuated Poisson Dirichlet approximations for divisibility configurations'] Let $J_n$ be uniformly distributed on $\{1,\dots,n\}$ and let
\begin{align*}
