{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.252775+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58e005f76a6fb4067ec0c13e8ee39337fe5ecbd08ea88f9153b09ae2c5d92bd2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main of arXiv:2609.04092, 'Short character sums of inhomogeneous polynomials'] Fix a prime $p$ and let $n\geq 1,k\geq 2$ be integers. Let $F\in \mathbb{F}_p[X_1,...,X_n]$ be a polynomial in $n$ variables and of degree $k$, and let $F_k$ denote its leading form. 
 Suppose  
    \begin{align}
         n-\dim_{\overline{\mathbb{F}}_p}{\rm sing } F_k \geq 2^{k-2}(k-1)^2(k+1),
    \end{align}
    where ${\rm sing } F_k$ denotes the singular locus in affine space of the hypersurface defined by $F_k=0$ over $\mathbb{F}_p$. Let $\mathbf{N}=(N_1,...,N_n)$ and $\mathbf{H}=(H_1,...,H_n)$ with $H_i\leq p$, and define $\|\mathbf{H}\|=H_1\cdots H_n$ and $H_\mathrm{min}=\min_i H_i$.  Let $\kappa>0$ and $H_{\mathrm{min}}\gg p^{1/(k-1)+\kappa}$.
    Then for any $\varepsilon>0$,
      \begin{align}
            S(F;\mathbf{N},\mathbf{H}) \ll_{n,k,\varepsilon} \|\mathbf{H}\| p^{-\kappa/2 + \varepsilon}.
        \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

