{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.374897+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58e50eeaa66895bda464961b45dab3d92b68df21a3998e02a6a3a9961f563434","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary of arXiv:2412.06420, 'Accuracy, Estimates, and Representation Results'] Assume $\mathsf{acc}_k:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}$ is absolutely continuous for each $k\in\mathbb{R}$. \\
