{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.708614+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58fa91a589ae6e3863aa3e9760eac4628f806f64422bf3b6c6f19ed241ad67c3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def cps of arXiv:2605.30017, 'Conditional Probability Spaces and the Structure of Agreement\footnote{We thank Emiliano C'] A \textbf{conditional probability space} (\textbf{CPS}) is a pair $(\mathcal G, p)$, where $\mathcal G \subseteq \mathcal F$ is a family of nonempty conditioning events, and $p$ associates with each $G \in \mathcal G$ a probability measure $p_G$ on $\Omega$, satisfying:
\begin{enumerate} [label=(\roman*)]
\item $p_G(G) = 1$ for every $G \in \cal G$;
\item $p_G(E) = p_G(F) \, p_F(E)$ for every $E \subseteq F \subseteq G$ with $E \in \cal F$ and $F, G \in \cal G$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.950423+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58fb08f6bc9136537fcd9f7f47d1461a3ba3902b1bda05db57a706d3d305cf2a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem T:biane of arXiv:2412.03521, 'On ergodic properties of stochastic PDEs'] {biane:86:relations}}]
