{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.255743+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59411ed086c3d67aee8858c82a72f92feaec08f74493b06a8b4049aae2f0392f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2604.19220, 'Split merge dynamics for expanding intervals and point processes on the real line.'] If  $\forall (n,k)\in I \; p_{n,k} = p \in (0,1), $ $ a_{n,0}= - \frac{n+1}{2},  $ and $ a_{n,n+1}=  \frac{n+1}{2} $ then $ \forall k \in \NN,$
