\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.299622+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_594c8cf207e126da877a74672cd5fd82589b7441bd24f66177b325d1c3dc1251","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 (Consistency from comparisons) of arXiv:2609.02362, '\textbf{Farthest-cell triplet entropy: high-dimensional shell limits and hyperbolic curvat'] If the prototype triples and witnesses in \cref{eq:comparison-estimator} are sampled independently from $P^3$ and $P$, respectively, then
