{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.962161+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59de7ecae1a5fceaf5a2773ec7f5f6510e5c34324873a43f1c4ec1cc3c07993f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:gradient-recurse of arXiv:2506.23062, 'Shifted Composition IV\@: \\ Toward Ballistic Acceleration for Log-Concave Sampling'] {scr3}}]
    Suppose that $-\beta I \preceq \nabla^2 V \preceq \beta I$ and $\bs\pi(x,p) \propto \exp(-V(x) - \frac{1}{2}\, \norm{p}^2)$.
    Write $G_n^\mathsf{x} \coloneqq \max_{k < n}\mathbb{E}_{\bs\nu^\mathsf{aux}_k}[\norm{\nabla V(X)}^2]$, $G_n^\mathsf{p} \coloneqq \max_{k < n}\mathbb{E}_{\bs\nu^\mathsf{aux}_k}[\norm{P}^2]$.
    Suppose that the following holds for iterations $n \geqslant 0$:
        \begin{align*}
            \KL(\bs\nu_n^\mathsf{aux} \mathbin{\|} \bs\pi) \leqslant \mathsf{A}_\mathsf{x}^2\,(G_n^\mathsf{x})^2 + \mathsf{A}_\mathsf{p}^2\, (G_n^\mathsf{p})^2 + \mathsf{B}^2\,. 
        \end{align*}
    If $\mathsf{A}_\mathsf{x}^2\beta \vee \mathsf{A}_\mathsf{p}^2 \lesssim 1$ for a sufficiently small implied constant, then for all $n \geqslant 0$,
        \begin{align*}
            \KL(\bs\nu_n^\mathsf{aux} \mathbin{\|} \bs\pi) &\lesssim (\mathsf{A}_\mathsf{x}^2 \beta + \mathsf{A}_\mathsf{p}^2)\, d + \mathsf{B}^2\,, \\
            \text{and} \qquad (G_n^\mathsf{x})^2 &\lesssim \beta d + \mathsf{B}^2 \beta\,, \\
            \text{and} \qquad (G_n^\mathsf{p})^2 &\lesssim d + \mathsf{B}^2\,.
        \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.009855+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59e6bc4bdfd3062c3e875d076a30ccd2a0ae50062de044f7f92e392dacff1166","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 6 of arXiv:2609.02850, 'Canonical-row Chern flow on Bott--Samelson towers:\\ realizable-volume models for Schubert'] Let $\kk$ be a field.  A homogeneous polynomial
$f\in\QQ[x_1,\ldots,x_n]_d$ belongs to $\RV$ if
\begin{equation}
 f(x)=\frac{q}{d!}\int_X\left(x_1D_1+\cdots+x_nD_n\right)^d
\end{equation}
for some $q\in\QQ_{\ge0}$, an integral projective $d$-fold $X/\kk$, and
semiample Cartier divisor classes $D_1,\ldots,D_n$ on $X$.  The case $q=0$
includes the zero polynomial.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:33:11.958994+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59ebc9d304504f3456b48f75871dcda4b2d4cdaa21394bce395390505ede79b0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:rectangle of arXiv:2607.14087, 'Stochastic Domination of Gaussian Maxima: A Resolution of the Weak Simplex Conjecture'] \label[lemma]{lem:rectangles}
Let $V=(V_1,\ldots,V_m)$ be a centered Gaussian vector with
$\operatorname{Var}(V_i)=1$ for every $i$.  For
$r_1,\ldots,r_m\in[0,\infty]$,
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb P\{|V_i|\leq r_i\text{ for all }i\}
  \geq\prod_{i=1}^m\mathbb P\{|Z|\leq r_i\},
  \qquad Z\sim\mathcal N(0,1).
\end{equation}
If $0<r_i<\infty$ for every $i$, then equality in
(equation eq:rectangle of the paper) holds if and only if
$\operatorname{Cov}(V)=I_m$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.947420+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59f23e96bd0995d6964f8a789bb8823198943fd9f13bfd5c2eb9fd85e8e5bc69","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 19 (Besov Spaces) of arXiv:2608.01860, 'A Variational Characterization of a Gibbs Measure related to the Aviles-Giga Functional'] Let $\rho,\chi\in C^\infty(\R^d)$ such that
\begin{itemize}
   \item $ \supp \rho \subset B_{2R}(0)\setminus B_R(0) \text{ and } \supp \chi\subset B_R(0)$
    \item$\rho\leq 1,\chi\geq 0 \text{ and } \chi(\xi)+ \sum_{j\geq 0}\rho(2^{-j}\xi)=1 \quad \text{for all }\xi\in\R^d  $
\end{itemize}
and denote $\rho_j=\rho(2^{-j}\cdot)$ for $j\geq 0$ and $\rho_{-1}=\chi$ and $\Delta_jf\coloneq \mathcal{F}^{-1}\rho_j\mathcal{F}f$. \\
 We define for $\alpha\in\R$  
 \begin{align*}
     B_{p,q}^\alpha\coloneq \{f\in\mathcal{S}'(\mathbb{T}^d):\Vert f\Vert_{B^\alpha_{p,q}}<\infty\}
 \end{align*}
 with
 \begin{align*}
     \Vert f\Vert_{B^\alpha_{p,q}}\coloneq \Vert (2^{\alpha j}\Vert \Delta_jf\Vert_{L^p})_{j\geq-1}\Vert_{l^q}.
 \end{align*}
 For $p=q=2$ we have the fractional Sobolev spaces $H^\alpha\coloneq B_{p,q}^\alpha$.\\
 Moreover, we define
 \begin{align*}
     \mathscr{C}^\alpha\coloneq \overline{C(\mathbb{T}^d)}^{B_{\infty,\infty}^\alpha}.
 \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.258972+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59f269d2ee1bd4da3833e0022c80b4066340d0b79d45c86c0234d1bacebdb4f3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 88 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] For any $\varepsilon,K>0$ and $\alpha>2$, it holds that
  \begin{align*}
    \bbE\left[\sup_{|x|\le K}\mu_n([x-\varepsilon,x+\varepsilon])\right]\lesssim \varepsilon+(\varepsilon+K)^{1/2}n^{-1/2}.
  \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.526002+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59f3a5edd24fd4874a008d02d9f32a6711960550025aed93fe840278eb2824fc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main2 of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] Assume that  $\{X_k\}_{k\geq 1}$ is a $d$-dimensional $\alpha$-mixing identical sequence on a sublinear expectation space $(\Omega,\mathcal{H},\hat{\mathbb{E}})$ for some $\alpha>0$ with $\hat{\mathbb{E}}[|X_1|^{2}]<\infty$. Let $t_k=\lfloor P(k)\rfloor\vee 1$ for each $k\in\mathbb N$, where $P(x)=a_mx^m+\cdots+a_1x+a_0$ is a real-valued polynomial with $a_m>0$ for some $m\geq 2$, and 	$\Gamma:=\{\mathbb{E}[X_1]: \mathbb{E}\in \Theta\}.$  
		Then there exists $C>0$ such that for any $\phi\in C_{lip}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ with Lipschitz constant $l_{\phi}>0$ and for all $n\in \mathbb{N}$,
		\begin{equation*}
			\left|\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\phi\left(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^n X_{t_k}\right)\right]-\max_{x\in \Gamma}\phi(x) \right|\leq C  l_{\phi}n^{-1/2}.
		\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.784729+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59f6c0747864ea8e4c5773376c43418cb7ae0b85d186d598f2371c6a0164e7dc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem annulus-coupling-estimate-linear of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] Fix $r/100 \le m \le  (R-r)/2$. There exist $C(d), \beta_0(d)<\infty$ such that the following holds for all $\beta>\beta_0$:
    \begin{align*}
        \|\pi_{A_{r,R}}^\pm ( \cdot \mathord{\upharpoonright}_{\Lambda_{r+m}}) - \pi_{A_{r,r+2m}}^\pm (\cdot \mathord{\upharpoonright}_{\Lambda_{r+m}})\|_{{\textsc{tv}}}  \le Ce^{ - \beta m}\,.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.787789+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59fa11a7c9b119d37272111f401d69902476644548ecb096d20daee94c41efd7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:converge of arXiv:2411.08295, 'Improving the convergence of Markov chains via permutations and projections'] Let $\pi \in \mathcal{P}(\mathcal{X}), P \in \mathcal{S}(\pi)$ and $Q \in \mathcal{I}(\pi) \cap \mathcal{L}$ to be an isometric involution transition matrix. Let $\Pi$ be the matrix where each row equals to $\pi$. We have
	\begin{itemize}
		\item(One-step contraction measured by $D^{\pi}_{KL}$) \begin{align}
			D^{\pi}_{KL}(P \| \Pi) &= D^{\pi}_{KL}(P Q \| \Pi) = D^{\pi}_{KL}(Q P \| \Pi) = D^{\pi}_{KL}(Q P Q\| \Pi).
		\end{align}

		\item(KL-divergence Dobrushin coefficient)
		\begin{align}
			c_{KL}(P) = c_{KL}(PQ) = c_{KL}(QP) = c_{KL}(QPQ).
		\end{align}

		\item(Projection is trace-preserving)
		\begin{align}
			\mathrm{Tr}(P) = \mathrm{Tr}(QP^*Q) = \mathrm{Tr}(\overline{P}(Q)).
		\end{align}
	\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.019129+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59fdee69dcc51d3b83d3cb142a335f95c96baaff0b27a95167b7f884d37227a3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Fourier of arXiv:2605.15545, 'Crossover from subcritical to critical decay: \\ random walk, self-avoiding walk, percolat'] Let $d\ge 1$, $a > b \ge 0$, and $1 \le p \le \infty$.
Suppose $f : {\mathbb Z^d} \to \mathbb{R}$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
\bignorm{ \abs y^b f(y) }_{1} ,
\bignorm{ \abs y ^a f(y) }_{p \wedge 2} \le M
\end{equation}
for some constant $M < \infty$.
Then its Fourier transform $\hat f$ is $\floor a$ times weakly differentiable on ${\mathbb T^d}$, and we have
\begin{equation}
\norm{ \nabla^\gamma \hat f }_q \le M
\quad \text{with}  \quad
\frac 1 q = \frac{ \abs \gamma - b }{ a -b }
	\biggl( 1  - \frac 1 p \biggr) ,
\end{equation}
for all multi-indices $\gamma$ with $b \le \abs \gamma \le a$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:36:12.194299+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59fdff2c70b10452810926130b8de844f50af7b54bddffdacb88f42d24e9ee57","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 (Dynamic master inequalities for cumulants) of arXiv:2609.03924, 'Beyond normal fluctuations in local laws for Wigner matrices'] Let $W$ be an $N\times N$ Wigner matrix satisfying Assumption~\ref{ass:momass}. For any fixed $p, n,S\in \N$ with $p\ge 3$ it holds that
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
\Xi_t^{(p)}(n,S) \lesssim &\Xi_0^{(p)}(n,S) + \int_0^t \left(\Xi^{(p)}_s(n,S-1) +\frac{1}{N}\Xi^{(p)}_s(n+1,S+2)\right) \dif s\\
+&\int_0^s\left(\sum_{S'\le S} \frac{1}{N\eta^{S-S'+2}}\Xi^{(p)}_s(n-1,S') + \sum_{S'\le S-2} \frac{1}{\eta^{S-S'+1}}\Xi^{(p)}_s(n-2,S')\right)\dif s\\
+&\int_0^s\left(\sum_{S'\le S} \frac{1}{N\eta^{S-S'+2}}\Xi^{(p-1)}_s(n-1,S') + \sum_{S'\le S-2} \frac{1}{\eta^{S-S'+1}}\Xi^{(p-1)}_s(n-2,S')\right)\dif s,\\
\Theta_t^{(p)}(n,S) \lesssim &\Theta_0^{(p)}(n,S) + \int_0^t \left(\Theta^{(p)}_s(n,S-1) +\frac{1}{N}\Theta^{(p)}_s(n+1,S+2)\right) \dif s\\
+&\int_0^t \left(\frac{1}{N}\Theta_s^{(p-1)}(n-1,S) +\Theta_s^{(p-1)}(n-2,S-2)\right)\dif s,
\end{split}

\end{equation}
for any fixed $\xi>0$, uniformly in $t\in [0,T]$ and $z=z_T\in\mathcal{D}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.712834+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a026b6c8827c73db500b9d11619bd382d0cf1a8129971a30c97400b2406fb13","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm2 of arXiv:2411.18775, 'Limit Theorems for the Dynamical Foundation of the Fractional Brownian Motion and Related '] Fix any $t_0>0$. Under Assumptions~(asmp:hyp1 of the paper),~(asmp:coef new of the paper),~(asmp:m new of the paper),~(assmp:u0 new of the paper),~(assmp:coef2 of the paper), and Assumption~(assmp:m extra new of the paper)~(i) or  Assumption~(assmp:m extra new of the paper)~(ii) 
