{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.570531+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a0e104ea50818f176ee08e0bbc25cbf040036c404370bc442c7c25ad2ca3a4d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$. There exists $c>0$ such that, for every $n\geq 1$,
