{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.460291+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a69b38e94caf4de4ff036bcc2a63349a34c560190bd82e55c190cea329d0290","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 49 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $(k_j)_{j \in \mathbb{Z} } \subset \mathbb{Z}$ be such $k_j - k_{j-1} >0$, for any $j \in \mathbb{Z}$. Moreover, for any $j \in \mathbb{Z}$ let $F_j: [0, T] \times \Omega \mapsto \mathbb{R}$ be such that, for every $s \in [0, \; T]$, $\supp \big( F_j(s, \cdot) \; \big) \subset \{k_{j-1}+1, \ldots ,  k_j\}$, and $\mathbb{E}_{\nu_{\rho}} \big[ F_j(s, \eta) \big]=0$. Therefore, there exists some universal constant $\kappa$ such that
	\begin{align*}
		\forall t \in [0, T], \quad \mathbb{E}_{\nu_{\rho}} \Bigg[ \sup_{s \in [0,t] } \Bigg(  \int_{0}^s \sum_{j} F_j(r, \; \eta_r^n) \; \dd r \Bigg)^2  \Bigg] \leq  \kappa \int_0^{t}  \sum_{j}   \frac{(k_j - k_{j-1})^{\gamma}}{\Theta(n)} \mathbb{E}_{\nu_{\rho}} \big[ \big\{ F_j(s, \eta) \}^{2} \big] \dd s.
	\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.337890+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a6b87dadd3fcdbf95581efcc48824f18cfaf7162643ea1fb273f6b8c69910ca","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L: eta_decomposition of arXiv:2606.18654, 'Rigidity of infinite exchangeable sequences with Gaussian marginals'] Assume for any fixed $a,b \in \mathbb{R}$ that $q_{a,b} = 0$ almost surely.
