{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.848778+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a89742d3893fe13ef8cba6301e133a9cc1476c55c1ba14534a08f110b556af2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defination 6 (Stochastic Process of Order $\eps^\kappa$) of arXiv:2511.10814, '\Large \bf \boldmath\ \\ Convergence of the extended Kalman filter with small and state-de'] A family of stochastic processes $ \x(t)=(\x^\eps(t))_{t\ge 0}$, $\eps>0$ is said to be \textbf{ of order $\eps^\kappa$} 
