{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.131975+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ad2f0319a62feecf71ba8aa61f93c241d8642cfc6b363840c0247f34140c878","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:apply-bar-main-quadratic of arXiv:2510.11015, 'An interpretable universal bound for multiserver queues via a leave-one-out technique'] Consider the modified $GI/GI/n$\xspace system satisfying Assumptions~(assump:bdd-exp-remain of the paper) and (assump:modified-ggn-stable of the paper), with the load $\rho < 1$. We have
    \begin{equation}

        (1-\rho) \Ep{\pi}{Q}
        =  \frac{\rho\textnormal{Var}\left[\Lambda A\right] + \textnormal{Var}\left[\mu S\right] + 1-\rho}{2} +  \sum_{j=1}^n \Gamma_{{s,j}}  - \Gamma_a \;, 
    \end{equation}
    where $\Gamma_{{s,j}}$ and $\Gamma_{a}$ are defined as: 
    \begin{align}

        \Gamma_{{s,j}} &= \Ep{s}{\vmathbb{1}{\left\{Q=0\right\}} \mu R_{{s,j}}} - (1-\rho) \Ep{\pi}{\mu R_{{s,j}}} \quad \forall j\in [n]\\

        \Gamma_{a} &= \Ep{s}{\vmathbb{1}{\left\{Q=0\right\}} \Lambda R_a} - (1-\rho) \Ep{\pi}{\Lambda R_{a}},
    \end{align}
    and $\Ep{s}{\cdot} \triangleq \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n \Ep{{s,i}}{\cdot}$ is the Palm expectation with respect to all completion events. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.312101+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ad4b3a85e357ce9ca530a9874fac7756a97663d29ee3909acf5fe4e2bd519eb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 of arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random H\"older velocity '] Fix $\alpha\in(0,1)$, $\lambda>0$, and $p\geq 1$, and let, for all $j\geq 0$, $u^j$ be defined by~\eqref{eq:autonomous poisson}. Suppose there exists $M\geq 1$ such that for all $j\geq 0$, $n\in\{0,1,2\}$, and $y\in\T^d,$
\[\|\nabla^n f^j_y\|_{L^p_\omega C^0_x}\leq M 2^{(n-\alpha-d/p)j}.\]
Then 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item the $u^j$ are mutually independent with $\E u^j =0$,
\item for each $j\geq 1$, $u^j$ has a finite spatial range of dependence $2^{-j}$,
\item and there exists a constant $C(d)>0$ such that for all $j\geq 0$ and $n\in\{0,1,2\}$,
\[\|\nabla^n u^j\|_{L^p_\omega C^0_x}\leq CM(\lambda+p)2^{(n-\alpha)j}.\]
\end{enumerate}
Letting $U:=\sum_{j= 0}^\infty u^j$, we further have that
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[(i)] if for all $j\geq 0$ and $y\in\T^d$, $\nabla\cdot f^j_y=0$, then $\nabla\cdot U=0$,
    \item[(ii)] if there exists $r\in(0,1)$ and $C>0$ such that for all $j\geq 0$
    \begin{equation}
    \sup_{\substack{x,y\in\T^d\\d_{\T^d}(x,y)\leq 2^{-(j+2)}}}\bigg\|\frac{d\mu^j_{y,x}(z)}{dz}\bigg\|_{L^\infty(\R^d)}\leq Cr^j e^{\lambda j},
    \end{equation}
    then it almost surely holds that for all $\alpha'<\alpha$
    \[\lim_{\eps\rightarrow 0} \eps^{-\alpha'd}|Z_\eps|=0,\]
    where $Z_\eps$ is defined as in~\eqref{eq:zero sets}.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.320995+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ad579ebcfeaf197ffa4552dffab863995e858562b9f1e36927bd2daa7ac5121","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2607.27150, 'Modelling Anomalous Diffusion: The Role of CTRWs and Non-Local Dynamics'] Suppose that the assumptions of Theorem \ref{thmGS} are satisfied, and let $\Xi(t)$, $t\in \RR$, be defined as in \eqref{next-jump}. Then the process $(Y^+(t), \Xi(t))$, $t \geq 0$, is a time-homogeneous Markov process, under all $\PP^{(x,s)}$, $(x,s)\in \RR^d\times (-\infty,0]$, and the filtration $\mathcal{G}_t$, $t \geq0$, generated by $N(s), S_0, \dots, {S_{N(s)+1}}, T_0, \dots, {T_{N(s)+1}}$, $s \leq t$. Its semigroup $\wt P_t^+$, $t \geq 0$, satisfies for $(x,s)\in \RR^d\times (0,+\infty)$
		\begin{align}
			\wt P^+_tf(x,s)&=\mathds{1}_{[0\le t<s]}f(x,s-t)+\mathds{1}_{[0<s\le t ]}\int_{\RR^d}\int_{(0,+\infty)}\wt P^+_{t-s}f(y,w)\mu_{x}(dy,dw),
		\end{align}
		for any function $f \in \mathcal{B}_b (\mathbb{R}^d \times (0, +\infty))$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.725300+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5adc5f94852f55c1fa641e2f6184cac76cbfd17fb10291e2ea3bbfcb830dcd69","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma prop:Morerageneral of arXiv:2411.04238, 'Holomorphic jump-diffusions'] Let $F$ be a non-negative measure on a measurable space $E$, $R\in(0,\infty]^d$ and for some $\varepsilon>0$, let
