\end{eqnarray} 
where \(C_{x_0,T}>0\) only depends on \(x_0\) and \(T\) and \(\bar x\) is the solution to the Young SDE \eqref{averaged-system}.
Moreover, \(\bar g\) is globally Lipschitz continuous. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:55:56.990917+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5b3a7b6f648221835a4a8bbcbbf8fc45fa99edfdad7ace9b3b400d10fce4dcc9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2609.02779, '2609.02779'] There is $C>0$ such that every lift of a $u_0$-calibrated curve
