{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.773891+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ba613b0f927a3ed09c31ac878dffc51284265a2e5921f730204e878d14f686e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma range_estimates_main_text of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Consider a random walk on $\mathbb Z^d$ driven by $Q$. Let $D \subseteq H(r)$ with $|D|/|H(r)| \leq 3/4$. Define $\widetilde{\mathrm{R}}(k) := \mathrm{R}(k) \cap (H(r) \setminus D)$. Then, there exist positive constants $c_0, c_1$ depending on $Q$ such that for any $r \in \mathbb N^+$ and any $x \in H(r)$:
    \begin{align} 
