{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.356507+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5bc85c964e939e0c7c45da689d6004d4a87d0846087352aa0a734b0a07dceec6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:um:SPDE of arXiv:2607.20956, 'Sharp moduli of continuity for Gaussian fields and stochastic PDEs via correlation bounds'] Suppose $2H\alpha =3$. Fix a compact rectangle $I\times J \subset (0\,,\infty) \times \mathbb{R}$, $t_0 > 0$ and $x_0 \in \mathbb{R}$.
Then, a.s.,
\begin{align}
    \lim_{h\to0^+} \sup_{x,y \in J: 0<|x-y|\le h} \frac{|u(t_0\,,x)-u(t_0\,,y)|}{|x-y|\log(1/|x-y|)} = K_3,
\end{align}
\begin{align}
    \lim_{h\to0^+} \sup_{t,s\in I: 0<|t-s| \le h} \frac{|u(t\,,x_0)-u(s\,,x_0)|}{|t-s|^{1/\alpha}\sqrt{\log(1/|t-s|)}} = K_4,
\end{align}
\begin{align}
    \lim_{h\to0^+} \sup_{z,z'\in I\times J: 0<\phi(z,z') \le h} \frac{|u(z)-u(z')|}{\phi(z\,,z')\sqrt{\log(1/\phi(z\,,z'))}} = K_5,
\end{align}
for some non-random numbers $K_3, K_4, K_5 \in (0\,,\infty)$ that may depend on $I, J$ or $t_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.974342+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5bcaf559fdd9dc778aaad307388fbbd49dc1007f834a30294e9f764f34a5eb1f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2606.11142, 'Strong invariance principles for diffusions, Markov chains and their perturbations.'] When A1, A2, A3 hold, there exists a probability space supporting versions of the processes $Y_{\tau_k}$ and $Y^{(\epsilon)}_{\tau_k}$, where $Y$ and $Y^\epsilon$ are both chain and perturbed chain, or diffusion and perturbed diffusion, and a positive constant $C$ such that the probability of their paths coinciding on the entire grid satisfies:
