{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:33.534060+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5bce72ef95a8874d659b39d2ebfb2673ad01dd408690c576d5ab0fbb348f3b14","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2603.28093, 'Random Stability of Random Variables'] Under the condition~\eqref{eq:ln-N}, any symmetric $N$-stable $X$ has the following characteristic function 
\begin{equation}

f(u) = \mathbb E\left[e^{\mathrm{i}uX}\right] = L(\beta |u|^{\alpha})
\end{equation}
for some $\beta > 0$ and $\alpha \in (0, 2]$, where $L$ is the Laplace transform of the standard $N$-stable random variable $Y$. This $X$ can be represented as 
\begin{equation}

X \stackrel{d}{=} Y^{1/\alpha}Z,\quad \mathbb E\left[e^{\mathrm{i}uZ}\right] = \exp\left(-\beta |u|^{\alpha}\right).
\end{equation}
Here, $Z$ is independent of $Y$, and is symmetric $\alpha$-stable. Conversely, any $X$ having representation~\eqref{eq:repr-N-stable-symm}, or characteristic function~\eqref{eq:repr-N-stable-symm}, is symmetric $N$-stable. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.277513+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5bd5c451c98abe78fc535d3ea100d565bcb8677e705f7551c024b9ad58b1251e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2604.22257, 'On necessary and sufficient conditions for the local large deviation principle'] {\rm (i)}~In the general case, if  the LDP is satisfied for a family of random vectors then the LLDP with the same rate function~$D$ is also satisfied for that family.

{\rm (ii)}~The converse implication holds true provided that the following condition is met{\rm :}  for any $N>0$ there exists a $v>0$ such that
\begin{align}

\limsup_{T\to\infty} \frac1T \ln \pr (|\zeta_T|> v) \le -N.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.413991+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5bda5455f03216c35620ac1ca8f2cee7f95cbd8f4c62c5d4d399a9ddc523ca95","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: estimates for um of arXiv:2609.02073, 'Existence of closed non-planar $p$-elasticae'] Let $(\lambda,C^2) \in S^0$, i.e.\ $C^2>0$.
  \begin{enumerate}
    \item[(i)] If $0\leq \lambda < \frac{p-1}{2}$ and $\gamma_p = \min\left(\frac{4p}{2p-2}, \frac{6p-4}{2p-2}\right)$, then there exist $B_{\lambda,p}, \varepsilon_{\lambda,p} \in (0,\infty)$ such that for all $C^2<\varepsilon_{\lambda,p}$
    \begin{equation*}
      \left(\frac{(p-1)(p-1-2\lambda)}{p^2} \right)^{\frac{p}{2-2p}} C^{\frac{2p}{2p-2}} -B_{\lambda,p} C^{\gamma_p} < u_m < \left(\frac{(p-1)(p-1-2\lambda)}{p^2} \right)^{\frac{p}{2-2p}} C^{\frac{2p}{2p-2}}.
    \end{equation*} 
    Moreover, for $0<\delta\ll 1$ fixed, if $\lambda \in [0,\frac{p-1}{2}-\delta]$, then $B_{\lambda,p} \in [m_{\delta,p}, M_{\delta,p}]$ for some constants $0<m_{\delta,p}, M_{\delta,p}$.

    \item[(ii)] If $\frac{p-1}{2}<\lambda < p-1$, then there exists $B_{\lambda,p}>0$, continuous in $\lambda$ with $\lim_{\lambda\to p-1}B_{\lambda,p}=\frac{5p}{2(p-1)}$, and $\varepsilon_{\lambda,p} \in (0,\infty)$ such that for all $C^2<\varepsilon_{\lambda,p}$
    \begin{equation*}
      \frac{2\lambda}{p-1}-1  < u_m < \frac{2\lambda}{p-1}-1 + B_{\lambda,p} C^{2}.
    \end{equation*}
    Also for $0<\delta\ll 1$ fixed, if $\lambda \in [\frac{p-1}{2}+\delta,p-1)$, then $B_{\lambda,p} \in [m_{\delta,p}, M_{\delta,p}]$ for some constants $0<m_{\delta,p}, M_{\delta,p}$.
  \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.362688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5bdaaec1052004bffbe21cb6ca4615a4f11224270a1bb102014e925f689514e7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (~\cite{Trip26Law}) of arXiv:2606.18047, 'Analysis of the asymmetric shelf shuffle'] Let $n\geq 2, m\in \mathbb{N}$ and $p\in (0, 1)$. Then, for any $\pi\in S_n$, we have 
