{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:29:27.983667+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c10803257110d8e63a1d0d756ed48e79d6c6fd305503a5717bd75ebca9a7191","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Planar weighted Gaussian inequalities) of arXiv:2608.24863, 'Uniform Logarithmic Sobolev Inequalities for the 2D Coulomb Gas at the Diffusive Temperatu'] There exist finite constants $C_{\rm wt}(\gamma,Q)$ and $\rho_{\rm wt}(\gamma,Q)>0$, depending only on $(\gamma,Q)$, such that every such measure $\nu$ satisfies
\begin{align}
 \Var_\nu(f)&\le C_{\rm wt}(\gamma,Q)\int_{\C}|\nabla f|^2\,\D\nu,\\
 \Ent_\nu(f^2)&\le\frac2{\rho_{\rm wt}(\gamma,Q)}\int_{\C}|\nabla f|^2\,\D\nu.
\end{align}
The inequalities hold for every real-valued $f$ in the closed Dirichlet-form domain generated by $C_c^\infty(\C\setminus\{y_j:a_j>0\})$.  The constants are uniform in the number and locations of the points and in the individual exponents, subject only to this total-exponent bound. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.935349+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c1330eafc9c89014dfbf1d84976a56a9c2e6d7315226a9b261851520ebbb5ad","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem lem:explicit-left-M of arXiv:2602.07920, 'On the position matrix of single-shelf shuffle and card guessing'] Let $n\ge 2$ and let $i\in \mathcal E_n$. For each
$1\le a\le n$, the $a$th coordinate of the left eigenvector
$\widetilde\zeta^{(i)}=(\widetilde{w}^{(i)})^\top B^{-1}$ is given by
\begin{equation}
\widetilde\zeta^{(i)}(a)
= \frac{1}{i!(n-i)}\Bigl[
   (-1)^{\,i-a}\binom{i-1}{a-1}
 + (-1)^{\,n-1-a}\binom{i-1}{a-1-(n-i)}
 \Bigr],
\end{equation}
where, as usual, $\binom{m}{r}=0$ if $r<0$ or $r>m$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:33.540422+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c1972440eb7f809847b20dc212ff473b2ca98249e72c2c7c6d7b9294a0f0ee8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 10 (Two-dimensional Coulomb gas) of arXiv:2603.28734, 'Free energy analyticity of the disordered XY model and Debye screening in the 2D Coulomb g'] Fix $d=2$ and $\beta\in\R_{\geq 0}$.
    The \emph{two-dimensional lattice Coulomb gas} on $\Lambda_n$ with free boundary conditions at inverse temperature $\beta$
    is the probability measure on $q\in\Z^{F(\Lambda_n)}$
    given by
    \begin{equation}

        \mu_{\Coulomb,\Lambda_n,\beta}^\free[\{q=Q\}] = \frac{1}{Z_{\Coulomb,\Lambda_n,\beta}^\free} \mathbf{1}\Big[\sum\nolimits_{f\in F(\Lambda_n)}Q(f)=0\Big]\cdot e^{-\frac{\beta(2\pi)^2}{2} \langle Q , -\Delta^{-1} Q \rangle}.
    \end{equation}
    Notice that, contrary to the XY model,
    the Hamiltonian of the Coulomb gas is non-local due to the presence of the inverse Laplacian.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.993781+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c1aec55c0a308aa2855d982f19cd4f001cefe2b7c99f6052e7f45d9701735f6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm ferro of arXiv:2608.25362, 'Fluctuations of the free energy of the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick model with ferromagnetic i'] Suppose $\Omega(\boldsymbol{\beta},\gamma,h) = \{\mu\}$ for some $\mu\ne0$, or $\Omega(\boldsymbol{\beta},\gamma,h) = \{-\mu,\mu\}$ for some $\mu>0$. Then
