{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.675963+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c3448c4bddd62947b2312d7cd2aabd30601529253edc6801e44ba4f28449944","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2608.30077, 'Lie groupoid integration of singular isometries of the Poincaré disk'] The following vector fields in $\Dbarstar$
 \begin{align*}
    E &= \frac{1}{n}((z^{1-n} - z^{1+n})\partial_{z} + (\overline{z}^{1-n} - \overline{z}^{1+n})\partial_{\overline{z}}) \\
    F &= \frac{i}{n}((z^{1-n} + z^{1+n})\partial_{z} -(\overline{z}^{1-n} + \overline{z}^{1+n})\partial_{\overline{z}}) \\
    H &= \frac{2i}{n}(z\partial_{z} - \overline{z}\partial_{\overline{z}})
\end{align*}
  span a Lie algebra isomorphic to $\mathfrak{sl}_2(\mathbb{R})$ and provide the infinitesimal action for the formula \eqref{nformula}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.571333+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c35b61653be14bcbbd342fffc253f8bfccdf4c8ce2092163b4646e872c56c61","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:joint-decorr of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] Let $\mathcal{M}(t) = \mathbb{E}[\mathbf{X}(t)\mathbf{X}(t)^T]$ be the covariance matrix. For $t = t_*$:
