{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.462622+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c39b9fb9dc1edfafccecd435acba5d661708d52fc37b57a6044a9cd6bf16ca7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:Deltaz of arXiv:2603.28578, 'Exponential Bounds and Analyticity for the Tree Builder Random Walk'] Fix $\kappa \in (0,1]$ and $j\ge 1$. Then there exists $c = c(\kappa)>0$ such that
