{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.278942+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ca08c06150b40fcbf7e076e8a691d641acb89a33c2b31efc37b518215097d22","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2604.22461, 'Large deviation principles for stationary solutions and invariant measures of a class of S'] Assume that $A^{\epsilon}$ and $B$ satisfy the conditions {\rm [A1-A5]}, for any $t_0 \in \R$, $T>t_0$ and $\xi \in H$, let $X^{\epsilon}_{t;t_0,\xi}$ be the unique solution of Eq. \eqref{eq: SPDE}, the following results hold.
