{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.966137+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5cc29146a8323d20abb4b3b9728895e50a226c93348196a80455366bfa4c3144","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor cor1b of arXiv:2505.11700, 'Distribution of the cokernels of determinantal row-sparse matrices'] Let $p$ be a prime such that $p \nmid k_n$ for all sufficiently large $n$ and $G$ be a finite abelian $p$-group. Assume that a sequence $(k_n)_{n=1}^{\infty}$ satisfies the following:
