{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.308257+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5cc8d0b974e34cf8c5d9254b589758c88d4baca021b400ed777d59f198ae50f6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:lln_ini_prob of arXiv:2411.14818, 'Scaling limits of solitons in the Box-Ball system'] Suppose that $\mathbf{q} \in \mathcal{Q}$ and ${\mathbb{E}}_{\nu_\mathbf{q}}\left[ {s_{\infty}\left(1\right)}^2 \right] < \infty$. Then, for any $k \in {\mathbb{N}}$, $u \in {\mathbb{R}}$, we have
                    \begin{align}
                        \lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{1}{n} X^{\left( \left\lfloor nu \right\rfloor \right)}_{k}\left(0\right) = \frac{\bar{s}_{\infty}\left(\mathbf{q}\right) \bar{J}_{k}\left(\mathbf{q}\right) u}{\bar{\Xi}_{k}\left(\mathbf{q}\right)}, \quad \nu_{\mathbf{q}}\text{-a.s.}, 
