{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.833454+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ce177342ada9c281b5863bcd93253ded119cc2f3464170124d963455d86da32","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 35 (Explicit product-rule matrix criterion) of arXiv:2604.10792, 'Variable-Length Markov Chains on Finite Quivers: Boundary-Window Identifiability, Exact De'] In the setting of \cref{thm:selected-criterion}, let $L_I:T_0\to\RR^s$ be the linear map whose $j$th coordinate covector is
