{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.846713+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d18a2b30024bc58a778b1bd914ec1dd14ea4b023b2dc7cdea2774924ae05b0d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Wicksformula of arXiv:2510.01021, '\Large Random Matrices, Intrinsic Freeness, and Sharp Non-Asymptotic Inequalities\relatedv'] Let $g_1,\dots,g_n$ be iid $\mathcal{N}(0,1)$ random variables and let $u:[2p]\to[n]$ then
