{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.602658+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d7e2e191f51cd8c9a675502e8a672ede1bc07abc80a3edfba8373b182eea00c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 40 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] Let $\X$ be denumerable and let $q$ be a non-negative multi-time Markov renewal kernel. For every non-negative function $G=(G_i(k))_{i\in\X,k\in\N^d}$, the function

