{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.161304+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5deb68369d74bf2636e7d18ead45b20830abbec9df51bd658f00696ee2258e3a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:IorderedRandom of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] Fix some $v \geq 1$ and let $I$ be a function acting in the space of  recursive trees and returning a subset of vertices of $[v]$, such that for any recursive tree $\mathrm{t}$ of size $n\geq v$,

    \begin{itemize}
        \item for any permutation $\tau$ of $I(\mathrm{t})$, the tree $\mathrm{t}^{\tau}$ is recursive and $I(\mathrm{t}^{\tau})=I(\mathrm{t})$;
        \item for $\mathrm{t}_v$, the subtree of $\mathrm{t}$ spanned by vertices in $[v]$, $I(\mathrm{t}_v)=I(\mathrm{t})$. 
    \end{itemize}
    Then, for any label-invariant estimator $\widehat{\sigma}$ and any set $\mathcal{I}$ in the image of $I$ with $i,v \in \mathcal{I}$,

    $$
     \widehat{\sigma}\left(v,T_n\right)\mid I(T_n)=\mathcal{I} \quad 
     \overset{\mathcal{L}}{=} \quad 
     \widehat{\sigma}\left(i,T_n\right)\mid  I(T_n)=\mathcal{I}.
     $$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.953501+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ded5327648000e8c4bf0bcc1ada7ef5f68fbe3cebc5272a30eca81aa0c2afc9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:tilted_gen_density of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] The semigroup $(P_t^{k,\rho})_{t \geq 0}$
