{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.885840+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5df01906a16c257fc85a473666f720ff88ea81ce86e63a4afdccbbff28a6f962","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:existence of time dep non rev of arXiv:2607.02367, 'Flux solutions for stochastic chemical systems with sources and sinks'] Assume that $(\Omega, \mathcal R, \mathcal R_s, \mathcal K , \mathcal K_s) $ is a non-bidirectional chemical system with sources and sinks and that the set of reactions $\mathcal R $ is conservative. Assume moreover that $f_0 \in \mathcal P (\mathbb N^M)$ is such that 
\[ 
\sum_{ n \in \mathbb N^M } |n| f_0(n) < \infty . 
\]
    There exists a weak solution $f:  [0, \infty ) \rightarrow \mathcal P (\mathbb N^M) $ that satisfies 
    \begin{align*}
    \sum_{  n \in \mathbb  N^M  } \varphi(n) \partial_t   f (t, n) &=    \sum_{ \rho =1}^r  R_\rho(n) \left[ \varphi(n+ S_\rho) - \varphi(n)  \right] +    \sum_{ k \in \Omega_c }  A_k (n)   \left[ \varphi(n+ e_k ) - \varphi(n)  \right] \\
    & +    \sum_{ k \in \Omega_c } B_k (n)   \left[ \varphi(n-  e_k ) - \varphi(n)  \right] 
    \end{align*}
    for every $ \varphi \in c_{ 00 } ( \mathbb N^M) $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:06:18.011602+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5dfefd91c8d04f0c87613810011002e06ff69cd6a476d50d5f0f7d98e4d35871","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2608.14802, 'Dynamical Gibbs-non-Gibbs transitions for finite-alphabet models on trees'] Let $t> 0$, $\theta>4$ and $k\in \{2,3\}$. Further, define the sequence $(z_{n}^k(t))_{n\in \N_0}$ recursively by
    \begin{equation*}
        z_0^k(t):=\begin{cases}
            (x_-,1),~&\text{if}~~l=l_-^{(1)},\\
            (1,1),~&\text{if}~~l=l_{\mathrm{free}},
        \end{cases}
    \end{equation*}
    where $x_-$ is defined in Lemma \ref{lem: Fixed points normalized simplex Potts model}, and by $z_{n+1}^k(t):=\widetilde{g}_t^{[k]}(z_{n}^k(t))$ for all $n\in \N_0$. Then, the limit $z^*_k(t):=\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}z_{n}^k(t)$ exists and is a fixed point of $\widetilde{g}_t^{[k]}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.582013+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5dffaf46880842124e9e26022150b6268678dda60ee55e8c96e3c7158231387e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Moment of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] For each $p\geq 1$, there exists a constant $C>0$  such that for any $\zeta,t\geq 0$,
  \begin{eqnarray}
   \sup_{n\geq 1}\mathbf{E}\Big[\big| X_\zeta^{(n)}(t) \big|^p  \Big] 
   \leq C\cdot (\zeta \vee \zeta^p) \cdot (1+t)^{2p-1}. 
  \end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.664113+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e04ef178a83b6123697375e7c65ffb459575bfbd044ee6b71054c0698e7f4d6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem hazard-residual of arXiv:2609.00110, 'Phase Transition and Fluctuation Results for First-Passage Percolation on Spread-Out Cycle'] Let $\mathcal{I}$ be a finite set of edges and let $L_e\geqslant0$, $e\in\mathcal{I}$, be deterministic lower bounds. Conditionally on the event
$
 \{\go_e>L_e\text{ for all }e\in\mathcal{I}\},
$
the random variables
\begin{align*}
 H(\go_e)-H(L_e)=\go_e^\theta-L_e^\theta,
 \quad e\in\mathcal{I},
\end{align*}
are independent rate-one exponentials. The same holds conditionally on any exploration history that reveals only the lower bounds $L_e$ for the edges in $\mathcal{I}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.520988+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e0622d8a57795c89daf9935d73f58a891bfb8083e8ecd2d335c3b56c4c98097","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:u_pm of arXiv:2512.17808, 'Zeros of polynomial powers under the heat flow'] We define the two solutions to $\frac u {\sqrt t} +\frac{\sqrt t} u =\frac z{\sqrt t}$ by
	\begin{align}

		u_{t}^{\pm}(z):=\frac{1}2(z\pm\sqrt{z^2-4t}), \quad z\in\mathbb{C}\setminus \big( (-\infty,-2\sqrt t]\cup [2\sqrt t,\infty) \big),
	\end{align}
	where we choose the branch of the root such that $u_t^+(z)\sim z$ as $|z|\to\infty$ with $z\in \mathbb{C}_+$, and $u_t^-(z)\sim z$ as $|z|\to\infty$ with $z\in \mathbb{C}_-$, respectively.
	If $t=1$ we will denote the solutions by $u^{\pm}(z):=u_1^\pm(z)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.829512+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e078ba4bfd90857fee1415f8034e9f7c48bb20c4e77df23906af35c04df4856","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem eq:diffHa of arXiv:2609.01751, 'Orthogonal polynomials which are eigenfunctions of a partial differential operator'] Let $\rho: {\mathbb R}^{d_2} \mapsto {\mathbb R}$ and $h: {\mathbb R}^{d_1} \mapsto {\mathbb R}$ be differentiable. Then the function
$$
   H({\bm x}, {\bm y}) := [\rho({\bm y})]^m h\left(\frac{{\bm x}}{\rho({\bm y})} \right)
$$
satisfies the following relations
\begin{equation} 
  \rho({\bm y})  \partial_{y_i} H = \partial_{y_i} \rho({\bm y}) \left( m  - {\langle} {\bm x},\nabla_{\bm x}{\rangle} \right) H, \quad 1 \le i\le d_2,
\end{equation}
and, in particular, 
 \begin{equation} 
