{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.893384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e13843080b69afc3bb10564274b11d9e49929688b8aa2902c32390681334a36","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:sources of arXiv:2606.30475, 'Ancestries in random $d$-DAGs'] For $M>0$, denote by $Z_M$ the number of sources (that is, vertices with in-degree 0 in $G_n$) among the first $\floor{Mn^{d/(d+1)}}$ vertices. As $n\to\infty$, we have
