{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:12:46.875882+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e287a9ce70f11c12049a2dcbb51b26119e2f43de75be72a0c4df1aca900e844","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_animal of arXiv:2608.08532, 'Constrained Maximum Weight Paths in Random Geometric Graphs'] Suppose the conditions in Theorem~(thm_path of the paper) hold and  let~\(F_c(.)\) be the edge weight ccdf. There are constants~\(\delta_1,\delta_2 > 0\) such that for any~\(x,y > 0\) and~\(Q \geq 1,\)
