{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:07.957906+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e2c6df56933237f84492dc20d604db68ae03ceeafcd60feecf1e30011c461ab","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Intersection patterns/shapes of arXiv:2608.12415, 'Sharp Phase Transition for Ellipsoid Fitting'] Given two shapes $\tau_1$ and $\tau_2$ that are composable, we define an intersection pattern for $\tau_1$ and $\tau_2$ to be a non-empty set $I \subseteq \left(V(\tau_1) \setminus V_{\tau_1}\right) \times \left(V(\tau_2) \setminus U_{\tau_2}\right)$ of intersection edges where each vertex is incident to at most one edge. Whenever we have an intersection edge $e = \{a,b\}$ (between vertices of the same type), this means that when we consider maps $\sigma: V(\tau_1) \cup V(\tau_2) \to [n]\cup [d] $, we have the restriction that $\sigma(a) = \sigma(b)$.

We define $\tau_{I} = \tau_{I}(\tau_1\cdot \tau_2)$ to be the shape obtained from $\tau_1$ and $\tau_2$ as follows:
\begin{enumerate}
\item Start with the properly concatenated shape $\tau_1\circ \tau_2$;
\item For each intersection edge $e = \{a,b\}$, merge $a$ and $b$ together into one vertex.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.432480+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e2fd7e533a643a5548a1c87c949544cc016c76a8d3ce29622600b502040e1d0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:defannealedgaussian of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] A potential $V : \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}} \to \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}$ is said to be an annealed Gaussian potential if the map $k \mapsto k^2 e^{-V(k)}$ is summable over $\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}$ and if there exists a Borel probability measure $\mu_V$ on $(0,\infty)$ such that, for any $x \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}$,

\begin{equation} 
    e^{-V(x)} = \int_0^\infty e^{- \frac{x^2}{2J}} \mu_V(d J).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.320240+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e334c093b8d69d9cc212b58191a07cf223c3061d79fe5ef092880891c5becbf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:scalinv of arXiv:2411.09058, 'Time-dependent averages of a critical long-range stochastic heat equation'] For any radius $R>0$,
