{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.447257+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e3d3abe2746f6871d97a9ef21850b5dd93da6608aed221704734ad0b8f6276b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn non-separableplanar-embedded of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] Fix a loop $\ell$ and a plaquette assignment $K$ such that the pair $(\ell,K)$ is balanced.
We say that a planar embedded map $M=(m,\psi)$ with boundary $\ell$ and plaquette assignment $K$ is \textbf{non-separable} if for every lattice edge $e\in E^+_{\Lambda}$,
\begin{itemize}
	\item[8.] removing all blue faces sent to the edge $e$ by $\psi$ does not disconnect the dual graph of $m$.
\end{itemize} 

We denote by $\mathcal{N}\mathcal{P}\mathcal{M}(\ell,K)$ the set of non-separable planar embedded maps with boundary $\ell$ and plaquette assignment $K$.
For a non-balanced pair $(\ell,K)$, we define $\mathcal{N}\mathcal{P}\mathcal{M}(\ell,K)=\emptyset$.","status":"unverified"}

