{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:11.418026+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e4b7056e6f82989a31375482b9cd8b8d67981a2bf3270121ac743e495ede06e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 8 of arXiv:2606.08776, 'Approximation of certain stochastic integrals with anticipating integrands'] Assume $Z$ has the admissible representation \eqref{eqn:definition:admissible_representation_Z}
and let $\sigma_N^\theta$, $N>M$, be the time-nets from \cref{def:time_nets}.
