{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.771595+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e506a56e8c3ff52530d7f355061062b7ba1d51c86eabcb380a39ebc305a88be","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq: discrete approx of arXiv:2411.02917, '\hspace*{2mm}\\[-16mm] Stein's Method for Spatial Random Graphs'] Let  $(\Xi,\Sigma)$ be an $\mathrm{RGG}(\lambda,\kappa)$ such that $\Xi$ is an inhibitory pairwise interaction process with constant activity function~$\beta$, i.e.\ $\lambda(x\,|\, \xi) = \beta \prod_{y\in\xi} \varphi(x,y)$ for $\beta\in\R_+$ and $\varphi:\mathcal{X}^2\to \R_+$ with $\varphi\leq 1$. Then
\begin{align} 
    W_{\mathbb{G},i}(&P^\lambda\otimes Q^{\kappa},P^{\lambda_{\Lambda}}\otimes Q^{\kappa_{\Lambda}}) \leq r_V + C_iB^*\,\beta^2\, \norm{\varphi - \varphi \circ t}_1 
      + \frac14 C_E\,\beta^2\,\norm{\kappa - \kappa_{\Lambda}\circ t}_1,
