{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:44.993628+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ea353ad3d91c9c993257db2e397618f5eefe561ba9ad9b9fadc7b1895747245","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2605.11801, 'A non-local singular non-linear Fokker-Planck PDE'] Let $\gamma \in (0,1)$ and $K\in \shp(\R^d)$.  Let us suppose Assumption \ref{ass:F}. Then we have the following.
