{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.833285+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5efe6cd31e0e82e569bd25ee500a39a7bcbca467e567a1c4f67f51d5d730abfd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 33 (Coordinatewise stationary-fiber representation) of arXiv:2604.10792, 'Variable-Length Markov Chains on Finite Quivers: Boundary-Window Identifiability, Exact De'] Fix a pair $(y,a)$ consisting of a visible state $y\in\cS_m$ and an admissible appended edge $a$ from the terminal vertex of $y$, and write $y_a:=U_m(y,a)$. For each $z\in F_y$ define
\begin{equation}
