{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.630126+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f36f84f0317152836b0d3db06ff3c2454b75b16bf0af7c427db08ad79421f0b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2506.17045, '\LARGE{On bivariate Archimax copulas: Level sets, mass distributions and related results}'] Let $\psi \in \mathbf{\Psi}$, $A \in \mathcal{A}$, $C_{\psi,A} \in \mathcal{C}_{am}$, $t \in (0,1)$, $\fg^t$ be defined as in eq. \eqref{eq:fct_g_t}, $R$ be defined according to eq. \eqref{eq:definition_L_R} and $g^R$ be defined as in eq. \eqref{eq:fct_f}. Then the following assertions hold:
