{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.329764+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f59e18c06002aeafd9e0b8b65075c03aa58d9013f57f6ba28c0407884c6aafd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma meanfieldspectralgap of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] For $\alpha\in [0,1]$, define the binomial product measure $\varpi_\alpha = \mathrm{Bin}(\kappa ,\alpha )^{\otimes\mathbb{Z}}$. There exists a universal constant $C_{11}=C_{11}(\kappa )>0$ such that for any local function $f:\Omega\longrightarrow\mathbb{R}$ supported in $\{0,\hdots ,\ell -1\}$ for some $\ell\ge 1$, and such that~$\varpi_\alpha(f)=0$ for any $\alpha\in [0,1]$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \mathrm{Var}_{\varpi_\alpha}(f) \le \frac{C_{11}}{\ell}\sum_{x,y=0}^{\ell -1}\int_{\Omega}\eta_x(\kappa -\eta_y)\big[ f(\eta^{x\to y})-f(\eta )\big]^2\,\mathrm{d}\varpi_\alpha(\eta ).
