{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.672928+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f7cb9fd19bab53ccc8198b572e221ff9a94b6fe0442a6139e5cfc9f6a6003e6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:gamma:summing of arXiv:2605.28106, 'Gaussian Processes with Sample Paths in Reproducing Kernel Banach Spaces'] An operator \( A \in \mathcal{L}(H,X) \) is \emph{\( \gamma \)-summing} if
