{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.131738+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5fb4e10c129777cdf5e151b7855bb0dca11b6372c85698152a3714be745a31a9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main-upper-bound of arXiv:2510.11015, 'An interpretable universal bound for multiserver queues via a leave-one-out technique'] Consider the $GI/GI/n$\xspace queue with homogeneous servers under the FCFS policy, whose service-time and interarrival-time distributions satisfy Assumptions~(assump:bdd-exp-remain of the paper), (assump:non-lattice of the paper) and (assump:modified-ggn-stable of the paper). When the load $\rho < 1$, let $\pi$ be the unique stationary distribution of the system. Then the steady-state mean queue length, $\Ep{\pi}{Q}$, is bounded as
    \begin{equation}

        \begin{aligned}
            \Ep{\pi}{Q} &\leq \frac{\rho\textnormal{Var}\left[\Lambda A\right] + \textnormal{Var}\left[\mu S\right] + 1-\rho}{2(1-\rho)} + \min\Big(n, \frac{1}{1-\rho}\Big) \Big(R_{s}^{\max} - \frac{1}{2} \mathbb{E}\left[(\mu S)^2\right]\Big) \\
            &\mspace{23mu} + \Big(\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[(\Lambda A)^2\right] - R_{a}^{\min}\Big).
        \end{aligned}
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.375528+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5fba2c31b03233ac5415c932c042c3cc70a7ee54c13670463d7cc867ca4ef316","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition multishelfcorrespondence of arXiv:2507.10294, 'Guessing Strategies for Shelf-Shuffling Machines'] Let $m\geq 1$ and let $S_{2^{m-1}}$ be the transition matrix for a $2^{m-1}$-shelf shuffle. Let $M$ be the transition matrix for a single-shelf shuffle. Then, we have $S_{2^{m-1}}=M^m$.
