{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.576808+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5fc03a17d106ac96de9c2587b5b12f79bc1721d4382e156bc9de457a927016be","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2606.14812, 'Joint convergence in Wiener chaos via transport hierarchy and Malliavin covariances'] Let $(X_N=I_p(f_N), N\geq 1)$, where $p\geq 2$ and $f_N\in H^{\odot p}$ 
	for each $N\geq 1$. Assume that $X_N$ satisfies \eqref{c1}. Consider a 
