{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:32:20.721279+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5fcbabb449be26969764cfe35edf8b2054a1bf7f184189da59e16da030d2c97b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2609.00285, 'Multicrossing complex of knot and secant classes'] Let links $L=K_1\cup\cdots\cup K_m$ and $L'$ obtained from $L$ by switching a crossing on components $K_p$ and $K_q$, $1\le p,q\le m$. Then for any $i\ne j\ne k\ne i$
