{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.274911+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5fd01bff94873dd8e9ead52694f4b6cbe828b3d42af5ae171a7ef3a064cc446a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:gtp-quant-clt of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\mathcal{Y},\hat\mathcal{Z},n)$
  with $\mathcal{Y}\subseteq\mathbb{R}$ satisfy Condition~(cond:usa-minimax of the paper).
  Let $\overline V_n = \sum_{t=1}^n \overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}}[Y_t^2 | Y_{1..t-1}]$ and
  $\underline V_n = \sum_{t=1}^n \underline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}}[Y_t^2 | Y_{1..t-1}]$ be real-valued, and let $X_n = \sum_{t=1}^n Y_t$.
  Suppose that for constants $M$, $C$, and $D$ we have

  \begin{equation}

    \max_{t\leq n} |Y_t| \leq n^{-1/2} M \quad \text{g.t.a.s.}~,
  \end{equation}
  and
  \begin{equation}

    \overline{\textsf{\textbf{P}}}\left[ \max(1- \underline V_n, \overline V_n - 1) > 9M^2 D n^{-1/2} (\log n)^2 \right] \leq C n^{-1/4} / (\log n)~.
  \end{equation}
  Then for $n \geq 2$,
  \begin{equation}

    \sup_{-\infty < x < \infty} \max\left( \overline{\textsf{\textbf{P}}}(X_n \leq x) - \Phi(x), \Phi(x) - \underline{\textsf{\textbf{P}}}(X_n \leq x)\right) \leq (2 + C + 7 M D^{1/2}) n^{-1/4} \log n~.
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.686157+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5fd0b1c7e7c4cca21b0502f1f662803a48720c7f782c0a06731dcd7c46162a52","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor degree-times-uniform of arXiv:2510.18856, 'Evolution of recursive trees with limited memory'] Let $\set{\left(\mathscr{E}_{j,k}\right)_{k\geqslant 1}:j\geqslant 0}$ be \emph{iid} copies of $\left(\mathscr{E}_{k-1\leadsto k}\right)_{k\geqslant 1}$ and $T_1$ be an exponential random variable of rate $1$ independent of $\set{\left(\mathscr{E}_{j,k}\right)_{k\geqslant 1}:j\geqslant 0}$. Then 
