{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.471436+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5fdc9c8f5452819cc5db22631a79087e0256b8c2e83a5da7306da92c079de7b9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 32 ({cf.~\cite[Definition 3.1) of arXiv:2609.02561, 'NON-NEF LOCI IN MIXED CHARACTERISTIC'] {LX} and \cite[Chapter~3, Section 4.a]{Nak}}]
Let $f: X \rightarrow S$ be a projective surjective morphism of integral excellent schemes with $X$ normal.
Let $D$ be a $\Q$-Cartier $\Q$-divisor on $X$, and let $\Gamma\subset X$ be a prime divisor on $X$. We define $\ord_{\Gamma}(X/S,\|D\|)$ and $\ord_{\Gamma}(\|D\|,X/S)$ by
\begin{equation*}
\begin{gathered}
\ord_{\Gamma}(X/S,\|D\|) := \inf_{m\in\Z_{>0}} \dfrac{1}{m} \min \left\{ \ord_{\Gamma}D' \middle| mD \sim_{S} D' \geq 0 \right\}, \\
\ord_{\Gamma}(\|D\|,X/S) := \inf_{m\in\Z_{>0}} \dfrac{1}{m} \max \left\{ l \in \Z_{\geq 0} \middle| f_{*}\sO_{X}(mD-l\Gamma) \xrightarrow{\sim} f_{*}\sO_{X}(mD) \right\},
\end{gathered}
\end{equation*}
where $m$ runs through all positive integers such that $mD$ is Cartier.
If there are no positive integers $m$ such that
$\{ D' \mid mD \sim_{S} D' \geq 0 \}\neq\emptyset$, we set $\ord_{\Gamma}(X/S,\|D\|) := +\infty$, and if the maximum in the latter equation does not exist, we set
$\ord_{\Gamma}(\|D\|,X/S):=+\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.339666+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5fe72d1e8a4e15826fae519c4a54c583c21b00d31d81eaf0aebaa7d9accbf5ca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:Bessel_property of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Let $B$ be a ball of radius $\varrho\leq 1/2$. Then, for all $f\in L^2(B;{\mathbb R}^d)$ and $\delta\in (0,1]$, 
