{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:10.029132+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_600650c949a8666f99cde90bfe90a0b9179f79d526b54eadfab21c84baca6ef4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2506.09609, 'Schramm-Loewner evolution contains a topological Sierpi\'nski carpet when $\kappa$ is clos'] The following holds almost surely. For any $w \in [-1/2,1/2]^2$, suppose that the following conditions are satisfied:
