\] 
A mild solution is called unique if any two mild solutions are indistinguishable.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.500023+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_60115237b8514aeb733193579258195a4a78a047d332f72fbdcb3df7d0ab6d7c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro eq:pibar of arXiv:2411.07158, 'Markov chains on trees: almost lower and upper directed cases'] If ${\sf M}$ is the transition of an irreducible random walk on $T$, then the $h$-invariant measure of ${\sf M}$ is $\overline\pi=(\overline\pi_u,u\in T)$ defined by  $\overline{\pi}(\varnothing)=1$, and for $u\in T$,
\begin{eqnarray}
\overline{\pi}_u=\overline{\pi}(\varnothing)\prod_{j=1}^h\frac{ M_{u[j-1],u[j]}}{ M_{u[j],u[j-1]}},~~\textrm{ for } u\in T.
\end{eqnarray}
Therefore, ${\sf M}$ is positive recurrent, if and only if $\sum_{u \in T} \overline{\pi}_u<+\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.824108+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6017e239de3975f95bce84bc3eee82e5a9575611513cd644324e08d8ef663654","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2604.10244, 'Ergodicity for regime-switching neutral stochastic functional differential equations with '] Suppose that assumptions of Proposition  \ref{Pro:0929}  hold. Then there exist constants $C,\lambda>0$  such that for any   $\xi$, $\eta \in  C_r$,  $i \in \mbb S $, and  $t\geq 0 $,
