{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:38:37.405627+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_603945d9fbd1bdd72d24987aa6f5c7226e9a13d1b549226d5657020479a8721e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2605.15781, 'Mean-Field Backward Stochastic Differential Equations with Nonlinear Resistance and Double'] Let $s\in C[0,T]$,  and $l,r:[0,T] \times \mathbb{R}\rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ be two functions with $l\leq r$.  A pair of functions $(x,K)\in C[0,T]\times BV[0,T]$ is called a solution to the  Skorokhod problem for $s$ with nonlinear constraints $l,r$ ($(x,K)=\mathbb{SP}_l^r(s)$ for short) if 
\begin{itemize}
\item[(i)] $x_t=s_t+K_t$;
\item[(ii)] $l(t,x_t)\leq 0\leq r(t,x_t)$;
\item[(iii)]  $K_{0-}=0$ and $K$ has the decomposition $K=K^r-K^l$, where $K^r,K^l$ are nondecreasing functions satisfying  
\begin{align}
\int_0^{T} I_{\{l(s,x_s)<0\}}dK^l_s=0, \  \int_0^{T} I_{\{r(s,x_s)>0\}}dK^r_s=0.
\end{align}
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.360791+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_603c9644280e3bc1b3cde4bb0da7059a3904c0e639bd50fa749f7307b9fa3eab","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 41 of arXiv:2511.09517, 'From Cannings model to Brownian motion conditioned on local time profile'] For any $\delta>0$, $n\ge 1$ and $h_*+\frac{n}{(\log n)^{1+\frac{\varepsilon}{8}}}\le s \le h^*$, we have on the event $(\Xi_n)^{\rm c}\cap \Big\{T^{(r)}_{\lfloor (\log n)^{1+\frac{\varepsilon}{2}} \rfloor}(s) < s^{\downarrow} \Big\}$,
\begin{align}
    X^{(r)}_s - X^{(r)}_{s^{\downarrow}} \ge \frac{2}{(\log n)^{\frac\varepsilon{12}}}\sum_{j=s^{\downarrow}+1}^{s} \widetilde N_j.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.299281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_603d0970ebfc6a022f611c74bf4058f6eaa5d538dbdb96e2a7c8fd1d74186153","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 8 (High-noise decay of the smoothed likelihood force) of arXiv:2608.21709, 'Posterior Information Dynamics of Diffusion Models for Linear Inverse Problems'] Under the assumptions of Lemma~\ref{thm:posterior-tweedie}, the force
\(g_t\) satisfies, under the joint law of \((X_t,R)\),
\begin{equation}

\E\|g_t(X_t,R)\|^2
=
\frac{a_t^2}{\Delta_t^2}
\E\big\|\E[X_0\mid X_t,R]-\E[X_0\mid X_t]\big\|^2.
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}

\E\|g_t(X_t,R)\|^2
\le
