{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:57:51.766907+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_604f37a3091ee788687929a4ba928864d79b842e8003fbb8b1058f4630347192","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2608.30223, 'Fairness in Multi-class Multi-group Classification Problems via Contextual Coherent Risk M'] Let  $\rho_{i,s} [\cdot]$ be coherent measures of risk for  all  $i\in\Jc$ and all $s\in\mathcal{S}$, 
