{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.123698+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6097497e1e4392a4726aeeb0232347c83ab650201966faf496dea1117175f25b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:spine-shifted-convolution of arXiv:2607.15966, 'Canonical Mandelbrot Cascades on Curves Are Rajchman'] Let \((a_k)_{k\geq1}\) be a nonnegative sequence such that \(a_k\to0\) as \(k\to\infty\).  
