{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.315666+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_60c385af3b28d771b37c1c70b2e0aa1ce7d5fbdaa79a861901a16212ab1f93f8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem3.4 of arXiv:2411.06089, '{\Large \bf Averaging principle for semilinear slow-fast rough partial differential equati'] For any given $x,x_1,x_2,y\in \mathcal{H}$, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that
