{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.455191+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_60d2c9394dfe87442b847be42e58496c349b304a8fb52c36e20036c07a80ef4a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro 2 (Supercritical persistence of regularity) of arXiv:2609.02523, '\bf Strong Ill-Posedness in critical and subcritical regimes for the Hunter--Saxton equati'] Let $s>\nicefrac{3}{2}$ and $u_0$ be a given initial datum in $ L^\infty \cap \dot H^1 \cap \dot H^s(\R)$.  
