{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.384332+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_60eaffe83fae2d2022296aee584fc73a867f970900709fb296c322ce4cc6d4b5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:PPP.clusters of arXiv:2411.02046, 'Speed of Convergence and Moderate Deviations of FPP on Random Geometric Graphs'] Let $d \geq 2$ and $r>r_c$. Then, there exist $C,c>0$ such that, for each $t>0$,
