{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:08.990707+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_613d68997cda980658c455e4e8c27af847ddf601d1bd94e63725de2b2628f9f4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def_whiteNoiseMeasure of arXiv:2608.17463, 'Persistence probabilities of fractional L\'evy fields indexed by hyperbolic space and othe'] Let $(E, \mathcal{E}, \nu)$ be a measure space and let $\mathcal{E}_\nu$ denote all sets in $\mathcal{E}$ with finite $\nu$-measure. A random field $\mathcal{W}:\mathcal{E}_\nu\to\mathbb{R}$, such that for any $A,B\in\mathcal{E}_\nu$ we have
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\mathcal{W}(A)\sim\mathcal{N}(0, \nu(A))$,
        \item $\mathcal{W}(A \cup B) = \mathcal{W}(A) + \mathcal{W}(B) - \mathcal{W}(A\cap B)$ almost surely,
        \item $A\cap B = \emptyset$ implies that $\mathcal{W}(A)$ and $\mathcal{W}(B)$ are independent,
    \end{enumerate}
    is called Gaussian white noise with control measure $\nu$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:53:39.146270+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_613f40af4453427732d4eac1497ffe0094cedc1ecb0df81e8ea10b1ed2cd7b9a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 8 of arXiv:2608.26953, '2608.26953'] A \emph{first-order differential calculus} (FODC) \((\Omega^1_A,d)\) on \(A\) consists of an \(A\)\nobreakdash–\(A\)-bimodule \(\Omega_A^1\) together with a \(\Bbbk\)-linear \emph{exterior derivative}
\( d\colon A \rightarrow \Omega^1_A\), satisfying the \emph{Leibniz rule}
\[d(fg)=(df)g + f(dg),
\quad \forall f,g\in A,\] and the \emph{surjectivity condition}, which states that \(\Omega_A^1\) is spanned by elements of the form \( f dg\), for \(f,g\in A\). A \emph{morphism of first-order differential calculi}
\((A, \Omega^1_A,d_A)
\rightarrow
(B, \Omega^1_B,d_B)\)
is given by an algebra morphism \(\varphi\colon A\rightarrow B\) together with an \(A\)\nobreakdash–\(A\)-bimodule map \( \varphi^* : \Omega^1_A \rightarrow\Omega^1_B\)
such that \(\varphi^* \circ d_A= d_B \circ \varphi.\) Here \(\Omega^1_B\) is seen as an \(A\)\nobreakdash–\(A\)-bimodule via \(\varphi\). Additionally, a FODC \(\Omega^1_A\) is called \emph{inner} if there exists an element \(\theta\in\Omega^1_A\) such that
\(d a  =  [\theta,a] = \theta a - a\theta, 
\text{ for any }a \in A\). It is called \emph{connected} if
\(\ker(d) = \Bbbk\cdot 1_A\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.617640+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6145fd39f83b121d573cfcaab0192af44a8d2561678cb796edebe7c70d4b59c2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 29 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Fix any $\sigma \in(0,1/10)$ and let~$X_0,X_1,\dots$ be a random walk with step distribution~$\NN(0,1/2)$. For each~$\epsilon\in(0,1)$ and each $\delta\in(0,1)$ there exists~$a_0=a_0(\epsilon,\delta)\ge1$ 
such that for all $a\ge a_0$, all naturals $k\ge2$ and all reals~$r,u$ satisfying
\begin{equation}

r,u\ge a^{1/\sigma}\quad\text{\rm and}\quad ru\le k^{1-\delta}
\end{equation}
and all~$\gamma\colon\{0, \dots,k\}\to\R$ obeying
\begin{equation}

\bigl|\gamma(i)\bigr|\le a+\bigr(\min\{i,k-i\}\bigr)^{\sigma},\quad i=0,\dots,k, 
\end{equation}
we have
\begin{equation}

(1-\epsilon)\frac{4ru}k\le
E\biggl(\,\prod_{j=1}^{k-1}1_{\{X_j\ge\gamma(j)\}}\,\bigg|\, X_0=r,\,X_k=u\biggr)\le(1+\epsilon)\frac{4ru}k.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.091569+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6148fca6eab07221c1c7d9cc205001fbd8e2ce87da7dd27a0aa2e18e7f2aa92a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def1 definition:debut of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] A point $u \in \mathcal{T}_{H(\upvarrho)}$ is called an excursion debut for $(\widehat{\omega}_a)_{ a\in \mathcal{T}_{H(\upvarrho)}}$ if the following properties hold: 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[\emph{(i)}] We have  $\widehat{\omega}_u = x$;
        \item[\emph{(ii)}] We can find $v \succeq u$ such that $\widehat{\omega}_a\neq x$ for every $a$ in  $\rrbracket u,v \llbracket$. 
    \end{enumerate}
    We denote the collection of excursion  debuts by $\mathcal{D}(\upvarrho, \omega)$. For every $u \in \mathcal{D}(\upvarrho, \omega)$,  we write  $\mathcal{C}_u(\upvarrho, \omega)$ for the subset of points $v \in \mathcal{T}_{H(\upvarrho)}$ fulfilling that $v \succeq u$ with  $\widehat{\omega}_a \neq x$ for every $a \in \, \rrbracket u,v \llbracket$ and we set
\begin{equation*}
    \mathcal{C}^\circ_u(\upvarrho, \omega) := \mathcal{C}_u(\upvarrho, \omega) \cap \{ a \in \mathcal{T}_{ H(\upvarrho) } : \widehat{\omega}_a \neq x \}. 
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.621994+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_614c515e71cb83107bd8745e0344b2f19a898416702356b5e6db3710dd22ddde","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 (Stable convergence of \(Z^n\)) of arXiv:2608.16256, 'Error Distribution of the Local Linearization Method for Stochastic Differential Equations'] \label[proposition]{prop:ll_forcing_stable_limit_new}
