{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.319672+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61912438809e5e61f36f9ef24075a361c0d1a81bd5cb49771fd429d3de264654","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $S\subset T$ be a cleft and let ${\mathcal{C}}_1,{\mathcal{C}}_2,{\mathcal{D}}$ be $S$-cocomplete $T$-$\infty$-categories. A functor ${\mathcal{C}}_1\times{\mathcal{C}}_2\to{\mathcal{D}}$ is called \emph{$S$-cocontinuous in each variable} or \emph{$S$-bilinear} if for every $A\in T$ and $X_1\in{\mathcal{C}}_1(A), X_2\in{\mathcal{C}}_2(A)$ the two composites
    \begin{align*}
        \{X_1\}\times\pi_A^*{\mathcal{C}}_2&\lhook\joinrel\longrightarrow \pi_A^*{\mathcal{C}}_1\times\pi_A^*{\mathcal{C}}_2\xrightarrow{\;\pi_A^*F\;}\pi_A^*{\mathcal{D}}\\
        \pi_A^*{\mathcal{C}}_1\times\{X_2\}&\lhook\joinrel\longrightarrow\pi_A^*{\mathcal{C}}_1\times\pi_A^*{\mathcal{C}}_2\xrightarrow{\;\pi_A^*F\;}\pi_A^*{\mathcal{D}}
    \end{align*}
    preserve $(T_{/A}\times_TS)$-colimits in the usual sense. Analogously, we define what it means for ${\mathcal{C}}_1\times\cdots\times{\mathcal{C}}_n\to{\mathcal{D}}$ to be $S$-cocontinuous in each variable (\emph{$S$-multilinear}).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.349294+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61973c30bc8276f884c2efba9b0558b90009fb9771936a20b645176a104a6ea5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2506.15159, 'Conditional central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] There exists a constant $c > 0$ such that for sufficiently large $n$, for any $f\in Lip(v)$
