{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.463949+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6198b3d8f37be0404abae6ac8bc8c5a0839a1520ee0bdad02364f43c1017166c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:tau_analytics of arXiv:2603.28578, 'Exponential Bounds and Analyticity for the Tree Builder Random Walk'] Let $B_n \in \mathcal{F}_n$, then there exists $A_n \in \mathcal{F}_n$, such that
