{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.122756+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_619a1165f749bd666d7fb9c33e36f740b1d075e5ab6c9e76ff0760c25285a14a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition d:cdm of arXiv:2510.00748, '\bf On irreducible central limit theorems'] {\rm Let $\{V_n\}_{n\ge 1}$ be sets with $|V_n| \to \infty$. Fix an integer $d\geq 2$, as well as a real number $\alpha\in (0,d]$. We consider subsets $$ J_n\subseteq \underbrace{ \, V_n\times \cdots \times V_n \, }_\text{$d$ times}, \quad n\geq 1,$$ (each $J_n$ is not necessarily symmetric and has possibly diagonal components) and say that the sequence $\{J_n\}$ has \emph{combinatorial dimension} equal to $\alpha$ if there exist finite constants $0<c'\leq c$ such that the following two properties are verified for $n$ sufficiently large: 
\begin{itemize}
    \item for all $A_1,...,A_d\subseteq V_n$,
\begin{equation}
| J_n \cap (A_1\times \cdots \times A_d)| \leq c \, \max_{i=1,...,d} |A_i|^\alpha\,;
\end{equation}
\item moreover, 
\begin{equation}
| J_n | \geq c' \, |V_n |^\alpha\,, \quad n\geq 1.
\end{equation}

\end{itemize}
}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.600638+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_619b391eeb4592ed9f00bbb2bdf150e378162393f1afc8131eb18122592fa5d3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def:local of arXiv:2606.21049, '\textsc{Locality of rough path lifts}'] Let $\mathbb{A}$ be an area process on $P\subset C^\gamma \times C^\gamma$.
We will say that $\mathbb{A}$ is \emph{local} if for $Z, Z' \in P$ and any $(s,t) \in \triangle$, one has the implication
\begin{equation*}
Z_{s,[s,t]} = Z'_{s,[s,t]} \implies \mathbb{A}_{s,t}(Z) = \mathbb{A}_{s,t}(Z') \;.
