{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.502265+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61ae141d8f0bcbc0d74cfcdd525befeec02c69664efc17ff1ffb9880a98e5a98","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 47 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $(Y,Y'), (Z,Z') \in \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],W)$ and $f \in C_b^{2\alpha,3}([0,T] \times W, \bar{W})$ be arbitrary. Then we have
\begin{align*}
\interleave (f(Y),f(Y)')-(f(Z),f(Z)') \interleave_{X,2\alpha} &\leq C \big( 1 + | Y,Y' |_{X,2\alpha}^2 + | Z,Z' |_{X,2\alpha}^2 \big)
\\ &\quad \interleave (Y,Y') - (Z,Z') \interleave_{X,2\alpha},
\end{align*}
where the constant $C > 0$ depends on $\alpha$, $T$, $X$ and $\| f \|_{C_b^{2 \alpha,3}}$. Moreover, for $T \leq 1$ the constant $C$ does not depend on $T$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.315001+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61b1536b8dbce43a395445197dbd9076b66397ecb8468cfe8d097ed39e257e92","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem giant-is-unique of arXiv:2606.01627, 'The geometry of the giant component of random geometric graphs'] Let $\lambda_0 > \lambda_c$.  Then there are constants $C = C(\lambda_0,M) > 0, c = c(\lambda_0,M) > 0$ so that for all $\lambda \geq \lambda_0$ and $r\phi \leq  c$ we have \begin{equation*}
            \mathbb{P}\left(
