{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.932929+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61ec0604f56991b9319694a3d816e28b6aa5ffdbf3fe153f5ffbd165754bff59","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition See {\cite[Definition 5.4.1 of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] {3Ddimers}}]
    Let $R\subset \mathbb{R}^d$ be a compact region with piecewise smooth boundary $\partial R$. We define the \textit{boundary value operator} $T:(\text{AF}^\infty(\Lambda,R),d_W)\to (\mathcal{M}^s(\mathbb{R}^d),\mathbb{W}_1^{1,1})$ by 
