{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.757696+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61f233fb8018d4a02ff746365c019a1cb8b2894bd5ade26b421394c02247f527","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:green-kernel-regularity-package of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] There exists a constant
$C_D\ge1$ such that
\begin{equation}
 0\le G_D(z,w)
 \le C_D+\log^+\frac1{|z-w|},
 \qquad z,w\in D.
\end{equation}
Away from the diagonal, the Green kernel is locally uniformly continuous in
its first variable.  More precisely, for every compact $K\Subset D$ and every
$r_\ast>0$,
\begin{equation}
 \begin{aligned}
 \omega_{K,r_\ast}(\delta)
 &:=\sup_{\substack{z,z'\in K,\ |z-z'|\le\delta\\
                    w\in D,\ |z-w|\ge r_\ast,\ |z'-w|\ge r_\ast}}
    |G_D(z,w)-G_D(z',w)|,
    \qquad \delta>0,\\
 \omega_{K,r_\ast}(\delta)
 &\xrightarrow[\delta\downarrow0]{}0.
