{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.431026+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61fc107c1046f19a2528bdbb79c1af17cbcb48f632f9c5244191b7d04409f620","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:restricted-FG-barycenters of arXiv:2604.22453, 'Adapted Wasserstein Barycenters of Gaussian Processes'] The restricted problem
\[
\inf_{\mathbb{Y}\in\mathcal{FG}(T,d)}\sum_{k=1}^K\lambda_k\mathcal{AW}_2^2(\mathbb{X}^k,\mathbb{Y})
\]
admits a minimizer, and its value is (equation eq:restricted.value of the paper).  Moreover, \(\mathbb{G}^{
\accentset{\overline{\hphantom{a}}}{a}
,
\accentset{\overline{\hphantom{L}}}{L}
}\in\mathcal{FG}(T,d)\) is a restricted minimizer if and only if, for every \(t\in[T]\), there exist \( Q_t^1,\ldots,Q_t^K\in\mathscr O(d)\) such that
\begin{equation}

\accentset{\overline{\hphantom{L}}}{L}
_{\cdot,t}=\sum_{k=1}^K\lambda_kL_{\cdot,t}^k Q_t^k
\end{equation}
and the common-noise matrix
\begin{equation}

\mathbf P_t^{k,\ell}= Q_t^k( Q_t^\ell)^\intercal,
