{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.700562+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62245600834837fd013768bde4b07a720769c78df85fd2b43559b75a68290e04","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem asympdisc of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] If $\gamma > 0$ is chosen small enough then, for any $\eta > 0$ small enough (depending only~on~$\gamma$) we have that, for all $k$ sufficiently large and $T \in [2k,{\rm e}^{\frac{1}{2}k^\gamma}]$, 
