{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.194018+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62f465b56ab7c95125081e727903094608e48a4bb07d3f5fd8d47e59d228492f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 27 of arXiv:2606.31455, 'Discrete time-multidimensional renewal theory and applications'] For $a,b:I_N\to\mathbb{C}$, their circular convolution $a*_N b:I_N\to\mathbb{C}$ is

