{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.534079+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62f67168861b39f308a295b6b913cfe0cb43c0ddba8b4cb2b032f7158bae16fa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.decom_DF of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] Let $v_{m}$ defined in (equation eq.harmonicBC of the paper) follow the canonical grain extension (equation eq.def_extension_plan of the paper) on ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m$, then for every $F \subseteq E_d({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m)$ we have
