 \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.863272+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62fb33e10ba2278028c8b63c446e11c5922d788dc2091b0b35b6040076a0b0df","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $a_0,a_1,b_0,b_1>0$ be positive numbers and let $\delta \in (0,1)$. Assume that there is some $0<c\le 1\le C<\infty$ such that
    \begin{align*}
        c\le \frac{a_0}{b_0}\le C \text{ and } c\le \frac{a_1}{b_1}\le C.
    \end{align*}
    Then it follows that
    \begin{align*}
        \Bigl|\frac{\sqrt{a_0+\delta}}{\sqrt{b_0+\delta}}-\frac{\sqrt{a_1+\delta}}{\sqrt{b_1+\delta}}\Bigr|\lesssim \frac1\delta \Bigl(|a_0-a_1|+|b_0-b_1|\Bigr).
    \end{align*}
    Furthermore, it holds that
    \begin{align*}
        \Bigl|\frac{\sqrt{a_0+\delta}}{\sqrt{b_0+\delta}}-\frac{\sqrt{a_1+\delta}}{\sqrt{b_1+\delta}}\Bigr|^2 
        \le
        \frac{\sqrt{C}}{\sqrt{c}}\Bigl|\frac{{a_0+\delta}}{{b_0+\delta}}-\frac{{a_1+\delta}}{{b_1+\delta}}\Bigr|.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.872086+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62ff899970791e8658044f1418a8df379f3087aa3074e2a2fa6363f50cf4d63a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main of arXiv:2411.00629, '\Large Transformation of Stochastic Recursions and Critical Phenomena in the Analysis of t'] Let $\alpha>1$ and define $R_\alpha\subset \mathbb{R}$ by
\begin{equation}
R_\alpha=\left[0, \, \max \left\{1,  \frac{2\alpha-1}{4}-\frac{6\alpha^2-15\alpha+4}{4(\alpha-1)(2\alpha-1)}\right\}\right)\cup\{1\}. 
\end{equation}
Then, for any $u_0\in R_\alpha$ and $\lambda>0$, there exists a solution $u_\lambda$ to (equation diffalpha-ricc of the paper) such that
\begin{equation}
