{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.363772+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63000eb8f0ab559e9023ef9f5268684d597d3bd9941afc62520124d985dbada0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop-well-posedness-approx of arXiv:2507.09922, 'A scaling limit for Vlasov equations with electrostatic fluctuations'] Assume that $f^\delta_0\in C_c^\infty (\mathbb{T}^3\times \mathbb{R}^3, \mathbb{R}_+)$. Then for any $\delta>0$, the approximate equation (equation stoch-Vlasov-approx of the paper) admits a unique probabilistically strong solution $f^\delta$, represented as
