{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.759694+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_630bd96c2d778944225a11ce8658cf6482f7ec3c38ffb126c5c0da07a4c46ec7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2608.17493, 'Integrals of some compound processes'] Let $X$ be a stochastic process on $\mathcal{D}[0,T]$ such that $X(0) =0$ a.s.
	. Let $I(t) = \int_0^t X(s)\dif s,\ 0\le t\le T$, and $0\le t_1<t_2\le T, \ \gamma \in\mathbb{R}$.
	\begin{itemize}
		\item[($i$)] If $X$ has independent increments,
		\begin{equation}
			\mathbb{E}e^{i\gamma \big(I(t_2)-I(t_1)\big)} = \mathbb{E}e^{i\gamma (t_2-t_1)X(t_1)}\mathbb{E}e^{i\gamma \int_0^{t_2-t_1} \big(X(s+t_1)-X(t_1)\big)\dif s}.
		\end{equation}
		\item[($ii$)] If $X$ has independent and stationary increments,
		\begin{equation}
			\mathbb{E}e^{i\gamma \big(I(t_2)-I(t_1)\big)} = \mathbb{E}e^{i\gamma (t_2-t_1)X(t_1)}\mathbb{E}e^{i\gamma I(t_2-t_1)}.
		\end{equation}
	\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.211922+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_630e3d6bb58998dfdf7ae42d77d64e20d260773a3dd2689b5219b3a3e36601b1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma constantcomparison of arXiv:2512.06640, 'Existence and sharpness of the phase transition for the frog model on transitive graphs'] Fix a transitive directed graph $\vec{G}$ with outer degree $\Delta$. For any $\lambda, t > 0$, there exists a positive and finite constant $C(\Delta,\lambda,t)$ such that
