{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.778319+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63237f1068c759f57b061b4b622039e801f6112cc3b621200234526ec7261014","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro 5.2 of arXiv:2608.00420, '{Weighted $L^p$ solutions of scalar BSDEs with general unbounded stochastic coefficients}\'] Let $(h_t)_{t\in[0,\tau]}$ be an $(\mathcal{F}_t)$-progressively measurable nonnegative real-valued process satisfying $\int_0^\tau h_t {\rm d}t\leq C_1$ and let the generator $g$ satisfy that
