{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.768565+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6328aa9d67f0b6043ecb8aad48e531a3c6771148b7c9b539d49ff5431f232ffc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2609.02225, '\textbf{The direct moving plane method for weak solutions of the fractional $p$-Laplacian}'] Let \(a,b,\alpha>0\). Then there exists \(c=c(a,b,\alpha)>0\) such that, for every \(d>0\) and \(t\ge0\),
