\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:24:20.646345+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6393a1ad227d171e12e3ad7bdaa005d82f5092e4d91141251a76e88a575ee03a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:master-scalar-projections of arXiv:2608.11084, 'Sharp Frobenius-Norm Concentration for Sample Moment Tensors'] Let \(X_1,\ldots,X_N\) be i.i.d. copies of a centered sub-Gaussian random
vector \(X\in\mathbb R^d\) with covariance matrix \(\Sigma\) and
sub-Gaussian constant \(K\). Let \(p\ge2\) be an integer. Then, for every
\(q\ge1\),
\begin{align}
\sup_{\|A\|_{\mathsf F}\le1}\bigg\|
\sum_{i=1}^N
\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\langle
A,X_i^{\otimes p}-\mathbbm{E} X^{\otimes p}
\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\rangle_{\mathsf F}
\bigg\|_{L_q}
\lesssim_p K^p
\begin{cases}
\rho_p(\Sigma)\sqrt{N(q\land N)}
+
\|\Sigma\|^{p/2}q^{p/2},
& p \text{ even},\\[3pt]
\rho_p(\Sigma)\sqrt{Nq}
+
\|\Sigma\|^{p/2}q^{p/2},
& p \text{ odd},
\end{cases}

\end{align}
where \(\rho_p(\Sigma)\) is as in Theorem~(thm:main1 of the paper). Moreover, if \(X\) is Gaussian, then
\begin{align}
\sup_{\|A\|_{\mathsf F}\le1}\bigg\|
\sum_{i=1}^N
\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\langle
A,X_i^{\otimes p}-\mathbbm{E} X^{\otimes p}
\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\rangle_{\mathsf F}
\bigg\|_{L_q}
\asymp_p
\begin{cases}
\rho_{p,G}(\Sigma)\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft(\sqrt{Nq}+q\aftergroup\egroup\originalright)
+
\|\Sigma\|^{p/2}q^{p/2},
& p \text{ even},\\[3pt]
\rho_{p,G}(\Sigma)\sqrt{Nq}
+
\|\Sigma\|^{p/2}q^{p/2},
& p \text{ odd},
\end{cases}

\end{align}
where \(\rho_{p,G}(\Sigma)\) is as in Theorem~(thm:main1 of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.116007+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_639468c3a81c9c6d4a259d0c3a1c1531c37f560be2ebbe408a0a50f8223d5e7b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn of arXiv:2608.16170, '\bf On hitting time distributions of Markov processes with sub-Gaussian heat kernel bounds'] On ${\mathbb{R}}^d$ ($d\ge 3$),  we say a function $h: {\mathbb{R}}^d\rightarrow {\mathbb{R}}$ is in Kato class $\mathbf{K}_{d,k}$ (for $k=1,2$) if
\begin{equation*}
\lim_{r\downarrow 0}\sup_{x\in {\mathbb{R}}^n} \int_{|x-y|<r} \frac{\left|h(y)\right|}{|x-y|^{d-k}}dy=0.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.645664+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6398878165237e528dcf40028a14bf94867441b1fabf439c768f910b1273c0c1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn Two-valued sets of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $a,b\in \mathbb R$ and let $u$ be a harmonic function in $D$. Let $\phi$ be a GFF with boundary condition $u$ in $D$.  We say that a random closed set $\mathds A_{-a,b}^u$ is a two-valued set with boundary condition $u$ if
\begin{itemize}
    \item $(\phi,\mathds A_{-a,b}^u)$ is a local set,
    \item there exists a random function $h_{\mathds A_{-a,b}^u}$ such that 
    \[
        (\phi_{\mathds A_{-a,b}^u},f)=\int_{D\backslash \mathds A_{-a,b}^u} h_{\mathds A_{-a,b}^u}(z) f(z)dz
        \quad \text{a.s.}
    \]
    for all $f \in C_c^\infty(D)$,
    \item the function $h_{\mathds A_{-a,b}^u}-u$ takes values in the set $\{-a,b\}$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.411088+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_639b5bbb95e633995be8ae19e363d0f0dc61358cf9b0ba1f321550945ad314cf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Radial Lemma of arXiv:2608.27248, 'Optimal Transport and the ABP Method in Higher Codimension'] The function $F_B$ belongs to $\mathrm{BV}_{\mathrm{loc}}(0,\infty)$ and
