{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.733183+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_639c405df55c5e404853be6db0b868b0477b1f433dc22a3a80159013ae6c56e3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pr:hf_compactness of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Let $(W,d_W)$ be a compact metric space. Suppose that $\mathcal {K}^W$ is a collection of non-empty compact subsets $K \subseteq W$ each equipped with a continuous function $f\colon K \to Y$. Suppose that
 \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
  \item There exist $0_Y \in Y$ and $M \in (0,\infty)$ such that $\sup_{x \in K} d_Y(f(x),0_Y) \leq M$ for all $(K,f) \in \mathcal {K}^W$.
  \item For every $\varepsilon > 0$ there exists $\delta > 0$ so that $d(x,y) < \delta$ implies $d_Y(f(x),f(y)) < \varepsilon$ for all $(K,f) \in \mathcal {K}^W$.
 \end{enumerate}
 Then $\mathcal {K}^W$ is relatively compact with respect to the metric $d_\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.268417+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63a16b85de28d52147b916bc5747ce7e9718a96bb006f2785e82d43d7f0291ae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma cor:cheeky_zeta_K_min_T_K of arXiv:2507.12601, 'Multi-type logistic branching processes with selection: frequency process and genealogy fo'] There exists a coupling and a deterministic sequence of times $\zeta_K\to +\infty$ such that for any $\beta\in (0,1)$ $u\in \mathfrak{T}$,
