{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.778597+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63ce1ed36b18abb1e8bacccfaa52a7318adce4abaa4c349dab9b1e74d909f218","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 (Uniform height-dependent survival) of arXiv:2609.02257, 'Aperiodic random walks: uniform estimates, local limits and invariance principles'] There is a constant \(C>0\) such that, for all sufficiently large \(N\)
