{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.086242+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64142e595236fdca06e7e51fdf30341f09afacde6d3eb9f2d1d135a57ca1c110","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-Jordan of arXiv:2411.12623, 'Random signed measures'] Let $\xi$ be a random signed measure. Then, there exists two unique random measures $\xi_+$ and $\xi_-$ such that for every $\omega\in\Omega$ and every $B\in\hat{\mathcal{S}}$
