{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.304404+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64360e1010ad2608d8954eaf4837661772133f499b9c7d22c0f6ce9a78ce7155","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition CRP of arXiv:2411.06089, '{\Large \bf Averaging principle for semilinear slow-fast rough partial differential equati'] {\rm (Controlled Rough Path)}
Let $\mathbf X=(X,X^2) \in \mathscr{C}^\gamma ([0,T]; \mathbb R^d)$ for $\gamma \in (1/3,1/2]$.
We call a pair $(Y, Y')$ a controlled rough path,
if $(Y, Y') \in \hat{C}^\gamma ([0,T];\mathcal{H}_\alpha) \times \hat{C}^\gamma ([0,T]; \mathcal{H}_\alpha^d)$ for some $\alpha \in \mathbb R$
and the remainder term $R^Y$ defined by
	\begin{equation}
		R_{t,s}^Y=\hat \delta Y_{t,s}-S_{t-s}Y_s' \delta X_{t,s} ,
	\end{equation}
belongs to $C_2^{2\gamma} ([0,T];\mathcal{H}_\alpha)$,
where the component $Y'$ is the Gubinelli derivative of $Y$.
We denote by $\mathscr D_{S, \mathbf X}^{2\gamma} ([0,T]; \mathcal{H}_\alpha )$ the space of all controlled rough paths that are controlled by $\mathbf X$ according to the semigroup $S$.
Define a seminorm on this space by
\begin{equation*}
\|Y,Y'\|_{X, 2\gamma, \alpha}
	=\|Y'\|_{\gamma,\alpha}+|R^Y|_{2\gamma, \alpha},
\end{equation*}
and its norm is given by
\begin{equation*}
\|Y,Y'\|_{\mathscr D_{S, \mathbf X}^{2\gamma}}=
	\|Y_0\|_{ \mathcal{H}_\alpha}
	+ \|Y_0'\|_{\mathcal{H}_\alpha^d} +\|Y,Y'\|_{X, 2\gamma, \alpha}.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.499939+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_643646b721128e2fc81bf7d01e166f9128e9c7f3dd2b6c1bed449da6f4d26df8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2605.30030, 'Critical exponents for planar random-cluster model with cluster-weight~$q=4$'] For the critical random-cluster model on~$\mathbb Z^2$ with cluster-weight~$q=4$, as~$N$ tends to $\infty$, 
