{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.859968+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_643cb9e3d820cc07f5b0406132c3e3466bc9d4ff14ccb728d5ac852d078fa62c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 14 of arXiv:2608.21090, 'Ornstein--Uhlenbeck process conditioned to have restricted $L_2$-norm'] Let $x\in\R$, $t_0>0$ and take $h$ as defined in Lemma \ref{lem:ratiouniformasymptotics}. Assume there is a $K>0$ and $\beta\in(0,1/2)$ such that for the sequence $y_T$ we have $|y_T-\theta T|\leq K T^\beta$. Then, for any Borel-measurable $D\subset\CC([0,t_0])$, we have
