{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:08.025445+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64a41cc08b2f37ea48196426856e34f48d44bddd2473bfb6e49f918eca5bc5d9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:linearization-well-behaved-vert of arXiv:2608.12415, 'Sharp Phase Transition for Ellipsoid Fitting'] Let $\tau_I$ be a well-behaved intersection in the sense of (def:well-behaved-intersection-vertical of the paper); we define its linearized shapes as follows:
