{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.895330+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64a9528b7f9d4749fe41fd8ca1a56045aa0f098da31b55aeb9de8744dc1ce6bb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop u_R_L_x^2_priori_esti of arXiv:2606.31155, 'The well-posedness of stochastic Korteweg--de Vries equations revisited'] Assume $u_0\in L_x^2$ and $ k\in L_x^\infty L_y^2$. For any fixed $ R,T>0$, let $u_R$ be the solution constructed in Proposition (localwellres of the paper). Then for any stopping time $0\leq \sigma\leq \sigma_R^T(u_R)$ almost surely, we have
