{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:36.154348+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64b0a1e835a94db42a3ad863416ad0d95e4aa9b6275e7d3cc631b76c32b4ee17","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 (Inverse-sine envelope) of arXiv:2609.01570, 'A Proof of Fraenkel's Conjecture'] For integers \(Q\ge2\) and \(d\) with \(1\le d\le Q/2\), put
\(C_0=2\pi-4\).  Then
\begin{equation}
 \frac1d\le K_Q(d)
 <\frac1d+C_0\frac d{Q^2}
