{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:33:06.538943+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64d28a7c470a61455deea4081e021bc659b8af1e8a9682c63f016bd92d29993c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 7 of arXiv:2608.25829, 'Topology of low-dimensional generalized Ricci solitons and string backgrounds'] Let $(M^n, g, H, f)$ be a compact GRS.  Then $Y_{[g]} \geq 0$, with equality if and only if the soliton is trivial.
\begin{proof} Choose a Yamabe minimizer $u$.  Then we obtain
\begin{align*}
    \brs{\brs{u}}_{L^{2n/n-2}}^2 Y_{[g]} =&\ \int_M \left( R_g u^2 + 4 \frac{n-1}{n-2} \brs{\N u}^2 \right)\\
    \geq&\ \int_M \left( R_g u^2 + 4 \brs{\N u}^2 \right)\\
    =&\ \mathcal F(g, H, -2 \ln u)\\
    \geq&\ \gl(g, H) \brs{\brs{u}}_{L^2}^2.
\end{align*}
Both claims now follow immediately from Lemma \ref{l:lambdasign}.
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.677644+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64d50e544c1d596de42839340a445607270ba76b552a0cbf4612b796d9bcf368","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:sum of arXiv:2411.12149, 'Airy limit for $\beta$-additions through Dunkl operators'] Let $\mu_A$ and $\mu_B$ be exponentially decaying measures on $W_N$. Define $\mu_C:= \mu_A \boxplus_{N}^{\beta} \mu_B$ (also written as $C=A\boxplus_{N}^{\beta}B$) to be the measure whose Bessel generating function is given by
\begin{equation}
G_N (x_1,\ldots,x_N;\beta,\mu_C) = G_N(x_1,\ldots,x_N;\beta,\mu_A)G_N(x_1,\ldots,x_N;\beta,\mu_B).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:13:21.258428+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64d668062d5d6fc364171e0336120b1781d97609a6287c77f7bb13c10daaa4da","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 of arXiv:2609.01473, 'Keller sequences of exact $\infty$-categories'] Suppose that the localisation $p^l\colon \cal{C} \to \cal{B}^l$ sends cocartesian squares in $\cal{C}$ with parallel maps inclusions to cocartesian squares in $\cal{B}^l$.
If $f\colon x \to y$ in $\cal{B}^l$ is the image of some inclusion in $\cal{C}$ then for every $\tilde x\in \cal{C}$ lifting $x$ we can lift $f$ to an inclusion $\tilde f\colon \tilde x \mono \tilde y$ with domain $\tilde x$. 

Dually, if $p^r\colon \cal{C} \to \cal{B}^r$ sends cartesian squares in $\cal{C}$ with parallel maps projections to cartesian squares in $\cal{B}^r$ then any map in $\cal{B}^{r}$ which is the image of some projection in $\cal{C}$ can be lifted to a projection in $\cal{C}$ with any prescribed lift of its codomain.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:42:16.238646+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64d68950c2d3f3a810c546c091602130e9300d2e4646a2f83a7007b933828eee","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem subcritical case theo 2 of arXiv:2607.00731, 'Sharp Asymptotics for the Largest Component in the Subcritical Regime of Preferential Atta'] Assume that \(\alpha=\alpha(n)\to a\in(0,\infty]\), and set $m_c=\frac{\alpha n}{2(\alpha+1)}.$ If \(m=\lfloor m_c(1-\varepsilon)\rfloor\), \(\varepsilon=\varepsilon(n)=o(1)\), and
