{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.607273+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64da4e3a872fdfd001e2b95323c64938017b1d2f3e631bf311b25c22fda297a5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:S1S2 of arXiv:2412.05142, 'Strong convergence of the Euler scheme for singular kinetic SDEs driven by $\alpha$-stable'] For any $0<\epsilon$ and $\beta\in(1-\frac{\alpha}{2},(1+\alpha)(\alpha-1))$ there exists a constant $N=N(\alpha,p,\beta,d,\|b\|_{{\mathbb C}_{\boldsymbol{a}}^{\beta}},\epsilon)$ independent of $n$ so that for any $(s,t)\in[0,1]_\leqslant^2$ and any $\sigma$-algebra ${\mathscr G}\subset{\mathcal F}_{s}$ the following holds
     \begin{align}
          \|S_{s,t}^{b,n,1}\|_{L_p(\Omega)|{\mathscr G}} \leqslant& N|t-s|^{\frac{(\beta-1)}{\alpha}+\frac{3}{2}}[Y-Y^n]_{C_p^{\frac{1}{2}}|{\mathscr G},[s,t]}+N |t-s|^{\frac{(\beta-1)}{\alpha}+1}[Y-Y^n]_{C_p^0|{\mathscr G},[s,t]}; \\
          \|S_{s,t}^{b,n,2}\|_{L_p(\Omega)|{\mathscr G}}\leqslant &N |t-s|^{\frac{(\beta-1)}{\alpha}+\frac{3}{2}}n^{-(\frac{1}{2}+\frac{\beta}{\alpha}\wedge\frac{1}{2})+\epsilon}+N|t-s|^{\frac{(\beta-1)}{\alpha}+1}n^{-1}.
     \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.648629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64dc4180c5456705819be19cf7019bf224d0be70f71f72e2520e1681e7ec5041","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:locality of arXiv:2604.07711, 'Central Limit Theorem for Random Partial\\ Sphere Coverings in High Dimensions'] Let $Y=(Y_1,\ldots,Y_N)\in\mathcal{C}(X,X',\widetilde{X})$, and set $U:=\bigcup_{i=3}^N C_N(Y_i)$ and
    \[
    A:=C_N(Y_1),\quad A':=C_N(X_1'),\quad B:=C_N(Y_2),\quad B':=C_N(X_2').
    \]
    Then
    \begin{align}
        \Delta_{1,2}f(Y) &= \sigma(U\cup A\cup B)-\sigma(U\cup A'\cup B)
        -\sigma(U\cup A\cup B')+\sigma(U\cup A'\cup B').
    \end{align}
    Moreover,
    \begin{align*}
\{\Delta_{1,2}f(Y)\neq 0\}\Longrightarrow\, &(A\cap B)\cup(A\cap B')\cup(A'\cap B)\cup(A'\cap B')\neq\varnothing.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.668559+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64dca6d92c2fd1efe475f74b002584ee82e078a390c587dad5c9f5c4c2427994","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 16 of arXiv:2604.24189, 'Malliavin calculus and densities for chaos-driven stochastic differential equations'] Let $d$ be a positive integer and let $\mathbf{Y}=\left(Y_1, \ldots, Y_d\right)$ be a random vector satisfying the following two conditions:
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
	\item $Y_i \in \mathbb{D}^{1, p}$ for all $i=1, \ldots, d$, for some $p \in(1, \infty)$;
