{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.812710+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_655e8dcb38ed4f879fc06051d76ed5686b7e06685fe5dc6e93d247a9209e1212","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition superport response of arXiv:2609.01672, '\textbf{All-Minors Matrix-Tree Theory for Superport Networks:\\ Completed Quotient-Inciden'] For each \(x\in N\), prescribe the voltage difference \(y_x=U_x-U_{r(x)}\). Let \(j_x\) denote the independent incoming current at \(x\); the current at each root is then fixed by the zero-total-current condition in its superport. The linear map \(y\mapsto j\) is the superport response, and its matrix in the chosen ordered root coordinates is denoted by \(L\):
