{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.649812+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6581ae90cc7e2e66a3a8daa66c8cd32adfe1889e521f715ce744c528d1acd3cd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:comparison_effectiveresistance_percolation_domination of arXiv:2607.04002, 'Collisions of random walks in unimodular random graphs: applications to the random geometr'] Suppose that the following is true:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item On each good box $B_\mathbf z$ we can pick a vertex $v_{\mathbf z} \in V(G)$.
        \item There exists~$L > 0$ such that for any pair~$(\mathbf x, \mathbf y)$ satisfying~$X_{ \{\mathbf x, \mathbf y\} }=1$, the vertices~$v_{\mathbf x}$ and~$v_{\mathbf y}$ can be connected by a path $\gamma_{\mathbf x,\mathbf y}$ in $G$ totally contained within $B_{\mathbf x}\cup B_{\mathbf y}$ with length at most~$L$.
        \item The process~$\{X_e: e \in E(\mathbb{Z}^d)\}$ dominates a supercritical Bernoulli bond percolation process with parameter~$p$, which can be taken arbitrarily close to 1. 
    \end{enumerate}
    Then, there exists a probability space~$\widehat{\mathbb{P}}$ on which the domination holds, where the following statement is satisfied. There exists a constant~$C = C(d,L,p,M,R)>0$ such that
    $$ \widehat{\mathbb{P}} \left( \sup_{\mathbf z \in \partial_V\mathcal V_0} \mathcal R_\mathrm{eff}( \mathbf{z} \longleftrightarrow \infty ; \mathcal C_\infty ) \ge u \right) \leq \exp( -b u^\nu ), \quad \text{for } u \text{ large enough}. $$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.254688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6582f9372e526f686728704735a912922c388181e0f02da62e0bdb6cbf5eea3d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 97 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] We have w.o.p. that the following statements hold for all $t \in [\mathsf{T}', N^5]$. 

