{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.330353+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_658f56332a0504b9f2052dc4f76fea57e08a8891f1029e1ba9d682a1d396ba5c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2506.22020, 'Norm-dependent Lamperti-type MAP representations of stable processes and Brownian motions '] Let $(\xi,\Xi)$ be the underlying MAP of $Z$ from (\ref{item_a}) with respect to $\|\cdot\|_1$. The jump kernel of $(\xi,\Xi)$ is given by
