{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:33:21.477338+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_660b97c3a3db46a73ca86a25759ff0816ee3ede1a8cf408b8455b210342322fc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2606.21391, 'Extreme points and faces in the moment problem'] Let $\mathbb{N}:=\{1,2,3,\dots\}$ and $\mathbb{N}_0:=\{0\}\cup\mathbb{N}$. 
The convex set $K$ is 
\begin{enumerate}
\item 
\emph{linearly compact} 
[kendall62,klee63-compact] if $\ell\cap K$ is a compact line 
segment (possibly degenerated to a singleton) for every line 
$\ell$ in $V$ that meets $K$.

\item 
\emph{$k$-neighborly}\footnote{

The term \emph{$k$-neighborly} extends its homonym in the theory of 
polytopes [gruenbaum03,sturmfels88,ziegler95].}

if the convex hull of any $k$ or less extreme points of 
$K$ is a face of $K$, $k\in\mathbb{N}$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

