{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.329470+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66324336a908f6f2b84f475001985013b6321480f19be4a716cccfd55a36ce22","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 13 of arXiv:2607.06428, 'Impact of spinning on the early-warning signs in non-Markovian stochastic systems'] Let $(x_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a stationary process and $S_x(\omega)$ be its SD. If $S_x$ is bounded and satisfies $S_x(\omega)\xrightarrow{\omega\to\pm\I}0$, we define 
