{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:25.273614+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6634fa2b984bcb778c7e7715731f12a9d91613f38567d271006e672885ffb1bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 25 of arXiv:2606.21111, 'On Elephant Random Walk with Delayed Amnesia'] Let $p=(4a-1)/4a$ and $\{Z_n\}_{n\ge 1}$ be uniformly bounded. Then, we have the following law of iterated logarithm for $\{W_n\}_{n\ge1}$:
