{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.862454+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_664da58b3353cd7de36a613523d9616382da8d8f2fef464657ca1e060609c268","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lower-bound-prob of arXiv:2410.24170, 'Persistent hubs in CMJ branching processes with independent increments and preferential at'] Suppose that $(X_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}_{0}}$ and $(X'_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}_{0}}$ are independent sequences of exponential random variables, with $X_{i} \sim X'_{i} \sim \exponentialrv\left( f(i) \right)$. Suppose, moreover, that $n, \phi_{n} \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$ are given such that
