}$$
with the strings joining the numbers belonging to the same block of $\pi$. That is, the above diagram represents the partition $\{1,\ldots,8\}=\{1,3,4\}\cup\{2,5\}\cup\{6,7\}\cup\{8\}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.326702+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6659cd4d5aeef6f65c2c6a0b9174573ea9928fdca1f86bbe93dc0e525d5ff190","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:asymptotic-nonorientability of arXiv:2609.03532, 'Airy limit for the Jack process and topological expansion'] For $g\in\frac12\mathbb Z_{\geq0}$ and $0\leq\eta\leq2g$, the limit
\begin{equation*}
  \mathfrak M_{g,\eta}(\boldsymbol k)
  :=\lim_{N\to\infty}
  N^{2-m-2g}4^{-E_N}
  \operatorname{Map}_{g,\eta}
  (K_{1,N},\ldots,K_{m,N})
\end{equation*}
exists and is
\begin{equation*}
  \boxed{
  \mathfrak M_{g,\eta}(\boldsymbol k)
  =2C_2^m
  \sum_{i=0}^{\lfloor g\rfloor}
  \binom{i}{\eta-(2g-2i)}
  \mathbf B_{m-1+i,\,2g-2i}^{\mathrm{conn}}
  \left[\frac{\mu_+\mathfrak c_2}{2}\boldsymbol k\right],
  }
\end{equation*}
where the binomial coefficient is zero unless its lower argument belongs to
$\{0,\ldots,i\}$.  Equivalently,
\begin{equation}
  \mathfrak M_{g,\eta}(\boldsymbol k)
  =[b^\eta]\operatorname{Hom}_{\,3g-3+\frac32m}
  \left\{
    2(1+b)^{1-m}C_2^m
    \mathbf L_b^{\mathrm{conn}}
    \left[\frac{\mu_+\mathfrak c_2}{2}\boldsymbol k\right]
  \right\}.

\end{equation}
For fixed $(g,\eta,m)$, both formulas contain only finitely many nonnegative
Brownian integrals.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.437003+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_665d2b7de2d5cdaac5711ccf47d51692db150b3026bcadf93377d7993681ad29","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:ConnectTwoSetsExact of arXiv:2508.09291, '1+O(1) asymptotics for loop percolation in five and higher dimensions'] For $d\ge 3$. Suppose that $K, L\subset\mathbb{Z}^d$ satisfy $\mathrm{diam}(K)+\mathrm{diam}(L)=o\rk{\mathrm{dist}(K,L)}$. We then have
