{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.245287+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_665d56cc9d78a4c95b0e25a3a623addf589ea9575ee69f40afd48e08e703e270","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 67 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Fix some $M\in \N$ and $n\in \N$. 

Assume that for all $i\in \lbr M\rbr$, we have  $\hfix^{\per,(i),\varepsilon}_0$ in $\UCp$ converging to some $\hfix^{\per,(i)}_0 \colon \mathbb{T}\rightarrow \R$ as $\varepsilon \rightarrow 0$ with respect to the UC topology, and initial data $\hfix^{(i),1,\varepsilon,j}_0$ and $\hfix^{(i),2,\varepsilon,j}_0$ in $\UC$ with
