{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.588596+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66792f6d2cac4f5c9c55ed3c9f8ac016a4daa4c618c5befd98b8d6cbd1feee39","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Col Cor_loc_energy of arXiv:2608.30548, 'Finite speed of propagation and waiting time phenomena for stochastic porous media equatio'] Let $\zeta\in C^2(\mathbb{T}^d)$, $p\in [1,\infty)$ and $\tau\le T$ a stopping time. Then it holds
\begin{align}\begin{split}

&
 \mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(
        \sup_{t\le \tau} \int_{\mathbb{T}^d} \zeta^2 u^{\alpha+1 }\,\mathrm{d} x \,+\, \int_0^\tau \int_{\mathbb{T}^d}   \zeta^2 | \nabla (u^{(\alpha+m )/2 })|^2\,\mathrm{d} x\, \mathrm{d} t \biggr)^p
        \biggr]^{1/p}
        \\&\quad \lesssim_{(\alpha,m,n,p,\psi)} \,\int_{\mathbb{T}^d} \zeta^2 u_0^{\alpha+1 }\,\mathrm{d} x \,+\, \mathbb{E} \biggl[\biggl(\int_0^\tau \int_{\mathbb{T}^d} u^{\alpha+m}|\nabla \zeta|^2 \,\mathrm{d} x\,\mathrm{d} t \biggr)^p
        \biggr]^{1/p}
        \\&\qquad +\, \mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(
