{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.068975+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6699c626fdc85fffb6b3ba05531897af40d0e2e500e75656fb3e34f1e12f62aa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm OPRE-percolates of arXiv:2507.00329, 'Oriented bond-site percolation in random environment and contact processes with periodic r'] Assume that the environment $(\xi_x)_{x\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq0}},(\nu_{x,x+1})_{x\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq0}}$ in Definition~(def:OPRE-model of the paper) is given by mutually independent families of i.i.d.\ random variables that satisfy the moment condition 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E}[\xi_0^{1+\varepsilon}], \, \mathbb{E}[\nu_{0,1}^{1+\varepsilon}]<\infty\qquad\text{for some $\varepsilon>0$}.
    \end{equation}
 Furthermore, let $(\kappa_\lambda)_{\lambda\geq 0}$ be a family of connection functions satisfying
    \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
        \item $\kappa_\lambda\colon [0,\infty)\to[0,1]$ is monotonically decreasing for every $\lambda\geq0$, and
        \item there exists some $\sigma>0$ such that, for every $s\in\mathbb{N}$,        \begin{equation}
          \exp(-\sigma s) \leq \kappa_\lambda(s)  \quad \text{ for every }\lambda\geq0, 
