{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.091874+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66b92793b134f994bb4118ca1179571e4d7ca9fc9d5c6e915b2260e816486014","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop cor 1.3 of arXiv:2412.08497, 'Time discretization of Quadratic Forward-Backward SDEs with singular drift'] Let the assumptions of Theorem (thm1.1 of the paper) be in force. Let $\{\chi_i\}_{i=0}^{N-1}$ be a sequence of random variables such that $\chi_i \in L^{\infty}(\Omega,\mathfrak{F}_{t+i},\mathbb{P})$, $\mathbb{E}[\chi_i/\mathfrak{F}_{t_i}] =1$ and $\chi_i \in [\epsilon,2-\epsilon]$ for all $0\leq i\leq N-1$ with some $\epsilon \in (0,1)$ independent of $N$. Define the process $\hat{\chi}(t)$ and the probability measure $\mathbb{Q}^N$, respectively by 
				\begin{align*}
