{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:27.033736+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66ffc3a522d27c8564c5f7639cc5f2c464ed364dbfe1c6664bfb8278a0ba418b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:inv of arXiv:2505.14012, 'Ergodicity for stochastic neural field equations'] Suppose that
Assumptions (assu:space of the paper), (assu:noise of the paper), (assu:hat of the paper), and (assu:inv of the paper) hold.
Then, for
\[\eta:=\sqrt{2}|f(0)|\|\rho\|_{L^1(U)}^{1/2}+\tilde{\tilde{C}}_B,\]
and for any $u_0\in H_1$, and any $t\in [0,T]$, it holds that,
\begin{align*}
