  \end{equation}
  Furthermore, if $\mathfrak{f}$ is increasing, the second inequality is an equality. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.023798+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_671865a6617002a9593210dd176ce25cf9610b9df09f82afb2d207829905e39b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2606.06489, 'The Missing Central Limit Theorems for Local Functionals of Berry's Random Wave Model'] Let $d\geq 2$. As $q\to\infty$, $q\in\N$,
