{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.587948+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_674a73d9e68cf3069b28e9c4c54575e27616a9e9a40706059c4602c230c6c50a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition StoFubiniThm of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] Let $T\geq 0$, $m(dt)$ be a $\sigma$-finite measure on $\mathbb{R}_+$ and $h$ be a measurable function on $\mathbb{R}_+$ such that
