{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.644288+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_674f19850e9c223138fd0182ba0093b027a8cdb6bc2012f5b373d80a422a75b6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2605.13518, 'The inertial It\^{o} drift and its applications to particle collision'] For every $\alpha \in\,(0,\infty)$ and $x \in\,\mathbb{R}^d$, system \eqref{smf4} has a unique invariant measure  given by the centered Gaussian measure $\mu_{\alpha,x}$ having covariance matrix
