{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:35:57.269606+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6796c6472b954592808701eb6f638a10ca106671ea6693f089361e2ecba06fac","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def:na of arXiv:2604.10446, 'Least singular values of shifted sparse random combinatorial matrices'] (Negative association)
Random variables $X_i, i \in [n]$, are said to be negatively associated (NA) if for all disjoint subsets $I, J \subset [n]$ and all coordinate-wise non-decreasing functions $f: \mathbb{R}^I\to \mathbb{R}$ and $g: \mathbb{R}^J\to \mathbb{R}$ one has 
