\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.844053+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_67991f443538dd2b8488ee76065eb8590f480c7d34af75b71d0f7050d3a62138","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2511.09930, 'Martingale dimensions for a class of metric measure spaces'] Let $i\in\{1,2,\dots,d+1\}$, $u\in l(V_0)$, and $\tau=\{\tau_k\}_{k\in\N}\in T^\N$.
