{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:02:11.286543+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_67b8be6660bef89ec59a593d9a310d572985fce9a6886e8acd5392b61596ab88","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:1 of arXiv:2509.10225, 'Phase Transitions for Elephant Random Walks \\ with Two memory Channels'] Fix $i \in \{1,2\}$. Let $p \neq 7/8$ be such that $\lambda^{(i)}_p\left(\boldsymbol{\Gamma}^{(p)}\right) < - \frac{1}{2}$ almost surely.  
