In particular, if $\varepsilon_{m'}\to 0$ then $\textup{($ii$)}\xrightarrow{p}0$, and if $\varepsilon_{m'}\asymp (m')^{-1/2}$ then $|\textup{($ii$)}|=O_p((m')^{-1/2})$.","status":"unverified"}

