{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:27.915279+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_682e427c5a72857526a2174671403ae3d1387731e3a3df5d48b5481fb7ac4b35","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 (Continuity lemma, adapted from Lemma 6.1 in \cite{benaych2011eigenvalues}) of arXiv:2607.12667, 'Phase Transition of Eigenvalues of Covariances from the Spiked Mixture Model in High-dimen'] For $\lambda_1(\Lb) > \ldots > \lambda_r(\Lb) > \sqrt{\gamma}$ with $r\leq K$, there exists $r$ complex sequences, ${z_1}{(d,n)}, \ldots, {z_r}{(d,n)}$, such that $\operatorname{Re}({z_1}{(d,n)}) \geq \ldots \geq \operatorname{Re}({z_r}{(d,n)})$
