Hence, $\widehat{G}^\mathrm{Bub}_0(x_1,...,x_n)=C^n G^\mathrm{Bub}_0(x_1,...,x_n)$ where $G^\mathrm{Bub}_0(x_1,...,x_n)$ is defined in~(equation eq:def-gf-bub of the paper) and $C$ is the same constant as in Proposition~(prop:equivalence of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.947654+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_68538939815a12893fabab3585d7b5fb0a141a9c981cc2e26490884d82f4346a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 21 of arXiv:2608.01860, 'A Variational Characterization of a Gibbs Measure related to the Aviles-Giga Functional'] Let $\delta>0$. We have for any $s\in\R$ and $p,q_1,q_2\in[1,\infty]$, $q_1<q_2$
    \begin{align}
        \Vert f\Vert_{B_{p,q_2}^s}\lesssim \Vert f\Vert_{B_{p,q_1}^s}\lesssim \Vert f\Vert_{B_{p,\infty}^{s+\delta}}\quad \forall f\in\mathcal{S}'(\mathbb{T}^d).
    \end{align}
    If we denote the fractional Sobolev spaces by $W^{s,p}$ then for any $q\in[1,\infty]$
    \begin{align}
        \Vert f\Vert_{B_{p,q}^s}\lesssim \Vert f\Vert_{W^{s+\delta,p}}\lesssim \Vert f\Vert_{B_{p,\infty}^{s+2\delta}}\quad \forall f\in\mathcal{S}'(\mathbb{T}^d),
