{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.538791+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_69020b0179fe40a9c4f1985ad5d00817eb4e56a95bcc2a3ff1b2200e6984e3dd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-M_N martingale of arXiv:2505.24043, 'Weak solutions of Navier-Stokes Equation with purely discontinuous L\'evy Noise'] For every $n \in \mathbb{N}$, the process ${{M}}_{n}$ is a square integrable $\mathbb{F}$-martingale and 
\begin{align}

\sup_{n \in \mathbb{N}}\mathbb{E} \left[ \sup_{t\in [0,T]}\bigl\vert  {{M}}_{n} (t) \bigr\vert_{H}^2 \right]
&\leq C_2 \sup_{n \in \mathbb{N}}
\mathbb{E} \Bigl[   \int_0^{T} \int_{Y} \rvert P_n F(s, u_n(s),y)\vert_{H}^2 \, \nu(\mathrm{d} y) \, \mathrm{d}s
\Bigr]
\\
&\leq C_2 \sup_{n \in \mathbb{N}} \left( 1+ \mathbb{E} \left[ \int_0^T  \lvert u_n (t) \rvert^2_H \, \mathrm{d}t \right] \right) < \infty. 

