{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.189777+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6909036eb67eed4e28ae2e9118c896b4ac8c9658b61a30979b27dbf9281ac50b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:irre of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] For any $p\in\ensuremath{\mathcal P}_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(\O)$, there exists \(t_0>0\) and \(\varepsilon_0>0\)  such that for all \(t\ge t_0\) the solution \(p_t\) of (equation non-linear rqs of the paper) satisfies 
