{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.863548+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6929905c88b3044e075295d6071fb343e04b04f3e74e9885b6e819ef2576fce0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 11 (Moment bounds) of arXiv:2605.21459, 'Network evolution with self-reinforcement'] $\E([\hat\mvzeta_{\ve}(\gl)]^l) < \infty$ for every $l \geq 1$. This implies that for every $l\geq 1$, there exist constants $H_l^{\circ}, H_l^\prime < \infty$, such that
