{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.285785+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_694c9370e5603ead23cbeaf63379e295c20c28017cfb9841b45e97eee7e25b38","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 (Weakly geometric $p$-rough paths) of arXiv:2606.22964, 'Signature McKean--Vlasov stochastic differential equations'] Let $p\geq 1$. We define $C^{\textup{$p$-var}}_o([0,T],G^{\lfloor p\rfloor}(\mathbb{R}^k))$ as the set of continuous paths $\mathbf{x}:[0,T]\rightarrow G^{\lfloor p\rfloor}(\mathbb{R}^k)$ such that $\mathbf{x}_0=(1,0,\dots,0)$ and
