{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.329354+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_694cd4bebb5f11d6b700c9f7e15fabaf5fe86057c39b11dc3ce712e170b071ec","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:spectral0 of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] Let $(f_i)_{i\ge 1}$ be a sequence of local functions from $\Omega$ to $\mathbb{R}$ that have disjoint supports, and assume that the support of the function $f_i$ has cardinality $\ell_i$ for any $i\ge 1$. Assume that $\psi_{f_i}(\rho ,\mathcal{E})=0$ for any $\rho\in [0,1]$, any $\mathcal{E}\in [\rho ,\kappa\rho ]$ and any $i\ge 1$. Finally, assume that the series $\sum_{i=1}^\infty \mathrm{Var}_{\rho ,\mathcal{E}}(f_i)$ converges. Then, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \left\|\sum_{i=1}^\infty f_i\right\|_{-1}^2 \le C_6\sum_{i=1}^\infty \ell_i^2 \mathrm{Var}_{\rho ,\mathcal{E}}(f_i).
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.041661+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_694d5665b970ac0672f1eee8a8ded0c99b24b54794a82d0fa1b3aee62b374054","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 (Definition 4.1 of \cite{Chen2024}, with the omitted $\lambda^2S_{2424}$ term restored; cf.\ Definition 4.1 of \cite{Brendle2019}) of arXiv:2608.26598, 'Pinching cones for positive isotropic curvature in dimensions seven and eight'] Assume $0<b\le\tilde b_{max,2}$ and let $a=b+\frac{n-2}{2}b^2$. We denote by
        $\tilde{\mathcal{E}}(b)$ the set of all $S\in\CB(\mathbb{R}^n)$ such that
        $l_{a,b}(S)\in C(b_{max,2})$ and
        \begin{equation}
            Z:=S_{1313}+\lambda^2S_{1414}+S_{2323}+\lambda^2S_{2424}-2\lambda S_{1234}
            +\sqrt{2a}(1-\lambda^2)\bigl(\Ric(S)_{11}+\Ric(S)_{22}\bigr)\geq 0
