{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:08.996325+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_699edcba160f49a7b4904b9c6f0e6e4bc320543534e2e81860aeb239b90c0542","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def_condNegSemiDef of arXiv:2608.17463, 'Persistence probabilities of fractional L\'evy fields indexed by hyperbolic space and othe'] Let $A$ be a set and let $f:A\times A\to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}$ be a symmetric function. Then it is called conditionally negative definite, if for any $n\in\mathbb{N}$, any $\lambda_1, \ldots, \lambda_n \in\mathbb{R}$ with $\lambda_1 + \ldots + \lambda_n=0$ and any $x_1, \ldots, x_n \in A$ it holds that
