{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.766083+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6a0e9acdff6e8dfdcdd327da533463fd2c6c6e782849065e26a5c43d9ac35664","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2607.09575, 'Probabilistic estimates for a system of\\noisy integrate-and-fire neurons'] For any $s,t \in [0,T]$, there exist a $\beta > 0$ and a $C = C(\beta) > 0$, independent of $s$, $t$ and $N$, such that 
