{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.907553+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ad9efbb0a9240fcd0fabdf7e8e3f566ba4c992f28654867e2c0a97e474d7ebd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:bulinsk of arXiv:2411.11429, 'Functional Central Limit Theorem for topological functionals of Gaussian critical points'] [Bulinskaya]

Let \( p'<p \) be integers, \( A \) a bounded Borel  set of \( \mathbb R^{p'} \). For $ 1\le i\le p,$ let \( g_i:A\to \mathbb R^{d_i} \) be a smooth centred Gaussian field  {such that\begin{itemize}
\item $ \|g_i(x)\|$ and $ \| \nabla g_i(x)\|$ are bounded  by $ \| (\partial _{ \alpha }F(x);\alpha \in I_i)\|$ for some finite $ I_i$,
\item   $G(x) := (g_i(x))\in \mathbb R^{p^{*}}
$ has a uniformly bounded density, where \( p^{*} = \sum_id_i.\)
\end{itemize} }
Let \( h_i:\mathbb R^{d_i}\to \mathbb R \)  smooth functions such that $ h_{ i}$ and its derivative are bounded by $c_{ l} \|x\|^{ l}$ for some $l>0$, and \( f_i(x): = h_i(g_i(x)),1\le i\le p. \) Assume also that each \( h_i(X) \) has a density bounded on \( [-\varepsilon, \varepsilon ] \) for some \( \varepsilon >0 \) on the input \( X\sim \mathcal N(0,I_{d_i}) \). Let
 \(a\in (0,1) \) and
\begin{align*}\psi (x) = (f_i(x))_{i = 1}^p\in \mathbb R^p.
\end{align*}  There is \( c_a ,\tau_a >0 \) such that for \( \tau \in (0,\tau_a ) \), 
\begin{align*}
\mathbf P(\inf_{x\in A}\|\psi (x)\|\le \tau )\le c_a  (1 +  \text{\rm{diam}}(A))^{2d} \tau ^{a }.
