{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.735567+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b078ba4b5bbb93b18c8638b7a56dee8390eb769e572e6efd5ad1fc4e0888136","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:Push-TASEP-scalar of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] For $t > 0$ and $a < y_{n+1} - 1$, the one-point Fredholm
