{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.482124+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b26e46b46a65fecead12d87414bb65ce0dd572c2030ecec4dbf8895d73cc1af","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 23 (Uniform bounds for the defect measures of $u^h_{\alpha,n}$) of arXiv:2607.28238, 'Well-posedness and large deviations for the obstacle problem of first-order stochastic con'] For every $p\geq0$, there exists $C>0$ independent of $\alpha\in(0,1)$ and $n\in\mathbb N$, such that
