{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:48:17.119518+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b2b4faf724a88cf58cd5f66e874d5c22a1715b96b73849c0e2cd8a9d3813c16","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2605.27212, '2605.27212'] For every fixed \(M<\infty\) there is a constant
\(C_{p,\varepsilon,M}<\infty\) such that the following holds.  If
