{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:37:14.981166+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b2dd7eeccd7d3cc21280973efff31b95d008f2708513bfe60bb59c79bf8f6b9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 9 of arXiv:2607.11756, 'Full replica symmetry breaking in the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick model'] Every function obtained from $\log\cosh$ by finitely many transforms $T_{a,r}$ is even, smooth, and strictly convex, has all positive-order derivatives bounded, and satisfies
