{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:11.639324+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b37b363346d6475162a5be29b4cfc73a760d619a9d3c6d65dad1a01d7a19dc7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 13 of arXiv:2605.31344, 'Subcritical sharpness for real-valued spin models'] Let $\Lambda \subset V$ finite, $\beta \geq 0$, and $\sfb \in (\mathbb{R}^{+})^{\partial^{\mathrm{ext}} \Lambda}$. For every $x,y \in \Lambda,$ we have
