{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:15:54.903704+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b3b5aa42e8c47f5755f5d7666b34bd8f8ce57f1eec96b8f71025277d35eda0b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:lp of arXiv:2608.28007, 'Exact Risk Ratios for Weighted Data Selection in Linear Regression'] Let $D\in\mathcal D_r$ and let its whitened system have energies
$(R_j)$; let the budget be $n=d+k$ with $0\le k\le s-1$. Then there is a
strictly convex, strictly positively weighted selection of at most $d+k$
points with
\[
\lVert \hat q\rVert^2\;\le\;\min_{K\subseteq[s],\,|K|=k}\ \sum_{j\notin K}r_jR_j ,
\]
and the supremum of the right-hand side over admissible energies is exactly
\begin{equation}
\Phi(r,k)=\max_{J\subseteq[s],\,|J|\ge k+1}
\frac{|J|-k}{\sum_{j\in J}1/r_j}.
\end{equation}
For $k\ge s$ the budget completes every block and the excess is zero.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.423347+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b3ca4998d20c834b184f4f797c35f11c2009d5ddf9eb34d0bf41f5ae82e7920","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theorem4.3 of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] ([erdHos2011universality], Theorem 1.11.) Let $H\in\operatorname{Sym}_n(\zeta)$ where $\zeta\in\Gamma_B$ for some $B>0$. Let $\kappa>0$ and consider $E\in[-2+\kappa,2-\kappa]$. Denote by $\mathcal{N}_{\eta^*}(E)=\mathcal{N}_{I^*}$ the number of eigenvalues of $n^{-\frac{1}{2}}H$ in $I^*:=[E-\eta^*/2,E+\eta^*/2]$. Then we can find a universal constant $c_1>0$ and two constants $C$, $c>0$ depending only on $\kappa$ such that for any $\delta\leq c_1\kappa$ we can find a constant $K_\delta$ depending only on $\delta$ such that 
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}\left\{\left|\frac{\mathcal{N}_{\eta^*}(E)}{n\eta^*}-\rho_{sc}(E)\right|\geq\delta\right\}\leq Ce^{-c\delta^2\sqrt{n\eta^*}},
\end{equation}
for all $\eta^*$ satisfying $K_\delta/n\leq\eta^*\leq 1$ and all $n\geq 2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.328456+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b3e8465b74c7a7efd37da134056552e1b8d066c2e6d6042cecfb7c9e951609a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:stokes_rough of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Suppose that Assumption (ass:homogenized_PDE_linear_model_problem of the paper) holds. Fix $\varphi\in C^{\infty}_{{\rm c}}(B)$ such that $\int_B \varphi =1$. Then there exists a unique solution 
$v$ 
to (equation eq:homogenized_PDE_linear_model_problem of the paper) in the transposition sense satisfying 
$$
\nabla \cdot v=0 \text{ in }\mathscr{D}'(B) \text{  a.e.\ on } I,
$$ 
and a unique
$\Pi\in H^{-1}(I;H^{-1}(B))$ such that 
\begin{align*}
&\partial_t v =-\nabla \Pi +\kappa \Delta v+\nabla \cdot R \  \text{ in }\ \mathscr{D}'(Q),\\
&\langle \Pi,\eta\otimes \varphi \rangle =0 \ \text{ for all } \ \eta\in C^{\infty}_{{\rm c}}(I).
\end{align*}
Finally, there exists a constant $C>0$ depending only on $d$ and $\kappa$ such that 
\begin{align}

\|v\|_{L^{2}(Q)}
+\|\Pi\|_{H^{-1}(I;H^{-1}(B))}
\leq C\big( \|\xi(0)\|_{L^2(B)}+ \|\xi\|_{L^2(I\times \partial B)}+ \|R\|_{L^2(Q)}\big).
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.365311+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b4076b02a1a40dca155892c2c19c9ca1a0a65e1adf59c91e72355ce28f33463","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 19 of arXiv:2506.20146, 'Parabolic Anderson Model in the Hyperbolic Space. Part I: Annealed Asymptotics'] With some universal constant $C=C_{d,r}>0,$ one has 
