{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.571838+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b4b15703b25ef24c67f9520342bf0a3609ba3a9c3ec33a0575275f4c34a610f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 22 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under Assumption~\ref{ass:basic}, let $E_*$ be a regular right edge in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:reg_r_edge}. Then there exists a constant $\eps_*>0$ such that, for every $z=E+\ii\eta\in\C^+$ with $|E-E_*|\leq\eps_*$ and $0<\eta\leq\eps_*$,
        \begin{align}
                \|(\calI-\calJ(z))^{-1}\|+\|\calB(z)^{-1}\|\lesssim(|E-E_*|+\eta)^{-1/2}. 
        \end{align}
        Moreover, with $\kappa:=|E-E_*|$,
        \begin{align}
                \Im m(E+\ii\eta)\sim \begin{cases} (\kappa+\eta)^{1/2},               & E\leq E_*, \\[1mm]
              \dfrac{\eta}{(\kappa+\eta)^{1/2}}, & E\geq E_*,\end{cases} 
        \end{align}
        and consequently
        \begin{align}
                \Im m(z)+\frac{\eta}{\Im m(z)}              & \sim (|E-E_*|+\eta)^{1/2}, \nonumber                                       \\
                \|(\calI-\calJ(z))^{-1}\|+\|\calB(z)^{-1}\| & \lesssim \frac{1}{\Im m(z)+\eta/\Im m(z)}. 
        \end{align}
        The same $\eps_*$ may be chosen so that, uniformly for $|E-E_*|\leq\eps_*$ and $\eps_*\leq\eta\leq\eta_0$,
        \begin{align}
                \|\Pi(z)\|+\|(\calI-\calJ(z))^{-1}\|+\|\calB(z)^{-1}\|\lesssim1. 
        \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.368674+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b4ec9e700559798145d6bb50b00aec62bb088ddcb439f2d51dfec83056fd692","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conj conj1 of arXiv:2411.13419, 'Forest Fire Model on $\Z_{+}$ with Delays'] There is a $c\ge 1$, such that a.s.\ there exists a (possibly random) $\kappa$ such 
