weakly with respect to $\Delta_{\GHf}$ as $n\rightarrow\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.467947+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b6ca4301fae216ed2647de2b761b42eef509689aa306b7a228846960e6fa04f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem-intro main-thm of arXiv:2608.27904, 'Instantons, indefinite 4-manifolds, and Dehn surgery'] The invariant $q_3(Y)$ of $\Bbb F_2$-homology spheres satisfies the following properties. 
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*), ref=(\roman*)]
	\item If $-Y$ denotes the orientation-reversal, we have $q_3(-Y) = -q_3(Y)$.
	\item If $W:Y\to Y'$ is a cobordism between $\Bbb F_2$-homology spheres such that $H_1(W;\Bbb Z)$ has no 2-torsion, then 
	\begin{equation}
		-b^+(W) \le q_3(Y')-q_3(Y) \le b^-(W).
	\end{equation}	
	\item If $Y$ is an integer homology sphere and $P$ is the Poincar\'e homology sphere, then  \[q_3(Y \# P) = q_3(Y) + 1.\]
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.631008+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b6fc5b687afa0d6739b34562d2113119ab2863bfef844f5653ef7524886f2c7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2506.17045, '\LARGE{On bivariate Archimax copulas: Level sets, mass distributions and related results}'] Let $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_\mathcal{W}$, $\psi$ be its corresponding generator, $\varphi$ be its pseudo-inverse, $\vartheta \in \mathcal{P}_\mathcal{A}$, $A$ be the corresponding Pickands dependence function, $C_{\psi,A} \in \mathcal{C}_{am}$, $K_{\psi,A}$ be the Markov kernel of $C_{\psi,A}$ according to eq. \eqref{eq:markov-kernel} and $L$, $R$ be defined according to eq. \eqref{eq:definition_L_R} with $L<R$. 
Moreover, let $t \in (0,1)$ if $\psi$ is strict, $t \in [0,1)$ if $\psi$ is non-strict and let $\fg^t$ be defined according to eq. \eqref{eq:fct_g_t}. Then for all but at most countably many $x \in \left(t, \psi\left(\frac{L\varphi(t)}{1-L}\right)\right)$ the following equivalence holds:
\begin{equation*}
    K_{\psi,A}(x,\{\fg^t(x)\})>0 \text{ if, and only if } \frac{1}{\varphi(t)} \text{ is a point mass of } \gamma.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.594527+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b717683da6748e28f159719ed15b3930d5da5782164ca77f2187f3a74f35fcc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor dexp of arXiv:2412.03415, 'Critical first passage percolation on random graphs'] Under the assumptions of Theorem (thm:main of the paper), consider the following special cases for the positive part of the edge distribution:
\begin{enumeratea}
\item Suppose  $(t_e|t_e>0)$ has cumulative distribution function $H_\gamma(t)=e \cdot \exp(-\exp(1/t^\gamma))$ for $0< t \leqslant 1$. Then as $n\to\infty$, 
\begin{enumeratei}
\item  For $\gamma < 1$, $ T_n(1,2) \stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow} \Xi $ where $\Xi = \Xi(\mathbf{p}, H_\gamma) < \infty$ a.s., 
\item  For $\gamma \geqslant 1$, $T_n(1,2)\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow} \infty$.
\end{enumeratei}
\item Suppose $t_e\overset{d}{=}p_c \delta_0+(1-p_c)\delta_1$, namely the passage time distribution has mass at either zero or one. Then $T_n(1,2)\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow} \infty$.

\end{enumeratea} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.458212+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b74b910becf9c33f1b0914a875e20d2e2acb5bddced30cda71e06e02bd121a3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:isoflow of arXiv:2411.16572, 'Optimal decay of eigenvector overlap for non-Hermitian random matrices'] Fix small $n$--independent constants $\tau,\omega_*,\epsilon>0$, and for $i=1,2$ fix spectral parameters $\Lambda_{i,0}$ as in (equation eq:defincond of the paper). Fix an exponent $b\in [0,1]$.
	For $t\le T^*$ let $\Lambda_{i,t}$ be the solution of (equation eq:charflowmat of the paper) with initial condition $\Lambda_{i,0}$. Let $G_{i,t}:=(W_t-\Lambda_{i,t})^{-1}$, and let $M_{12,t}^A$, $M_{121,t}^{A_1,A_2}$ be defined in (equation eq:defm12 of the paper) and (equation eq:defm121 of the paper), respectively. Let $\ell_t, \gamma_t$ be from (equation eq:defcontrolparam of the paper), and assume that for some small $0<\xi\le \epsilon/10$, with very high probability, it holds
	\begin{equation}

		\begin{split}
			\big|\big\langle {\bm x}, \big(G_0^{z_{1,0}}(\mathrm{i}\eta_1)A_1G_0^{z_{2,0}}(\mathrm{i}\eta_2)-M_{12}^{A_1}(\eta_1,z_{1,0},\eta_2,z_{2,0})\big) {\bm y}\big\rangle\big|&\le 
			\frac{n^\xi (\rho^*)^{\frac{1-b}{2}} }{\sqrt{n} \eta_*^{\frac{3-b}{2}}\gamma_0^{\frac{b}{2}} }, \\
			\big|\big\langle {\bm x}, \big(G_0^{z_{1,0}}(\mathrm{i}\eta_1)A_1G_0^{z_{2,0}}(\mathrm{i}\eta_2)A_2G_0^{z_{1,0}}(\mathrm{i}\eta_1)-M_{121}^{A_1,A_2}(\eta_1,z_{1,0},\eta_2,z_{2,0})\big) {\bm y}\big\rangle\big|&\le \frac{n^\xi}{\eta_*^{2-b}\gamma_0^b},
		\end{split}
	\end{equation}
	where $\eta_*:=|\eta_1|\wedge|\eta_2|$,  uniformly in $\lVert A_i\rVert\le 1$, $\lVert {\bm x}\rVert+\lVert {\bm y}\rVert\lesssim 1$, and for any $|\eta_i|\in [|\eta_{i,0}|,n^{100}]$, where $\ell_0,\gamma_0$ are evaluated at $(\eta_1,z_{1,0},\eta_2,z_{2,0})$. Then,
	\begin{equation}

		\begin{split}
			\big|\big\langle {\bm x}, \big(G_{1,t}A_1G_{2,t}-M_{12,t}^{A_1}\big) {\bm y}\big\rangle\big|&\le
			\frac{n^{2\xi} (\rho^*_t)^{\frac{1-b}{2}} }{\sqrt{n} \eta_{*,t}^{\frac{3-b}{2}}\gamma_t^{\frac{b}{2}} },\\
			\big|\big\langle {\bm x}, \big(G_{1,t}A_1G_{2,t}A_2G_{1,t}-M_{121,t}^{A_1,A_2}\big) {\bm y}\big\rangle\big|&\le \frac{n^{2\xi}}{(\eta_{*,t})^{2-b}\gamma_t^b},
		\end{split}
	\end{equation}
	where $\eta_{*,t}:=|\eta_{1,t}|\wedge|\eta_{2,t}|$, with very high probability uniformly in $\lVert A_i\rVert\le 1$, $\lVert {\bm x}\rVert+\lVert {\bm y}\rVert\lesssim 1$, and all $t\le T^*$ such that $n\ell_t\ge n^\epsilon$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.519721+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b7a41ec4efb8aa8195e07fb96182938c55f545347d59c2d8c7619212f387bf2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:sp_method of arXiv:2512.17808, 'Zeros of polynomial powers under the heat flow'] Under the assumptions above, we have
