{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.382174+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b82f71f34aaa03786f5af3e34c969febbe4286c5959386f613a50540e97b86b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:noninvariant of arXiv:2411.02030, 'Finite ergodic components for upper probabilities'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},P)$ be a probability space and $T:\Omega\to \Omega$ be a measurable invertible transformation. If the limit (equation eq:20.19 of the paper) exits, then the following statements are equivalent:
