{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.358200+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b9478fa08716db74878a53f4610799b7bca3bb2967fece2d4a979e7cf3d3faf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.equivstrong of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] Fix $(t_0,m_0) \in [0,1) \times \mathcal{P}_2({\mathbb R})$. Let $\big(\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mathbb{F} = (\mathcal{F}(t))_{0 \leq t \leq 1}, \mathbb{P}\big)$ be any filtered probability space satisfying the usual conditions, which supports an $\mathcal{F}(t_0)$-measurable random $X_0$ with law $m_0$, and an $\mathbb{F}$-Brownian motion $(B(t))_{0\leq t \leq 1}$. Then, we have
   \begin{align}
       \mathcal{V}^{\infty}(t_0,m_0) = \inf_{\alpha} \Big\| X_0 + \int_{t_0}^1 \alpha(t) \, dt + B(1) - B(t_0) \Big\|_{\infty},
