{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.866211+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6bfe2d2443b4bf22d3b6f8bcb42c18815868f7903526756fe77959a7a17f6d75","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition d:eid of arXiv:2510.13659, 'On the energy image density conjecture of Bouleau and Hirsch'] Let $(X,\mathcal{X},\mu,\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$ be a Dirichlet structure with the associated carr\'e du champ operator $\gamma: \mathcal{F} \times \mathcal{F} \to L^1(\mu)$. We say that the Dirichlet structure  $(X,\mathcal{X},\mu,\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$ satisfies the \emph{energy image density property}, if 	 for any $n \in \mathbb{N}$, $f \in \mathcal{F}^n$, we have
