\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.299316+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c25a8ea47a5c4aadae162eca3b2f0054da2c713f836651358ae841a1dee758d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 of arXiv:2606.23383, 'Near-Lipschitz stability of the Kim--Milman flow map'] Fix $t > 0$ and let $\mu = \cN(0,1)$; it holds that
