{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.705392+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c5da9b60bbc2ebda49a4b24169a35ccda88eeebe7523eba34e327669b5b98e1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma estimates for the characteristic fuction using bobkov et al of arXiv:2605.29095, 'Asymptotics of the number of components of random polynomial lemniscates'] Let $p_r(x)$ denote the density of the random variable $\log|r-X_1|$ and let $\nu_r(t) = \mathbb{E}[e^{it\log|r-X_1|}]$ be its characteristic function. Then, $p_r(x)$ is uniformly bounded for $x\in \mathbb{R}$, and $r\in [1/2, 1]$. Moreover, for every $\delta>0$, there exists a $\eta = \eta (\delta) > 0$ such that
