{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.261628+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c7c5c1626c6870aebe2c24428cd396e8e50c2c2e606c0c85f6b17de3dd05e26","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_conformal_covariance of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] The law ${\mathbb{P}}_{h}^{(\Omega,a,b)}$ is conformally covariant in the following sense. If $\gamma$ has law ${\mathbb{P}}_{h}^{(\Omega,a,b)}$ and $\psi: \Omega \to \tilde \Omega$ is a conformal map, then $\psi(\gamma)$ has law ${\mathbb{P}}_{\tilde h}^{(\tilde \Omega,\psi(a),\psi(b))}$ where $\tilde h$ is given by, for $w \in \tilde \Omega$,
