and $\lambda_{d,\mathbb H}'=\lambda_{d,\mathbb H}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.156546+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c99e7451864799d70206dd5b27f06f8dafd28b1ad5fa89afb4bf4565921555b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 (Marginals) of arXiv:2607.02108, 'A Two-Color Lift of the Shifted \texorpdfstring{$t$}{t}-Schur Measure'] The $\lambda$-marginal is
