{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.462164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c9d58d0931568780b7ae7272634affb5057a29c6de65e98538deb6f7cf756d8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 11 ({\cite[Section 2) of arXiv:2609.02561, 'NON-NEF LOCI IN MIXED CHARACTERISTIC'] {Les}}]
Let $D$ be an $\R$-Cartier $\R$-divisor.
We say that $D$ is:
\begin{enumerate}
\item
$f$-ample if its numerical class lies in the real cone generated by numerical classes of $f$-ample line bundles;
\item
$f$-nef if $(D.C)\geq 0$ for every irreducible curve $C\subset X$ that is closed in $X$ and satisfies that $f(C)$ is a closed point of $S$;
\item
$f$-big if $D|_{X_{\eta}}$ is a big $\R$-Cartier $\R$-divisor on $X_{\eta}$;
\item
$f$-pseudo-effective if $D|_{X_{\eta}}$ is a pseudo-effective $\R$-Cartier $\R$-divisor on $X_{\eta}$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.375086+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ca12a265bcf78f6949f1cc1d755fc39748c5fdd72b8bbc31962969a37cdf902","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 6 of arXiv:2606.04636, 'A Thomson-type variational principle for diffusion coefficients'] Let $l\in\R^{d}$, and consider the diffusion
