{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:36:12.192488+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6cb0c157336484cde4cd42131b232ac9b434e4e66b00ee68a67a18410ba63144","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 (Gauss divisible case) of arXiv:2609.03924, 'Beyond normal fluctuations in local laws for Wigner matrices'] Assume the set-up \eqref{eq:OU_flow}--\eqref{eq:char_flow} and denote $X_t:=N\eta_t\langle G_t-m_t\rangle$ for $t\in [0,T]$. For any fixed $p,q\in\N\cup\{0\}$ with $p+q\ge 3$ it holds that
\begin{equation}
\kappa_{p,q}\left(X_t\right) = \frac{\eta_t^{p+q}}{N^{(p+q-2)/2}}K_{p,q}(z_t)\kappa_{p+q}^{\mathrm{d}}(t) + \frac{N^\xi}{N\eta_t} \mathcal{O}\left( \frac{1}{N^{(p+q-3)/2}}+ \frac{1}{(N\eta_t)^{p+q-3}}\right),

\end{equation}
for any fixed $\xi>0$, uniformly in $t\in [0,T]$ and $z=z_T\in\mathcal{D}$. Here $\kappa^\dif_{p+q}(t):=\kappa_{p+q}\left(N^{1/2} (W_t)_{11}\right)$ and $K_{p,q}$ is defined in \eqref{eq:def_K}. We further have
\begin{equation}
\kappa_{p,0}\left(N\eta_t\langle G_t-m_t\rangle\right) = \frac{\eta_t^p}{N^{(p-2)/2}}\left(K_{p,0}(z_t)\kappa_p^{\mathrm{d}}(t) + \mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{N^{1/2}}\right)\right),

