By construction, \hskip.03cm $\aM_{G,\ba}$ \hskip.03cm is a balanced weight function for vertices of $H_X$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.297206+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6cc5151fecd4b5fa692bbe42da2f80f51ebd5a8ace2fbc40181020f6adfec257","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem inv th2Pre of arXiv:2411.05534, 'Inverse problems for stochastic partial differential equations'] Let $h \in L_{\mathbb{F}}^2 (0, T ; H^1 (G^{\prime} ) )$ and $R \in C^{1,3}(\overline{Q})$ satisfy

\begin{align}
    |R(t, x)| \neq 0 \quad \text { for all }(t, x) \in[0, T] \times \overline{G}.
