{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.931836+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6cd8d0f118fb140d611ff3bf21e904964a5085353552ccad39f7d694dc14d012","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop.H1TwoScale of arXiv:2606.13442, 'Scaling limit of additive functionals for reversible non-gradient exclusion process: criti'] There exists a finite positive constant $C(c_{-},c_{+},\mathbf{r},\rho)$ such that for every $\lambda\in(0,\tfrac{1}{2})$, the following estimates about the expectation and variance of the carr\'e du champ of $\widetilde{G}_\lambda$ hold:
