{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.352127+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6cdd062279d0b23ad23a5839b9ac996f91dd3bca3b4d33a26b3fe62002ac3d7c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2506.16259, 'Two-dimensional Rademacher walk'] Let $d_1,d_2,d_3\dots$ be a sequence of distinct positive integers, and let $T_k=d_1\eps_1+\dots+d_k\eps_k$ where  $\eps_i$ are i.i.d.\ Rademacher. Then for every integer $\displaystyle  m\ge \max_{1\le i\le k}d_i$ and every  $M\in\Z$ we have
