{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:10.191652+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d45e6a12ad75c4e6c3f4164662edfad980b108f31f01b1ad5e69e4bbaab595e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3 (Bounding Wasserstein distance by the uniform discrepancy) of arXiv:2605.03528, '\bf Kolmogorov-Smirnov distance and discrepancies {\em versus} Wasserstein distances'] Let $\mu$ and $\nu$ two probability measures on $([0,1]^d, {\cal B}or([0,1]^d),\lambda_d)$.  Then,
\begin{itemize}
