{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:08.951511+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d54cbc488221550d0144c3a17f97c8c70a54bdbfe385010110e8957d070496e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Definition_virtual_block of arXiv:2411.10829, 'Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble and its Laplace transform'] For a block process $\vec \mathbf p$, a compatible \emph{virtual block process} is a vector $\vec\boldsymbol{\upsilon}=(\boldsymbol{\upsilon}_1,\ldots, \boldsymbol{\upsilon}_m)\in (\mathbb R_+\cup \{\varnothing\})^m$ satisfying the following conditions: for each $\ell \in \llbracket 1,m\rrbracket$,
\begin{itemize}
    \item if $\boldsymbol{\upsilon}_\ell\neq \varnothing$, then $\mathbf Q_{\ell-1}+\boldsymbol{\upsilon}_\ell < \min\bigl( \bigcup_{j=1}^{m+\mathbf u}\mathbf \Delta_{j,\ell}\cup \{\mathbf Q_\ell\}\bigr)$;
    \item if $\ell=1$, or $\ell>1$ and $\mathbf p_\ell(\mathbf Q_{\ell-1}-)=0$, then $\boldsymbol{\upsilon}_\ell=\varnothing$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.413938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d5ae81aa2a085365e896a06718ce882e0817e772c726c92dca650d44c5e63bd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:peierls_argument of arXiv:2601.07808, 'Supercritical long-range percolation on graphs of polynomial growth: the truncated one-arm'] \label[lemma]{lem:peierls_argument}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 2$.

    There exists $c_{\mathrm{pei}} = c_{\mathrm{pei}}(G) > 0$ such that

    \begin{equation}

        \#
        \{
            A \in \mathcal{A} 
            : 
