{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.446198+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6de81fa1f4d30a9c11528038314952dfb47bb14817d51a1a28478c9bd5d0ddd9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:generalisedWells of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] Given an integer $L \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, an integer $n \geq 3$, two inverse temperatures $\beta_1 , \beta_2 \geq 0$, a parameter $\lambda > 0$ and an integer $m \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, one has the inequality
    \begin{equation} 
        \left\langle \cos \left( m  \theta_{0g} \right) \right\rangle_{L , n , \beta_1/2 , \beta_2 , \lambda}^{\mathrm{XY}} \leq \mathbb{E}_{\nu_{L , n , \beta_1 , \beta_2 , \lambda}} \left[ \left\langle \cos \left( m \theta_{0g} \right) \right\rangle_{L , n , \beta_1 , \beta_2 , \lambda,r }^{\mathrm{XY}} \right].
