{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.805663+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e3b116827bc2d236cb86f6751bf3d2284cc62d9d1d091587767cb60d3afd60f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm l:polymer-measure-is-measurable of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] For each $(s,x;t,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{4}_{\uparrow}$ and $\beta>0$, the map $\xi\mapsto \mathbb{P}_{\beta, (s,x),(t,y)}^\xi$ is a measurable map $(\Xi,\mathcal{F}_{[s,t]\times \mathbb{R}},\mathbb{P}) \to \mathrm{Prob}(C([s,t]))$,
