{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:15:46.791572+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e49e09db9c6d13ca009e192ee2418a115fa44f01ea87280ec0005024f5d5574","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[OPEN PROBLEM - not a proved fact. Stated in arXiv:2506.09609, 'Schramm-Loewner evolution contains a topological Sierpiński carpet when $κ$ is close to 8' (conjecture environment labelled conj:exotic-1).] For each $\underline{\kappa} \in (0,4)$, there exists $\rho_c = \rho_c(\kappa) \in (-2-\underline{\kappa}/2,-2) \cap [\underline{\kappa}/2-4,-2) $ such that the following holds. Let $\eta$ be an SLE$_{\underline{\kappa}}(\rho)$ curve from $0$ to $\infty$ on $\mathbb{H}$ with force point always located to the right of the tip.
