{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.375014+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6eb9cfe0c62c1307363fd06b2a8ea94b60532f45c9a65cd94c626c84d09c77df","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 5 of arXiv:2606.04636, 'A Thomson-type variational principle for diffusion coefficients'] $V_{0}$ is the space of admissible flows with vanishing
divergence, that we write formally as
\begin{equation}
V_{0}=\left\{ \phi\in\cH_{2}:\left\langle \div\phi,\div\phi\right\rangle =0\right\} .
\end{equation}
For $\phi\in\cH_{2}$, $\left\langle \div\phi,\div\phi\right\rangle =0$
should be understood by the completion under $\left\langle \cdot,\cdot\right\rangle $.
That is, there exists a sequence $(\phi_{n})_{n\in\N}$ of flows with
well defined divergence that converge in $\cH_{2}$ to $\phi$, such
that $\left\langle \div\phi_{n},\div\phi_{n}\right\rangle \xrightarrow{n\to\infty}0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.365608+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ec3ca2079e5f5c394db831053464af315b6aacb83d100a84f5ef85be2e87273","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theo:jog loh of arXiv:2606.02472, 'Correlated uniform attachment trees'] For all $\varepsilon >0, K\in \N$ there exists $m \in \N$ such that for a uniform-attachment tree $(T_n)_{n\in \N}$ one has
