\end{multline*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.826281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ed597aa5f0bea2a0eb0ec88d813ca7deb51cebfb043607408b5b3935fe8f372","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Informal statement of \autoref{thm:exponentialconvergence} of arXiv:2606.24385, 'Gradient Mean-Field Dynamics with Measure-Valued States: Well-Posedness, Chaos, and Long-T'] Under additional assumptions imposing a gradient structure and uniform convexity of the drift fields, the nonlinear McKean--Vlasov dynamics admits a unique invariant measure $\mu_\infty$. Moreover, the flow converges exponentially fast:
