{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.521259+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f5a7b402e3d05810f13fe26dd879bac2ca62930d63565909356f348b871c337","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:u_t_small_t of arXiv:2512.17808, 'Zeros of polynomial powers under the heat flow'] For any fixed $z\in\mathbb{C}\setminus B$ and $t\to 0$, there exists one saddle point that converges to $\lambda_j$ for each initial zero $\lambda_1,\dots,\lambda_d$ of $P(z)$, and one saddle point that converges to $z$. For fixed $\tilde z\in\mathbb{C}$ and $j\le d$, set $z=\lambda_j+\tilde z \sqrt{\frac{t\alpha_j}{\alpha}}$ and assume $z\in\mathbb{C}\setminus B$ for all sufficiently small $t$. Then there exist branches of the saddle points satisfying
	\begin{align}
		u_t^{d+1}(z)&= \lambda_j + \sqrt{\frac{t\alpha_j}{\alpha}}
		u^+(\tilde z)+o(\sqrt t), \\
		u_t^j(z)&= \lambda_j + \sqrt{\frac{t\alpha_j}{\alpha}}
		u^-(\tilde z)+o(\sqrt t) , \\
		u_t^k(z)&=\lambda_k+\frac{\alpha_k t}{\alpha (\lambda_j-\lambda_k)}+o(t)\quad \text{for }k\neq j, d+1,
	\end{align}
	where $u^{\pm}(\tilde z)=\frac 1 2(\tilde z \pm \sqrt{\tilde z^2 -4})$ are defined in (equation eq:u_pm of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.418294+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f6490a5d315e61fe49d3b2d34b48caad5ddd410ef4fff34267d7cd12d917b6f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:MHn72 of arXiv:2511.15893, 'On a Class of Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Tessellations'] Let $v>0$ and $(s_1, \ell_1), (s_2, \ell_2)$ be two points such that $s_1<s_2$. Suppose the ellipses in ((eq:v_ellipses of the paper)) intersects at $(t(v), h(v))$. Then the area of the region $E^{s_1,v}_{\ell_1}\cup E^{s_2,v}_{\ell_2}$ is given by

