{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.740399+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6fcfeb7ce371d476df37883d8fce6a7e466c9f689aba00a0e216684a07966539","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 11 of arXiv:2605.02430, '\textbf{Scaling limit of the range of tree-valued branching random walks in random environ'] Let $(T, o)\ino \overline{\bbT}^\bullet$. When $\varnothing\ino T$ but $T\! \neq\!\{\varnothing\}$, we use the convention $\bbn \varnothing \bbn\! =\! \bbn T\bbn_-$. If $T\!=\!\{\varnothing\}$ then we set $\mathtt{cent}(T,o)\! =\! (T,o)$, and otherwise, we set
