{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:25:41.599399+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7008f90125c8a6e5012594a5f3b46a2a78308f344729a428b7659930393baaa6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:modulus of arXiv:2608.11931, '\texorpdfstring{Nonlinear parabolic characterizations of stochastic completeness at infini'] Let $I\subset\mathbb R$ be a compact interval of length $l$ and let $\phi \colon I\to\mathbb R$ be continuous and increasing.  Then there exists a continuous, strictly increasing, concave function $\omega \colon [0,l]\to[0,\infty)$ with $\omega(0)=0$ such that
