{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.943609+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71145115f90287544fdc3fe9493efc62bd69be600c5c856c13b41fe7bee7a9b6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 3 of arXiv:2608.01860, 'A Variational Characterization of a Gibbs Measure related to the Aviles-Giga Functional'] Let $\mu$ be a probability measure on $X$. Then the functional $F:L^\infty(X)\to \R$, $f\mapsto \log\left(\int_X\exp(f(x))\ \mu(dx)\right)$ is continuous, convex and for $\gamma\in P_\mu(X)\subset (L^\infty(X))'$ the Fenchel conjugate is of the form
