{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.659129+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71397f59b9837adc672373e25a053f262323026b1de7a34936eea3d16300e59c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 20 (An equivalent condition for matrix scalability; Thm. 4.1 in \cite{menon1969spectrum}) of arXiv:2604.23461, 'Scaling limit of Sinkhorn-rescaled Random Matrices \\ via Stability of Static Schrödinger '] Let $\A\in \R_{\ge 0}^{m\times n}$ be an $m\times n$ nonnegative matrix and let $(\r,\c)$ be an $m\times n$ margin with strictly positive row and column sums. Then the following are equivalent:
