{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.415271+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7157694a47a4be7471ebad5d7d3b6b7a55d272471ccc72eb0a4dd62464fd3843","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2608.27904, 'Instantons, indefinite 4-manifolds, and Dehn surgery'] Let $Y$ be a rational homology sphere. \textit{Abelian data} on $Y$ consists of a pair $\mathfrak a = (\sigma, p)$, where \[\sigma: \mathfrak A(Y) \to 2\mathbb Z, \quad p: \mathfrak A(Y) \to H^2(Y;\mathbb Z)\] are functions satisfying the following hypotheses: 
\begin{itemize}
\item For $\alpha = \{x, -x\} \in \mathfrak A(Y)$, we demand $\sigma(\alpha) \equiv \dim_{\mathbb R} H^1(Y; \mathbb C_{2x}) \mod 4$. 
\item For $\alpha = \{x, -x\} \in \mathfrak A(Y)$, we demand $p(\alpha) \in \{x, -x\}$.
\end{itemize}
A class $z\in H^2(Y;\mathbb Z)$ determines a flat complex line bundle on $Y$, and hence a local system $\mathbb C_z$; here $\mathbb C_{2x}$ denotes the bundle corresponding to $2x$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.077950+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_715832c74f220f60db8bbb7cde3a937608ba1f2f5eb22717bff77734dde0ebb0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem A. lem: precompactness in tau for hatC of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] A non-empty subset $\{\mathcal{X}_{\alpha} = (S_{\alpha}, d^{\alpha}, \rho_{\alpha}, f_{\alpha}) \mid \alpha \in \mathcal{A} \}$
  of $\mathfrak{M}_{c}(\tau^{\widehat{C}_{c}(M, \cdot)})$ 
  is precompact if and only if the following conditions are satisfied.
  \begin{enumerate} [label = (\roman*)]
    \item 
