{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.010144+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71794f69b0177487013489875c0036e5035516d6c3b67b927d86e8063bf54c31","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 10 of arXiv:2609.02850, 'Canonical-row Chern flow on Bott--Samelson towers:\\ realizable-volume models for Schubert'] Let $|\alpha|=d$, let $i\ne j$, and suppose $\alpha_i,\alpha_j\ge1$.  Then
