{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.658318+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_718fb2a19a172e9de76b739bf29c24cbc8af1956e67ac830d0a7e077e7aa648b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 (Bulk Rigidity of the Sample Covariance Matrix) of arXiv:2604.23461, 'Scaling limit of Sinkhorn-rescaled Random Matrices \\ via Stability of Static Schrödinger '] Suppose Assumptions \ref{assump:random_matrix}--\ref{assump:bounded_cost} hold and the aspect ratio is bounded: $\gamma \le m/n \le \gamma^{-1}$ for some $\gamma \in (0,1]$.  Let $\xi := \min_{i,j,k,\ell} \frac{\Var(X_{ij})}{\Var(X_{k\ell})}>0$.  
		Let $\nu$ be the measure from the Dyson equation \eqref{eq:dyson_system} for the variance profile $\mathbf{S}$ in \eqref{eq:variance_profile_def}, with atom $\pi_*=\max\{0, 1-n/m\}$ and $\operatorname{supp}(\nu)\subseteq[0,4]$. 
		Fix $\eps,\Delta > 0$ and $\eps_* > 0$. Let $\eps_{\textup{cov}}$ be the covariance deviation error defined in Lemma \ref{lem:rescaled_approx} and let $\mathcal{E}_{2}$ be as in Theorem \ref{thm:first_approximation_rescaled}.
		For any $D > 0$, there exist constants $C_3=C_{3}(D,\eps, \Delta,\eps_*, \xi, K)$ and $C_4=C_{4}(D,\eps,\eps_*, \xi, K)$ such that the following hold:
		\begin{description}
			\item[(i)] $m \ne n$ (rectangular): 
			\begin{align}
				\P\left( \{ \X \in \mathcal{S}(\r,\c) \} \cap \left\{ \exists \tau \in (\Delta,4] : \pi(\tau) \ge \eps_*, |\lambda_{i(\tau)}({\A}{\A}^T) - \tau| \ge \frac{m^{\eps}}{m} + \eps_{\textup{cov}} \right\} \right) \le \P(\mathcal{E}_2^c) + \frac{C_3}{m^D}.
			\end{align}

			\item[(ii)] $m = n$ (square):
			\begin{align}
				\P\left( \{ \X \in \mathcal{S}(\r,\c) \} \cap \left\{ \exists \tau \in (0,4] : \pi(\tau) \ge \eps_*, |\lambda_{i(\tau)}({\A}{\A}^T) - \tau| \ge \frac{m^{\eps}}{m}\left(\sqrt{\tau} + \frac{1}{m}\right) + \eps_{\textup{cov}} \right\} \right) \le \P(\mathcal{E}_2^c) + \frac{C_4}{m^D}.
			\end{align}

			\item[(iii)] For $m$ sufficiently large, there are asymptotically no eigenvalues far outside the support of $\nu$:
			\begin{align}
				\P\left( \{ \X \in \mathcal{S}(\r,\c) \} \cap \left\{ \sigma({\A}{\A}^T) \cap \left\{ \tau : \text{dist}(\tau, \text{supp}(\nu)) \ge \eps_* + \eps_{\textup{cov}} \right\} \ne \emptyset \right\} \right) \le \P(\mathcal{E}_2^c) + \frac{1}{m^D}.
			\end{align}
		\end{description} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

