{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.286269+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71f4f781fb082cba4ec0578b90e1797eb3b65e8e438681c0b792f89fbfda5729","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi prok of arXiv:2603.21634, 'Individual-based stochastic model with unbounded growth, birth and death rates: a tightnes'] The Prokhorov distance is defined for every $\mu,\nu \in M_{1}(\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+})$ by
\begin{align*}
d_{P}^{1}(\mu,\nu) := \inf \{ \varepsilon >0, \forall A \in \mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+}), \hspace{0.1 cm}  \mu(A) \leq \nu(A^{\varepsilon}) + \varepsilon, \hspace{0.1 cm} \nu(A) \leq \mu(A^{\varepsilon}) + \varepsilon \},
\end{align*}
where $\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+})$ is the usual Borel $\sigma$-algebra on $\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+}$, and $A^{\varepsilon} := \{ y \in \mathbb{R}^{*}_{+}, \inf_{x \in A} |x-y| < \varepsilon \}.$ For any positive function $w$, we extend this definition to the $w$-Prokhorov distance $d_{P}^{w}$, defined for every $\mu,\nu \in \mathcal{M}_{w}(\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+})$ by
\begin{align*}
d_{P}^{w}(\mu,\nu) := d_{P}^{1}(w*\mu,w*\nu),
\end{align*} 
where $w*\mu$ is the usual pushforward of $\mu$ by $w$ (\textit{i.e.} for every measurable function $f$, $\langle w*\mu, f \rangle := \langle \mu, w f \rangle$).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:03:59.345589+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71f9892b338764d660a25f1d50e0ba4b3534a55fb12e360aaf2f309a947ed14d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition recovery of arXiv:2507.08757, 'Strong existence and uniqueness of the tilt-indexed Busemann process in the planar corner '] Given real weights $\omega=(\omega_x)_{x\in\mathbb{Z}^2}\in\mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{Z}^2}$, a function $A:\mathbb{Z}^2\to\mathbb{R}$ is said to \emph{recover} the weights $\omega$ if it satisfies the following \emph{recovery property}:
\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}
A(x,x+e_1)\wedgeA(x,x+e_2)=\omega_x\quad\text{for all $x\in\mathbb{Z}^2$}.
\end{aligned}\qedhere\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

