{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.760982+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_722d713f9c809d5e1632dc73c95d92588e7d63eab7542a6b084fc190d5f82836","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:canonical-borel-compression-traces of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] For every $0<a<b$, bounded real Borel function $v$, and $k\ge1$, the map
