{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.161633+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_724fa7d70b8e902256c0d8452ab41cd0b5b83cddd0fb2f78e911959473d698dc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2606.29512, '2606.29512'] There exists a constant $N>0$ depending only on $d$, $r$ and $\frc$ 
 such that if $u$ is a solution to \eqref{eq1}-\eqref{bin1} from the restricted 
 Leray-Hopf class, satisfying 
