{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.279844+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72596e69c7d04840daa4326f144da026d8f4589e07ff390b8a95d57bd7b96f21","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro: Moment Bounds on hat q for JSQ of arXiv:2603.14163, '\LARGE \bf Tail Bounds for Queues with Abandonment: Constant, Moderate, Large Deviations, '] \textnormal{(Moment Bounds on $\hat{q}_{\Sigma}$)}

    Under the assumption (ass:heavy_overload of the paper), with $\hat{q}_{\Sigma}:= \sum_i q_i - \frac{\lambda-\mu}{\gamma}$, we have the moment bounds for any $p\geq 1, p\in \mathbb{R}$:
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{E}[|\hat{q}_{\Sigma}|^p]^{1/p} &\leq \max\{C_{\lambda,\mu,n}'' \cdot\frac{\sqrt{p}}{\sqrt{\gamma}} + C_{\lambda,\mu,n}'\cdot p, \: n(A_{\lambda,\mu,n} +\frac{1}{n}) \frac{p}{\log(1+\frac{n\gamma}{\lambda}p)}\} \\
        \mathbb{E}[|\hat{q}_{\Sigma}|^p]^{1/p} &\geq  C_{4,\lambda,\mu} \exp(-8(15+A_{\lambda,\mu})\frac{\lambda}{\gamma p}) \frac{p}{\log(1+\frac{p\gamma}{\lambda})}
    \end{align*}
    Constants $C_{\lambda,\mu,n}'$, $C_{\lambda,\mu,n}''$ and $A_{\lambda,\mu,n}$ are defined in (equation eq: subexpo L-p norm JSQ of the paper) and (equation eq: MGF upper bound JSQ of the paper), respectively. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

