{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:43:55.658416+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73c818935bfd537ec38304baedcac50c9281e8fb81e722456d76c15909682f16","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm oracle_split of arXiv:2604.07183, 'Stopping on the last success with unknown odds: asymptotic minimax optimality of the plug-'] Fix~$p_0\in(0,1)$ and~$a\in(0,1)$, and let~$M_0$, $\mathcal B_{p_0}$ and~$\Delta_p$ be as in Theorem~(thm:finite_oracle_ineq_p0 of the paper). Then, (i) there exist positive constants~$C_1(p_0)$, $C_2(p_0,a)$ and~$c(p_0,a)$ such that, for all~$n\ge2$ and all~$p\in[p_0,1)$,
\begin{equation}

V_n(p)-W_n^{\pi_a}(p)
\le
C_1(p_0) \Delta_p\,e^{-2\lfloor an\rfloor\Delta_p^2}
+
C_2(p_0,a)e^{-c(p_0,a)n}
.
\end{equation}
(ii) Consequently, for~$p_0\le\frac12$, there exists a positive constant~$C(p_0)$ such that
\begin{equation}

\sup_{p\in[p_0,1)}\bigl(V_n(p)-W_n^{\pi_a}(p)\bigr)
\le
