{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.495877+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73d51e7b891d030f296cb693b4394dde8cc6dad81a5a4e361e01cdb733f627b5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma smoothing-properties-clean of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] Let $C$ be an absolutely continuous
copula with density $c$, and let $C_{\varepsilon }$ be defined by (\ref
{822.2})--((822.3 of the paper)). Then, for each $\varepsilon >0$:

\begin{enumerate}
\item[(1)] $C_\varepsilon$ is a copula with continuous density $
c_\varepsilon $;

\item[(2)] if $C_{1}\leq _{c}C_{2}$ in concordance order and the smoothing
kernels are $TP_{2}$, then 
\begin{equation}
C_{1,\varepsilon }\leq _{c}C_{2,\varepsilon };  
\end{equation}

\item[(3)] if $c$ is continuous, then $c_{\varepsilon }\rightarrow c$
