{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.384717+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7403c990acff911672b156044e9e13239bb4366e3e490e6f4735055aecae6828","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:T.bds.sup of arXiv:2411.02046, 'Speed of Convergence and Moderate Deviations of FPP on Random Geometric Graphs'] Let $d \geq 2$, $r>r_c$, and $\beta, \accentset{\rule{.4em}{.5pt}}{\beta}>0$ be as defined in (lm:T.bar.all,lm:T.bds of the paper). If (equation A2 of the paper) is satisfied, then there exist $c,c'>0$ such that, for all $t'>1$ and any ~$t>\beta t'$,
