{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.683158+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74206816192cd2e3076de7cd43f84766cd4cc190e63561f01bdb020f57a628e4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:asymp_miss_rate of arXiv:2412.00279, 'Optimal local storage policy based on stochastic intensities and its large scale behavior'] Suppose $\left\{L_N\right\}_{N\geqslant 1}$ is uniformly integrable. Let $c\in(0,1]$ be such that $1-c$ is a continuity point of $Q_\infty$, and that $\theta^*:=Q_\infty(1-c)\notin D_L\cdot D_{G_0}$. If $C/N\to c$ as $N\to\infty$, then
