{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.820672+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74b8842aa23f22f735f558831f4820959062d3dc65a895fce88ab2b2bbfd1bcb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Useful proposition of arXiv:2607.18531, 'Doubly reflected BSDEs driven by Inhomogeneous simple Lévy processes: Applications to gene'] Assume given two $\mathbb{F}$-stopping times $\tau$, $\sigma$ such that $\tau \in \mathcal{T}_0^T$ and $\sigma \in \mathcal{T}_{\tau}^T$. Then, for any $\beta >2$, there exists a constant $\mathfrak{C}_{\beta}>0$ such that,
	\begin{equation*}
		\begin{split}
			&\mathbb{E}^{\mathcal{F}_\tau} \left[ \sup_{\tau \leq t \leq \sigma} e^{\beta A_t} \left| \overline{Y}_t \right|^2  \right]+ \mathbb{E}^{\mathcal{F}_\tau}\left[\int_\tau^\sigma e^{\beta A_s} \left| \overline{Y}_s \right|^2 dA_s \right]\\
			&\qquad+\mathbb{E}^{\mathcal{F}_\tau}\left[\int_\tau^\sigma e^{\beta A_s}  \left|\overline{Z}_s \right|^2 ds \right]+\mathbb{E}^{\mathcal{F}_\tau}\left[\int_\tau^\sigma e^{\beta A_s}   \|\overline{V}_{s}\|^2_\lambda ds \right] \\
			&  \leq \mathfrak{C}_{\beta}\Biggl\{ \mathbb{E}^{\mathcal{F}_\tau}\left[e^{\beta A_\sigma} \left| \overline{Y}_{\sigma} \right|^2\right]+\mathbb{E}^{\mathcal{F}_\tau}\left[\int_{\tau}^\sigma e^{\beta A_s} \left|\dfrac{ \bar{f}(s,Y^{\prime}_s,Z^{\prime}_s,V'_s)}{\alpha_s}\right|^2 ds \right]\\
			&\qquad +\mathbb{E}^{\mathcal{F}_\tau}\left[\int_{\tau}^{\sigma}e^{\beta A_s}\left\{ \bar{L}_{s-}^{+}dK^{+}_s+\bar{L}_{s-}^{-} dK^{\prime,+}_s \right\}\right] 
			+\mathbb{E}^{\mathcal{F}_\tau}\left[\int_{\tau}^{\sigma}e^{\beta A_s}\left\{\bar{U}_{s-}^{-}dK^{-}_s+\bar{U}_{s-}^{+}dK^{\prime,-}_s \right\}\right] \Biggr\}.
		\end{split}
	\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.356403+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74bba7ab3a2d67173eb139b2d14aad4980829232fa913e8ace80be232d43fc78","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2506.18313, 'A stochastic model for the diffusion of competing opinions with trend-following, oppositio'] Assume that $(\xi_n)$ satisfies, for some integer $m\ge 1$ and for some real number $h > 2m$, that
