{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.338611+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74bc2f81d0fc1b33d9d78846f5785c6b3856bd7c8a294e9a2983c0bd7449878b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:wp:marginalSDE of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Suppose $(U, W)$ satisfy Assumption (as:results:lyapunov of the paper) and $(\mu, \gamma, \mathbf{X})$ is a linear growth solution to $\kappa$-MLFE{} on $[0, T]$ with potentials $(U, W)$  and initial condition $\lambda \in \mathcal{Q}_{\kappa, d}$. Then for all $t \in [0, T]$, the edge time marginal $\bar{\mu}_t$ satisfies $\bar{\mu}_t = \mathcal{L}(\bar{X}_0(t), \bar{X}_1(t))$, where $(\bar{X}_0, \bar{X}_1)$ solve the following SDE with initial condition $\bar{\lambda}$:
        \begin{equation}
        \begin{aligned}
            d{\bar{X}}_0(t) &= \gamma(t, \bar{X}_0(t), \bar{X}_1(t)) dt + \sqrt{2}d\tilde{B}_0(t), \\
            d{\bar{X}}_1(t) &= \gamma(t, \bar{X}_1(t), \bar{X}_0(t)) dt + \sqrt{2}d\tilde{B}_1(t), 
                    \end{aligned}

    \end{equation}
    where $\tilde{B}_0, \tilde{B}_1$ are independent $d$-dimensional Brownian motions. Moreover, we have
    \begin{equation*}
    \int_0^T \int_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d \times \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d} \frac{|\nabla_{(x_0, x_1)} \bar{\mu}_t(x_0, x_1)|^2}{\bar{\mu}_t(x_0, x_1)} dx_0 dx_1 dt < \infty.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:10.186680+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74c1b02a41544a1e88e8b201918a433463d22c7d28477406f0b57b644800ed47","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 122 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] Under the above assumption
suppose also that the first  assumption of
