{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.318989+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74f705f270a4307b415125aa80b06067d75530ca44040600ba45c40bfa04d4ed","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma S-cocompleteness-repr of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] A $T$-$\infty$-category $\mathcal C$ is $S$-cocomplete if and only if the following three conditions are satisfied: 
\begin{enumerate}
\item The $T$-$\infty$-category $\mathcal C$ is fiberwise cocomplete. 
\item For every morphism $s\colon A\to B\in S$, the restriction $s^*\colon\mathcal C(B)\to \mathcal C(A)$ admits a left adjoint $s_{!}$. 
\item For any pullback
    \[
        \begin{tikzcd}
            X\arrow[d,"s'"']\arrow[dr,pullback]\arrow[r,"f'"] & A\arrow[d,"s"]\\
            C\arrow[r,"f"'] & B
        \end{tikzcd}
    \]
    in $\PSh(T)$ with $s$ in $S$ and $C\in T$, the restriction along $s'$ admits a left adjoint $s'_!$, and the Beck-Chevalley map $s'_!f'^*\to f^*s_!$ is an equivalence. 
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.471797+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74fa9369363fa094fc55226463978ef9274a3be053aa9e44212c06a1ba4dc40c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 105 (Transport equation satisfied by $\partialmodquant{\tanderY^{N-1}}$) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] The following identity holds:
