{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.802997+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7504d4c7a5558483f5f7274801f2828eca47d887f2a6fa9602521b8931dd048d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm l:cond-var-comparison of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] Let $X$ be a random variable such that $\mathbb{P}(|X|>m) \leqslant Ce^{-cm^{3/2}}$ for some $C,c>0$ and all $m\geqslant0$.
    Let $Y,Z$ be random $d$-dimensional vectors on the same probability space as $X$, for some $d\geqslant 1$.
    We have
    \begin{align*}
        \Bigl|
            \mathbb{E}[\Var(X|Y)] - \mathbb{E}[\Var(X|Z)]
        \Bigr|
        \leqslant C'\,\mathbb{P}(Y\ne Z)^{0.9}
    \end{align*} 
    for some $C'>0$ depending only on $C,c$.
    (The exponent $0.9$ can be replaced with any $\kappa<1$.) (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.617168+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75090fd5a7f9c83d9f72b6a4cff79c0c8eb95da937f8d506c742d4391048bd90","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:face-integral of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] We say that a vector $\vec\ell\in \mathbb{R}^s$ is \emph{of convergent type} for the face $\cal F$ if the integral
