{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:08.969583+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7530babf394737b5a7699e67dc9b6ff097b231e1e19a509cde4852e64d5e9ab2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Definition_Bessel_function of arXiv:2411.10829, 'Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble and its Laplace transform'] For any reals $\lambda_1\ge \lambda_2\ge \dots \ge \lambda_N$, the \emph{multivariate Bessel function} $\mathcal B_{(\lambda_1, \ldots, \lambda_N)}(x_1, \ldots, x_N; \beta)$ is a function of $N$ complex variables $x_1,\dots,x_N$ defined as
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal B_{(\lambda_1,\dots,\lambda_N)}(x_1,\dots,x_N;\,\beta)= \mathbb E_{\{y^k_i\}}\!\left[\exp\left(\sum_{k=1}^{N} x_k
 \cdot \left(\sum_{i=1}^{k} y_i^k-\sum_{j=1}^{k-1} y_j^{k-1}\right)  \right) \right],
\end{equation}
where the expectation is with respect to $\beta$-corners process with top row $(\lambda_1,\dots,\lambda_N)$ from Definition (def_betacorner of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:59:24.050109+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7531230eb273b7711c00ec73eaebfc6055c9290d9870bb93ab57f32f4ed92de3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:subcritical of arXiv:2608.30831, 'Sharp discrete Hardy constants in dimensions three and four\\ and strict upper bounds from'] For $N=3,4$, let $h_N$ be the supersolution in Lemma~(lem:N3 of the paper) or
Lemma~(lem:N4 of the paper), respectively, and define
\begin{equation}
 V_N(n):=\frac{(-\Delta_{\!d} h_N)(n)}{h_N(n)}-\frac{A_N}{|n|^2},
 \qquad n\in X_N.
\end{equation}
Then $V_N(n)>0$ for every $n\in X_N$, and
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal E_N[u]-A_N\mathcal D_N[u]
 \ge\sum_{n\in X_N}V_N(n)|u(n)|^2
\end{equation}
for every finitely supported $u$ with $u(0)=0$.
Thus the form on the left is subcritical, although $C(N)=A_N$.
In particular, $A_N|n|^{-2}$ is not a pointwise optimal Hardy weight.","status":"unverified"}

