{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.731533+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7593a98790fea569a729d73804d4e0c945eb7d6fbc30363cda63f7315f025d0f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem ratesofconv of arXiv:2412.00593, 'A new approach to strong convergence II.\\The classical ensembles'] There exists a linear functional $\nu_m$ on $\mathcal{P}$ for every $m\in\mathbb{Z}_+$ 
