{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.289871+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7669b81d26619c6bf8903fef22fa96f6256241e8115fa62cfeff2f7499a18e0a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop tensor of arXiv:2602.17579, 'Non-equilibrium functional inequalities for finite Markov chains'] Let $d \geq 1$. For each $i\in \{1,\ldots,d\}$ let $\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}_i$ be a finite state space, $M_i$ be an irreducible  generator on $\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}_i$ and $\zeta_i\in \mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}_i)$. Define 
    \begin{equation*}
    \displaystyle
        \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}} \coloneqq\prod_{i=1}^d \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}_i, \quad
        \zeta \coloneqq\zeta_1\otimes\ldots\otimes \zeta_d \in \mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}), \quad
        M \coloneqq\frac1d\sum_{i=1}^d \underbrace{I\otimes \ldots I}_{i-1} \otimes M_i \otimes \underbrace{I\otimes\ldots\otimes I}_{d-i} \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^{|\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}| \times |\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}|}.
    \end{equation*}
    Then, $M$ is an irreducible generator on $\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}$ and $\zeta$ satisfies the gPI and gLSI with constants 
    \begin{equation*}
        \alpha_{\gPI}(\zeta, M) =\frac1d \min_{1 \leq i \leq d} \alpha_{\gPI}(\zeta_i, M_i), \ \ \alpha_{\gLSI}(\zeta, M) =\frac1d \min_{1 \leq i \leq d}\alpha_{\gLSI} (\zeta_i, M_i).
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.969246+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_766ca6b80aad8f5585756d6d1aa6baa7ac97059de4fae6076f0616b26dca10fe","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 33 of arXiv:2606.09904, 'Non-explosion principles for branched rough differential equations with unbounded coeffici'] For any \(f \in \CF_{N - 1}\) and \(n \le N - |f|\), we have that 
  \begin{equation}
    \|D^n \partial^f_X \phi(Y)\|_{\infty; I_r} \lesssim l(r)^{(1 - n)\alpha + \delta}
  \end{equation}
  for any \(r, \delta > 0\). Moreover, in the special case where \(n = 1\), we have that 
  \begin{equation}
    \|D\partial^f_X \phi(Y)\|_{\infty; I_r} \lesssim (\log l(r))^{\gamma \Lambda_1([f])}. 
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.364739+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7677aafde325501088cc572dfbc33ad73ee444fca8dfdf1ac21e72b967285fe3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:continuous-version of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] Let $s \in [0,1]$, $k\in\mathbb{N}$ and $f \in \mathcal{C}^1({\mathbb{R}}^{kd})$. Then, for each $x_1,\ldots,x_k \in {\mathbb{R}}^d, t_1,\ldots,t_k \in [s,1]$, with probability one, we have
    \begin{equs}                       
        \mathbb{E}_s f(\phi^{s,x_1}_{t_1},\ldots,\phi^{s,x_k}_{t_k})= \mathbb{E}_s^Bf(\phi^{s,x_1}_{t_1},\ldots,\phi^{s,x_k}_{t_k}). 
    \end{equs}
    Moreover, the random fields in (equation eq:swap_filtrations of the paper) have continuous modifications in the variables $x_1,\ldots,x_k$ and $t_1,\ldots,t_k$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.617951+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_767a52eba0fddac78e466ae02590662bfecfbe3a42e317195234418189ceefe0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 27 of arXiv:2608.25785, 'Proper Actions on Homogeneous Spaces of the Upper Triangular Matrix Group via Coarse Geome'] Regard $\mathbb{R}_{>0}$ as a group under multiplication, equip it with the LR-coarse structure and 
