{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.251597+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77272de8afa12ded33352e1d73abc338b917f4d865fe4f00e7cd07adce402ec0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:supermartingale of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\mathcal{Y},\hat\mathcal{Z},T)$ be a sequential gamble space.
  A sequence $\{X_t:\mathcal{Y}^t\to\overline{\mathbb{R}}\}_{t\leq T}$ is a \emph{game-theoretic supermartingale} if for all $t< T$ and situations $s\in\mathcal{Y}^t$, we have 
  \begin{align}

    \overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}}[ X_{t+1} \mid s] \leq X_t(s)~,
  \end{align}
  and a \emph{game-theoretic martingale} if $\textsf{\textbf{E}}[ X_{t+1} \mid s] = X_t(s)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.518414+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_772dfa16d66db1a2a10a7c794dba14442fc445969c7c8c393d9fb3aaf3c25125","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:biskup_iterative_renormalisation of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{lem:second_iterative_renormalisation}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 1$ and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel satisfying $J(x,y) = \Omega (d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha})$ with $\alpha \in (0,2)$.

    Let $\beta > \beta_c$, and let $((\Tile{i}{j})_{j \geq 0})_{i \geq 0}$ be the renormalisation scheme in \thref{def:renorm_scheme_2}.

