{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.238057+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_779b4651bceaac6c8a373d985f2413b0ca49a5c9d55e2f5743cb8302e8c4f637","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:iter_int_of_mal_der of arXiv:2604.22528, 'Malliavin calculus for signatures with applications to finance'] For all $i_1, \ldots, i_n \in \{1, \ldots, d\}$ and $j_1, \ldots, j_n \in \{0, 1, \ldots, d\}$, we have
    \begin{equation*}
        \int_{0 \le s_1 \le \ldots \le s_n \le t} 
