{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.621468+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77d82c5a64d60c42568271e6dfca031c7594629bbe38f5e6d14bde43c0ee5e00","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 179 (The coercivity of the velocity $L^2$-controlling quantities) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $\totalfluxcontrolvelocity_N(\ubar,u), \dots, \weakspacetimetransvelocitycontrol_N(\ubar,u)$ be the velocity $L^2$-controlling quantities from Def.\,\eqref{E:UNIFIEDCOMMUTATORVELOCITYNULLFLUXL2CONTROLLINGQUANTITY}--\eqref{E:UNIFIEDCOMMUTATORVELOCITYSPACETIMEL2TRANSCONTROLLINGQUANTITY},
