{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.869139+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78830ed3190f5c66ee5099067f516b291d81a79e52a8d3b525af08490f5b5847","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop regularforitselfreflecting of arXiv:2605.06488, 'Continuous-state branching processes with L\'evy-Khintchine drift-interaction: Laplace dua'] Let $Y^{\mathrm{e}0}$ be the extension of the minimal $\mathrm{CBDI}(\hat\Psi,\Psi)$  at $0$ with the latter regular (Theorem~(thm2zero of the paper)). The boundary $0$ is non-sticky for $Y^{\mathrm{e}0}$ if and only if $\infty$ is regular for itself for $X^{\mathrm{e}\infty}$: 
\begin{center}
$\mathbb{P}_{\infty}(R^{\mathrm{e}\infty}=0)=1$ where $R^{\mathrm{e}\infty}:=\inf\{t>0:X_t^{\mathrm{e}\infty}=\infty\}$.     
\end{center}
Similarly, by exchanging the roles of the processes and the boundaries, $\infty$ is non-sticky for $X^{\mathrm{e}\infty}$ if and only if $0$ is regular-for-itself for $Y^{\mathrm{e}0}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.464491+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7883779799d7c289f9800d6dfccc97ba0b0720b28bc86489c3628a6d037ff774","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 (Approximation) of arXiv:2608.17540, 'Pathwise stability for one-dimensional SDEs driven by Brownian motion and a symmetric stab'] For all $x\in\R$, $\delta\ge2$, and $\eps\in(0,1)$,
