{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.551613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_788ae44b7bce51764ea1720a29a41cc5d23a33327f97eee6d2f9ce699cd275ac","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 (Exponential law of large numbers for the Stein velocity) of arXiv:2608.28827, 'Quantitative Target Convergence and Uniform-in-Time\\ Propagation of Chaos for Langevin-Re'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:core-target} and \ref{ass:concentration}, together with either kernel assumption, there are $\lambda>0$ and $1\le C_G<\infty$, independent of $N$ and $t$, such that
