{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.276748+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78a30dc7236aedd6d74904c0036fad3bdbfc16057661ccb106f12d02db3cc4d8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 (Signed Bell generating function) of arXiv:2606.22066, 'A Bessel-zero obstruction to hyperbolic complete monotonicity of noncentral chi-square den'] With \(d_m\) as in Proposition~\ref{prop:bell-obstruction},
\begin{equation}

\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}
\mathcal B_n(d_1,\dots,d_n)\frac{z^n}{n!}
=
e^{-bz}F_a(b\theta z).
\end{equation}
Equivalently,
\begin{equation}

\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}
(-1)^n\mathcal B_n(d_1,\dots,d_n)\frac{t^n}{n!}
=
e^{bt}F_a(-b\theta t).
\end{equation}
Moreover, equivalently as an ordinary Taylor expansion,
\begin{equation}

e^{bt}F_a(-b\theta t)
=
\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}
\frac{b^n}{(a)_n}L_n^{(a-1)}(\theta)t^n,
\end{equation}
where \(L_n^{(a-1)}\) denotes the generalized Laguerre polynomial, with normalization
\begin{equation}
L_n^{(a-1)}(\theta)
=
\frac{(a)_n}{n!}\,{}_1F_1(-n;a;\theta).
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}

(-1)^n\mathcal B_n(d_1,\dots,d_n)
=
\frac{n!b^n}{(a)_n}L_n^{(a-1)}(\theta).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:27.915449+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78a3e110f8bce1aecc49bf682b2aa596c20660ff9d497f670954de5ab38bd81f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 (Concentration of Lipschitz functions on the sphere \cite{vershynin2018high} (section 5.1.2)) of arXiv:2607.12667, 'Phase Transition of Eigenvalues of Covariances from the Spiked Mixture Model in High-dimen'] Consider a random vector $\y \sim \textnormal{Unif}(\mathbb{S}^{d-1})$ and a Lipschitz function $f$: $\mathbb{S}^{d-1} \to \mathbb{R}$, with Lipschitz constant $\|f\|_{\Lip}$. For every $t\geq 0$ and $d$ large enough, 
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{P}\{|f(\y) - \E f(\y)|\geq t\} \leq 2 \exp\left(- \frac{cdt^2}{\|f\|^2_{\Lip}}\right),
