{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:11:57.321556+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78adce845ddf8bf1cd83bcd9d5eb911a1e7e72528a5ce589ce9a40aaa14a2b89","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 (Exact-shell Equivalence) of arXiv:2607.23526, 'Equivalence of Canonical and Microcanonical Ensembles for Euclidean Lattices'] Suppose $H(\Lambda)$ is lattice with maximal span $h>0$. Let $E_N\in\im(H_N)$ satisfy $E_N/N\to u>0$, and set $\beta=m^{-1}(u)$. Then for every $k\geq1$,
\begin{equation}
\left\|(\pi_k)_*\mu^{\sh}_{N,E_N}-p_{\beta}^{\otimes k}\right\|_{\TV}\to0,\quad N\to+\infty.
\end{equation}
Moreover, let $u_N=E_N/N$ and $\beta_N=m^{-1}(u_N)$, then
\begin{equation}
g_N(E_N)=\frac{hZ(\beta_N)^Ne^{\beta_NE_N}}{\sqrt{2\pi N\sigma^2(\beta_N)}}(1+o(1)).
\end{equation}
Consequently, the thermodynamic limit
\begin{equation}
\lim_{N\to+\infty}\frac{1}{N}R^{\sh}_{N,E_N}=\psi(\beta)+\beta u=s(u).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

