{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.038152+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78cdc01d283d77442860990c2161e49a43dcf1e503d9685c737c5dd08d35893d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 11 (Free Brownian motion) of arXiv:2606.31528, 'Well-posedness and stationary distribution of free stochastic differential equations'] A stochastic process $\{W_t\}_{t\ge 0}$ is called a \emph{free Brownian motion} if it satisfies 
