{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.301221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78d3de707da80e037625b5c1de9db4f6ed16c93f9b8be19fa2edb9f3504aac28","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 21 (Baseline-corrected posterior cloning) of arXiv:2608.21709, 'Posterior Information Dynamics of Diffusion Models for Linear Inverse Problems'] Define the conditional cloning observable
\begin{equation}

\phi_r(t)
=
\E_{Z_t\mid r}
\left[
\sum_{c\in\{\pm1\}}P(C=c\mid Z_t,r)^2
\right].
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}

\phi_r(\infty)
=
\alpha_+^2+
\alpha_-^2
=
\sum_cP(C=c\mid r)^2.
