{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.873507+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78ec493cf34fa43daa2d1f18c583186424327e9d49e26dbda8f00b5a800c9719","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2608.26765, 'Beyond Client Averaging: A Client-Independent Second-Order Stationary-Bias Component in St'] Under the assumptions of (sec:setting of the paper), including full participation, for fixed $H\ge2$ there exist $\gamma_{0,H}>0$ and $C_H<\infty$, independent of $N$ and $\gamma$, such that for every $N\ge2$ and $0<\gamma\le\gamma_{0,H}$,
