{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.317440+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78eecebf7b93ecfcd69792c67bacadc601651986c871c95837d93320b81d2a13","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:continuous curve of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] Let $x_0\in U\setminus \{x_1,\ldots,x_k\}$. For $\mathbb{P}_{\vec{x}}$-almost every $\mathcal{D}$ and any $0<\beta<1$, there exist a constant $c_5=c_5(\beta,\mathcal{D},x_0)>0$ such that for all $x\in \mathcal{D}$, we can construct a rectifiable curve $\gamma_x \subseteq \mathcal{D}$ connecting $x$ and $x_0$ satisfying
