{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:11:57.323803+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78f3237e095ceb0889f4c95fb1f2a61d46a2738ba957d3300207b4f1a3105c11","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 17 (Windowed Equivalence) of arXiv:2607.23526, 'Equivalence of Canonical and Microcanonical Ensembles for Euclidean Lattices'] Suppose $H(\Lambda)$ is nonlattice. Fix $\Delta>0$, let $E_N\in\R$ satisfy $E_N/N\to u>0$, and set $\beta=m^{-1}(u)$. Then $G_N(E_N,\Delta)>0$ for all sufficiently large $N$, and for every fixed $k\geq1$,
\begin{equation}
