{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.779503+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7921e930822f555700f9cc89d2247eef3673c6db4916bebcd96203a13447478d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary Cor:PW_dabrRobin of arXiv:2609.02325, 'A Payne-Weinberger inequality\\for quantum dot Dirac operators'] Let $\Omega\subset \mathbb{R}^2$ be a bounded simply connected domain with $C^2$~boundary and let~$\delta_\Omega$ denote its isoperimetric deficit, as in (equation Eq:IsopDeficit of the paper).
