{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.806836+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_79da2fd329bf6983187e842187afab2e5a2b5ab2e646574012a8ad46e5e6186e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem HMbsde of arXiv:2606.24304, 'Quantitative Homogenization of PDEs with Neumann boundary conditions: a probabilistic appr'] Suppose that the  conditions of Theorem (HM_RSDE_W of the paper) and  \textbf{(H.3)} hold.
Then for every $0\leqslant t<T$, 
as $\varepsilon \to 0$, $U^{\varepsilon,t, x,y}$ converges  in distribution 
