{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.443571+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_79f4346e871573e0793f17e32a1a8982bfc14df9a8d38f0f2faab9c8afe8a525","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem prop:monotonicity of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] For any finite set $\Lambda \subseteq \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^2$, any collection of conductances $J , \widetilde J \in [0, \infty)^{E(\Lambda)}$ and any $x \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^2$, we have
