{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.421860+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a06bc7b3dad234dc19ffe85e743358e4af2497fc65362f5951ac867440beac3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:matching of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[definition]{def:matching}
Let \(G\sim\mathcal N(0,1)\).  We say that \(\xi\) matches the Gaussian moments through order \(m\) if
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb E\xi^r=\mathbb E G^r,
 \qquad r=1,\ldots,m.
\end{equation}
In particular, for \(m\ge2\), \(\xi\) is centered and has variance one.","status":"unverified"}

