{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.768248+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a8218a1513e8a606c9a310dc53266ad4614797250e5c105fec68e794fcc8e7b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Step1 of arXiv:2609.01464, 'Removability of non-isolated singularities for Einstein metrics and RCD spaces'] Let $(Z,d,\mathfrak{m})$ be as in (Setting of the paper), and let us assume it verifies the global Sobolev inequality (equation eqn:GlobalSobolev of the paper) in (assumptions of the paper). Then we have the following:
