{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.371016+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a8833aac19fa76ce213d65e803ae2123f8c9715a781c7b542626211ca854374","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2512.08595, 'Small time asymptotics of spectral heat content of isotropic processes'] For any nonnegative measurable function $f$ on $\R^d$ one has
