{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.414147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aa161a9a346a39fc611be932186590f934933d2cd63f944da043ec3428fb777","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:limit_of_kernel of arXiv:2507.22011, 'Random Lozenge Waterfall:\\Dimensional Collapse of Gibbs Measures'] We have the following limits of the correlation kernel $K_t$ on a slice.
	On the center line, that is
	$\mathsf{N}<\mathsf{T}$,
	$\mathsf{t}_l<\mathsf{t}<\mathsf{t}_r$,
	$\mathsf{x}=\tfrac12(\mathsf{S}+\mathsf{t})$, and $\lfloor L\hspace{1pt} \mathsf{x}\rfloor=\tfrac{1}{2}(S+t)$,
	we have
	\begin{equation}

		\lim_{L\to+\infty} K_{\lfloor L\hspace{1pt} \mathsf{t} \rfloor }(\lfloor L\hspace{1pt} \mathsf{x}\rfloor+\Delta x,
		\lfloor L\hspace{1pt} \mathsf{x}\rfloor+\Delta y)=\mathbf{1}_{\Delta x=\Delta y}\quad \textnormal{for all
		$\Delta x,\Delta y\in \mathbb{Z}$}.
	\end{equation}
	Outside the waterfall region, that is,
	for $(\mathsf{t},\mathsf{x})\in \mathcal{W}^+\cup \mathcal{W}^-$,
	we have
	\begin{equation}

		\lim_{L\to+\infty}
		K_{\lfloor L\hspace{1pt} \mathsf{t} \rfloor }
		(\lfloor L\hspace{1pt} \mathsf{x}\rfloor+\Delta x,
		\lfloor L\hspace{1pt} \mathsf{x}\rfloor+\Delta y)=0\quad \textnormal{for all
		$\Delta x,\Delta y\in \mathbb{Z}$}.
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.663351+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aa458233043015f4683c55b27abd499c128da973ce2d490a3fec98aebea7e9a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:nointersectAT of arXiv:2604.15146, 'Renormalised two-point functions of CLE$_4$ gaskets'] Let $\widetilde F_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}$ denote the event that at least two different odd CLE$_4$ gaskets of the family of CLE$_4$ gaskets constructed in Theorem (thm:twopointAT of the paper) intersect both 
$\mathbb{D}(z_1, \varepsilon_1)$ and $\mathbb{D}(z_2, \varepsilon_2)$. Then
\begin{itemize}
    \item Let $E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm{odd},k}(z_1,z_2)$ denote the event that the $k$-th odd nested CLE$_4$ gasket intersects 
    $\mathbb{D}(z_1,\varepsilon_1)$ and $\mathbb{D}(z_2,\varepsilon_2)$. Then there is a constant $C > 0$
    such that for all $k \geq 1$,
    $$\mathbb{P}(\widetilde F_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2} \cap E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm{odd},k}(z_1,z_2)) \leq C(\varepsilon_1\varepsilon_2)^{1/4}\left(\mathbb{P}(E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm{odd},k}) + \1_{k \geq 2}\mathbb{P}(E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm{odd},k-1})\right).$$
    \item Further, for some $\widetilde C > 0$, 
    for all $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2 > 0$ sufficiently small, 
