Further, the same holds when we replace odd by even everywhere. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.355788+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aa632ee5f89e202ee504d1f12078bdfa8d9ec0df7b6cb3bed1047a35f5b6a96","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 37 of arXiv:2606.17501, 'Critical spectral behavior and large deviations for geometric $\alpha$-stable processes'] For any $x \in \mathbb{R}^{d}$ and $\theta \in \mathbb{R}$, the following inequality holds:
