{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.771087+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aaa6dbed73d567bb52ba6bf1a9e06270642b7b0b82a7b3c10019304f2709472","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 45 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Fix $m \in \mathbb{N}$,  $t_1 < \cdots < t_m$, and set $\mathcal{T} = \{t_1, \dots, t_m\}$. If $\nu = (\nu_{t_1}, \dots, \nu_{t_m})$ is an $m$-tuple of locally finite measures on $\mathbb{R}$, we define the (locally finite) measure $\mu_{\mathcal{T},\nu}$ on $\mathbb{R}^2$ by
