{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.833104+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ae78995c8c17e9054a13c36f30b18abe44eab396bf98d6807904635f6ec9669","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 31 (Global selected-coordinate criterion via quotient rank) of arXiv:2604.10792, 'Variable-Length Markov Chains on Finite Quivers: Boundary-Window Identifiability, Exact De'] Fix $m<r$ and assume exact depth $r$ at $\theta_0$ together with \cref{ass:regularity}. Let $T\subset T_{\theta_0}\Theta$ be a tangent block. Let $I$ be a finite family of visible state--appended-edge pairs as in \cref{def:coordinate-map}, and let
\begin{equation}
