\end{enumerate}
Then the depth-$m$ window is not first-order locally sufficient relative to depth $r$ on $T$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:32.055727+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aeb320dc7e13faae82a3ed4e751829488aef82e8c04b4801c0cfe398aff203d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary c.interpolation of arXiv:2411.14105, 'Simultaneous replica-symmetry breaking \\ for vector spin glasses'] Under the same setting as in Lemma~(l.interpolation of the paper), we have
\begin{align*}
    \left|\mathbf{f}_\mu(q,x,z) - \mathbf{f}_\mu(q',x',z')\right|\leqslant \left|z -z'\right| + \left\|q-q'\right\|_{L^1} + |x-x'|,
\end{align*}
and, there is a constant $C_n$ depending only on $n$ such that
\begin{align*}
    \left|\left\langle \mathbf{F}(\cdots) \right\rangle_{\mu,q,x,z} - \left\langle \mathbf{F}(\cdots)\right\rangle_{\mu,q',x',z'}\right|\leqslant C_n \|\mathbf{F}\|_{L^\infty} \left(\left|z -z'\right| + \left\|q-q'\right\|_{L^1}+|x-x'|\right).
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.368515+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aebd1ad0e700bb4df056166dc3dd903719ef358c9a8442467b3b725346e65df","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 (Size-biased law) of arXiv:2606.18458, 'Stable size-biasing and the positive scale-mixture order of generalized Gaussian laws'] Let $Y\ge0$ satisfy $0<\E Y<\infty$. The $Y$-size-biased version $Y^*$ of $Y$ is the positive random variable whose law is defined by
\[
\Prob(Y^*\in A)=\frac{\E[Y\mathbf{1}_{\{Y\in A\}}]}{\E Y},
\]
for Borel sets $A\subseteq[0,\infty)$. Equivalently,
\[
\E h(Y^*)=\frac{\E[Yh(Y)]}{\E Y}
\]
for all bounded measurable $h$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.610357+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7af365f473a40dde567d8c6be9b51bb5bfee6a29e003a1dae9293adf226b3e15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2607.08536, 'Soft edge limit of the Laguerre beta-ensemble at the lower edge'] Fix $\beta>0$ and assume $(\log\log n)^3\ll a_n\ll n$ as $n\to\infty$. There exists a coupling of the kernels $\mathsf{K}_n$ and $\mathsf{K}_{\Ai}$ such that  
