\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.162348+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7af5976a8788068f777c8c9089d254041bb15a45ba08af558cfca61d3f28fc09","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:final of arXiv:2603.00773, 'Long-time $L^p$ Wasserstein contraction for diffusion processes without global dissipativi'] For $\overline{\rho},\overline{\rho}',\overline{S},\overline{M},\overline{\theta},\overline{q}>0$, $\overline{S_2}>\overline{S}$ and $p\geqslant 1$, there exist $\overline{\delta},\overline{C},\overline{\lambda}>0$ (depending only and explicitly on $\overline{\rho},\overline{\rho}',\overline{S},\overline{S_2},\overline{M},\overline{\theta},\overline{q},p$) such that the following holds. Let  $d\in\mathbb N^*$, $b\in\mathcal C^1(\mathbb R^d,\mathbb R^d)$ and $\sigma\in\mathbb R^{d\times d}$ satisfying Assumptions~(assum:decomposeYZ of the paper) and (assum:Contract_at_infty of the paper) with
\begin{equation}

\min(\rho_1,\rho_2) \geqslant \overline{\rho}\,,\quad \max(L_1,L_2,L_3,|Q|,|Q^{-1}|,|\sigma|) \leqslant \overline{M}\,,\quad S^* \leqslant \overline{S},\quad \theta \geqslant \overline{\theta},
\end{equation}
and such that, moreover, for all $x\in\mathbb R^d$ and $v\in\mathbb R^d$ with $v\cdot Q v= 1$,
\begin{equation}

v\cdot Q \nabla b(x) v \leqslant \left\{\begin{array}{ll}
\overline{\delta}&  \text{if }|x| < \overline{S} \\
- \overline{\rho} & \text{if }|x|\geqslant\overline{S}\,,
\end{array}\right.
\end{equation}
and  the invariant measure\footnote{whose existence and uniqueness is implied by Theorem~(thm:contractionMarkov of the paper) applied with $p=1$.} $\mu_\infty$ of~(equation eq:EDS_X of the paper) satisfies
\begin{equation}

\mu_\infty\left( \mathcal B(0,\overline{S_2})\right) \leqslant 1 - \overline{q}\,,
\end{equation}
where $\mathcal B(x,r)=\{y\in\mathbb R^d,\ |y-x|\leqslant r\}$.  

Then, the $L^p$ Wasserstein contraction~(equation eq:contraction_def of the paper) holds with $C = \overline{C}$ and $\lambda = \overline{\lambda}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.723472+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7af779e67cdf46cd0703018247ae48609e833a14d03749dd95320edf131f4667","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:finalintegral of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] Under the assumptions of Proposition~(prop:theRGthm of the paper),  
also for $\hash\in \{{\sf o},{\sf x}\}$,  let $|\lambda_{\hash,{\sf o}}^{(\emptyset)}| ,  |\lambda_{\hash,{\sf x}}^{(\emptyset)}| \le 1$ and $\lambda_{\hash,{\sf o}}^{(\km)} = \lambda_{\hash,{\sf x}}^{(\km)} =0$ for $\km \neq \emptyset$.  Then $Z_N = \E_{w_N} \theta \exp(-V_{0} (\Lambda))$ satisfies
