where $I_N = \cI_N (V_N)$,  $K_N \in M \cK_{N}$ for some (possibly $L$-dependent constant) $M >0$ and $u_N = \sum_{j=1}^{N-1} \delta u_j + \delta u_{N}^{\Lambda_N}$ for some $(\delta u_j)_{j \le N-1}$ that does not depend on $N$.   
Moreover,  if $u_{N,\varnothing}$ and $V_{N,\varnothing}$ are those given by Proposition~(prop:theRGthm of the paper),  we have $\pi_\varnothing (u_N,  V_N ) = (u_{N,\varnothing} ,V_{N,\varnothing})$ and if $\lambda_{N,\hash}^{(\km)}$ are the coefficients of $\pi_\hash V_N$ ($\hash \in \{{\sf o},{\sf x}\}$),  then they satisfy the estimates of Corollary~(cor:lambdainfty of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.598311+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7af79ad208969cf743043b694774e5bd5f55cef407aa05dcdec377823c34d1cf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 (Gaussian predictive excess) of arXiv:2608.25706, 'Fast rates in Bayesian online learning with approximate posteriors'] \label[lemma]{lem:gp-pred-formula}
Let $P$ be a Gaussian law on $L^2(\bP_X)$. Let $m_P$ be the mean function of $P$ and $v_P$ be the variance of $f(x)$ for $f\sim P$. Then
    \begin{equation}
    \cM_t(P)-\cM_t(\delta_{f^\star})
    =\frac12\int \sbr{ g\del[3]{\frac{v_P(x)}{\sigma_\xi^2}}
    +\frac{\{m_P(x)-f^\star(x)\}^2}{\sigma_\xi^2+v_P(x)} }\bP_X(\d x),
    \end{equation}
where $g(u)=\log(1+u)-u/(1+u)$. In particular,
    \begin{equation}
    0\le \cM_t(P)-\cM_t(\delta_{f^\star})
    \le\frac1{2\sigma_\xi^2}\W^2(P,\delta_{f^\star}).
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.846756+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7af93d498ee14837e12dba9e368005a23638fa51ca1419b92dc0bfddbb1e199f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:zt-zs of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] If $X$ is of class $C^1$ and $\sigma$ is smooth, any solution $Z$ to (equation Eq: controlled ODE of the paper)-(equation integral form of the paper) satisfies for all $m\geq 0$
