{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.128317+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7bc2a3be205df166556dbfb842cb31204bf52ab36c9101328269069f062ce904","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:inverse of arXiv:2411.15954, 'A gradient model for the Bernstein polynomial basis'] For each $n,L\in\mathbb{N}$ with $L>n$, it holds that
    \begin{align}
