{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.889235+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c421f35a2718da71c0a81e54af3446c5f9725fc064f1215837dbef5e6a55deb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:common-reference-final of arXiv:2606.29557, 'Propagation of chaos for Belavkin equations beyond pure states'] For every \(t\in[0,T]\),
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb E_{\mathbb Q^{N,\alpha}}
  \left[
    \left\|
      \rho_t^{N,\alpha}
      -
      \rho_t^{N,\beta}
    \right\|_1
  \right]
  \le
  2d_N.

\end{equation}
The same estimate holds for every marginal:
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb E_{\mathbb Q^{N,\alpha}}
  \left[
    \left\|
      \rho_t^{N:n,\alpha}
      -
      \rho_t^{N:n,\beta}
    \right\|_1
  \right]
  \le
  2d_N,
  \qquad
  1\le n\le N.

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.251952+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c43c6065f5fa429d2c03464fbf822b0a86b884bbba2b330eb7e23d2f3a199bf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:ville-expectation of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\mathcal{Y},\hat\mathcal{Z},T)$ be a real-valued sequential gamble space.
