{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.298609+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c5736c7f9ac7c7f4dae1ae2de5f58b298e98e697fc2594975cd54113a84f291","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_sticky_kernel of arXiv:2411.08846, 'On the Number of Crossings and Bouncings\\ of a Diffusion at a Sticky Threshold'] The probability transition kernel of the sticky Brownian motion of stickiness parameter $\rho $ with respect to its speed measure $m_{\rho}(\mathrm{d} y) = \,\mathrm{d} y + \rho \delta_0(\mathrm{d} y)$ is the function defined for all $t>0 $, 
