{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.633325+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c5ba570e9822099a3e5d70ed3c3b2cfd1f87fe39e9b4f1ebeeb2d16ee12948e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma hitting3dLERW of arXiv:2411.13505, 'Capacity of loop-erased random walk'] There exist $C,\alpha>0$ such that for all $\varepsilon>0$, there exists $\delta_0$ such that for all $\delta\leq\delta_0$ and for all $n$,
