{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.862053+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c7db7f99f2b69d936b4023fcb33c8f29c9338036fbd0156cd5deb4c9d10f2fe","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $\lambda,\delta \in (0,1)$ and $\mu\in \mathcal{P}_2(\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{R})$  induced by some random variables $(\xi,X)$ such that $\xi$ is bounded from above and below as in Assumption \ref{Aspt_new}. For $j\ge 0$ consider $\Psi_j$ with its dependence on $\delta$ and $\lambda=c_{min}^2\rhobar^2h$ as defined in \eqref{Eq:Psi_Def}. Then the map $y \mapsto \Psi_j^{-\frac12}(y,\mu)$ is Lipschitz and for all $\gamma \in (0,1)$
