{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.850157+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c8280b7049d847a2ef032122fc043e9f60c3b53e0c63d46a75e50b9c6f6a12a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 68 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] The following conditions are equivalent:
\item[(i)] $F$ is countably ($r$-)monotonically complete;
\item[(ii)] Every countable directed dominable subset of $\Ba_{F_{+}}$ has a supremum in $F$ (of norm at most $r$);
\item[(iii)] $F$ is norm complete and every countable disjoint $D\subset F_{+}$ such that $D^{\vee}\subset\Ba_{F}$ has a supremum in $F$ (of norm at most $r$);
\item[(iv)] The sequential order adherence of $\Ba_{F}$ in $F^{u}$ is contained in $F$ (in $r\Ba_{F}$);
\item[(v)] Every uo-Cauchy sequence in $\Ba_{F}$ has a uo-limit (of norm at most $r$).\medskip

In particular, $F$ is countably monotonically complete and $\sigma$-semicontinuous if and only if $\Ba_{F}$ is sequentially complete with respect to uo convergence.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.889782+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c82d4f5a620e2869b834363874b3c44df8796a2f5a1912ce3d29eacb47b6a10","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:sup:to:pointwise of arXiv:2607.04047, 'Top Singular Value in Sum-Products of Random Matrices'] There exists a universal constant $C > 0$ such that, for any $\epsilon \in (0,1)$ and $\theta \in \mathcal{S}^{n-1}$, we have
\begin{align*}
    {\mathbb P}\Big( 
        \Big| 
            \mfrac{1}{N}
            \log \| X \theta \|
            - 
            \mfrac{1}{N}
            \sup_{\theta' \in \mathcal{S}^{n-1}} 
            \log \| X \theta' \|
        \Big|  
        \,\geq\,
        \mfrac{1}{2 N} \log \Big( \mfrac{n}{\epsilon^2} \Big)
    \Big)
    \leq 
    (C \epsilon)^{1/2}
    \;.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:32.009936+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c848945c2b1edbd8d798a2604a06a70ceae07da246985811ebacab909990e24","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo 14 of arXiv:2512.02766, 'Fine-Graining and Continuous Space Scaling Limit of the $H^{2|2}$ Model on the Hierarchica'] Recall from Theorem~\ref{th:VRJP_Dichotomy} that the Vertex Reinforced Jump Process on $\mathbb{X}$ with spectral dimension $d_s=2$ is either almost surely recurrent or almost surely transcient. Furthermore,
\begin{itemize}
    \item If every vertex is visited infinitely often, then almost surely, the limiting measure $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathbb{X}}$ is singular with respect to the Lebesgue measure $d\lambda$;
    \item If every vertex is visited finitely often, then almost surely, the limiting measure $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathbb{X}}$ has an absolutely continuous component with everywhere non-trivial density with respect to the Lebesgue measure $d\lambda$.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.474145+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c853c43e3b100f9668e4c209274813d1f2f5b012139802a08aa296ee9e3827d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:linear-stat-uniform of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[lemma]{lem:GOE-linear-stat}
Let \(f\in\mathcal F_m\), or let \(f=\ell_\eta\) for a fixed \(\eta>0\), and
define
\[
 L_{N,f}(u)=\operatorname{Tr} f(\gamma_{N,p}M_n-puI_n).
\]
For every compact \(K\subset\mathbb R\),
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{u\in K}\left|
 \frac1N\log\mathbb E e^{L_{N,f}(u)}-\ell_{p,f}(u)
 \right|\longrightarrow0.
\end{equation}
Moreover, uniformly in \(u\in\mathbb R\),
\begin{equation}
 \frac1N\log\mathbb E e^{L_{N,f}(u)}
 \le
 \begin{cases}
  \left\lVertf\right\rVert_\infty,&f\in\mathcal F_m,\\
  C_{p,\eta}+\log(2+\left\lvertu\right\rvert),&f=\ell_\eta.
 \end{cases}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

