{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:08.133273+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c8f8e71b4a3685326b8cdee68c38c1c5bdf2bc1a05aa101526b6866d6b34f87","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:simultaneous-appearance of arXiv:2608.12415, 'Sharp Phase Transition for Ellipsoid Fitting'] Given an $L$-block-step at block-step $i$, the edge(s) in the current block-step must have appeared altogether (potentially with some other edge) in a previous $F$-step, or there is a local-gap (potentially from a previous step).

