{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:16:49.563910+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7cacc19aaf318c4b12ac97b556dee0d8132e01a60b043fdd3c503e15697593ce","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 7 (The 6\,dB/bit rule) of arXiv:2608.25188, 'Transforms for LLM Quantization:\\ The Great Inversion and Format Co-Design'] Under the high-resolution noise model of \Cref{lem:bennett}, for a symmetric $b$-bit uniform quantizer with AbsMax scale on a group of RMS $\sigma$ and max $M$, the signal-to-quantization-noise ratio is
