{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.803421+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7d6b842f3ea0b4eac63b46824632b57903ea421aa60918f0707b81fbabcc7b66","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm l:large-TF-is-uncompetitive of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] For $z,w\in J^\delta$, define the set of paths
    \begin{align*}
        \mathrm{BigTF}^\delta(z;w) \coloneqq  
        \left\{
            \pi \in C([0,\delta^{3/2}]) : \pi(0)=z,\quad \pi(\delta^{3/2})=w,\quad 
            \exists r\in[0,\delta^{3/2}]\text{ such that }
            \pi(r) \not\in J^{\delta'}
        \right\}.
    \end{align*}
    Define also the event
    \begin{align}
        {\mathsf{BigTFCostly}^{\delta}} \coloneqq  
        \left\{
            \inf_{z,w\in J^\delta}
            \left(
                \mathcal{L}(0,z;\delta^{3/2},w) - 
                \sup_{\pi\in \mathrm{BigTF}^\delta(z;w)}
                \int_0^{\delta^{3/2}} d\mathcal{L}\circ \pi
            \right)
            \geqslant 
            \delta^{1/2}\log^7(1/\delta)
        \right\}.
    \end{align}
    There exist $C,c>0$ such that for all sufficiently small $\delta$,
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{P}\left( {\mathsf{BigTFCostly}^{\delta}} \right)
        \geqslant 1- Ce^{-c\log^2(1/\delta)}.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.311076+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7d7498428f508caa1782a450f41de1cc35eb2a0a7b508bf5be2edea348f0f83c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random H\"older velocity '] Let $\alpha \in (0,1/2)$. Suppose $U:\T^d \to\R^d$ is a $C^{\alpha-}(\T^d)$ multiscale finite range random velocity field; that is, $U$ satisfies Assumption~\ref{asmp:main for autonomous}, and \eqref{eq:main theorem hypothesis} holds for all $p\geq 1$.

