{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.617284+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7d78ecea40e701f76f76628b8e7dd608f02fb49c120c0b628e417b54920e79c0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Writing $x_0:=\varrho,x_1,\dots,x_n:=\zero$ for the vertices on the unique path in~$\T_n$ from the root to vertex~$\zero$, for any Borel sets $E_k\subseteq\R^{\T_k'}$ indexed by $k=1,\dots,n$ we have
\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
P^\zero\biggl(\,\bigcap_{k=1}^{n}\Bigl\{\bigl\{\ell_{\tau_\varrho}(x)&\colon 
x\in \T_{n-k}^{\prime} (x_k)  \bigr\}\in E_{n-k}\Bigr\}\,\bigg|\, \sigma\bigl(\ell_{\tau_{\varrho}}(x_k)\colon k=1,\dots,n\bigr)\biggr)
\\
&=\prod_{k=1}^n P^\varrho\Bigl(\bigl\{L_{t_k}(x)\colon x\in
\T_{n-k}^{\prime}\bigr\}
\in E_{n-k}\Bigr)\Big|_{t_k:=\ell_{\tau_\varrho}(x_k)}\quad\text{\rm a.s.}
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where~$\T_{n-k}'(x_k)$ is the connected component of~$\T_n$ containing~$x_k$ when the edges on the path $(x_0,\dots,x_n)$ are removed from~$\T_n$. (We regard $\T_{n-k}'(x_k)$ as isomorphic to~$\T_{n-k}'$ defined earlier.) (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.651716+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7d859f0bd088fa7003a691b550baccab0ab3f2813ea85fe11b59c4c817f93735","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm21 of arXiv:2605.16160, 'Revisiting Toeplitz and Hankel random matrices via $*$-convergence of circulant-type matri'] Let $C_n$ be a random circulant matrix with independent entries that satisfy Assumption I. 
