{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.725096+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7d94c93f9b296b210038202f43396ba0565ec0caa7d7d58001ee9cc5262c78b6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 34 of arXiv:2511.13559, 'Asymptotic analysis of rare events in high dimensions'] The derivative bounds~\eqref{forq},~\eqref{forw} of Proposition~\ref{prop:main} imply 
\begin{alignat}{2}
\sup_{x\in\us(R\e)}\|\nabla_x^\ell\z(x,0)\|_H&\les d^{\lceil\ell/2\rceil-2}, &\quad&\ell=3,\dots,2N+2,\\
\sup_{(x,y)\in \us(R\e)\times[0,(R\e)^2]}|D_{\z}^{k-1}\g(x,y)|&\les 1,& &k=1,\dots,N+1,\\
