{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:48:00.290663+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ddcd1717fa8be4efdc6edbca22c5ead4b7e5556a183bbe8976e52fd883f753d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:variationalForm of arXiv:2609.03094, 'Discrete Gromov--Wasserstein Duality: Algorithms and Isomorphism Testing'] Any symmetric matrix $\mathrm{M}\in\mathbb R^{k\times k}$ can be decomposed as $\mathrm{M}=\mathrm{B}_1^{\intercal}\mathrm{B}_1-\mathrm{B}_0^{\intercal}\mathrm{B}_0$ for some $\mathrm{B}_0\in\mathbb R^{r_0\times k},\mathrm{B}_1\in\mathbb R^{r_1\times k}$ with $r_0,r_1\leq k$. With this, 
\begin{equation}

    \inf_{u\in\mathbb R^{r_0}}\sup_{v\in\mathbb R^{r_1}}\left\{ \frac12\|u\|^2-\frac 12 \|v\|^2+\inf_{x\in\mathcal K}\left\{\left( \mathrm{B}_1^{\intercal}v-\mathrm{B}_0^{\intercal} u \right)^{\intercal}x-\varepsilon\mathsf{H}(x)  \right\} \right\}
\end{equation} is equivalent to (equation eq:entropicQP of the paper)  
in the sense that the optimal values of both problems coincide and  
\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*]
    \item If $x^{\star}$ solves (equation eq:entropicQP of the paper), then $(u^{\star},v^{\star})=(\mathrm{B}_0 x^{\star},\mathrm{B}_1 x^{\star})$ solves the outer $\inf$-$\sup$ problem in (equation eq:variationalForm of the paper) and $x^{\star}\in\argmin_{x\in\mathcal K}\left\{\left( \mathrm{B}_1^{\intercal}v^{\star}-\mathrm{B}_0^{\intercal}u^{\star} \right)^{\intercal}x-\varepsilon\mathsf{H}(x)  \right\}$. 
    \item If, conversely, $(u^{\star},v^{\star})$ solves the outer $\inf$-$\sup$ problem in (equation eq:variationalForm of the paper), then there exists  
    $
    \bar x \in \argmin_{x\in\mathcal K}\left\{\left( \mathrm{B}^{\intercal}_1v^{\star}-\mathrm{B}_0^{\intercal} u^{\star} \right)^{\intercal}x-\varepsilon\mathsf{H}(x)  \right\}$ which
    solves (equation eq:entropicQP of the paper) and $(u^{\star},v^{\star})=(\mathrm{B}_0 \bar x, \mathrm{B}_1\bar x)$.  
\end{enumerate} 
Moreover, $\argmax_{v\in\mathbb R^{r_1}}\left\{ \frac12\|u\|^2-\frac 12 \|v\|^2+\inf_{x\in\mathcal K}\left\{\left( \mathrm{B}_1^{\intercal}v-\mathrm{B}_0^{\intercal} u \right)^{\intercal}x-\varepsilon\mathsf{H}(x)  \right\} \right\}\subset \mathrm{B}_1\mathcal K$ for any $u\in \mathbb R^{r_0}$. Thus, the outer $\inf$ and $\sup$ in (equation eq:variationalForm of the paper) can be restricted to $\mathrm{B_0}\mathcal K$ and $\mathrm{B_1}\mathcal K$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

