{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.257742+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7df8636797d1fc90af7d5988058ef550e9be164ae23de47408c59fe5a209269c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro 2 (Case of $\Rr^d$) of arXiv:2609.01105, 'Obstruction to quasi-invariance of Gaussian measures under transport flows on Riemannian M'] Assume that~\((M,g)\) is the Euclidean space $\Rr^d$ equipped with the flat metric. Then the following statements are equivalent: 
