{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.018856+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e9388ff49940c06f786536847c8cfd6b4970b2d7f303928681b1c9f8c76730b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 5 of arXiv:2605.05986, '\bf Convergence rate of the occupation measure of { classes of ergodic processes toward th'] Let $(X_t)_{t\ge0}$ denote an $({\cal F}_t)_{t\ge0}$-adapted right continuous  process with values in $\ER^d$. Let $q>1$, $\gamma\in(0,1/2]$, {$\nu\in{\cal P}(\ER^d)$},  and a bounded function $e:\ER_+\rightarrow\ER_+$ such that

