{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.280116+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ef52da550139b0d6ab91707426fcb9ce59c2a08c6f31ee00a1997cc9c78dd44","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 (Comparison of free energies and Gibbs averages) of arXiv:2606.22611, 'Upper and Lower Bounds on Expected Soft Maxima\\of Gaussian Processes'] The functions $\beta \mapsto \langle X \rangle_{\beta,\mu}$ and $\beta \mapsto \eG_\beta(X;\mu)$ are monotonically increasing. Moreover, the following inequality holds:
