{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.694476+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8068a31d0b7591d8611ae3a5aac63fb0b46823cc6f2dfdcc601750634a38860e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop LT-2 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] Given $c,\theta>0$, there exists $C=C(c,\theta,\gamma) > 0$ such that, if $k$ is large enough, given any integer $j>1$, $n \geq k$ and $\widetilde{x} \in {\rm D}_n$ such that $\overline{{\rm B}^+[\widetilde{x};j]}\subseteq {\rm D}_n$, for all $x,x' \in {\rm B}^-[\widetilde{x};j-1]$ with $\log \| x-x'\| \geq k+(j-2-c)k^\gamma$ we have
\begin{equation}
	\mathbb{P} \Big( \max\{L_t(x), L_t(x')\} \leq \theta \,\Big|\, \sqrt{\widehat{N}_t[\widetilde{x};j]} \geq v \,; 
\mathcal F[\widetilde{x};j]\Big) \\ \leq  {\rm e}^{ - 4(k+jk^\gamma) -4\sqrt{2}\widehat{v}  + Ck^\gamma}.
