{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.999832+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_807f111a622b36f08fc977a3556f2752a0c9003d8c8ab200a6a8cfb3264b78a3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2604.17253, 'Large Deviations for the Nonlinear Schrödinger Equation with Randomized Quasi-Periodic Ini'] The {\em first counting function} $\sigma$ on $\Gamma^{(k)}$ is defined by
