{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.801547+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_80f0bdfea66b63e8307dea397322ecede188d44952d2d416d69ea2bf83f41b07","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] $F$ is $r$-semicontinuous if and only if the common order and uo closure of $\Ba_{F}$ is contained in $r\Ba_{F}$. Moreover, the following conditions are equivalent:
