{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.583326+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8115469ccc529b335bccc2c1e65abd714a24df8881009e951fd570516dcb447b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] For  $\mathsf{P}_i\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$, $i=0,1$ we denote by $ \mathsf{Cpl}_{s,m}(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1)$ the set of all $\sigma$-finite stationary  (with respect to the shifts $(\theta_x)_{x\in \IR^2}$) measures  $ \mathsf{Q}$ on $\Gamma_{\IR^2}$ such that:
