{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.280370+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8170c8ce481fba5a18a535634b9a491f46f2101b414c1e04b77af32795d8922b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2606.22611, 'Upper and Lower Bounds on Expected Soft Maxima\\of Gaussian Processes'] Let a centered stationary Gaussian process $(X_t)_{t\in T}$ be given. Then, for any $\mu \in \eP(T)$,
