{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.502460+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81f987be72be3b877d1270e16ccb9582698fd1d8166061e4b246c1353e222c04","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 50 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] For all $t \in [0,T]$ with $t \leq 1$ and all $(Y,Y') \in \bbb_t$ we have
