{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.108043+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_820125ab119d117f651c27a228a25a4ea7b16c3fe6ff349997a82ee82550a736","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:multi-agent-macroscopic-intermediate-solved-weights of arXiv:2606.21556, 'Mean field limit of non-exchangeable interacting diffusions on co-evolutionary networks'] For every \(N\in \mathbb{N}\), we define the piecewise-constant extensions of the state processes
	and the initial weight laws as
	\begin{equation*}
		\begin{aligned}
		\bar X^N(t,\xi) &:= \sum_{i=1}^N \bar X_i^N(t)\,\mathds{1}_{I_i^N}(\xi), \quad t\in [0,T],\,\xi\in [0,1],\\
		q^{N,\xi,\xi'}_0 &:= \sum_{i,j=1}^N q^N_{ij,0}\,\mathds{1}_{I_i^N\times I_j^N}(\xi,\xi'), \quad \xi,\xi'\in [0,1].
		\end{aligned}
	\end{equation*}
	With this notation, the independent projection system (equation eq:multi-agent-discrete-independent-projection-solved-weights of the paper)
	can be equivalently rewritten as the following system of path-dependent McKean-Vlasov SDEs parameterized by \(\xi \in [0,1]\):
	\begin{align}
		d\bar X^N(t,\xi) &= \int_0^1\int_{\mathcal{C}^d_t} \int_{\mathbb{R}} \Phi_t(\bar{X}^N(\cdot,\xi)_{[0,t]},\gamma,w) K(\bar X^N(t,\xi),\gamma(t)) \, dq^{N,\xi,\xi'}_0(w)\,d\bar \mu_{[0,t]}^{N,\xi'}(\gamma)\,d\xi' dt + \sqrt{2\nu}\,dW^N(t,\xi),\nonumber\\
		\bar X^N(0,\xi) &= X^N_{0}(\xi), \quad \bar \mu^{N,\xi}_{[0,t]} := \mathrm{Law}(\bar X^N(\cdot,\xi)_{[0,t]}) \in \mathcal{P}(\mathcal{C}^d_t).
	\end{align}
	The initial states are analogously set as
	\begin{equation*}
		X_0^N(\xi) := \sum_{i=1}^N X_{i,0}^N\,\mathds{1}_{I_i^N}(\xi), \quad \xi\in [0,1],
	\end{equation*}
	and the driving noise \(W^N(t,\xi)\) is defined piecewise by
	\[
		W^N(t,\xi) := \sum_{i=1}^N W_i^N(t)\, \mathds{1}_{I_i^N}(\xi),\quad t \in [0,T],\,\xi\in [0,1].
	\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.972126+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8207ca2fde1ed6d6ea303c1029291b14e6b1d6293dbf2e86d6d91cc9dbd13ed3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:grafting_full of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] We define, for any $\mu \in [0,1]$, a ``grafting with scale'' $\graft^{\mu}: \text{${\mcb{C}}$} \otimes \text{${\mcb{C}}$} \rightarrow \text{${\mcb{C}}$}$. 

Let $\mu \in [0,1]$. 
Given $\tau_1,\tau_2 \in \mathfrak{T}$ and $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_1} \in \text{${\mcb{C}}$}[\tau_1]$, $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_2} \in \text{${\mcb{C}}$}[\tau_2]$, we define $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_2} \graft^{\mu} \text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_1} \in \text{${\mcb{C}}$}$ as follows. 
We first choose $\underline{\tau}_1 \in \tau_1$, $\underline{\tau}_2 \in \tau_2$, and write  $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\underline{\tau}_1} = \iota_{\tau_1,\underline{\tau}_1} \text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_1}$, $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\underline{\tau}_2} = \iota_{\tau_2,\underline{\tau}_2} \text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_2}$. 
We then set
\begin{equ}
\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_2} \graft^{\mu} \text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_1} 
\eqdef \sum_{n \in N(\underline{\tau}_1)} 
\pi_{\underline{\tau}_{1,2,n}} \big(
\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\underline{\tau}_1}\graft^\mu_n\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\underline{\tau}_2}\big)\,,
\end{equ}
where $\graft^\mu_n$ is given in Definition~(def:scaledlabeledgraft of the paper). 
where we are writing $\underline{\tau}_{1,2,n} = \underline{\tau}_{2} \graft_n \underline{\tau}_{1}$, and using, for $\underline{\sigma} \in \sigma \in \mathfrak{T}$, the shorthand $\pi_{\underline{\sigma}} =\pi_{\sigma,\underline{\sigma}}$. 
We then extend $\graft^\mu$ to ${\mcb{C}}\otimes{\mcb{C}}$ by linearity.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.182630+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_820c0eb551490cb4d9f4214ff5e2c65f410326e259165543380f950ce685eedb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Xdev of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] Suppose $\mathbf{x} \in \mathrm{Meso}(N)$. Then, for all $t \geqslant 0$ and $\Delta>0$, we have
