Moreover, $A_t\geq c\operatorname{Id}_E$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.436624+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_825d047b15abb443cad8536336d93829469a0cb8acf0a00a96bf68dda8dc2e2e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lemma1.5 of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] Let $\Lambda \subseteq \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}^d}$ be a finite set and let $\nu$ be a strictly positive probability measure on $\left\{ 0 , 1 \right\}^{\Lambda}$. We assume that for any vertex $x \in \Lambda$ and any configuration $r_1 \in \Lambda \setminus \{ x \}$, one has the inequality
        \begin{equation*}
            \nu \left( r_x = 1 \, | \, r = r_1 ~ \mbox{in} ~ \Lambda \setminus \{ x \} \right) \leq p.
        \end{equation*}
        Then $\mathbb{P}_{\Lambda,p}^{\mathrm{site}}$ stochastically dominates $\nu$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.749582+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_825fc99af98004eb218713f08fba9e0dc087d4aa5333095bc5bf3bdd233e2962","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Lambda-diamond of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] For $v \in \mathcal{V}^m$, set $P(v) \vcentcolon= I + B_v(v, v) \in \mathrm{End}(E^m)$.  Then $P(v)$ is invertible with $P(v)^{-1} = I - B_v(\mathcal{T}v, \mathcal{T}v)$, and the edge weights $(C_k, \Lambda_k)$ with
    \begin{equation}
        \Lambda_k(u) \vcentcolon= P(u) D_k(u) P(\mathcal{S}_k u)^{-1}

    \end{equation}
    satisfy the diamond equations (equation eq:diamond-C-ij of the paper)--(equation eq:diamond-mixed-ij of the paper) on $\mathcal{G}^m$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.762988+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_82605b7927a0302e26af09ff9ceb59ead1b514ec2701f3a39f810328755846b2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:lemflow of arXiv:2411.02541, 'The hockey-stick conjecture for\\ activated random walk'] \thlabel{lem:flow}
  Let $u$ be an extended odometer on $\ii{0,n}$.
  Let $f_v=\rt{u}{v}-\lt{u}{v+1}$, the net flow from $v$ to $v+1$.
  Let $s_v=\sum_{i=1}^v\1\{\mathsf{instr}_i(u(i))=\ensuremath{\mathtt{sleep}}\}$.
