{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.264777+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_828a120f3165fced8bf4319724a332c4481cb632a64b57b217be8e7803b0cf8d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2604.19924, 'Fluctuation theory for spectrally negative Lévy processes killed by additive functionals'] Let $x \leq b$ and $q \geq 0$. Then
