{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.472147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_828ac5e06bb5222fd7cb5892b177c2668de7c34000465bbb85bba3776dc5b77c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 109 (H\"older norms on $\datahypfortimefunctiontwoarg{0}{[\timefunction_0,0) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] }$]  Let $f$ be a scalar function on $\datahypfortimefunctiontwoarg{0}{[\timefunction_0,0]}$, let $m \geq 0$ be an integer. Then we define the H\"older norm of $f$ relative to geometric coordinates (see the embedding \eqref{E:XMUISMINUSCAPPISAGRAPH}): 
	\begin{align} 
