{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.473613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_82d0c7b64b99c8de3459013d5ad2bfeb81b8d46fa2942b836391badd40002a92","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop adj-functor-thm of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] \begin{enumerate}
        \item Let ${\mathcal{C}}$ be $T$-presentable and let ${\mathcal{D}}$ be $T$-cocomplete and locally small. A $T$-functor $F\colon{\mathcal{C}}\to{\mathcal{D}}$ is a left adjoint if and only if it is $T$-cocontinuous.
        \item Let ${\mathcal{C}},{\mathcal{D}}$ be $T$-presentable. A $T$-functor $G\colon{\mathcal{C}}\to{\mathcal{D}}$ is a right adjoint if and only if it is $T$-continuous and fiberwise accessible (meaning that each ${\mathcal{C}}(A)\to{\mathcal{D}}(A)$ is accessible).\qedhere\qed
