\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.590804+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8316e3da084db1a08d4169a28416b2db3d0329e1effbcedcc50baf81e870ce95","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop pro:limit_thm_2.2 of arXiv:2412.03370, 'TASEP with a general initial condition and a deterministically moving wall'] Recall $\tilde{x}_n(0)=x_n^f$ and suppose $\{x_n^f, n \in \mathbb{N}\}$ fulfils Assumption~(assumpt:2.9 of the paper). Then, it holds 
	\begin{equation}
	\begin{aligned} 
	\lim_{T \to \infty} \mathbb{P}(\tilde{x}_{\alpha T}(T) > g_\alpha T - S T^{1/3})
	&= \mathbb{P} \left( \sup_{\tau \in \mathbb{R}} \{ \mathcal{A}_2(\tau) - \tau^2 - y(-\tau) \} < c_1^{-1} S \right)
	\end{aligned}  
	\end{equation}
	with $g_\alpha = 1-d^{-1}-d\alpha$ and $c_1 = (1-d^{-1})^{2/3} d^{1/3}$. 

	Suppose $\{x_n^f,n \in \mathbb{N}\}$ fulfils Assumption~(assumpt:2.7 of the paper). Then, we have $g_\alpha = 1-2\sqrt{\alpha}$. If $d = \tfrac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}}$, then it holds
	\begin{equation}
	\begin{aligned} 
	\lim_{T \to \infty} \mathbb{P}(\tilde{x}_{\alpha T}(T) > g_\alpha T - S T^{1/3})
	&= \mathbb{P} \left( \sup_{\tau \leq 0} \{ \mathcal{A}_2(\tau) - \tau^2 - y(-\tau) \} < c_1^{-1} S \right).
	\end{aligned}   
	\end{equation}
	If $d < \tfrac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}}$, then it holds
