{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:09.042535+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8324f55c88c2315f748c9d382041d145d9ff2aeb3bfa72bd403cabaeb89f48b6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 2 of arXiv:2606.27078, 'Semimartingale Optimal Transport with Jumps: A General Framework and Equivalent Formulatio'] Let $\Theta\subseteq\mathbb{R}^d\times\mathbb{S}_+^d\times\mathcal{L}$ be closed, convex, and satisfy Assumptions~\ref{B} and~\ref{J}. Moreover, let the cost function $L$ satisfy Assumption~\ref{L}. Then we have
