{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:48:00.184587+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_834d529c6b122b8167ab1f907ff821886db5400dcc9e0180f3d002994919aaf9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem BGST of arXiv:2609.02882, 'A new proof that more than $2/3$ of the zeros of the Riemann zeta function are simple and '] Let $f\in L^{1}(\mathbb R)$ be a real-valued even function with support in $[-1,1]$, and suppose that $f$ is Lipschitz continuous at $x =0$ (that is, $
