{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.088540+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_83536032dbe445ac6a2bdb80ed853345d62ab968fd15dc569c6bebdd846836e9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro-marked-signed of arXiv:2411.12623, 'Random signed measures'] A $T$-marked signed point process $\xi$ on $S$ has independent $S$-increments iff a.s.
	\begin{equation*}
		\xi=\eta_+-\eta_-+\sum_{k}(\delta_{s_k}\otimes\delta_{\tau_k})
	\end{equation*}
	for some independent Poisson processes $\eta_+$ and $\eta_-$ on $S\times T$ with $E[\eta_+(\{s\}\times T)]\equiv 0$ and $E[\eta_-(\{s\}\times T)]\equiv 0$, some distinct points $s_1,s_2,...\in S$, and some independent random elements $\tau_1,\tau_2,...\in T^{\Delta}$ with distributions $\nu_1,\nu_2,...$, such that the measures
	\begin{equation*}
		\rho_1=\mathbb{E}[\eta_+]+\sum_{k}(\delta_{s_k}\otimes\nu_{k}),\quad\text{and}\quad 	\rho_2=\mathbb{E}[\eta_-]
	\end{equation*}
	on $S\times T$ are locally finite. Here $\rho_1$ and $\rho_2$ determine uniquely $\mathcal{L}(\xi)$, and any measures $\rho_1$ and $\rho_2$ on $\mathcal{M}_{S\times T}$ with $\sup_{s}\rho_1(\{s\}\times T)\leq 1$ and  $\sup_{s}\rho_2(\{s\}\times T)=0$ may occur. Further, $\eta_+$ and $\eta_-$ are the Jordan decomposition of the non-fixed atomic component of $\xi$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:40:21.311355+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_83551a37bc28ea42cf8b9b37bc8c37f3275e83f0a4f92243c8799b34a4594e1e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2604.08127, 'Asymptotics of Brownian occupation measures \\ with unusually large intersections'] For any integer $m \ge 0$,

