{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.905840+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_83a5fb13f25a7731b9605db685110aa9e6527dc5ac7b45eec4cc424627e117d2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:HW of arXiv:2608.26707, 'An Exponential Lower Bound for the Permanent\\of Random Bernoulli Matrix'] Let $\varepsilon=(\varepsilon_1,\dots,\varepsilon_N)$ have independent uniform sign coordinates, and let $A$ be a deterministic real symmetric $N\times N$ matrix.
