{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.594238+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_83dbccb49e83dc0e140d788edde5c21227753414c8bb7a7df0961c9723657c97","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Sufficient conditions of  \cref{ass:predictive-stability}) of arXiv:2608.25706, 'Fast rates in Bayesian online learning with approximate posteriors'] Let $\Theta\subset\R^d$ be convex and compact. Suppose that, for every $t$, almost surely, the map $\ell_t(\cdot;(x,y))$ is continuously differentiable on a neighborhood of $\Theta$ for almost every conditional realization $(x,y)$ of $(X_t,Y_t)$, and there are nonnegative $\cG_t$-measurable envelopes $H_t,G_t,D_t$ such that
     \begin{align}
     \|\nabla\ell_t(\theta;(X_t,Y_t))-\nabla\ell_t(u;(X_t,Y_t))\|
     &\le H_t\|\theta-u\|,\qquad \theta,u\in\Theta, \\
     \sup_{\theta\in\Theta}\|\nabla\ell_t(\theta;(X_t,Y_t))\|
     &\le G_t,\\
     \sup_{\theta,u\in\Theta}|\ell_t(\theta;(X_t,Y_t))-\ell_t(u;(X_t,Y_t))|
     &\le D_t.
    \end{align}
Assume that there exists an absolute constant $C_{\rm env}>0$ such that
    \begin{equation}
    \E\sbr{\e^{\eta D_t}(H_t+\eta G_t^2)\mid\cG_{t-1}}
    \le C_{\rm env}\qquad
    \text{a.s. for every }t\in\bN.
    \end{equation}
Moreover, assume that there exists $\theta^\star\in\operatorname{int}(\Theta) $ such that
    \begin{equation}
    \E[\nabla\ell_t(\theta^\star;(X_t, Y_t))\mid\cG_{t-1}]=0
    \qquad\text{a.s.}
    \end{equation}
Then \cref{ass:predictive-stability} holds for all probability measures supported on $\Theta$, with a deterministic constant depending only on $C_{\rm env}$, $\eta$, and $\operatorname{diam}(\Theta)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.647058+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_83e60471b4202a90f4133f09d262d4473d3c9206b17031d427b6b5f9026619e2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:W as a sum of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] Let $\mu=\mu_n$ be such that $(\log^{3/2}n)/\sqrt{n}\ll\mu\ll n$ and {recall $t_{\mu/n}=\argmin_{t \in (0,2)}\lambda_{\mu/n}(t)$.}
    Then, for any $\epsilon_n\ll1$ such that $(\mu^2n)^{1/3}\epsilon_n^2\gg\log n$ and $\epsilon\gg(\mu/n)^{1/3}$ (which are both possible thanks to the assumption on $\mu$) the sum $W_n$ defined in~(equation eq:def W of the paper) satisfies
    \begin{align*}
        W_n=\big(1+o(1)\big)\frac{\mu}{2n}e^{-n\lambda_{\mu/n}(t_{\mu/n})}\sum_{|m-t_{\mu/n}|<\epsilon_nt_{\mu/n}}\exp\left(-\left(\frac{3}{2}+o(1)\right)\left(\frac{\mu^4}{2\pi^2n}\right)^{1/3}\big(m-t_{\mu/n}\big)^2\right)\,,
    \end{align*}
    where the $o(\cdot)$ in the exponential are uniform over all terms of the sum.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:57:28.722744+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_83e67e6c2a0e7a031fec18830c23d82faa13cc3eaf130f33d1ea6b6747e3e09f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 13 of arXiv:2609.01190, 'Rough differential equations on manifolds via natural bundles'] Let $m,n\in\Nsf$, let $M$ be an $m$-dimensional manifold, and let $(U,x)$ be a chart on $M$. Let $f: M\to R_n^2M$ be a rough velocity field whose representation in the induced chart $(\overline{U},\overline{x})$ on $R_n^2M$ is $(f^i_\tau)$. Let also $\delta: M\to\Rsf$ be a smooth function. A \emph{rescaling} of $f$ by $\delta$ is the rough velocity field $\widetilde{f}: M\to R_n^2M $ whose representation $(\widetilde{f}^i_\tau)$ in chart $(\overline{U},\overline{x})$ is given by 
	\begin{equation}

		\widetilde{f}^i_{\ta} = \delta f^i_{\ta}, 
			\quad 
		\widetilde{f}^i_{\tab} = \delta^2f^i_{\tab},
			\quad \mbox{and} \quad 
		\widetilde{f}^i_{\tc} = \frac{\partial \delta}{\partial x^j}f^j_{\ta}\delta f^i_{\tb} + \delta^2f^i_{\tc}
	\end{equation}
for $i\in \llbracket 1,m \rrbracket$ and $\alpha,\beta\in\llbracket 1,n \rrbracket$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.302164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_83e7519309aeefae4802353c8b8d9c563bbd23f2337e65bb384e9f6896d431a9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:o4 of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] Let $\mathcal{F}\subseteq \Phi$ be such that 
 \begin{enumerate} [label=\rm(\roman{*}), ref=\rm(\roman{*})]
     \item Uniform boundedness.
     \begin{equation}
     \sup_{\varphi\in\mathcal{F}}\sup_{\xi\in\mathfrak{X}}\varphi(\xi)<\infty    
     \end{equation}
     \item For any $R\in\mathbb{R}$ there exists $I_R\subseteq \mathfrak{X}$ compact such that\ 
     \begin{equation}
         \sup_{\varphi\in\mathcal{F}}\sup_{\xi\in I^c_R}\frac{\varphi(\xi)}{\mathcal P(\xi)^2}<R.
     \end{equation}
