{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:49:21.120677+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_84ea64c3584f4f132eefd994b82adf37f68b913354cdf4a35976efdafdb8636c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 6 of arXiv:2608.26642, '2608.26642'] Assume that $(X,\mathbb{P}_x)$ admits transition densities $p_u(\cdot)$ for $u>0$. For $x\in \R$, we then have
\begin{align}
  \Q_x^\mu=\frac{1}{\varphi^\mu(x)}\int_0^\infty \Big((\Gamma_u^\mu\cdot\P_{x,0}^u)\bullet (\Gamma_\infty^\mu\cdot\P_0^{(0)})\Big)p_u(-x)du+\frac{h(x)\cdot \Gamma_\infty^\mu}{\varphi^\mu(x)}\cdot\P_x^{(0)},
\end{align}
where $\mathbb{P}_{x,0}^u$ denotes the \Levy\ bridge from $X_0=x$ to $X_u=0$, $\mathbb{P}_x^{(0)}$ denotes the law of the \Levy\ process conditioned to avoid zero, and the symbol $\bullet$ denotes concatenation. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.366838+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_84f02d4b72a8e880175ddd956bbb3f6dc8727a7984786ababf922f36655103d6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem -1 of arXiv:2411.13403, 'Path weighting method for spot sensitivities and its variance reduction'] Let $X$, $\tilde{X}$ be two $n$-dimensional random
variables such that $\mathbb{E}(X)=\mathbb{E}(\tilde{X})=x_{0}$,
