{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:19:42.449615+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8505a4b6b77b40a9dcb12383f1e9672c17d0b2738ead802c4eb66597b468bcc0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2609.03418, 'Sampling and Density Theorems for the Fractional Opdam--Cherednik Transform'] Let $\alpha \geq \beta \geq -\frac{1}{2}$ with $\alpha > -\frac{1}{2}$. The Opdam--Cherednik transform $\mathcal{H}_{\alpha, \beta} (f)$ of a function $f \in C_c(\R)$ is defined by
\begin{equation} \H_{\alpha, \beta} (f) (\lambda)=\dint_{\R} f(x)\; G^{\alpha, \beta}_\lambda(-x)\; A_{\alpha, \beta} (x) dx \quad \text{for all } \lambda \in \C. \end{equation}
The inverse Opdam--Cherednik transform for a suitable function $g$ on $\R$ is given by
\begin{equation} \H_{\alpha, \beta}^{-1} (g) (x)= \dint_{\R} g(\lambda)\; G^{\alpha, \beta}_\lambda(x)\; d\sigma_{\alpha, \beta}(\lambda) \quad \text{for all } x \in \R, \end{equation}
where $$d\sigma_{\alpha, \beta}(\lambda)= \left(1- \dfrac{\rho}{i \lambda} \right) \dfrac{d \lambda}{8 \pi |C_{\alpha, \beta}(\lambda)|^2}$$ and
$$C_{\alpha, \beta}(\lambda)= \dfrac{2^{\rho - i \lambda} \Gamma(\alpha+1) \Gamma(i \lambda)}{\Gamma \left(\frac{\rho + i \lambda}{2}\right)\; \Gamma\left(\frac{\alpha - \beta+1+i \lambda}{2}\right)}, \quad \lambda \in \C \setminus i \mathbb{N}.$$","status":"unverified"}

